{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"ef9f3fc8-12b6-4fe4-9f49-aaeedec05648","hash":"c88b82820b03979a1de2ea8af5a817593fcd14e5090fa8c2c27bd7433e9ba158","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016jo6U8MYS5Dg7LaaoYy9wV","type":"tool_result","content":"src/lib/spec-dsl-figures.ts:462:  return `A fired failure mode loops back, runs its on_exhausted handler once the loops run out, or ends the run; ${plural(rows.length, 'branch', 'branches')} in all, ending with ${list(codes)} where no handler takes over.`;\n255:| `retry` | object | `{max, backoff}`: up to `max` further attempts after R401, R402 or R406 (not after an R402 the executor raises itself before asking the host, such as an `invoke` input the target refuses: another attempt would be refused the same way); `max` an integer from 0 to 1000 and `backoff` one of `none` (also when absent or null), `linear`, `exponential` (else S303) |\n433:| `on_error` | code or list | No | Fires on a code the step failed with: R401, R402, R403, R406, F501, F502, F504 (§5.12) |\n631:code or a list: R401, R402, R403, R406, F501, F502, F504; anything else is S303 —\n672:  (R402), so a reference is checked then.\n689:| No loop (prose or absent `recovery`) | The run ends with the step's code; a failure mode fired by `when` on a step that did not fail ends it R402 (\"failure mode N fired\") |\n716:(R402), before a waiting `delegate` delegates: an event that lacks the key\n755:`task_id` (else R402), and the wait's `correlate` gains it, so only that\n762:R402. A `retry` of the step delegates again, and the new capability call\n896:that ends so is, for its invoke step, an escalated nested run (R402).\n929:fails the step (R402): an empty list would drop every sender, and a null","is_error":false}]}}
