{"parentUuid":"528b0f38-c1e2-4e76-a5eb-ce74d4f88929","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgykydb3gE924BTp3w57E","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01VJ5j3QHm8LpopzxGiadycY","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Review removed diagrams, restore useful ones","prompt":"Repository synaptiai/agent-capability-standard, worktree /Users/danielbentes/agent-capability-standard/.claude/worktrees/wf_08f3cd25-fc3-8, branch feature/issue-125-site-visuals (head 8d94ad0, pushed). Work directly in that worktree.\n\nCommit f5b1243 (\"docs: drop diagrams that repeat the table, list or code beside them\") removed 98 Mermaid diagrams from Markdown files. About 45 were removed only because an automatic score found 80%+ of their labels in the neighbouring table, list or code block, without anyone reading them. The maintainer wants every removed diagram judged by reading, and restored when it adds something.\n\nTask:\n1. For EACH of the 98 removed diagrams (`git show f5b1243` lists them; a pre-extracted list with titles and edge counts is at REDACTED.json), read the diagram and the text beside it in the CURRENT file. Restore it when it shows something the neighbouring text does not show at a glance: an order the text gives only in prose or an unordered list, branching or conditions, a loop, which item feeds which, or a sequence spread over a long code block. Keep it removed when it says the same thing in the same shape as the neighbour, for example a numbered list redrawn as a straight chain, or a table redrawn as boxes with no added relation.\n2. Before restoring, check the diagram against its text: every node and edge is stated there, edges point the right way, no unordered list is drawn as a chain, labels add no claims, accDescr matches. Correct it if needed. Restore it in the same place as before.\n3. Rules: no Mermaid in skills/*/SKILL.md, skills/*/reference/, CHANGELOG.md or spec/STANDARD-v*.md. Every diagram keeps a title: front matter and an accDescr: line.\n4. Run in site/: npm run check, npm test, npm run build, npm run check:axe (all must pass; check:axe also enforces the run-length limit). From the repo root: python tools/validate_doc_links.py. Fix any failure.\n5. Commit with a message written to a file and `git commit -F <file>`; end the message with:\n\nRefs #125\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Jea2Va3FATnCydAsWsbLXR\n\nPush normally (never force), and confirm local HEAD equals `git ls-remote origin refs/heads/feature/issue-125-site-visuals`. Do not post on GitHub or open a PR.\n\nReport: a table of all 98 (file, title, kept removed / restored / restored with correction, one-line reason), check results with the pushed SHA.","run_in_background":"true"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3336,"cache_read_input_tokens":301324,"output_tokens":1407,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":324},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3336,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1407,"cache_read_input_tokens":301324,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3336,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3336},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":10380,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01VJ5j3QHm8LpopzxGiadycY":{"description":"Review removed diagrams, restore useful ones","prompt":"Repository synaptiai/agent-capability-standard, worktree /Users/danielbentes/agent-capability-standard/.claude/worktrees/wf_08f3cd25-fc3-8, branch feature/issue-125-site-visuals (head 8d94ad0,