{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"ef9f3fc8-12b6-4fe4-9f49-aaeedec05648","hash":"9e8ee9bd08105eee9d3451a430ca097852b128b4840c0e64b8e14e2747cf79b6","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Running the five-reviewer pass that the PR workflow requires before opening the PR. The only uncommitted path, `.decisions/`, was already untracked before this work, so I'm leaving it out.\n\n","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018rUKDTZrs8dL7b9Rb6saqa","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Code review of the branch","subagent_type":"flow:code-reviewer","run_in_background":"true","prompt":"Working directory: /Users/danielbentes/agent-capability-standard/.claude/worktrees/wf_08f3cd25-fc3-8 (branch feature/issue-125-site-visuals, head f254598). Review the branch diff against origin/main (`git diff origin/main...HEAD`) for code quality, logic correctness, edge cases and security. The diff is large (290 files, mostly site/ — an Astro docs site that draws figures from repository data — plus Mermaid diagrams added to Markdown docs). Prioritise: site/src/lib/*.ts (data parsing for figures), site/src/plugins/*.ts (rehype/remark plugins), site/scripts/*.mjs (build checks: check-dist, check-runs, check-axe, check-contrast), .github/workflows/site.yml (CI; the deploy job must only run on push to main), and correctness of figures against their source data. No review exceptions apply. Every finding must name a concrete trigger (a failing input/state and the wrong output), a file:line, a priority P1/P2/P3, and a confidence HIGH/MEDIUM/LOW, in the canonical finding table. Do not edit files. Do not post on GitHub."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01NajjYTeuZBoFm4rA6sm9Tf","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Security review of the branch","subagent_type":"flow:security-reviewer","run_in_background":"true","prompt":"Working directory: /Users/danielbentes/agent-capability-standard/.claude/worktrees/wf_08f3cd25-fc3-8 (branch feature/issue-125-site-visuals, head f254598). Review `git diff origin/main...HEAD` for OWASP Top 10, secrets, injection (notably: HTML built from Markdown/YAML repository content in site/src/plugins and site/src/lib, inline SVG, `set:html`/innerHTML use, Mermaid label rendering), CI workflow safety in .github/workflows/site.yml (permissions, secrets exposure, deploy only on push to main, untrusted input in run steps), and dependency changes in site/package.json and site/package-lock.json (new: playwright/axe tooling, elkjs). Emit DEP- findings with category=dependency where relevant. Return P1/P2/P3 findings with file:line, confidence and trigger in the canonical finding table. Do not edit files; do not post on GitHub."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MR1Z796c38pPufd7uVz6Wz","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Error handling inspection","subagent_type":"flow:error-handler-inspector","run_in_background":"true","prompt":"Working directory: /Users/danielbentes/agent-capability-standard/.claude/worktrees/wf_08f3cd25-fc3-8 (branch feature/issue-125-site-visuals, head f254598). Inspect the files changed in `git diff origin/main...HEAD` under site/ (src/lib, src/plugins, src/twins, scripts) for error-handling gaps: parsers that silently return empty/wrong figures on unexpected source formats instead of failing the build, swallowed exceptions, build checks (scripts/check-*.mjs) that can pass when they failed to measure (e.g. a page that fails to load, a server that never starts), and missing edge cases (empty lists, missing headings, max of empty arrays, division by zero in bars). Return P1/P2/P3 findings with file:line, confidence and trigger in the canonical finding table. Do not edit files."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01CASZhGB5FhRQdcnvmvB6MR","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Convention check of the branch","subagent_type":"flow:convention-checker","run_in_background":"true","prompt":"Working directory: /Users/danielbentes/agent-capability-standard/.claude/worktrees/wf_08f3cd25-fc3-8 (branch feature/issue-125-site-visuals, issue #125). Validate the commits in `git log origin/main..HEAD` (conventional commit format, issue reference \"Refs #125\", trailers), branch naming, and code conventions against the repository's CLAUDE.md (notably: no YAML file under site/; every new public .md file needs a route; no hand-typed counts). Return findings with priority and trigger. Do not edit files or rewrite history."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Q4HUpMSJ5n9fGpzSYddBP2","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Run all quality commands","subagent_type":"flow:test-runner","run_in_background":"true","prompt":"Working directory: /Users/danielbentes/agent-capability-standard/.claude/worktrees/wf_08f3cd25-fc3-8 (head f254598). Run the repository's quality commands and report a structured results table with the exact summary line each printed. Site (in site/): `npm ci`, `npm run check`, `npm test`, `npm run build`, `npm run check:axe`. Repo root (activate /Users/danielbentes/agent-capability-standard/.venv first): `pytest tests -q`, `python tools/validate_workflows.py --strict`, the catalog loop `for c in schemas/workflows/*.yaml examples/*.workflow_catalog.yaml; do python tools/validate_workflows.py --catalog \"$c\" --strict; done`, `python tools/validate_profiles.py`, `python tools/validate_skill_refs.py`, `python tools/validate_ontology.py`, `python tools/validate_canonical_schemas.py`, `python tools/validate_rfcs.py`, `python tools/validate_constraints.py`, `python tools/validate_doc_links.py`, `python tools/validate_yaml_util_sync.py`, `python tools/validate_transform_refs.py`, `python tools/validate_benchmark_deps.py`, `python tools/sync_skill_schemas.py --check`, `python scripts/gen_runtime_fixtures.py --check`. Do not edit files. If a command fails, include its error output."},"caller":{"ty