{"parentUuid":"412f2169-58bd-49c3-809c-2b9a0bbca416","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"30cabfb8-5381-4fed-9b53-205ab567daa7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MbyhWTsRDdkPaq2hzo9HbC","type":"tool_result","content":"## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Each of these page types shows at least one figure drawn from the repository data: home, capability, layer, workflow, domain, edge types, diagnostics, and the section index pages.\n- [ ] Prose pages (the Standard, the guides, the FAQ, the compliance documents) also carry diagrams where a diagram conveys the content better than text. These diagrams live in the Markdown itself, so GitHub shows them too, and the site draws them in its own pixel style.\n- [ ] Every section card and concept card has its own pixel icon. No two different concepts share an icon.\n- [ ] Each figure has an accessible name. Its information is also in the page's Markdown copy as text.\n- [ ] The maintainer reviews and approves a small set of exemplar pages before the design is rolled out to the rest of the site.\n- [ ] The automated accessibility check reports no violations on any page, in light and dark themes, and the colour contrast check passes.\n- [ ] Pages remain readable and do not scroll sideways at phone width (360 pixels).\n- [ ] No artwork, code or design tokens are copied from synapti.ai. Public fonts and general techniques are allowed.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"1eec2982-369f-4ce5-9ef1-490fd9b22d35","timestamp":"2026-11-13T06:42:15.681Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Each of these page types shows at least one figure drawn from the repository data: home, capability, layer, workflow, domain, edge types, diagnostics, and the section index pages.\n- [ ] Prose pages (the Standard, the guides, the FAQ, the compliance documents) also carry diagrams where a diagram conveys the content better than text. These diagrams live in the Markdown itself, so GitHub shows them too, and the site draws them in its own pixel style.\n- [ ] Every section card and concept card has its own pixel icon. No two different concepts share an icon.\n- [ ] Each figure has an accessible name. Its information is also in the page's Markdown copy as text.\n- [ ] The maintainer reviews and approves a small set of exemplar pages before the design is rolled out to the rest of the site.\n- [ ] The automated accessibility check reports no violations on any page, in light and dark themes, and the colour contrast check passes.\n- [ ] Pages remain readable and do not scroll sideways at phone width (360 pixels).\n- [ ] No artwork, code or design tokens are copied from synapti.ai. Public fonts and general techniques are allowed.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[],"moreFiles":0,"shared":true}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"412f2169-58bd-49c3-809c-2b9a0bbca416","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"session_id":"ef9f3fc8-12b6-4fe4-9f49-aaeedec05648","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/danielbentes/agent-capability-standard/.claude/worktrees/wf_08f3cd25-fc3-8","sessionId":"ef9f3fc8-12b6-4fe4-9f49-aaeedec05648","version":"2.1.322","gitBranch":"feature/issue-125-site-visuals","slug":"i-just-came-across-imperative-newell"}
