{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-11-13T06:45:04.176Z","sessionId":"ef9f3fc8-12b6-4fe4-9f49-aaeedec05648","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>abda64af4c8d0e0b1</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>REDACTED</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>REDACTED.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Convention check of the branch\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>I found no P2 violations on this branch. There are three P3 style notes, and none of them needs history rewritten. I fetched `origin/main` at `824eea1`, which is also the merge base, and checked the 275 commits from there to `HEAD` (`f254598`): 253 regular commits and 22 merges.\n\n**Where the rules came from:** the repository's `CLAUDE.md` sets no rules for commit messages or branch names. Those checks use the flow defaults (the standard commit types, `feature/issue-{N}-{desc}`) plus what this repository's history shows. The site rules come from `CLAUDE.md`. Its documented copy at `origin/main` is the same as the one in the worktree.\n\n### Commit messages\n| Check | Result | How checked |\n|---|---|---|\n| `type(scope): subject` format, allowed type, lowercase scope, no trailing period | Pass, 253/253 regular commits | Pattern match on every subject |\n| Capitalised subjects | Pass | The 8 that start with a capital start with a proper noun (Standard, Mermaid, FAQ, QUICKSTART, F-S14) |\n| \"Refs #125\" | Pass, all 275 including merges | Searched each commit message |\n| `Co-Authored-By` and `Claude-Session` lines | Pass, all 275 | Searched each commit message |\n\n### Branch and issue\n- The branch `feature/issue-125-site-visuals` matches `feature/issue-{N}-{desc}`. Pass.\n- Issue #125, \"Documentation site: diagrams, pixel-art iconography and visual structure\", is open and has no assignee. Pass.\n- There is no pull request for this branch yet, so I could not check the title, the body or the labels.\n\n### Site rules from `CLAUDE.md`\n| Rule | Result | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| No YAML file under `site/` | Pass | No tracked `.yml` or `.yaml` file under `site/`, and none added on the branch |\n| Every new public `.md` file needs a route | Pass | The branch adds or renames no `.md` file. `npm test` in `site/` passed (38 test files, 875 tests) and printed no \"no route\" or \"routed twice\" errors |\n| No hand-typed counts | Pass | `npm run check` passed: type check 0 errors, contrast check 412 pairs pass, and \"no hand-typed counts in 263 source files\" |\n\n### Findings\n| # | Finding | Priority | What triggered it | Fix |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Merge subjects use three styles: git's default \"Merge branch '…'\" (13), a made-up `merge:` prefix (8), and one free-text \"Merge the release notes figures…\" (`f254598`). `merge` is not one of the commit types. | P3 | The merge subjects don't match each other or any commit type | Note only. Use git's default merge subject from now on, which is what `main` uses |\n| 2 | 70 regular subjects are longer than 72 characters, for example `5119a6c` and `9190375` (over 90). | P3 | Only the usual git convention. This repository sets no length limit, and 58 of the last 200 regular commits on `main` are also longer than 72 | Note only. Keep them short when a sentence allows |\n| 3 | Many subjects describe a result (\"release notes get a timeline\", \"edge type names stay whole…\") instead of giving a command. | P3 | Only the flow default asks for command-form subjects. This repository's `CLAUDE.md` says nothing about it | Note only |\n\n**Not checked:**\n- `npm run build` and its check of the built pages. I ran only `npm run check` and `npm test`, as you named.\n- The Python validators.\n- The pull request format, because no pull request exists yet.\n\nThere is an untracked `.decisions/` folder in the worktree containing `issue-120.md`. It is not part of the branch, but if it is ever committed, the site tests would fail on it as a public Markdown file with no route.\n\nI edited no files and rewrote no history. The full `npm test` log is at `REDACTED.log`.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>38008</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>9</tool_uses><duration_ms>180836</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
