{"parentUuid":"7dd817c5-1481-486e-a1a8-353746f9f4a4","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"ff076c29-70a3-4217-9ec9-9fbc19d16d68","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a6199c2d270c6660b</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01NajjYTeuZBoFm4rA6sm9Tf</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>REDACTED.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Security review of the branch\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>I found no security findings in this change, so the security facet's decision is **APPROVE**. This covers `origin/main` at 824eea1 to HEAD f254598, read on 2026-11-13.\n\n## Security Review Findings\n\n### P1 — Critical Security Issues (Blocks Merge)\n| Finding | Suggested Fix |\n|---------|---------------|\n\n### P2 — Security Concerns\n| Finding | Suggested Fix |\n|---------|---------------|\n\n### P3 — Security Improvements\n| Finding | Suggested Fix |\n|---------|---------------|\n\n### Dependency Audit (separate from finding schema — no file:line)\n| Package | Severity | Advisory | Fix |\n|---------|----------|---------|-----|\n| (none) | — | `npm audit` in `site/`: 0 info, 0 low, 0 moderate, 0 high, 0 critical | — |\n\n### Summary\n- Security findings: P1: 0, P2: 0, P3: 0\n- Dependency findings (`DEP-`, in the tables above): 0\n- Dependency read: ok (both changed manifests read: `site/package.json` and `site/package-lock.json`)\n- Advisory audit: ran (`npm audit --json` in `site/`, this is your own PR); 0 advisories\n- Secrets scan: none (37,704 added lines checked; no keyword or high-entropy hits apart from lockfile integrity hashes; no `.env` files)\n- Overall risk: Low\n\n## What was checked\n\n**HTML built from Markdown, YAML and diagram text**\n- **One processor for all Markdown.** Every Markdown page goes through the same processor (`site/src/lib/markdown.ts:71`, wired in `site/astro.config.mjs:40`). It includes the existing raw-HTML allowlist (`site/src/plugins/remark-html-allowlist.ts`), which only lets through `details`, `summary`, `br`, `sup`, `sub` and `&lt;a name|id&gt;`. No changed plugin adds raw HTML of its own; a search of `plugins/`, `lib/`, `components/`, `templates/` and `pages/` found none.\n- **The new `set:html` calls are safe.** The roughly 25 new calls (in `SpecFigure.astro`, `SpecPage.astro`, `ProsePage.astro`, `RfcPage.astro`, `SkillPage.astro`, `capabilities/[id].astro`, `domains/*.astro`, `spec/edge-types.astro`) only re-insert pieces of that processor's output.\n- **The fold helpers are safe.** `foldFirstTable`, `foldFirstTaskList` and `foldFirstBox` (`site/src/lib/inject.ts:78-94`, `site/src/lib/prose-figures.ts:26-34`) and `foldCapabilityList` (`site/src/lib/domain-figures.ts:368`) wrap already-rendered HTML. Their summary text is a fixed string and is HTML-escaped. `h2Section` (`site/src/lib/domain-figures.ts:309`) builds its regex from constant anchors only.\n- **Mermaid diagrams.** `site/src/lib/mermaid/render.ts` builds the SVG as a structured element tree. Every label, title, caption and text-version item is a text node, so it is escaped when written out. The Markdown copy escapes `\\ * [ ] &lt;` and backticks (`site/src/lib/mermaid/text.ts:52`).\n- **Links.** Every `href` in the new figure components comes from a route helper (`workflowHref`, `layerHref`, `domainHref`, `sectionLink`, `githubBlobUrl`) or from internal route URLs. Astro escapes attribute values. I searched for these rather than reading all 9 changed plugins line by line; I read `remark-mermaid.ts` and `remark-html-allowlist.ts` in full.\n\n**One case I looked at but did not raise.** `site/src/components/fig/WorkflowSpine.astro:81` puts the workflow id, unescaped, into a CSS selector, which line 228 writes into `&lt;style set:html&gt;`. Nothing limits the characters in an id: the catalog schema allows any key, and `parseCatalog` in `site/src/data/workflows.ts` does not check them. However, ids come only from catalog files in this repository, which go through the same review as the component itself. Someone who could plant a bad id could edit the component directly, so it is outside the review scope. A rule in the site loader limiting ids to `^[a-z0-9_]+$` would close it cheaply if you want that.\n\n**CI workflow (`.github/workflows/site.yml`)**\n- Permissions stay at `contents: read`.\n- Deploy still runs only on a push to `main` with `SITE_DEPLOY_ENABLED`. It uses the action pinned to a commit and takes the build output from the same run.\n- No step interpolates pull-request text into a shell command; the deploy step uses only `github.sha`.\n- The new steps run in the build job, which has no secrets:\n  - `npx playwright install --with-deps chromium` uses the `playwright` 1.64.1 installed from the lockfile.\n  - `npm run check:axe` starts a local server that listens only on `127.0.0.1` on a random port and refuses `..` paths (`site/scripts/check-axe.mjs:47-68`).\n- The new step that removes `dist/_review` runs before deploy. Those review pages are not in the search index, because they lack `data-pagefind-body` and every published page template has it. They are also absent from `sitemap.xml`. That last check was on a local `dist/` built at 07:43 today from an unknown commit.\n\n**Dependencies, one judgment per package**\n\n| Package | Advisory | License | Install hook | Imported | Near-name |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `elkjs@0.12.0` (runtime dependency) | none | EPL-2.0 OR GPL-3.0-or-later | none | yes, `site/src/lib/mermaid/layout.ts:11` | none |\n| `playwright@1.64.1` (dev) | none | Apache-2.0 | none | yes, `site/scripts/check-axe.mjs:88`, `site/scripts/check-runs.mjs:153` | none |\n| `@axe-core/playwright@4.14.0` (dev) | none | MPL-2.0 | none | yes, `site/scripts/check-axe.mjs:89` | none |\n| `axe-core@4.14.0`, `playwright-core@1.64.1` and `@1.65.0` (pulled in by the above) | none | MPL-2.0 / Apache-2.0 | none | — | none |\n\n- **elkjs license.** It does not conflict with the project's Apache-2.0 licence. elkjs runs only at build time:\n  - At HEAD, only `remark-mermaid.ts` imports it, through `layout.ts`.\n  - No browser `&lt;script&gt;` imports anything under `lib/mermaid`.\n  - The local `dist/_astro` (same build-vintage caveat as above) contains no elkjs code.\n  - `site/package.json` is marked private.\n\n  So the site does not redistribute elkjs, and the SVGs it draws are output, not a derived work. This would change if elkjs were ever imported by browser code.\n- **Install hooks.** The only `hasInstallScript` entry is `fsevents`, which was already in the lockfile before this change; CI still runs `npm ci --ignore-scripts`.\n- **`playwright-core@1.65.0`** is installed at the top level because `@axe-core/playwright` asks for it, while `playwright` uses its own 1.64.1. Both are locked with integrity hashes. This is a duplicate copy, not a security problem.\n\nNo `.md` report file was written.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>98753</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>39</tool_uses><duration_ms>339087</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"},"uuid":"2efbaac7-1816-4643-8fbb-82bf3cfd24dd","timestamp":"2026-11-13T06:47:36.070Z","permissionMode":"bypassPermissions","origin":{"kind":"task-notification","producer":"session-task","runId":"0mwelzvd9-0085878e"},"promptSource":"system","turnOrigin":"task_notification","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":15,"turnIndex":37},"queueSkipAttachments":true,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/danielbentes/agent-capability-standard/.claude/worktrees/wf_08f3cd25-fc3-8","sessionId":"ef9f3fc8-12b6-4fe4-9f49-aaeedec05648","version":"2.1.322","gitBranch":"feature/issue-125-site-visuals","slug":"i-just-came-across-imperative-newell"}
