(by `where`), and rethrow otherwise. |\n| **ERR-8 · silent-failure · `site/src/lib/inject.ts:78-94`, `site/src/lib/prose-figures.ts:26-34`, `site/src/lib/domain-figures.ts:367-372`**&lt;br&gt;`foldFirstTable`, `foldFirstTaskList`, `foldFirstBox` and `foldCapabilityList` return the HTML unchanged when their regex misses. Their callers have already drawn the figure that replaces the block, so a miss shows both. For `foldFirstBox`, the box also keeps its \"Fig n\" eyebrow. _(MEDIUM)_&lt;br&gt;Trigger: the renderer's markup for a table wrapper, task list or ASCII figure changes, for example attribute order or an added class → the source block is shown in full next to its figure, with no error. | Since each caller only calls these where the block is expected, have them throw `where: no &lt;block&gt; to fold`. |\n| **ERR-9 · silent-failure · `site/src/lib/domain-usage.ts:49,58-62`**&lt;br&gt;A README whose \"Capability Usage\" heading is renamed returns `[]` without even the warning that other skips get. A YAML parse error is reported as \"has no single-capability YAML fence\", which hides the parse message. _(MEDIUM)_&lt;br&gt;Trigger: a domain README's usage heading is reworded, or one example fence gets a YAML typo → the usage figure disappears silently, or the warning points at the wrong cause. | Warn on the missing heading, and include the YAML error's message in the warning. |\n| **ERR-10 · missing-fallback · `site/scripts/check-axe.mjs:145`, `site/scripts/check-runs.mjs:244`**&lt;br&gt;`--paths` with an empty or missing value gives `only = []`. Zero pages are checked, and check-axe prints \"0 pages, 0 runs … no axe violations\" and exits 0. _(MEDIUM)_&lt;br&gt;Trigger: a local or scripted run with `--paths \"$CHANGED\"` where the variable is empty → a passing result that checked nothing. | Throw when `--paths` is present but yields no paths. |\n| **ERR-11 · error-handling · `site/src/lib/index-figures.ts:508-511`**&lt;br&gt;`skillsCaption` calls `Math.min/Math.max(...runs)` with no empty guard, and neither caller (`SkillWorkflows.astro:33`, `twins/listing.ts:30`) guards. With no composed skill mapped to a workflow, the caption reads \"of Infinity to -Infinity steps\". _(MEDIUM)_&lt;br&gt;Trigger: every `COMPOSED_SKILLS` entry is set to null → the published caption contains \"Infinity\". | When `runs.length === 0`, write \"none of the N composed skills runs a catalog workflow\". |\n\n### Summary\n- Files inspected: 9 of 10 changed check scripts (the 5 `.mjs` scripts and 4 of the 5 `.d.mts` type-declaration stubs, the `check-contrast.d.mts` stub excepted). Of the 62 changed files under `site/src/lib`, `site/src/plugins` and `site/src/twins`, I read in full or in part release-figures, release-figures-hast, md-sections, inject, prose-figures, prose-page, runs (scope lists), layer-figures, the catch sites, every `Math.max/min(...)` spread, and the empty-return early exits that the grep found. I did not read these line by line: spec-dsl-figures, spec-slots, rehype-spec-slots, most of rehype-prose-figures, rehype-capability-skill, and most twins.\n- Total findings: P1: 0, P2: 5, P3: 6\n- Error handling coverage: the drawing primitives are strict. `PixelBar` and `pixelBarElement` throw on `max &lt;= min`; `heatStep` cannot divide by zero because it returns early for `count &lt;= 0`; `glyph()`, `parseMermaid`, `sectionBlocks`, `cutAfterHeadings`, the home principles parser and `parseReleases` with no sections all throw with the file location. check-contrast, check-design-data and check-dist report missing inputs. In `serve()`, a listen failure or a missing `404.html` raises an unhandled error event and crashes the process, which fails CI loudly. The weak points are the line-based Markdown parsers, which do not skip fences, and the gate scripts, which treat \"measured nothing\" as \"clean\" (ERR-1 to ERR-5).\n- Not run: the Step 2b LSP diagnostics and `npm run check` (astro check). The `.then(` grep over changed files found nothing unhandled. The catch blocks in the changed scripts record their errors as problems; `safeDecode` in check-dist predates this branch.\n\nPaths for the main findings:\n- /Users/danielbentes/agent-capability-standard/.claude/worktrees/wf_08f3cd25-fc3-8/site/src/lib/capability-figures.ts\n- /Users/danielbentes/agent-capability-standard/.claude/worktrees/wf_08f3cd25-fc3-8/site/src/lib/release-figures.ts\n- /Users/danielbentes/agent-capability-standard/.claude/worktrees/wf_08f3cd25-fc3-8/site/scripts/check-runs.mjs\n- /Users/danielbentes/agent-capability-standard/.claude/worktrees/wf_08f3cd25-fc3-8/site/scripts/check-dist.mjs\n- /Users/danielbentes/agent-capability-standard/.claude/worktrees/wf_08f3cd25-fc3-8/site/src/lib/runs.ts\n- /Users/danielbentes/agent-capability-standard/.claude/worktrees/wf_08f3cd25-fc3-8/site/dist/capabilities/persist/index.html (where ERR-1 shows on the built page)</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>152794</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>46</tool_uses><duration_ms>561876</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>\n</system-reminder>"}]}}
{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"ef9f3fc8-12b6-4fe4-9f49-aaeedec05648","id":"ca2610d7-f746-4408-8db8-1e575d6ab67c","timestamp":"2026-11-13T06:51:23.722Z","version":"2.1.322","querySource":"repl_main_thread","shapeHash":"48b90f4503f2dc4018bf5abcde7172dd084d167510d571f5e85bcd7dcf7346b0","params":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","dangerous-tool-use-2026-09-03","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"updates"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"medium"}},"base":"4acb8d92-218c-404b-a9d0-aef53b5b8335","keep":313,"tail":["dfd98c51908d0b6761005b9006e0199c5622caa20c1ab134202f1173bfbd0275","343d8b5b1e311304c7cf239ec1f1ef2461574a9cc8c9cd4d6388de86789e77a8"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",313,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",314,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"3858f165066fa911cc06e381f95df1da9b40b068eafdd7559a7578faa328bb9b"}
{"parentUuid":"844c465d-4a7a-453e-92de-98c13abd226c","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"6787b0af-15d0-49b4-b9c7-ea855a359685","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>aa39a6988813ee62c</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01MR1Z796c38pPufd7uVz6Wz</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>REDACTED.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Error handling inspection\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>## Error Handling Inspection\n\nAll findings are against HEAD f254598 (branch feature/issue-125-site-visuals, compared with origin/main at 824eea1). Where a finding says \"observed\", it was checked against the `site/dist` build from 07:43 on 2026-11-13, which is later than that commit.\n\n### P1 — Critical (Blocks Merge)\n| Finding | Suggested Fix |\n|---------|---------------|\n\n### P2 — Should Fix\n| Finding | Suggested Fix |\n|---------|---------------|\n| **ERR-1 · silent-failure · `site/src/lib/capability-figures.ts:571-574`**&lt;br&gt;The Examples parser reads the skill line by line and does not skip code fences, so any `### ` line inside a fence becomes a new example. This is live: the persist capability page's Fig 5 lists a fourth example, \"Architecture Decisions\", that writes no output field. That heading comes from a fenced Markdown sample. Its caption reads \"4 examples … no field is in every example\". In fact there are three examples and each writes every field. The page's Markdown copy repeats the phantom row. `exampleWorkflows` at :792 does `ex += 1` before its fence test, so its example numbers shift the same way. The section-end tests at :568, :707, :787 and :207 (`/^## /`) are also not fence-aware. _(HIGH)_&lt;br&gt;Trigger: a skill's Examples section has a fenced Markdown sample containing a `### ` line (`skills/persist/SKILL.md:228` today) → a phantom example is drawn and the caption's counts are wrong. | Read these sections from the mdast tree (`sectionBlocks`/`parseMarkdown`, as md-sections.ts already does), or toggle a fence flag before testing heading lines. Add a test using persist's SKILL.md that expects 3 examples. |\n| **ERR-2 · silent-failure · `site/src/lib/release-figures.ts:40,90`**&lt;br&gt;`RELEASE` only accepts an em dash before the date, and entries are only `- ` bullets. When I ran `parseReleases`, a `## [v2.1.0] - 2026-11-20` section was dropped entirely: it fell into the generic `## ` branch, which sets `rel = null`. `* d` / `* e` entries counted as 0. `scripts/release_notes.py:26` matches `## \\[v…\\](\\s\\|$)`, so the release tooling accepts the hyphen heading while the site leaves that release out of the timeline. The rendered-entry cross-check at `release-figures-hast.ts:145` only runs on sections the parser already counted at 8 or more entries, so it cannot catch a dropped release or a zero count. _(HIGH)_&lt;br&gt;Trigger: a release heading written with `-` or `–` before the date, or a kind section with `*` bullets → that release is missing from the timeline and section figures, or its bars show 0, and the build passes. | Throw on any `## [` line that `RELEASE` does not match. Accept `[-*+] ` bullets. Run the rendered-vs-parsed entry count for every kind section, not only long ones. |\n| **ERR-3 · silent-failure · `site/scripts/check-runs.mjs:111,180,205`**&lt;br&gt;When `.doc-main__body` is absent, `measurePage` returns null and the page is neither measured nor reported as failed. `summarise` then skips it (`if (!r.wide) continue`). When I ran `summarise` on pages with no measurement, it returned 0 results and 0 missing, and the main block exits 0. The self-check cannot catch this, because the fixture `test/fixtures/runs-page.html:16` hard-codes the same class. There is also no empty-sitemap guard, which check-axe has at :91. Today all 168 built pages have the element. _(HIGH)_&lt;br&gt;Trigger: the body wrapper class in DocLayout is renamed, or a template stops using DocLayout → the figure-gap sweep measures no pages, prints \"0 pages\", and CI passes. | Push the URL to `failed` when `measurePage` returns null. Throw when `results.length === 0` or when `results.length` is less than the number of paths. |\n| **ERR-4 · silent-failure · `site/scripts/check-dist.mjs` `checkDrawnFigures` / `pageTemplate`**&lt;br&gt;A page whose template is null, or is not in `DRAWN_TEMPLATES`, is skipped without a report. I ran the check on the real dist with `page--` renamed in memory: it reported 0 problems. Unmeasured and clean give the same result. A template renamed in the layout (for example `edge-types` to `edges`) also stops being checked without notice. _(HIGH)_&lt;br&gt;Trigger: the body template class prefix or a template name changes → the \"every generated page has a drawn figure\" check passes without examining any page. | Fail when any `DRAWN_TEMPLATES` entry matches no built page, and when an HTML page has no template class. |\n| **ERR-5 · silent-failure · `site/src/lib/runs.ts:132`**&lt;br&gt;`ENFORCED_URLS` pins `'/spec/1.1.0/'`, while the docstring at :113-116 says the enforced page is \"the current Standard\". The `spec` template is not in `ENFORCED_TEMPLATES`. Nothing reports an enforced URL, or a per-URL exempt entry, whose page is no longer the one intended: `summarise` only checks anchors on pages it measured. _(MEDIUM)_&lt;br&gt;Trigger: the next Standard version is published → the new current Standard is only reported on, and 1.1.0 stays enforced, with no failure. | Derive the current Standard's URL from the versions data instead of a literal. Fail when an `ENFORCED_URLS` entry or a non-template exempt entry matches no page in the sitemap. |\n\n### P3 — Consider\n| Finding | Suggested Fix |\n|---------|---------------|\n| **ERR-6 · swallowed-exception · `site/src/lib/skill-figures.ts:141-145,161`**&lt;br&gt;The bare `catch { return null }` covers both invalid YAML and `sectionFence`'s throw when the \"Output Contract\" heading or fence is missing. Either way the scorecard figure disappears without a message, although the function throws loudly for every other disagreement. Separately, a `### ` family heading that does not match `X) Name (CODE)` is skipped, so its `####` checks are attributed to the previous family. The id cross-check still passes, because the ids are all present. _(MEDIUM)_&lt;br&gt;Trigger: a skill with a CHECKLIST.md gets a YAML typo in its Output Contract, or a family heading without its `(CODE)` → no scorecard figure, or checks grouped under the wrong family, with no build error. | Return null only when the contract has no `scorecard` key, and rethrow parse errors with `where`. Throw on any H3 in CHECKLIST.md that is not a family heading. |\n| **ERR-7 · silent-failure · `site/src/lib/spec-tail-figures.ts:525-530`**&lt;br&gt;Any YAML error in a §12.5 fence falls back to `stepsByLine`. The comment justifies this for the 1.0.0 text, but the fallback also covers the current Standard, so a new syntax error there is quietly read line by line, which can lose steps. _(MEDIUM)_&lt;br&gt;Trigger: a §12.5 pattern fence in the current Standard is edited into invalid YAML → its strip is drawn from a partial line read and the build passes. | Allow the fallback only for the Standard versions known to need it (by `where`), and rethrow otherwise. |\n| **ERR-8 · silent-failure · `site/src/lib/inject.ts:78-94`, `site/src/lib/prose-figures.ts:26-34`, `site/src/lib/domain-figures.ts:367-372`**&lt;br&gt;`foldFirstTable`, `foldFirstTaskList`, `foldFirstBox` and `foldCapabilityList` return the HTML unchanged when their regex misses. Their callers have already drawn the figure that replaces the block, so a miss shows both. For `foldFirstBox`, the box also keeps its \"Fig n\" eyebrow. _(MEDIUM)_&lt;br&gt;Trigger: the renderer's markup for a table wrapper, task list or ASCII figure changes, for example attribute order or an added class → the source block is shown in full next to its figure, with no error. | Since each caller only calls these where the block is expected, have them throw `where: no &lt;block&gt; to fold`. |\n| **ERR-9 · silent-failure · `site/src/lib/domain-usage.ts:49,58-62`**&lt;br&gt;A README whose \"Capability Usage\" heading is renamed returns `[]` without even the warning that other skips get. A YAML parse error is reported as \"has no single-capability YAML fence\", which hides the parse message. _(MEDIUM)_&lt;br&gt;Trigger: a domain README's usage heading is reworded, or one example fence gets a YAML typo → the usage figure disappears silently, or the warning points at the wrong cause. | Warn on the missing heading, and include the YAML error's message in the warning. |\n| **ERR-10 · missing-fallback · `site/scripts/check-axe.mjs:145`, `site/scripts/check-runs.mjs:244`**&lt;br&gt;`--paths` with an empty or missing value gives `only = []`. Zero pages are checked, and check-axe prints \"0 pages, 0 runs … no axe violations\" and exits 0. _(MEDIUM)_&lt;br&gt;Trigger: a local or scripted run with `--paths \"$CHANGED\"` where the variable is empty → a passing result that checked nothing. | Throw when `--paths` is present but yields no paths. |\n| **ERR-11 · error-handling · `site/src/lib/index-figures.ts:508-511`**&lt;br&gt;`skillsCaption` calls `Math.min/Math.max(...runs)` with no empty guard, and neither caller (`SkillWorkflows.astro:33`, `twins/listing.ts:30`) guards. With no composed skill mapped to a workflow, the caption reads \"of Infinity to -Infinity steps\". _(MEDIUM)_&lt;br&gt;Trigger: every `COMPOSED_SKILLS` entry is set to null → the published caption contains \"Infinity\". | When `runs.length === 0`, write \"none of the N composed skills runs a catalog workflow\". |\n\n### Summary\n- Files inspected: 9 of 10 changed check scripts (the 5 `.mjs` scripts and 4 of the 5 `.d.mts` type-declaration stubs, the `check-contrast.d.mts` stub excepted). Of the 62 changed files under `site/src/lib`, `site/src/plugins` and `site/src/twins`, I read in full or in part release-figures, release-figures-hast, md-sections, inject, prose-figures, prose-page, runs (scope lists), layer-figures, the catch sites, every `Math.max/min(...)` spread, and the empty-return early exits that the grep found. I did not read these line by line: spec-dsl-figures, spec-slots, rehype-spec-slots, most of rehype-prose-figures, rehype-capability-skill, and most twins.\n- Total findings: P1: 0, P2: 5, P3: 6\n- Error handling coverage: the drawing primitives are strict. `PixelBar` and `pixelBarElement` throw on `max &lt;= min`; `heatStep` cannot divide by zero because it returns early for `count &lt;= 0`; `glyph()`, `parseMermaid`, `sectionBlocks`, `cutAfterHeadings`, the home principles parser and `parseReleases` with no sections all throw with the file location. check-contrast, check-design-data and check-dist report missing inputs. In `serve()`, a listen failure or a missing `404.html` raises an unhandled error event and crashes the process, which fails CI loudly. The weak points are the line-based Markdown parsers, which do not skip fences, and the gate scripts, which treat \"measured nothing\" as \"clean\" (ERR-1 to ERR-5).\n- Not run: the Step 2b LSP diagnostics and `npm run check` (astro check). The `.then(` grep over changed files found nothing unhandled. The catch blocks in the changed scripts record their errors as problems; `safeDecode` in check-dist predates this branch.\n\nPaths for the main findings:\n- /Users/danielbentes/agent-capability-standard/.claude/worktrees/wf_08f3cd25-fc3-8/site/src/lib/capability-figures.ts\n- /Users/danielbentes/agent-capability-standard/.claude/worktrees/wf_08f3cd25-fc3-8/site/src/lib/release-figures.ts\n- /Users/danielbentes/agent-capability-standard/.claude/worktrees/wf_08f3cd25-fc3-8/site/scripts/check-runs.mjs\n- /Users/danielbentes/agent-capability-standard/.claude/worktrees/wf_08f3cd25-fc3-8/site/scripts/check-dist.mjs\n- /Users/danielbentes/agent-capability-standard/.claude/worktrees/wf_08f3cd25-fc3-8/site/src/lib/runs.ts\n- /Users/danielbentes/agent-capability-standard/.claude/worktrees/wf_08f3cd25-fc3-8/site/dist/capabilities/persist/index.html (where ERR-1 shows on the built page)</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>152794</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>46</tool_uses><duration_ms>561876</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"},"uuid":"bc34c902-27b5-40b2-8d25-b87957f619e5","timestamp":"2026-11-13T06:51:22.488Z","permissionMode":"bypassPermissions","origin":{"kind":"task-notification","producer":"session-task","runId":"0mwelzy8g-13854aef"},"promptSource":"system","turnOrigin":"task_notification","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":15,"turnIndex":39},"queueSkipAttachments":true,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/danielbentes/agent-capability-standard/.claude/worktrees/wf_08f3cd25-fc3-8","sessionId":"ef9f3fc8-12b6-4fe4-9f49-aaeedec05648","version":"2.1.322","gitBranch":"feature/issue-125-site-visuals","slug":"i-just-came-across-imperative-newell"}
