{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-11-13T06:53:31.528Z","sessionId":"ef9f3fc8-12b6-4fe4-9f49-aaeedec05648","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a154811a559585f06</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>REDACTED</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>REDACTED.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Code review of the branch\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>## Code Review Findings\n\nAll evidence comes from branch head `f254598`. The site suite passed at that commit (vitest: 38 files, 875 tests). The `site/dist` I inspected carries commit stamp `f25459898eb6` on its capability pages.\n\nThe deploy guard is correct and this diff does not touch it. `.github/workflows/site.yml:92` still reads `if: github.event_name == 'push' &amp;&amp; github.ref == 'refs/heads/main' &amp;&amp; vars.SITE_DEPLOY_ENABLED == 'true'`. The new axe step runs in the `build` job, and the new `dist/_review` removal runs in `deploy` before the wrangler step.\n\n### P1 — Critical (Blocks Merge)\n| Finding | Suggested Fix |\n|---------|---------------|\n\n### P2 — Should Fix\n| Finding | Suggested Fix |\n|---------|---------------|\n| **F1 · correctness · `site/scripts/check-runs.mjs:199-221`** (with `site/src/lib/runs.ts:132`)&lt;br&gt;`summarise()` only looks at pages it measured. An `EXEMPT_RUNS` entry or an `ENFORCED_URLS` entry that names a URL missing from the sitemap is never reported. The script's own header says \"the map cannot go stale silently\", and this case breaks that. Reproduced: with no page at `/start/overview/`, `summarise(new Map([['/start/overview-renamed/', …]]))` returns `missing: []`. _(HIGH)_&lt;br&gt;Trigger: renaming the overview or SDK-guide route, or a 1.2.0 Standard taking over as current while `/spec/1.1.0/` stays hard-coded → the gate passes, the page that should be enforced is only reported, and the old exemptions keep applying to the older page. | When `complete` is true, report every URL-keyed `EXEMPT_RUNS` page and every `ENFORCED_URLS` entry that is not among the measured pages. Better still, build the current-Standard URL from `currentStandard()` instead of the literal `/spec/1.1.0/`. |\n| **F2 · correctness · `site/src/lib/release-figures.ts:40`**&lt;br&gt;`RELEASE` only matches `## [ver]` or `## [ver] — date` with an em dash. Keep a Changelog writes `## [1.0.0] - 2017-06-20` with a hyphen, and `scripts/release_notes.py:26` accepts any `## [vX.Y.Z]` followed by whitespace. A non-matching heading hits the `^## ` branch at line 76, sets `rel = null`, and that release's entries drop out without any error. Reproduced: a changelog with `## [v2.1.0] - 2026-12-01` parses to `[[\"v2.0.0\",[[\"Fixed\",1]]]]`. _(HIGH)_&lt;br&gt;Trigger: `## [v2.1.0] - 2026-12-01` in CHANGELOG.md → the release publishes on GitHub, but the site timeline, caption totals, section figures and folds all leave it out. | Accept `[—–-]` as the separator, or throw on any `## [` heading the regex does not match, so a format slip fails the build. |\n| **F3 · correctness · `site/src/lib/inject.ts:19-20`** (used by `site/src/pages/domains/[domain].astro:95-96`)&lt;br&gt;`decode()` handles only named entities. The built HTML writes `&amp;` and `&lt;` in headings as `&amp;#x26;` and `&amp;#x3C;`; I saw this in `dist`, for example `Safety &amp;#x26; Recovery`. `pickHeading` compares that undecoded `h.text` with the mdast heading text in `usageByHeading`, so the comparison fails and the usage figure is skipped without a warning. The edge-types caller fails loudly instead, because it throws when nothing matches. _(MEDIUM)_&lt;br&gt;Trigger: an H3 under a domain README's \"Capability Usage\" with `&amp;` or `&lt;` in it (e.g. \"Detect &amp; Classify\") → no usage figure and no build message. | Decode numeric entities too (`&amp;#x([0-9a-f]+);` and `&amp;#(\\d+);` through `String.fromCodePoint`). Also warn when a usage example in `usageByHeading` was never placed. |\n\n### P3 — Consider\n| Finding | Suggested Fix |\n|---------|---------------|\n| **F4 · correctness · `site/src/lib/inject.ts:90`**&lt;br&gt;`foldFirstTaskList` matches up to the first `&lt;/ul&gt;` with a lazy pattern, so a nested list ends the match early. Reproduced: `&lt;ul class=\"contains-task-list\"&gt;&lt;li&gt;a&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;sub&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;b&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;` comes out as `…&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;sub&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/details&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;b&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;`. _(HIGH)_&lt;br&gt;Trigger: a sub-list under one item of a skill's verification checklist → broken markup, and the remaining items fall outside the fold. | Find the end with depth counting (like `elementAt` in check-dist.mjs), or do the fold in hast instead of on the HTML string. |\n| **F5 · tests · `site/scripts/check-design-data.mjs:135`**&lt;br&gt;`findHexColours` misses 8-digit and 4-digit hex. Probed: `#00000080` → 0 hits, `#fffa` → 0 hits, `#a1b2c3` → 1 hit. _(HIGH)_&lt;br&gt;Trigger: a figure component written with `fill: #00000080` → the \"no hex colour\" check passes. | Use `/#(?:[0-9a-fA-F]{8}\\|[0-9a-fA-F]{6}\\|[0-9a-fA-F]{4}\\|[0-9a-fA-F]{3})\\b(?![-\\w])/`. |\n| **F6 · error-handling · `site/scripts/check-axe.mjs:145`** (and `site/scripts/check-runs.mjs:244`)&lt;br&gt;`--paths` with no value, or with an empty one, gives `only = []`. `paths` is then `[]`, nothing is checked, and the script prints the success line (\"0 pages … no axe violations\") and exits 0. _(MEDIUM)_&lt;br&gt;Trigger: `node scripts/check-axe.mjs --paths` → a local run that reports clean but checked nothing. CI does not pass `--paths`. | Throw when `only` is an empty array. |\n| **F7 · correctness · `site/src/lib/layer-figures.ts:88-93`**&lt;br&gt;`stepsCaption` ranks by sort position. When two layers have the same step count, one caption says \"the most\" and the other \"the 2nd most\". There are no ties in the current data; I checked the 9 counts against the catalogs, totalling 277. _(MEDIUM)_&lt;br&gt;Trigger: two layers with equal step counts → captions rank equal layers differently. | Rank as 1 + the number of layers with strictly more steps, and say \"joint\" on a tie. |\n| **F8 · error-handling · `site/src/lib/skill-figures.ts:142-146`**&lt;br&gt;A bare `catch { return null; }` around the Output Contract lookup and YAML parse hides a missing section, a missing fence and invalid YAML alike. _(MEDIUM)_&lt;br&gt;Trigger: a skill that has `CHECKLIST.md` but a malformed Output Contract fence → the scorecard figure disappears with no message. | Return null only when the section does not exist. Rethrow parse errors with `where`. |\n| **F9 · duplication · `site/src/lib/*-figures.ts`** (e.g. `layer-figures.ts:8`, `release-figures.ts:120`, `mermaid/text.ts:12`)&lt;br&gt;Layer B: `plural` is defined 17 times (16 lib files plus `review/Parts.astro`). `isEl` and the hast text walker are repeated in `rehype-figure-marks.ts:33-40`, `release-figures-hast.ts:34-41`, `rehype-spec-slots.ts:31` and `rehype-prose-figures.ts:67-76`. `andList` appears in 3 files. The template-class parsing in `check-dist.mjs:444` and `check-runs.mjs:97` is the same logic. None of these existed on `origin/main`, so every copy comes from this branch. _(MEDIUM)_&lt;br&gt;Trigger: a fix to one copy (e.g. irregular plurals, or a new `page--` modifier class) → the other copies drift. | Put `plural` and `andList` in one lib module and `isEl` and `hastText` in one plugin helper, and import them. |\n\n### Summary\n- **Files reviewed:**\n  - Read in full: `site.yml`, `check-axe.mjs`, `check-runs.mjs`, `runs.ts`, `inject.ts`, `md-sections.ts`, `domain-usage.ts`, `layer-figures.ts`, `release-figures.ts`, `release-figures-hast.ts`, `mermaid/parse.ts`, `mermaid/text.ts`, `mermaid/capabilities.ts`, `mermaid/twin.ts`, `remark-mermaid.ts`, `rehype-figure-marks.ts`, `rehype-spec-slots.ts` (first 205 lines), and `review.ts`.\n  - Read as diffs only: `check-dist.mjs`, `check-contrast.mjs`, `check-design-data.mjs`, `markdown.ts`, `status.ts`, `listing.ts`, `agent-files.ts`, `routes.ts`, `rehype-callouts.ts`, `rehype-tables.ts`.\n  - Partly read: `rehype-prose-figures.ts` (tail), `run-replay.ts`, `skill-figures.ts` and `spec-tail-figures.ts` (catch sites only).\n  - **Not read:** `rehype-capability-skill.ts`, `mermaid/layout.ts`, `mermaid/render.ts`, and most of `capability-figures`, `spec-dsl-figures`, `spec-figures`, `index-figures`, `workflow-figures`, `edge-figures`, `domain-figures`. The absence of findings covers only the files read.\n- **Figure correctness**, recomputed from the YAML sources, all matching the built pages:\n  - steps per layer, all 9 captions (277 steps);\n  - risk by layer (29 low, 5 medium, 2 high);\n  - the edge-type summary, all 7 counts (conflicts_with as 2 pairs, alternative_to as 6 pairs);\n  - \"12 pairs carry a second edge type\";\n  - in GROUNDED_AGENCY: the checkpoint → mutate, send, rollback edges, the recovery loop (max_loops 3) and the 50/10/8/2 seeded-error figures.\n\n  That is a sample: 1 of 47 documents with new Mermaid diagrams, plus 3 generated figure types.\n- **Other checks:**\n  - Dark mode does apply through `prefers-color-scheme` (`tokens.css:150`), so the dark axe pass is a real second theme.\n  - `pairs()` receives one theme's tokens at a time and produces 12 heat pairs per theme.\n  - The review pages are absent from the sitemap and the Pagefind fragments.\n- **Callers examined:**\n  - `walk`: 2 (git grep, both inside check-dist.mjs)\n  - `sourceStatuses`: 3 (git grep)\n  - `pairs`: 7 (git grep)\n  - `listingGroups`: 4 (git grep)\n  - `fullTextRoutes`: 1 (git grep)\n  - `rehypeCallouts`: 2 (git grep)\n  - `rehypeTables`: 2 (git grep)\n  - `remarkPageMeta`: 2 (git grep)\n\n  I did not use LSP for any of these.\n- **Blast radius:** `flow-contract-files.sh` exited 1 after a successful `git diff`, meaning none of the changed files is an API, schema or migration contract.\n- **Clone scan:** STATE=unavailable. REASON: jscpd is not installed, so no clone scan was performed. INSTALL: `npm install -g jscpd@5.3.1`. This review does not cover verbatim duplication.\n- **Candidates examined (Layer B):** `plural`: 17. `isEl`: 4. `andList`: 3. Template-class parsing: 2. Other new symbols were not searched.\n- **Total findings:** P1: 0, P2: 3, P3: 6\n- **Recommendation:** REQUEST_CHANGES under the decision table (MEDIUM/HIGH P2 findings). If this is your own pull request, the review is posted as COMMENT.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>185758</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>79</tool_uses><duration_ms>698052</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
