{"parentUuid":"e2ae51bb-f9ae-4501-80ff-d11d9d1994b3","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgzVCfvCaVdN5U4NjFrLo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both reviews are in. After removing duplicates, there are 6 P2 findings and about 11 P3s, and none are P1.\n\nThe P2s:\n- the persist page's phantom example;\n- release headings written with a plain hyphen get dropped silently;\n- two build checks treat \"measured nothing\" as a pass;\n- the enforced Standard page is hard-coded as version 1.1.0;\n- some domain usage figures can vanish without a warning when a heading contains `&`.\n\nOne agent will fix all of them, each with a test that fails without the fix."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5282,"cache_read_input_tokens":449953,"output_tokens":3156,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":315},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5282,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":3156,"cache_read_input_tokens":449953,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5282,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5282},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"a9d8b46e-d26e-4193-89db-5da0c27f1950","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgzVCePfhazi2Rr64V2ok","requestRef":"0154f473-8bd1-4b4d-8391-f5c1ffc53d21","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"cdd918bb-7f8f-42d0-85da-314883d9c97e","timestamp":"2026-11-13T06:53:39.655Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-2","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ef9f3fc8-12b6-4fe4-9f49-aaeedec05648","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/danielbentes/agent-capability-standard/.claude/worktrees/wf_08f3cd25-fc3-8","sessionId":"ef9f3fc8-12b6-4fe4-9f49-aaeedec05648","version":"2.1.322","gitBranch":"feature/issue-125-site-visuals","slug":"i-just-came-across-imperative-newell"}
{"parentUuid":"cdd918bb-7f8f-42d0-85da-314883d9c97e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgzVCfvCaVdN5U4NjFrLo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01AoKUzZdUMph7drxUeQgYqc","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Fix all review findings","run_in_background":"true","prompt":"Repository synaptiai/agent-capability-standard, worktree /Users/danielbentes/agent-capability-standard/.claude/worktrees/wf_08f3cd25-fc3-8, branch feature/issue-125-site-visuals, head f254598 (pushed). Work directly in that worktree. Fix every finding below from the pre-PR review, in the site/ Astro project. Each fix covers its class (other callers / other inputs of the same shape), and each P1/P2 fix gets a test whose expected value comes from the source data or a hand-written fixture, never the function's own output, and which fails without the fix.\n\nP2 (must fix):\n1. site/src/lib/capability-figures.ts ~571-574 (also exampleWorkflows ~792, and the section-end tests ~207, ~568, ~707, ~787): the Examples parser and section-end tests are not fence-aware, so a `### ` or `## ` line inside a fenced code block starts a new example/section. Live: /capabilities/persist/ shows a phantom 4th example \"Architecture Decisions\" (from a fenced Markdown sample at skills/persist/SKILL.md:228); its caption and Markdown copy are wrong. Make them fence-aware (prefer reading the mdast tree as md-sections.ts does). Test: persist has 3 examples.\n2. site/src/lib/release-figures.ts:40,90 — RELEASE only accepts an em dash; Keep a Changelog writes a hyphen; scripts/release_notes.py:26 accepts any `## [vX.Y.Z]` + whitespace. Accept `[—–-]` as the separator, throw on any `## [` heading the regex does not match, accept `[-*+] ` bullets, and in site/src/plugins/release-figures-hast.ts run the rendered-vs-parsed entry-count check for every kind section, not only long ones.\n3. site/scripts/check-runs.mjs ~111,180,205 — when `.doc-main__body` is missing, measurePage returns null and the page is silently skipped. Push it to `failed`; throw when results are empty or fewer than the paths.\n4. site/scripts/check-dist.mjs checkDrawnFigures/pageTemplate — a page with no template class, or a DRAWN_TEMPLATES entry that matches no built page, is skipped silently. Fail in both cases.\n5. site/src/lib/runs.ts:132 + check-runs.mjs summarise ~199-221 — ENFORCED_URLS hard-codes '/spec/1.1.0/'; derive the current Standard URL from the versions data (currentStandard / loadVersions). Report every URL-keyed EXEMPT_RUNS entry and every ENFORCED_URLS entry that is not among the measured pages (when the run is complete).\n6. site/src/lib/inject.ts:19-20 decode() handles only named entities; built HTML writes `&#x26;`/`&#x3C;`, so pickHeading misses headings with & or < and the domain usage figure is skipped silently (site/src/pages/domains/[domain].astro:95-96). Decode numeric entities; warn (or throw) when a usage example in usageByHeading is never placed.\n\nP3 (fix in one batch):\n7. site/src/lib/skill-figures.ts:141-146,161 — bare catch returns null for missing section, missing fence and invalid YAML alike; return null only when there is no scorecard key / section, rethrow others with `where`. Throw on an H3 in CHECKLIST.md that is not a family heading `X) Name (CODE)`.\n8. site/src/lib/spec-tail-figures.ts:525-530 — YAML-error fallback to stepsByLine also covers the current Standard; allow it only for the versions known to need it, rethrow otherwise.\n9. site/src/lib/inject.ts:78-94, site/src/lib/prose-figures.ts:26-34, site/src/lib/domain-figures.ts:367-372 — foldFirstTable / foldFirstTaskList / foldFirstBox / foldCapabilityList return the HTML unchanged when their regex misses; throw `<where>: no <block> to fold` instead. Also foldFirstTaskList's lazy `</ul>` match breaks on a nested list: find the end by depth counting.\n10. site/src/lib/domain-usage.ts:49,58-62 — warn on a missing \"Capability Usage\" heading; include the YAML error message in the warning.\n11. site/scripts/check-axe.mjs:145 and check-runs.mjs:244 — `--paths` present but empty must throw.\n12. site/src/lib/index-figures.ts:508-511 skillsCaption — guard empty runs (no Infinity in a caption).\n13. site/scripts/check-design-data.mjs:135 findHexColours misses 4- and 8-digit hex; use /#(?:[0-9a-fA-F]{8}|[0-9a-fA-F]{6}|[0-9a-fA-F]{4}|[0-9a-fA-F]{3})\\b(?![-\\w])/ and fix anything it then finds.\n14. site/src/lib/layer-figures.ts:88-93 stepsCaption — rank ties correctly (\"joint\").\n15. Duplication: `plural` is defined ~17 times across site/src/lib/*.ts and review/Parts.astro; `andList` in 3 files; `isEl` and the hast text walker in rehype-figure-marks.ts, release-figures-hast.ts, rehype-spec-slots.ts, rehype-prose-figures.ts; template-class parsing in check-dist.mjs:444 and check-runs.mjs:97. Put plural/andList in one lib module, isEl/hastText in one plugin helper, the template-class parse in one script helper, and import them.\n16. Hardening: site/src/data/workflows.ts parseCatalog — reject workflow ids that are not ^[a-z0-9_]+$ (they are written into a CSS selector in WorkflowSpine.astro). Check all current catalogs pass.\n\nRules: commit in small conventional commits (message in a file, `git commit -F <file>`), each ending with:\n\nRefs #125\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Jea2Va3FATnCydAsWsbLXR\n\nUse a normal merge-free history (no rebase of pushed commits, never force-push). No YAML files under site/. No hand-typed counts. Before reporting, run in site/: npm run check, npm test, npm run build, npm run check:axe (all must pass), and from the repo root with /Users/danielbentes/agent-capability-standard/.venv active: pytest tests -q, python tools/validate_doc_links.py. Then push normally and confirm local HEAD equals `git ls-remote origin refs/heads/feature/issue-125-site-visuals`. Open the built /capabilities/persist/ page's examples figure (screenshot via playwright-core at ~/.REDACTED with Chromium at ~/Library/Caches/ms-playwright/chromium-1248/chrome-mac-arm64/Google Chrome for Testing.app/Contents/MacOS/Google Chrome for Testing; serve dist with python3 -m http.server on 127.0.0.1) and Read the PNG to confirm 3 examples. Do not post on GitHub or open a PR.\n\nReport: per finding, what changed (commit SHA) and the test that covers it; any finding not fixed with the concrete reason; check results with the pushed SHA."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5282,"cache_read_input_tokens":449953,"output_tokens":3156,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":315},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5282,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":3156,"cache_read_input_tokens":449953,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5282,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5282},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":21888,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01AoKUzZdUMph7drxUeQgYqc":{"description":"Fix all review findings","run_in_background":"true","prompt":"Repository synaptiai/agent-capability-standard, worktree /Users/danielbentes/agent-capability-standard/.claude/worktrees/wf_08f3cd25-fc3-8, branch feature/issue-125-site-visuals, head f254598 (pushed). Work directly in that worktree. Fix every finding below from the pre-PR review, in the site/ Astro project. Each fix covers its class (other callers / other inputs of the same shape), and each P1/P2 fix gets a test whose expected value comes from the source data or a hand-written fixture, never the function's own output, and which fail