{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-11-13T07:39:58.136Z","sessionId":"ef9f3fc8-12b6-4fe4-9f49-aaeedec05648","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a8007b011278ffb09</task-id>\n<output-file>REDACTED.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Fix all review findings\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>All 16 findings are fixed and pushed. Local HEAD and `git ls-remote origin refs/heads/feature/issue-125-site-visuals` are both `bb97a74500ff82887d655df43b1c8c2544a6fa47`. Nothing was posted on GitHub and no PR was opened.\n\nEvery new test was run against the pre-fix code and failed there. Expected values come from the source files or hand-written fixtures.\n\n| # | Commit | What changed | Test |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 15 | `24f90fd` | `plural` and `andList` live once in `src/lib/words.ts`, replacing 17 `plural` copies and 9 list joiners under 4 names. `isEl` and `hastText` live once in `src/plugins/hast.ts`, used by 6 plugins. Template-class parsing lives once in `scripts/page-template.mjs`. `check-runs` now reads the body classes in the browser and works out the template in Node. The built site was byte-identical before and after. | Existing suite |\n| 1 | `c50c423` | The Examples, Verification and Composition Patterns parsers on the capability page, and `checkSteps` and the \"Preconditions\" check on the composed-skill pages, now read sections and examples from the parsed Markdown tree. The line-based heading scans of the Standard (§6.1, chapter 5, SpecFigure's section titles) and `check-design-data`'s glyph-key scan now skip code lines. | persist has exactly the three titles from its SKILL.md; fixtures with `##` and `###` inside a fence for all four parsers and `checkSteps`; `codeLines`; `withoutFences` |\n| 2 | `fa34e97`, `bb97a74` | Release headings accept an em dash, en dash or hyphen; any other `## [` heading throws. This covers the community page's release bars too, which had the same em-dash-only pattern. Entries may start with `-`, `*` or `+`. The rendered-against-parsed entry count now runs for every kind section and matches sections to headings by position. A heading rendered as a link (Keep a Changelog link definitions) now matches, and a release with no rendered heading throws. | Hyphen, en dash and `*`/`+` bullets; the throw; a short section with a count mismatch; the linked heading; a release with no heading |\n| 3, 5 | `aae623a` | A page with no `.doc-main__body` is recorded as failed, and `assertMeasured` throws, listing the failures, when the sweep measured no page or fewer than it was given. The enforced URL and the four Standard exempt runs now name a \"current Standard\" token. The sweep resolves it from the build's `/spec/` redirect, which comes from the versions data. A full sweep reports, and fails on, any enforced URL or URL-keyed exempt page that it did not measure. | `standardUrlFrom`, the not-measured list and `assertMeasured` |\n| 4 | `2fcadfa` | A page whose body has no template class, or a drawn-template entry that no built page uses, is now a problem. | Fixture test for both cases |\n| 6 | `2aa42d7` | Heading text is decoded with the existing one-pass decoder from `toc.ts`, which reads numeric entities and now also `&amp;#X`. A domain page throws when a usage example's figure finds no heading. | Decoding (including `&amp;amp;#x26;` staying literal); a README rendered through the real pipeline with `&amp; &lt;` in an H3 places its figure |\n| 7–14, 16 | `013d3aa` | All P3 items in one batch: scorecard errors, 1.0.0-only YAML fallback, folds that throw and count nested tags, usage warnings with the YAML error, empty `--paths` throws, no Infinity in captions, 4- and 8-digit hex, \"joint\" ranks, workflow id check. | Tests for each |\n\n**Changes you will see on the site:**\n- **`/capabilities/persist/`:** it has no examples figure now. Its three examples write out the same fields, so the page shows the sentence \"All 3 examples of the skill write out every one of its 11 output fields\" instead of the grid; the Markdown copy matches. I opened the built page in Chromium. The screenshot, with the folds closed, shows that sentence and exactly three examples: `REDACTED.png`.\n- **The two Standard pages:** the §12.5 pattern strips now carry a slug as their `data-workflow` value (`safe_mutation` instead of \"Safe Mutation\"). This was needed because pattern names would fail the new workflow id check. The accessible labels are unchanged.\n- **Build log:** the data-analysis, healthcare, manufacturing and personal-assistant READMEs have no \"Capability Usage\" section, so each build now prints a warning for them.\n\n**Where I went beyond or differed from the review:**\n- **Finding 6:** the domain page throws on an unplaced usage figure rather than only warning.\n- **Finding 9:** none of the current callers lacks the block it folds, so the stricter folds need no other changes.\n- **Finding 16:** all 235 workflow ids across the catalogs, examples and bundled copies pass the new pattern.\n\n**Limits and decisions for you:**\n- **Finding 3:** the line that records a page with no body as failed runs only in the browser. The unit test covers `assertMeasured`, not that line.\n- **Finding 2:**\n  - A heading such as `## [x] - date [YANKED]` now throws, although `release_notes.py` accepts it.\n  - The new rendering test imports `remark-rehype`, which the site gets indirectly through Astro rather than as a declared dependency.\n- **Finding 13:** the hex check scans only the figure components, and found nothing. A four-letter anchor made of hex letters, such as `#feed`, would be reported as a colour.\n- **Finding 1:** I left the §9 diagnostics parser (`src/data/diagnostics.ts`) line-based. It is deliberately matched line for line against the Rust parser in `core/src/diag.rs`, so making only the site side fence-aware would split the two. Whether to change both is your call.\n\n**Checks, all passing at `bb97a74`:**\n\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `npm run check` | 0 errors, 0 warnings, 0 hints |\n| `npm test` | 912 passed |\n| `npm run build` | every check-dist check passed |\n| `npm run check:axe` | 168 pages, 672 axe runs clean; check-runs 0 enforced pages over the limit |\n| `pytest tests -q` | 1550 passed |\n| `python tools/validate_doc_links.py` | 315 references resolve |</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>310050</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>183</tool_uses><duration_ms>2753858</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
