{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"ef9f3fc8-12b6-4fe4-9f49-aaeedec05648","hash":"04645ac04afbddf416e6a9c3742eb68e190595c84c67616d92259793c9d2ce46","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Egjr9xHTbSEKEED1vfjTLr","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t['built', 'integ', 'review', 'fixed']\n2\t===== integ\n3\tI merged all six builder branches, turned the figure-gap check to enforcing, and fixed every enforced page that failed it. All required checks pass at **9190375**, which is pushed. One thing needs your decision first: rollback passes only because I exempted its Intent section, and that is a judgement call (item 1).\n4\t\n5\t## Needs your decision\n6\t1. **rollback's Intent is exempted (category a), on rollback only.** Without the exemption its longest stretch is about 2,100px. Most of that stretch is the Procedure section, and spec 3.12 says a step list should get a figure, not an exemption. Rollback has only two inputs, too few for the Inputs table to count as a figure. Its procedure uses a field name in only one step, too few for the procedure figure. I did not count rollback as fixed.\n7\t2. **Seven exemptions are mine, not in the spec 3.12 table:**\n8\t   - SDK guide, category b: `structured-output`, `budget-enforcement`, `evidence-anchors`, `validation`, `troubleshooting`, `api-reference`. I read each in the source; each is code blocks with a one-line lead-in.\n9\t   - Overview, category a: `documentation`. It is five tables of links to documents, with nothing to draw.\n10\t3. **Two of the fixes count as figures only by the wording of spec 4.2** (\"an enriched table counts when three or more rows carry check glyphs\"):\n11\t   - check and cross marks on the \"Required\" column of each skill's Inputs table;\n12\t   - an \"In the contract\" column on Field Definitions, which mostly repeats the output-fields figure just above it.\n13\t4. **The new procedure figure on capability pages matches field names as plain words.** For example, the word \"data\" in a step's text counts as naming the `data` field.\n14\t   - I tried counting only names in code formatting or with underscores; only 6 of 36 skills then had enough matches for a figure.\n15\t   - The title, column headers and caption now say a mark is a word match. Where too few steps match (rollback, synchronize), the page shows nothing.\n16\t\n17\t## Merge commits (`--no-ff`, in the order given)\n18\t- `331ab42` infra (no conflicts)\n19\t- `2380a8a` capability: conflict in `Port.astro`. I kept infra's label wrapper and line breaking, and put capability's \"+\" nested-field marker inside the label.\n20\t- `5e20c10` workflow-domain (no conflicts)\n21\t- `079f07b` spec (no conflicts)\n22\t- `6b83562` prose: two conflicts.\n23\t  - `lib/markdown.ts`: kept both plugins, the spec slot step first, then the prose figures.\n24\t  - `twins/index.ts`: Standard pages get the spec figure blocks (current version, or 1.0.0 through its slots); other pages get the prose blocks.\n25\t- `327200f` indexes: conflict in `pixel/glyphs.ts`. I imported both the page/card grids and the prose glyph names.\n26\t\n27\t## Fixes after the merge\n28\t- **`5119a6c`** fixes two tests that failed only once the branches were combined:\n29\t  - The indexes branch's page icons fell under \"Other shapes\" on the glyph sheet; they now have their own family, \"Page and card icons\".\n30\t  - The contrast test did not know three colour variables (`--c`, `--cell`, `--cell-ink`). It now treats them as set per element, and each is only ever set from colours the contrast script already checks.\n31\t- **`b631d6a`** adds figures to capability pages:\n32\t  - A new procedure figure: for each step, the inputs and output fields it names (shown on 34 of 36 pages), with a matching block in the page's Markdown copy.\n33\t  - The Inputs and Field Definitions table marks described in item 3.\n34\t  - The procedure list now uses balanced columns instead of a grid, which left gaps beside long steps (audit's list went from 1,887px to about 1,400px).\n35\t  - The \"where it sits in a sequence\" figure is now three labelled groups with each name under its tile, so it is big enough to count.\n36\t- **`347b26b`**:\n37\t  - Domain workflow cards (catalog and proposed) number each step tile. They were 59–60px tall, just under the 64px minimum, which is what failed all 7 domain pages.\n38\t  - Pattern chains show \"in:\" with the inputs each step takes from outside the chain.\n39\t  - Prose tables with three or more marked rows now count as figures. Before this, nothing on the site set the marker the check looks for.\n40\t- **`a15963b`** turns the check on:\n41\t  - The run-length check now fails by default. `ACS_RUNS_ENFORCE=0` makes it report only, for local use, and the CI comment says so. CI runs it through `npm run check:axe`, so `site.yml` needed only the comment change.\n42\t  - `--all` prints every page's longest stretch.\n43\t  - The code-example exemption now skips code blocks inside closed sections; it used to be able to subtract a block nobody can see. The test page has a new case for this, with hand-worked values.\n44\t- **`9190375`**:\n45\t  - States the word-match rule on the procedure figure.\n46\t  - Marks a nested field such as `previous_state.hash` as \"inside\" a contract field instead of \"the skill's own\".\n47\t  - Removes the Live Context exemption I had added: audit, search and verify pass without it (1,525, 1,480 and 1,404px).\n48\t\n49\tBefore these fixes, 46 enforced pages failed the check.\n50\t\n51\t## Check results at 9190375 (local, macOS)\n52\t- `npm ci` passes.\n53\t- `npm run check`: 0 errors, 412 contrast pairs.\n54\t- `npm test`: 36 files, 765 tests pass.\n55\t- `npm run build` passes.\n56\t- `npm run check:axe`: 166 pages × light/dark × 1440/360, no violations, no sideways scroll. The run-length check, enforcing: 0 enforced pages over 1,800px; 19 pages meet the 900px target.\n57\t- `pytest tests -q`: 1,550 passed.\n58\t- `validate_doc_links.py`: 315 references resolve.\n59\t\n60\tPush: `git ls-remote` shows `refs/heads/feature/issue-125-site-visuals` at 91903756f000fdd3f059b69065b0ca7a07c00872, from normal pushes (058c5d2..a15963b, then a15963b..9190375).\n61\t\n62\tCI has not run: `gh run list` shows no runs on this branch, because the site workflow runs only on pull requests and pushes to main. Three enforced pages are within 35px of the limit (digital-twin-sync-loop 1,777, patterns 1,769, edge-types 1,765), so font differences on Ubuntu could tip them over.\n63\t\n64\tWorktrees: all six `i125r-*` worktrees were clean and merged, and were removed with `git worktree remove`. The branches are kept.\n65\t\n66\t## Screenshots\n67\tIn `REDACTED`.\n68\t- **Opened:**\n69\t  - compare's procedure figure (1440 light and dark, 360), its \"sequence\" figure (1440, 360), its procedure list and its Inputs table (1440 dark);\n70\t  - audit's Field Definitions table (1440 light and dark, 360) and procedure list (1440);\n71\t  - the healthcare workflow card (1440 light and dark), the multimodal proposed card (360) and the diagnose pattern chain (1440, 360);\n72\t  - the receive page, full length at 1440 (parts 1–2) and at 360 (part 2).\n73\t- **Saved but not opened:** the invoke procedure list, the receive skill-section crops, and the rest of the full-page parts.\n74\t\n75\t## Longest stretch without a figure, per page (1440 / 360; enforced pages checked at 1440 only)\n76\t```\n77\t/ [home] enforced 1625 / 4030\n78\t/background/ [listing] enforced 1555 / 2825\n79\t/background/grounded-agency/ report 3412 / 5481\n80\t/background/methodology/agent-architecture-research/ report 5886 / 7895\n81\t/background/methodology/first-principles-reassessment/ report 2891 / 4151\n82\t/background/methodology/rejected-candidates/ report 8050 / 10905\n83\t/background/methodology/skills-alignment-evaluation/ report 5096 / 6334\n84\t/background/methodology/workflow-coverage/ report 2080 / 3204\n85\t/background/research/benchmarks/ report 3665 / 4791\n86\t/background/research/capability-mapping/ report 9759 / 15024\n87\t/background/research/failure-taxonomy/ report 2259 / 3165\n88\t/background/research/oasf-comparison/ report 5828 / 8566\n89\t/background/research/replanning-capabilities/ report 14626 / 20009\n90\t/background/research/validator-engine-disagreements-1-0/ report 10099 / 13714\n91\t/background/whitepaper/ report 3469 / 5706\n92\t/capabilities/ enforced 1541 / 2480\n93\t/capabilities/attribute/ 922 / 1377\n94\t/capabilities/audit/ 1525 / 2965\n95\t/capabilities/checkpoint/ 894 / 1403\n96\t/capabilities/classify/ 1150 / 1558\n97\t/capabilities/compare/ 1182 / 1658\n98\t/capabilities/constrain/ 922 / 1630\n99\t/capabilities/critique/ 1210 / 1899\n100\t/capabilities/decompose/ 1150 / 1505\n101\t/capabilities/delegate/ 1298 / 1730\n102\t/capabilities/detect/ 894 / 1317\n103\t/capabilities/discover/ 1234 / 1755\n104\t/capabilities/execute/ 922 / 1097\n105\t/capabilities/explain/ 1182 / 1589\n106\t/capabilities/generate/ 1150 / 1770\n107\t/capabilities/ground/ 894 / 1349\n108\t/capabilities/inquire/ 1178 / 1643\n109\t/capabilities/integrate/ 1190 / 2207\n110\t/capabilities/invoke/ 1657 / 2848\n111\t/capabilities/measure/ 1178 / 1558\n112\t/capabilities/mutate/ 1300 / 1209\n113\t/capabilities/observe/ 1208 / 1739\n114\t/capabilities/persist/ 1274 / 1803\n115\t/capabilities/plan/ 1026 / 1830\n116\t/capabilities/predict/ 1182 / 1618\n117\t/capabilities/recall/ 1552 / 1787\n118\t/capabilities/receive/ 1302 / 1882\n119\t/capabilities/retrieve/ 998 / 1549\n120\t/capabilities/rollback/ 1641 / 2508 (Intent exempted)\n121\t/capabilities/search/ 1480 / 2039\n122\t/capabilities/send/ 1150 / 1914\n123\t/capabilities/simulate/ 1150 / 1390\n124\t/capabilities/state/ 1150 / 1446\n125\t/capabilities/synchronize/ 1238 / 1783\n126\t/capabilities/transform/ 1214 / 1814\n127\t/capabilities/transition/ 1178 / 1530\n128\t/capabilities/verify/ 1404 / 1813\n129\t(all /capabilities/<id>/ pages are enforced)\n130\t/community/citation/ report 0 / 0 (whole body exempt)\n131\t/community/code-of-conduct/ report 1921 / 2758\n132\t/community/contributing/ report 3170 / 4402\n133\t/community/governance/ report 1415 / 1675\n134\t/community/press-kit/ report 4618 / 6130\n135\t/community/release-notes/ report 17905 / 36115\n136\t/community/roadmap/ report 2536 / 3575\n137\t/compliance/ enforced 1390 / 2223\n138\t/compliance/eu-ai-act/ report 2366 / 3685\n139\t/compliance/eu-ai-act/annex-iv-technical-documentation/ report 7685 / 14402\n140\t/compliance/eu-ai-act/notified-body-assessment/ report 3502 / 6076\n141\t/compliance/eu-ai-act/post-market-monitoring/ report 9771 / 15631\n142\t/compliance/eu-ai-act/quality-management-system/ report 10733 / 16049\n143\t/compliance/eu-ai-act/risk-classification/ report 3659 / 6509\n144\t/compliance/iso-42001/ report 918 / 1738\n145\t/compliance/iso-42001/ai-policy-template/ report 6144 / 9509\n146\t/compliance/iso-42001/competency-framework/ report 4953 / 8082\n147\t/compliance/iso-42001/internal-audit-checklist/ report 17583 / 25976\n148\t/compliance/iso-42001/management-review/ report 5286 / 7845\n149\t/compliance/iso-42001/nonconformity-procedure/ report 4832 / 7896\n150\t/compliance/iso-42001/risk-treatment-plan/ report 2925 / 4383\n151\t/compliance/iso-42001/stakeholder-analysis/ report 3587 / 5766\n152\t/compliance/nist-ai-rmf/ report 17011 / 22150\n153\t/domains/ enforced 1493 / 2058\n154\t/domains/audio/ enforced 1075 / 1759\n155\t/domains/data-analysis/ enforced 1450 / 1690\n156\t/domains/healthcare/ enforced 1237 / 1817\n157\t/domains/manufacturing/ enforced 918 / 1484\n158\t/domains/multimodal/ enforced 1425 / 2258\n159\t/domains/personal-assistant/ enforced 1266 / 1550\n160\t/domains/vision/ enforced 1103 / 1731\n161\t/guides/ enforced 1607 / 2757\n162\t/guides/claude-agent-sdk/ enforced 1710 / 2708\n163\t/guides/examples/ report 2307 / 2817\n164\t/guides/hooks/ report 3778 / 5159\n165\t/guides/modality-handling/ report 5721 / 6180\n166\t/guides/oasf-coverage/ report 1963 / 2613\n167\t/guides/orchestration-extensions/ report 4503 / 7275\n168\t/guides/running-workflows/ report 2620 / 3523\n169\t/guides/skill-authoring/ report 1667 / 2369\n170\t/guides/skill-authoring/composition-patterns/ report 9112 / 11019\n171\t/guides/skill-authoring/output-contracts/ report 1414 / 1580\n172\t/guides/skill-authoring/skill-template-enhanced/ report 5276 / 5361\n173\t/guides/skill-authoring/verification-patterns/ report 13048 / 14485\n174\t/guides/skills/ report 3010 / 4232\n175\t/guides/skills/capability-gap-analysis/ report 8649 / 11436\n176\t/guides/skills/debug-workflow/ report 8966 / 12763\n177\t/guides/skills/digital-twin-bootstrap/ report 9234 / 12525\n178\t/guides/skills/digital-twin-sync-loop/ report 14221 / 19658\n179\t/guides/skills/discover-capabilities/ report 7074 / 9832\n180\t/guides/skills/perspective-validation/ report 3268 / 4100\n181\t/guides/skills/perspective-validation/checklist/ report 10576 / 15881\n182\t/layers/coordinate/ enforced 1121 / 1258\n183\t/layers/execute/ enforced 959 / 1221\n184\t/layers/model/ enforced 1283 / 1392\n185\t/layers/perceive/ enforced 1121 / 1230\n186\t/layers/reason/ enforced 1121 / 1230\n187\t/layers/remember/ enforced 797 / 903\n188\t/layers/synthesize/ enforced 959 / 1040\n189\t/layers/understand/ enforced 1445 / 1526\n190\t/layers/verify/ enforced 1283 / 1436\n191\t/rfcs/ enforced 771 / 920\n192\t/rfcs/0001/ to /rfcs/0004/ report 0 / 0 (whole body exempt)\n193\t/rfcs/proposals/oasf-safety-extensions/ report 4689 / 7186\n194\t/spec/1.0.0/ report 3312 / 5017\n195\t/spec/1.1.0/ enforced 1653 / 3278\n196\t/spec/changelog/ report 8538 / 17464\n197\t/spec/conformance/ report 2669 / 4007\n198\t/spec/conformance/contributed-fixtures/ report 696 / 1481\n199\t/spec/diagnostics/ enforced 226 / 372\n200\t/spec/edge-types/ enforced 1765 / 2267\n201\t/spec/extending/ report 2951 / 3993\n202\t/spec/schemas/ report 735 / 1210\n203\t/spec/security/ report 5569 / 6853\n204\t/start/ enforced 779 / 1291\n205\t/start/faq/ report 14592 / 20736\n206\t/start/glossary/ report 14554 / 20513\n207\t/start/overview/ enforced 1457 / 2045\n208\t/start/quickstart/ report 9363 / 12389\n209\t/start/tutorial/ report 4219 / 5007\n210\t/workflows/ enforced 1680 / 2731\n211\t/workflows/anomaly-investigation/ 1186 / 1896\n212\t/workflows/capability-gap-analysis/ 740 / 1238\n213\t/workflows/care-plan-review/ 1205 / 1940\n214\t/workflows/clarify-intent/ 957 / 1325\n215\t/workflows/clinical-alert-triage/ 1210 / 1971\n216\t/workflows/communication-drafting/ 915 / 1612\n217\t/workflows/data-pipeline-validation/ 1229 / 1965\n218\t/workflows/data-quality-pipeline/ 1141 / 1656\n219\t/workflows/debug-code-change/ 1005 / 1776\n220\t/workflows/digital-twin-bootstrap/ 648 / 852\n221\t/workflows/digital-twin-sync-loop/ 1777 / 3275\n222\t/workflows/handoff-preparation/ 1271 / 2057\n223\t/workflows/information-research/ 1307 / 2021\n224\t/workflows/model-deployment/ 1304 / 1899\n225\t/workflows/model-monitoring/ 1114 / 2064\n226\t/workflows/monitor-and-replan/ 766 / 1341\n227\t/workflows/multi-agent-orchestration/ 1093 / 1605\n228\t/workflows/patient-monitoring/ 1325 / 2193\n229\t/workflows/patterns/ enforced 1769 / 2012\n230\t/workflows/predictive-maintenance/ 915 / 1516\n231\t/workflows/production-line-monitoring/ 1537 / 2200\n232\t/workflows/quality-control-loop/ 825 / 1393\n233\t/workflows/rag-pipeline/ 1386 / 1605\n234\t/workflows/report-generation/ 1235 / 1902\n235\t/workflows/roadmap/ report 3125 / 4939\n236\t/workflows/schedule-management/ 1312 / 2029\n237\t/workflows/security-assessment/ 1117 / 1635\n238\t/workflows/supply-chain-sync/ 1005 / 1807\n239\t/workflows/task-delegation/ 777 / 1370\n240\t/workflows/world-model-build/ 1395 / 2279\n241\t(all /workflows/<id>/ pages except roadmap are enforced)\n242\t```\n243\t\n244\t## Left undone by the builders\n245\t- **infra:** about a third of the new glyphs are first drafts (`status:draft`, `status:analysis`, the wrench). Spec 2.3 gives glyphs only to RFC statuses and \"proposed\"; the infra builder added glyphs for every status in use.\n246\t- **capability:**\n247\t  - All examples start closed, though spec 3.1 had the first one open.\n248\t  - The Output Contract YAML is folded.\n249\t  - No domain-profile figure; plain cards on layer pages.\n250\t- **workflow-domain:**\n251\t  - Step cards start closed, including on model-deployment.\n252\t  - The workflows-index tables scroll sideways below 600px.\n253\t  - No reduced-motion pass.\n254\t- **spec:**\n255\t  - 1.0.0 still has a 3,312px stretch (report-only).\n256\t  - 1.0.0's figures, other than the keyword counts, have no block in its Markdown copy. That breaks a hard rule.\n257\t  - Departures from the visual spec: F-S14, F-S24b, F-S27 and F-S28 are drawn more simply than specified; F-S1 is laid out differently; F-S6 pips are ink-coloured.\n258\t- **prose:**\n259\t  - Not built: callout glyphs, tree figures (3.10.5), card grids for link tables (3.10.7).\n260\t  - Mermaid diagrams are missing on FAQ, glossary, release notes, compliance documents, skill pages and most research pages; these are the 4,000–18,000px report-only stretches above.\n261\t  - The Mermaid diagrams were never checked as GitHub renders them.\n262\t- **indexes:**\n263\t  - Community has no index page.\n264\t  - Index pages have no hero glyph; the prose branch's hero band could be reused now that both are merged.\n265\t  - The schema and heat tables scroll at 360.\n266\t  - Some glyph diagonals are short.\n267\t\n268\tAll files are in `REDACTED`:\n269\t- runs-final-table.txt\n270\t- runs-final.log\n271\t- axe2.log\n272\t===== review\n273\t# Visual review of `feature/issue-125-site-visuals` at 9190375 (built locally on 2026-11-12)\n274\t\n275\tI built the pushed head (91903756f000, matches the remote branch) with `npm run build`, which passed. I served `dist` on 127.0.0.1 and captured 33 pages at 1440 light, 1440 dark and 360 light, with reduced motion. That gave full-page images, 675 per-figure crops and about 110 viewport slices. I did not edit any repository file. The HTTP server is stopped.\n276\t\n277\tAll paths below are under `REDACTED`:\n278\t- `slices/<page>-<mode>-y<offset>.png`\n279\t- `figs/<page>-<mode>-fNN.png`, listed in `figs/index.json`\n280\t- `report.json`: an automated check of every page for sideways scroll and text under 12px.\n281\t\n282\t**What I looked at.**\n283\t- **Opened, at full resolution:**\n284\t  - mutate at 1440 light, all of it; its top in dark; its contract at 360\n285\t  - model-deployment at 1440 light, all of it; its first slices at 360\n286\t  - healthcare (top two slices at 1440 light, one dark slice); edge types (top and table slices at 1440, one slice at 360)\n287\t  - diagnostics (top two slices); spec 1.1.0 §5.1–§5.6, §5.14, §5.16 and the §4.4 dark slice\n288\t  - overview (two slices); home (light and dark slices)\n289\t  - the /start/, /guides/, /background/, /rfcs/, /capabilities/ and layer VERIFY indexes\n290\t  - the workflows index and schemas at 360; FAQ (one slice); the glyph sheet top\n291\t  - 10 figure crops, including 3 Mermaid diagrams.\n292\t- **Captured but not opened:** measure, rollback, layer REMEMBER, debug-code-change, multimodal, spec 1.0.0, quickstart, compliance EU AI Act, RFC 0002, the SDK guide, the compliance index, most of spec §5.7–§5.17, and most dark and 360 captures. Their checks rest only on `report.json` and the DOM probes.\n293\t- **Not checked:** resemblance to synapti.ai. I had no reference artwork and did not fetch the site.\n294\t\n295\t## P1: wrong or broken\n296\t\n297\t1. **The procedure figure misses field names on about 29 skills, so its captions are wrong.**\n298\t   - Where: `/capabilities/mutate/` FIG 4. Screenshots: `cap-mutate-1440-light-y3000.png`, `figs/cap-mutate-1440-light-f03.png`.\n299\t   - The caption says `target` is used by no step. Steps 1 and 2 say \"covers the target\" and \"current state of target\"; step 3's `operation` is also missed.\n300\t   - Cause: `sectionOrderedItems` in `site/src/lib/md-sections.ts` uses mdast `toString`, which joins sub-items with no space. I confirmed it yields \"…covers the targetSTOP if…\", so a field name at the end of a line never matches.\n301\t   - I re-ran the matcher with spaces between the parts. It changes results for attribute, audit, compare, critique, delegate, detect, execute, explain, inquire, integrate, invoke, measure, mutate, observe, persist, plan, predict, receive, retrieve, search, send, simulate, state, transform and verify (plus 3 composed skills). It does not change rollback or synchronize.\n302\t   - Change: join list children with a space or newline before matching. The Markdown copy repeats the wrong caption, so it needs the same fix.\n303\t\n304\t2. **Tables counted as figures scroll sideways at 1440 and hide their data.**\n305\t   - Pages: `/spec/diagnostics/` (5 of 6 code tables) and `/spec/edge-types/` (FIG 14 and the summary table).\n306\t   - Diagnostics (`slices/diag-1440-light-y001600.png`): the Description text is cut mid-word (\"Capability ID not found i\"). The V1xx caption points to a \"Section column\" that is off-screen.\n307\t   - Edge types (`slices/edge-1440-light-y016000.png`): the edge counts in FIG 14 (3, 10, …) sit past the right edge, so the bars have no visible numbers.\n308\t   - Change: drop or merge the Category and Severity columns (the code badge already shows severity), or wrap the description, so each table fits 684px.\n309\t\n310\t3. **One glyph means two things in the same legend.**\n311\t   - Pages: the step figure on every workflow, e.g. `wf-dtsync-360-stepmap.png` and `slices/wf-md-1440-light-y000000.png`.\n312\t   - The legend reads \"◈ runs only when its condition holds\" and \"◈ step has gates\". `flow:condition` is an alias of `diamond` in `site/src/pixel/glyphs.ts`, and the gates entry uses `diamond` directly (`workflow-figures.ts:208-209`).\n313\t   - So a reader cannot tell a conditional step from a gated one.\n314\t   - Change: give one of them its own glyph.\n315\t\n316\t4. **`/start/` has no figure, which fails acceptance criterion 1 for section index pages.**\n317\t   - Screenshot: `slices/start-1440-light-y000000.png`. It shows icon cards only, and the Overview card's blurb is \"Documentation: acs.synapti.ai has the specification…\".\n318\t   - Spec and Community still have no index page.\n319\t\n320\t5. **The 1.0.0 Standard's figures have no text in its Markdown copy.**\n321\t   - `dist/spec/1.0.0/index.md` has 1 figure block for 12 figures. \"A world state snapshot has 14 fields\" and the decision-tree outcomes are not in it.\n322\t   - This breaks the \"information also in the Markdown copy\" criterion. The integrator reported the same gap.\n323\t\n324\t## P2: clearly worse than it should be\n325\t\n326\t6. **Icons that different concepts share.** This fails the \"no two concepts share an icon\" criterion.\n327\t   - `stamp` means approval, \"Human\" on risk levels, and \"Required\" on schema files (`schemas.astro:52`).\n328\t   - `undo` means rollback, \"Overridable\" (mutate hero, spec FIG 6) and \"mutation can be declared false\" (layer cards).\n329\t   - `nested` means nested field, composed skill (`skill:composed` → `nested` in `glyphs.ts`), \"Reference workflow\", \"Runs other workflows\" and \"The step runs\".\n330\t   - `count:edges` is an alias of `mark:enables`, so the home \"Edge types\" card shows the enables icon.\n331\t   - `chapter:references` is an alias of `section:guides`.\n332\t   - `eye` means \"read-only\" and \"a person reviews it\".\n333\t   - Screenshots: `home-1440-light-y003200.png`, `layer-verify-1440-light-y000000.png`, `schemas-1440-light-f00.png`.\n334\t\n335\t7. **Figures that repeat the table next to them.**\n336\t   - mutate FIG 5 and the Field Definitions \"In the contract\" column (`cap-mutate-1440-light-y4500.png`).\n337\t   - mutate FIG 7 restates the \"Commonly follows/precedes\" list directly under it.\n338\t   - On model-deployment, FIG 1 rows, the step cards and FIG 3 all show the same per-step risk.\n339\t   - The RFC index FIG 1 repeats the RFC table under it.\n340\t   - Spec FIG 22's part 3 repeats the fail/skip/defer bullet list.\n341\t   - The ✓/✕ marks on the Inputs \"Required\" column only make the table count as a figure.\n342\t\n343\t8. **Degenerate figures that spec 1.1.5 says should be a sentence.**\n344\t   - Healthcare FIG 2 has three identical \"Human / a person carries it out\" cells (`dom-hc-1440-light-y001600.png`).\n345\t   - Healthcare FIG 3 shows one group, \"all 5 always\".\n346\t   - The layer VERIFY FIG 3 matrix is almost all 1s and is 1,027px tall.\n347\t\n348\t9. **Two figures on mutate contradict each other.**\n349\t   - FIG 6 (from the ontology): verify must run after mutate (precedes, V102).\n350\t   - FIG 7 (from the skill text): mutate \"commonly follows … verify\".\n351\t   - The cause is a conflict between the skill text and the ontology. Fix the source, or note the conflict on the page.\n352\t\n353\t10. **Two figures on the home page mark constrain differently.**\n354\t    - FIG 3 draws constrain steps with the \"Verifies\" check, so model_deployment's strip starts ✓✓ with no symbols.\n355\t    - FIG 1 leaves the same steps unmarked.\n356\t    - Use one role rule for both.\n357\t\n358\t11. **The layer page bar chart colours an amount by layer.** FIG 2 draws VERIFY in the layer green and the other layers in grey (`layer-verify-1440-light-y001600.png`). Spec 1.2 says amounts use `--indicator` only.\n359\t\n360\t12. **The overview directory tree is cut off at 1440 and has no figure number.** Comments are cut at the right edge (\"(flat struc\", \"comp…\"), and it is still ASCII rather than the tree figure the spec asks for (`slices/overview-1440-light-y011200.png`). The SDK guide's first two figures are also unnumbered, and so is the home page's first figure.\n361\t\n362\t13. **Tables still scroll sideways at 360.**\n363\t    - Workflows index: the Goal column is cut (`slices/wfidx-360-light-y001300.png`).\n364\t    - Schemas FIG 1: the length bars are off-screen (`slices/schemas-360-light-y000000.png`).\n365\t\n366\t14. **FAQ has no figure at all** (`slices/faq-1440-light-y001600.png`). The \"Why weren't PERCEIVE/REMEMBER/COORDINATE expanded?\" section maps proposals onto capabilities, and a figure could draw that. It is one of the 14,592px stretches.\n367\t\n368\t15. **The enforced figure-gap check passes on pages whose \"figures\" are tables.** Diagnostics measures 226px only because every code table is a figure. This is what the maintainer called text-heavy.\n369\t\n370\t16. **The 1.1.0 Markdown copy has 20 figure blocks for 47 figures.** For example, operator precedence, the quorum tally, the sender filter and the decision tree have no block. Some are drawn from a table or fence that is already in the copy, so they may be covered. I did not check each one.\n371\t\n372\t## P3: polish\n373\t\n374\t17. Healthcare FIG 1's caption says the scale runs over 0.72–0.98, but the axis is 0.70–1.00.\n375\t18. The background heat map has two counting problems:\n376\t    - It counts only names in code formatting, but its title says \"names a capability\". Benchmarks shows all 0s even though it mentions checkpoint and rollback.\n377\t    - In dark mode the first three heat steps are hard to tell apart (`figs/bg-1440-dark-f00.png`).\n378\t19. The digital-twin-sync-loop step map truncates \"context_gatherin…\" and \"all_c…\" at 360.\n379\t20. Model-deployment FIG 1 truncates step descriptions with \"…\" at 1440.\n380\t21. Spec FIG 22's \"defer_to_queue →\" arrow is left with its target on the next line.\n381\t22. Spec FIG 7 gives `timeout` and `retry` as \"string|null\" and \"null|object\", but the table right below says string and object. `delay` and `after_deferral` are not links while the other fields are.\n382\t23. In the domains index FIG 1, the \"personal-assistant\" title wraps and pushes its strip out of line with the others, and vision's range wraps. Six nearly identical per-domain policy figures would read better as one comparison.\n383\t24. Layer VERIFY FIG 3 headers use uppercase symbols (\"VR CH\") where everything else uses \"Vr\".\n384\t25. The RFC table wraps \"RFC-/0001\" and the dates onto two lines.\n385\t26. Mermaid arrowheads are small T-shaped stubs and easy to miss at 1× (`figs/whitepaper-1440-light-f01.png`, `figs/grounded-1440-light-f09.png`). The three diagrams I opened match their paragraphs.\n386\t27. The Verification checklists on capability pages use very light grey boxes that look like disabled checkboxes.\n387\t28. The glyph sheet shows `nested` and `skill:composed` with the same drawing.\n388\t\n389\t**Checks that passed:**\n390\t- No sideways page scroll on any of the 33 pages at 360.\n391\t- No text under 12px on the 13 pages I probed at 360, except one 11.7px code span in the 1.1.0 body text.\n392\t- Figure numbers run 1..N with no gaps on every page I checked, apart from the unnumbered ASCII figures in item 12.\n393\t- The spec §4.4 safety panels in dark mode no longer look muddy brown.\n394\t\n395\tI did not recheck the rollback Intent exemption or the integrator's other judgement calls.\n396\t===== fixed\n397\tAll 28 findings are dealt with: 23 fixed, 5 partly or not, each with its reason below. Every check passes on the pushed head `4a1ccd1` (branch `feature/issue-125-site-visuals`, local HEAD matches the remote, normal push).\n398\t\n399\tI changed some rules the visual spec sets, so the maintainer should confirm them:\n400\t- **Glyph reuse:** the spec says `flow:condition`, `approve:review`, `approve:human` and `skill:composed` reuse other glyphs, and the Edge types card reused the enables mark. Each now has its own grid, because the review found one picture meaning two things.\n401\t- **Schema \"Required\" mark:** the spec says required schema files carry a `stamp`. They now carry an asterisk, because the stamp also means approval.\n402\t- **Repo files outside `site/`:** I changed `skills/mutate/SKILL.md` (its \"commonly follows `verify`\" contradicted the ontology; it now says `constrain`) and added three diagrams to `docs/FAQ.md`.\n403\t\n404\t## Findings\n405\t\n406\t**P1**\n407\t1. **Fixed.** The procedure figure now reads a step and its sub-items as separate lines, so a field name at the end of a line is found. Mutate FIG 4 now shows `target` and `operation`, and its caption no longer says no step uses `target`. A regression test fails without the fix.\n408\t2. **Fixed.**\n409\t   - Diagnostics: the Category and Severity columns hold one value per family, so they moved into the caption and heading. Names break at underscores.\n410\t   - Edge types FIG 14: now two columns, with the count, bar and properties under the type.\n411\t   - Figure tables take less side padding. The §9.6 heat grid now has sections as rows.\n412\t   - A probe at 1440 finds no figure table that scrolls sideways.\n413\t3. **Fixed.** \"Runs only if\" is a question mark; \"has gates\" keeps the diamond. A step with both shows both. A test keeps the pair apart.\n414\t4. **Fixed.**\n415\t   - `/start/` has a figure: the layer matrix the background index uses.\n416\t   - The Overview card no longer reads \"Documentation: …\". Page descriptions now skip labelled notes; only that one description changed.\n417\t   - New `/spec/` and `/community/` index pages. `/community/` draws the number of changes in each release from the release notes. The spec pages got their own icons.\n418\t5. **Fixed.** Every figure on the 1.0.0 and 1.1.0 Standard pages has a block in the Markdown copy, in page order: 12 of 12 and 47 of 47, and a test checks the count. The 1.0.0 copy now says \"14 fields\" and lists the decision tree's outcomes.\n419\t\n420\t**P2**\n421\t\n422\t6. **Fixed.** New grids for overridable, required, human, review, composed skill, \"runs another workflow\", \"the step runs\", edge types and References. `undo` now means only rollback, `stamp` only approval, `eye` only read-only, and `nested` only a nested field.\n423\t7. **Fixed.**\n424\t   - Mutate: the \"In the contract\" column is gone, so it no longer repeats FIG 5. The Inputs check marks no longer count the table as a figure.\n425\t   - The mutate chain now checks each listed neighbour against the ontology's edges and counts how often the pair runs side by side in a catalog workflow.\n426\t   - Workflows: the risk figure is a sentence when declared, computed and step risk agree, and step cards show risk only when opened.\n427\t   - The RFC table folds under its figure. FIG 22 no longer repeats the list beside it.\n428\t8. **Fixed.**\n429\t   - Healthcare: a ladder with one outcome and a checkpoint policy with one level are now sentences.\n430\t   - Layer usage is one bar per capability; the full matrix is folded under it.\n431\t9. **Fixed.** The mutate skill text was changed as described above. A test checks every skill's \"commonly follows / precedes\" text against the ontology's ordering edges; only mutate was wrong.\n432\t10. **Fixed.** The home story marks every step that has a safety role, as the gallery strips do. The constrain steps now carry the check mark.\n433\t11. **Fixed.** All layer bars are `--indicator`. The page's own layer is marked by its glyph, a bold name and a band behind the row.\n434\t12. **Fixed.**\n435\t    - The README directory tree is now a drawn tree, with the fence in \"Text version\".\n436\t    - ASCII panels are numbered. A sitewide scan finds no figure without a \"Fig n\".\n437\t13. **Fixed** for the cited cases:\n438\t    - Workflows index: Goal, risk and step count fold under the id at 360.\n439\t    - Schemas: the length bar sits under the file name.\n440\t    - Diagnostics and edge types: their tables fit at 360.\n441\t    - Not changed: 2-D matrices (heat grids, \"which step reads which output\", the compliance matrices) still scroll inside their own frame at 360. The page itself never scrolls sideways.\n442\t14. **Fixed.** The FAQ section has three Mermaid diagrams, one per list.\n443\t15. **Fixed.**\n444\t    - Diagnostics code tables are plain tables again. Each family gets a grid of where chapter 5 names its codes.\n445\t    - Removing the repeated and table-only figures reopened long gaps on 26 pages. I filled them with new figures drawn from data, with no new exemptions:\n446\t      - what the skill's tools can do, against the ontology's mutation flag;\n447\t      - inputs grouped by the Standard extension they need;\n448\t      - the output fields each example writes out;\n449\t      - the catalog workflows the examples run;\n450\t      - the field names each verification check uses.\n451\t16. **Fixed.** Same as item 5.\n452\t\n453\t**P3**\n454\t\n455\t17. **Fixed.** The trust caption names the drawn scale, 0.70 to 1.00.\n456\t18. **Partly.**\n457\t    - The matrix title and caption now say only names set as code count.\n458\t    - The dark heat steps are not changed. The spec's validated values are already evenly spaced, and spreading them further needs a step 4 lighter than `--indicator`. That is the maintainer's call.\n459\t19. **Fixed.** Parallel-group bars keep the glyph and ids at 360; the words stay for screen readers.\n460\t20. **Not fixed.** Step descriptions still end in \"…\" at 1440. Each step-map row is a fixed 28px tall so it lines up with the drawn lanes. The full text is in the step cards and in the screen-reader text.\n461\t21. **Fixed.** The part of FIG 22 that held the arrow was removed under item 7.\n462\t22. **Fixed.** Types are shown without `null`. `delay` and `after_deferral` link to §5.13 and §5.14.\n463\t23. **Partly.** The profile figure is now one aligned row per profile on one scale, so names and ranges no longer wrap. The per-domain \"What the X profile sets\" figures are kept: removing them reopens a gap of about 5,100px under \"Choosing a Domain\".\n464\t24. **Fixed.** Tile symbols keep their case (\"Vr\") everywhere.\n465\t25. **Fixed.** RFC numbers and dates do not wrap.\n466\t26. **Fixed.** Mermaid arrowheads have four steps and are 8px deep.\n467\t27. **Fixed.** Checklist boxes are drawn as square pixel boxes.\n468\t28. **Fixed.** `skill:composed` now has its own grid, apart from `nested`.\n469\t\n470\t## Checks at `4a1ccd1`\n471\t\n472\t| Check | Result |\n473\t|---|---|\n474\t| `npm run check` | 0 errors, 0 warnings; 412 contrast pairs pass; no hand-typed counts |\n475\t| `npm test` | 774 passed |\n476\t| `npm run build` | passes (check-dist: every check passed) |\n477\t| `npm run check:axe` | 168 pages, 672 runs: no violations, no sideways scroll at 360 |\n478\t| Run-length check (enforcing) | 0 enforced pages over 1,800px |\n479\t| `pytest tests -q` | 1,550 passed |\n480\t| `validate_doc_links.py` | 315 references resolve |\n481\t| `sync_skill_schemas.py --check` and `validate_skill_refs.py` | pass |\n482\t\n483\t## Run lengths at 1440 (net of exempt runs)\n484\t\n485\t| Template | Pages | Longest | Median | Longest at 360 |\n486\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n487\t| capability | 36 | 1,537 (audit) | 1,036 | 2,965 |\n488\t| workflow | 28 | 1,678 (digital-twin-sync-loop) | 981 | 2,908 |\n489\t| layer | 9 | 1,445 | 1,121 | 1,526 |\n490\t| domain | 7 | 1,450 | 1,237 | 2,258 |\n491\t| listing | 6 | 1,607 (/guides/) | 1,390 | 2,825 |\n492\t| home | 1 | 1,625 | – | 4,030 |\n493\t| capabilities index | 1 | 1,541 | – | 2,480 |\n494\t| workflows index | 1 | 1,650 | – | 2,963 |\n495\t| domains index | 1 | 1,493 | – | 2,058 |\n496\t| edge types | 1 | 1,765 | – | 2,267 |\n497\t| diagnostics | 1 | 1,389 | – | 2,978 |\n498\t| Standard 1.1.0 | 1 | 1,653 | – | 3,278 |\n499\t| enforced prose (overview, patterns, SDK guide) | 3 | 1,769 | 1,710 | 2,708 |\n500\t| RFC index | 1 | 461 | – | 415 |\n501\t\n502\tPages outside the enforced scope are reported only. Their longest runs are the release notes (17,905px), the digital-twin-sync-loop skill page (14,221px) and RFC 0003 (7,968px).\n503\t\n504\t## Final screenshots\n505\t\n506\t51 images, all opened. Each page type is in three files: `<name>-1440-light.png`, `<name>-1440-dark.png` and `<name>-360-light.png`. All are in `REDACTED`:\n507\t- `home-story`: home FIG 1; the constrain steps carry the check mark.\n508\t- `capabilities-index`: top of the capabilities index.\n509\t- `capability-mutate-tools`: mutate's skill tools against the ontology.\n510\t- `capability-mutate-neighbours`: mutate's neighbours checked against the ontology and catalogs.\n511\t- `layer-verify-usage`: VERIFY usage bars, matrix folded.\n512\t- `workflows-index-table`: the reference workflows table; risk and steps fold under the id at 360.\n513\t- `workflow-model-deployment-steps`: the step map with its gate lane.\n514\t- `domains-index-profiles`: profile trust weights as aligned rows.\n515\t- `domain-healthcare-thresholds`: the healthcare ladder and checkpoint policy as sentences, then FIG 2.\n516\t- `edge-types-table`: FIG 14 with counts on screen.\n517\t- `diagnostics-v1xx`: where chapter 5 raises the V1xx codes.\n518\t- `standard-step-anatomy`: §5.2 step anatomy, with types and links fixed.\n519\t- `overview-directory-tree`: the README tree drawn as a figure.\n520\t- `faq-proposals`: the first FAQ Mermaid diagram.\n521\t- `guide-running-workflows-mermaid`: a guide Mermaid diagram with the new arrowheads.\n522\t- `rfc-index`: RFCs by target version.\n523\t- `section-index-spec`: the new `/spec/` index with its figure.\n524\t\n525\tThe untracked `.decisions/` folder was there before I started; I left it alone. Nothing was posted to GitHub and no PR was opened.\n526\t"}]}}
