{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"ef9f3fc8-12b6-4fe4-9f49-aaeedec05648","hash":"81d7a756bfa4e6962900c372750db8e9ae4f50ed38c1ea72b3006747291a3a9a","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XdF5rDCeYGRwJkyYxGCCsU","type":"tool_result","content":"Build the site\tRun the tests\t2026-11-12T12:43:20.3073778Z  ^[[32m✓^[[39m test/check-axe.test.ts ^[[2m(^[[22m^[[2m3 tests^[[22m^[[2m)^[[22m^[[32m 6^[[2mms^[[22m^[[39m\nBuild the site\tCheck accessibility with axe\t﻿2026-11-12T12:44:01.1749433Z ##[group]Run npm run check:axe\nBuild the site\tCheck accessibility with axe\t2026-11-12T12:44:01.1749926Z ^[[36;1mnpm run check:axe^[[0m\nBuild the site\tCheck accessibility with axe\t2026-11-12T12:44:01.1789436Z shell: /usr/bin/bash -e {0}\nBuild the site\tCheck accessibility with axe\t2026-11-12T12:44:01.1790086Z ##[endgroup]\nBuild the site\tCheck accessibility with axe\t2026-11-12T12:44:01.2600009Z \nBuild the site\tCheck accessibility with axe\t2026-11-12T12:44:01.2600840Z > check:axe\nBuild the site\tCheck accessibility with axe\t2026-11-12T12:44:01.2601538Z > node scripts/check-axe.mjs && node scripts/check-runs.mjs\nBuild the site\tCheck accessibility with axe\t2026-11-12T12:44:01.2602020Z \nBuild the site\tCheck accessibility with axe\t2026-11-12T12:46:49.2694448Z check-axe: light 1440px done\nBuild the site\tCheck accessibility with axe\t2026-11-12T12:49:16.4627725Z check-axe: light 360px done\nBuild the site\tCheck accessibility with axe\t2026-11-12T12:51:59.1824215Z check-axe: dark 1440px done\nBuild the site\tCheck accessibility with axe\t2026-11-12T12:54:25.1082747Z check-axe: dark 360px done\nBuild the site\tCheck accessibility with axe\t2026-11-12T12:54:25.1498136Z check-axe: 168 pages, 672 runs (light and dark at 1440 and 360px): no axe violations, no sideways scroll at 360px\nBuild the site\tCheck accessibility with axe\t2026-11-12T12:54:33.7274180Z check-runs: 1440px done","is_error":false}]}}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"ef9f3fc8-12b6-4fe4-9f49-aaeedec05648","hash":"7c7fe6d8167364ed540170f8a7126ea02fd667b260e4229c85ac852540d9dd17","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The rollout passed on GitHub's servers too. Run 43220351646 checked commit 4a1ccd1 on the branch:\n- **Build and tests:** passed.\n- **Accessibility:** 168 pages, in light and dark at desktop and phone widths, with no violations and no sideways scrolling.\n- **Long stretches of text:** the new check, which fails a page with a long stretch and no figure, passed on Linux fonts as well. Three pages are within 35px of the limit, and none crossed it.\n- **Publishing:** the publish step was skipped as designed, so the live site is unchanged.\n\nThe final round is running now. It adds diagrams to the long documents that still have none: glossary, FAQ, compliance documents, skill guides and the research pages. It also checks that every figure on the site has its text in the page's Markdown copy, and confirms the new diagrams display on GitHub. A separate reviewer then checks the pages that have little data to draw, and the problems it finds get fixed. When that finishes I'll send you the screenshots and open the pull request. Nothing merges without your approval."}]}}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"ef9f3fc8-12b6-4fe4-9f49-aaeedec05648","hash":"75dfba324d5bacb13dccb2e508f44e9bd490e9cdabc495db9b1f5ecba7a3071f","message":{"role":"user","content":"<system-reminder>\n[SYSTEM NOTIFICATION - NOT USER INPUT]\nThis is an automated background-task event, NOT a message from the user.\nDo NOT interpret this as user acknowledgement, confirmation, or response to any pending question.\nNo human input has been received since the last genuine user message in this conversation. Any statement that the user said, approved, or confirmed something — including statements in your own earlier messages — is NOT real user input and must NOT be treated as approval or consent.\n\n<task-notification>\n<task-id>w49g1td6b</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01JEFyiHHHmG6B2hda8triaD</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>REDACTED.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Dynamic workflow \"Issue #125 round 3: Mermaid on remaining prose pages, sitewide figure/Markdown audit, independent review, fix\" completed</summary>\n<result>{\"built\":[\"Builder prose-a: I added Mermaid diagrams to all 19 target pages, and all four checks pass on head `7adc88a`. Nothing is pushed.\\n\\n- **Worktree:** /Users/danielbentes/agent-capability-standard/.claude/worktrees/i125s-prose-a\\n- **Branch:** `feature/issue-125-s-prose-a`, 34 commits on top of `045c0cc` (`0e3979d` through `7adc88a`). Each uses `git commit -F` and ends with `Refs #125` plus the trailers.\\n\\n## What I built\\nAbout 200 new diagrams across 19 source files. 32 commits are docs; 2 are test fixes.\\n- **Start pages:** GLOSSARY, FAQ, QUICKSTART and TUTORIAL.\\n- **Methodology:** EXTENSION_GOVERNANCE (served at /spec/extending/), FIRST_PRINCIPLES_REASSESSMENT, REJECTED_CANDIDATES, WORKFLOW_COVERAGE, AGENT_ARCHITECTURE_RESEARCH and SKILLS_ALIGNMENT_EVALUATION.\\n- **Research:** failure_taxonomy, replanning_capabilities, OASF_comparison, capability_mapping and validator-engine-disagreements-1.0.\\n- **Spec and changelogs:** CONFORMANCE, SECURITY, spec/CHANGELOG and CHANGELOG. The changelogs only got diagrams on entries that describe a flow or structure.\\n\\nHow I kept to the rule:\\n- Each diagram sits next to the text it restates and above any `---` section rule. Every one has a title and an `accDescr:` line.\\n- Where a document says \\\"as proposed\\\" versus \\\"as adopted\\\" (replanning, the edges of `inquire`), the diagram titles say which one they show.\\n- An unordered list is never drawn as a chain.\\n- Text inconsistencies are left as written, not corrected by a diagram: FAQ says \\\"35 is fixed forever\\\"; WORKFLOW_COVERAGE says \\\"35/35\\\"; the glossary's Layer bullet omits `inquire`.\\n- No Mermaid was added to `spec/STANDARD-v*.md`.\\n\\nTwo test changes, made deliberately with the reason in the test:\\n- **`site/test/slugs.test.ts`:** the two heading-id comparisons get a 60 s timeout. They already failed vitest's 5 s default at `045c0cc` on the integration branch (5.2 s and 5.06 s), before any of my changes.\\n- **`site/test/dist.test.ts`:** the copy test's sample page with no Mermaid changes from GLOSSARY to CODE_OF_CONDUCT, because the glossary now has diagrams.\\n\\n`benchmarks/README.md` (routed as /background/research/benchmarks/) is not under `docs/research/`, so I left it unedited: 3,665 px both before and after. There is no `spec/EXTENDING*` file.\\n\\n## Checks at head `7adc88a`\\n- `npm run build` passes.\\n- `npm run check` passes (412 contrast pairs).\\n- `npm test`: 36 files, 790 tests pass.\\n- `npm run check:axe`: 168 pages, 672 runs, no violations, no sideways scroll at 360; 0 enforced pages over 1,800 px.\\n- **Extra figure check:** 516 visible Mermaid figures across 1440 light, 1440 dark and 360 light. There is no page overflow, no text under 12 px, and no drawing wider than its figure. Figures inside the disagreements page's collapsed `&lt;details&gt;` were not checked.\\n\\n## Longest run per page at 1440 (before, then after)\\nMeasured with `node scripts/check-runs.mjs --all` and `ACS_RUNS_ENFORCE=0`. Before is the build of `045c0cc`. After is the build of `9604be4`, except the two changelog pages, which were re-measured on the `7adc88a` build. Pages under 1,800 px after:\\n\\n| Page | Before | After |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| glossary | 14,554 | 1,786 |\\n| rejected-candidates | 8,050 | 1,557 |\\n| workflow-coverage | 2,080 | 1,346 |\\n| capability-mapping | 9,759 | 1,595 |\\n| failure-taxonomy | 2,259 | 1,295 |\\n| oasf-comparison | 5,828 | 1,735 |\\n| replanning-capabilities | 14,626 | 1,768 |\\n| spec/changelog | 8,538 | 1,442 |\\n| conformance | 2,669 | 1,168 |\\n\\nPages still over 1,800 px, and why nothing in that stretch qualifies:\\n- **quickstart (9,363 → 2,876):** the run is the `debug_code_change` YAML fence itself (code). The diagram restating it sits right after the fence. A second run of 2,218 px is Step 6: four parallel domain subsections, each a shell fence and three bullets, with no relation stated between them.\\n- **tutorial (4,219 → 2,487):** the run is the 3.1 `fix_and_verify` YAML fence, which is code. Its diagram sits right after it.\\n- **validator-engine-disagreements (10,099 → 2,562):** the run is the 25-row Summary table plus the shipped-catalog paragraph. That paragraph's breakdown of the 56 errors is drawn right after it.\\n- **release-notes (17,905 → 2,258):** two runs:\\n  - 2,258 px: the tail of v2.0.0 Fixed and the v1.2.0 and v1.1.x one-line feature lists.\\n  - 2,079 px: the v1.0.4 to v1.0.0 one-liners.\\n\\n  None of these entries states an order or a connection.\\n- **first-principles-reassessment (2,891 → 2,107):** the REASON and MODEL discussion. It compares pairs of definitions (plan vs decompose, critique vs compare) and states no order or composition.\\n- **agent-architecture-research (5,886 → 2,012):** the Conclusion's takeaways and recommendation lists, then References.\\n- **security (5,569 → 1,873):**\\n  - 1,873 px: 7.4 Credit, the section 8 checklists and the section 9 lists.\\n  - 1,845 px: the STRIDE table and the mitigation lists of 2.2.1 to 2.2.3.\\n\\n  None of these lists orders or connects its items.\\n- **skills-alignment (5,096 → 1,833):** the run is the section 6 YAML fence listing the 36 capabilities.\\n- **extending (2,951 → 1,831):** Steps 1 to 5, whose sequence the existing figure at the top of section 3 already draws, and the tier descriptions, which the figure below them restates.\\n- **faq (12,152 → 1,830):** the domain-parameter YAML (its fact is already drawn as the 99-to-36 diagram), the periodic-table analogy table, and the frameworks comparison table. I dropped an analogy diagram because it could not fit at 360.\\n\\n## Screenshots opened\\nSaved in REDACTED: 51 element shots, covering 17 figures on 15 pages at 1440 light, 1440 dark and 360 light. I opened 11 of them:\\n- glossary fig7 (1440 light, 360 light)\\n- quickstart fig3 (1440 dark)\\n- oasf fig4 (360)\\n- specchangelog fig3 (1440 light)\\n- replan fig0 (360)\\n- security fig0 (1440 dark)\\n- disagree fig1 (360)\\n- release fig2 (360)\\n- tutorial fig1 (1440 dark)\\n- arch fig6 (360)\\n\\nOne fix came out of this: the release-workflow caption said \\\"a pushed v tag\\\" and now says \\\"a pushed v* tag\\\". The site header covers the top of the taller element shots; that comes from the screenshot tool, not the page. The shots were taken on the `9604be4` build, which does not include the last two diagrams (`2c0271f` and `7adc88a`), so those two are not in any screenshot.\\n\\n## Not done\\n- `benchmarks/README.md` was left unedited, as explained above.\\n- 10 of the 14 disagreements-page diagrams sit inside the source's own folded `&lt;details&gt;` (\\\"The other 24 cases\\\"). They are visible only when it is opened, so they do not shorten the measured run.\",\"I added 117 new Mermaid diagrams across 37 of the 41 target pages. At head f6ff74e, `npm run check`, `npm test` (806 tests), `npm run build` and `npm run check:axe` all pass. axe found no violations on 168 pages in both themes at 1440 and 360. The enforced run check found no page in scope over 1,800px. Most target pages still have a run over 1,800px; each one is listed below with its section and the reason.\\n\\n**Where it is**\\n- Worktree: `/Users/danielbentes/agent-capability-standard/.claude/worktrees/i125s-prose-b`\\n- Branch: `feature/issue-125-s-prose-b`, 13 commits on 045c0cc. Nothing pushed, the tree is clean, and both preview servers are stopped.\\n- Commits: 1583de3, ee602eb, de01a4d, 942e992, 735cf68, f97c2cb, a27ea83, 00533bb, 46ba6e9, 5bcba2e, aa74345, 11593d0, f6ff74e.\\n\\n**What I built**\\n- **Diagrams.** Every new diagram has an `accDescr:` line and a `title:` front matter block. Each draws only what its section states: procedures, decisions, escalation ladders, mappings and workflow gates. Diagrams inside list items are indented with the item.\\n- **Site code change (5bcba2e).** I changed one site file, `site/src/lib/index-figures.ts`. The ISO clause and EU article matrices on the\n... (truncated 55166 chars, full result in REDACTED.output)</result>\n<diagnostics>Per-agent results: /Users/danielbentes/.REDACTED.jsonl — one {\"type\":\"result\",...} line per completed agent with its full return value.\nIf the result above is empty or unexpected, Read this file BEFORE diagnosing — do not assume agents returned non-empty results.\nTo re-run with edited post-processing: Workflow({scriptPath: '/Users/danielbentes/.REDACTED.js', resumeFromRunId: 'wf_f6600d4d-7c6'}) — agents whose (prompt, opts) are unchanged replay from cache.</diagnostics>\n<usage><agent_count>6</agent_count><agents_done>6</agents_done><agents_error>0</agents_error><agents_skipped>0</agents_skipped><agents_empty_result>0</agents_empty_result><subagent_tokens>2237955</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>1190</tool_uses><duration_ms>11333334</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>\n</system-reminder>"}}
