{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"ef9f3fc8-12b6-4fe4-9f49-aaeedec05648","hash":"49408f0cc0d458a1cd33d947a91e58772d6e99b7d270ac008ba3ed2ab9790ac2","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WLJ4T5g8YzdN8tpztSQhmv","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t===== integ\n2\tI merged all three builder branches into `feature/issue-125-site-visuals` and pushed. Every check passed, so no fixes were needed. The remote branch is at `6e33b5aa182e865e31e36dd6fdb5157f055607e5` (`git ls-remote` matches local HEAD). On GitHub, all 213 Mermaid diagrams I probed, across 20 files, render as diagrams, with no error boxes.\n3\t\n4\t## Merges\n5\tAll three used `--no-ff`, in the order given, with messages written through `git commit -F` and the `Refs #125` and trailer lines.\n6\t- `2c76884`: `feature/issue-125-s-prose-a` (head 7adc88a)\n7\t- `ae4f1dc`: `feature/issue-125-s-prose-b` (head f6ff74e)\n8\t- `6e33b5a`: `feature/issue-125-s-audit` (head 30c1a14)\n9\t\n10\tThere were no textual conflicts. Three files were touched by two branches each: `site/test/dist.test.ts` (prose-a and audit), and `site/src/lib/index-figures.ts` and `site/test/index-figures.test.ts` (prose-b and audit). Git merged all three cleanly, and the full suite passes on the result, which is the check that the two sides' changes still work together.\n11\t\n12\t## Fixes\n13\tNone to the repository. One fix was to my own GitHub check script: its \"open every `<details>`\" step also opened GitHub's full-screen diagram dialogs, which covered the screenshots. I limited it to the document's own `<details>` blocks and ran it again.\n14\t\n15\t## Check results at 6e33b5a\n16\t- `npm ci` and `npm run check`: 0 errors, 0 warnings. Contrast: 412 pairs pass. Design-data check passes.\n17\t- `npm test`: 36 files, 834 tests pass.\n18\t- `npm run build`: passes, including the Markdown copies, sitemap, figures, legends and review-sheet checks (168 pages, 27,270 internal links).\n19\t- `npm run check:axe`: 168 pages, 672 runs (light and dark at 1440 and 360) with no violations and no sideways scroll. The enforced run-length check found 0 enforced pages with a run over 1,800px.\n20\t- `pytest tests -q`: 1550 passed.\n21\t- `validate_doc_links.py`: 315 references resolve. `sync_skill_schemas.py --check`: 107 files up to date. `validate_skill_refs.py`: 42 skills pass.\n22\t\n23\t## GitHub render check (blob pages at 6e33b5a)\n24\tI checked 20 files with headless Chromium. For each `section[data-type=\"mermaid\"]`, the script looked inside its iframe and counted it as rendered only when an SVG with nodes appeared and no \"Unable to render\", \"Parse error\", \"Syntax error\" or \"Unsupported markdown\" text did. All 213 sections passed:\n25\t\n26\t| File | Diagrams | File | Diagrams |\n27\t|---|---:|---|---:|\n28\t| docs/FAQ.md | 14 | spec/CONFORMANCE.md | 2 |\n29\t| CHANGELOG.md | 18 | docs/TUTORIAL.md | 14 |\n30\t| docs/GLOSSARY.md | 15 | NIST AI RMF profile | 9 |\n31\t| docs/research/replanning_capabilities.md | 13 | templates/verification_patterns.md | 7 |\n32\t| docs/guides/RUNNING_WORKFLOWS.md | 8 | skills/perspective-validation/CHECKLIST.md | 7 |\n33\t| docs/methodology/AGENT_ARCHITECTURE_RESEARCH.md | 7 | docs/guides/ORCHESTRATION_EXTENSIONS.md | 12 |\n34\t| validator-engine-disagreements-1.0.md | 16 | ISO 42001 internal audit checklist | 7 |\n35\t| spec/SECURITY.md | 9 | skills/digital-twin-sync-loop/SKILL.md | 4 |\n36\t| spec/WHITEPAPER.md | 15 | docs/guides/MODALITY_HANDLING.md | 15 |\n37\t| hooks/README.md | 3 | docs/GROUNDED_AGENCY.md | 18 |\n38\t\n39\tI opened 15 screenshots, and each shows a drawn diagram:\n40\t- **FAQ, with its `title:` front matter shown as the heading:**\n41\t  - REDACTED.md-0.png\n42\t  - REDACTED.md-4.png (\"Where the 36 comes from\")\n43\t  - REDACTED.md-1.png\n44\t- **CHANGELOG:** REDACTED.md-0.png\n45\t- **GLOSSARY, a label containing `${…}`:** REDACTED.md-7.png\n46\t- **GLOSSARY, with a subgraph:** REDACTED.md-8.png\n47\t- **TUTORIAL, with a subgraph:** REDACTED.md-8.png\n48\t- **Replanning capabilities:**\n49\t  - REDACTED.md-0.png\n50\t  - REDACTED.png\n51\t- **RUNNING_WORKFLOWS, a diagram indented inside a list item:** REDACTED.md-3.png\n52\t- **Disagreements page, a diagram inside its folded `<details>`:** REDACTED.0.md-8.png\n53\t- **SECURITY:** REDACTED.md-0.png\n54\t- **ISO internal audit checklist:** REDACTED.md-2.png\n55\t- **NIST AI RMF:** REDACTED.md-0.png\n56\t\n57\tThe other 198 diagrams were checked only by the script, not by opening a screenshot.\n58\t\n59\tThe element screenshot of replanning diagram 3 came out blank. That diagram is 1,010px tall, which is taller than the 1,000px window. A full-window capture at 1,400px tall (the `replanning-3-viewport.png` above) shows it drawn correctly, so blank shots of diagrams taller than the window come from how the screenshot was taken, not from the page. The per-diagram results are in REDACTED.jsonl.\n60\t\n61\t## Worktrees\n62\tI removed the `i125s-prose-a`, `i125s-prose-b` and `i125s-audit` worktrees, which were all clean. Their three branches are kept. No check script is still running.\n63\t\n64\t## Longest run per page\n65\tBuilt from 6e33b5a with `node scripts/check-runs.mjs --all`; lengths are in px. \"Enforced\" pages fail the build if a run exceeds 1,800px; \"report\" pages are only measured. 44 pages have a run over 1,800px at 1440, and all of them are report-only. No enforced page has one.\n66\t\n67\t| Page | Type | Scope | Longest at 1440 | Longest at 360 |\n68\t|---|---|---|---:|---:|\n69\t| /guides/skills/digital-twin-sync-loop/ | skill | report | 9174 | 10935 |\n70\t| /compliance/nist-ai-rmf/ | prose | report | 7972 | 11606 |\n71\t| /guides/skills/digital-twin-bootstrap/ | skill | report | 6734 | 8494 |\n72\t| /guides/skills/capability-gap-analysis/ | skill | report | 5996 | 6843 |\n73\t| /guides/skills/debug-workflow/ | skill | report | 5787 | 7050 |\n74\t| /guides/skill-authoring/composition-patterns/ | prose | report | 5364 | 5858 |\n75\t| /guides/skill-authoring/skill-template-enhanced/ | raw | report | 5276 | 5361 |\n76\t| /compliance/eu-ai-act/quality-management-system/ | prose | report | 4599 | 6508 |\n77\t| /compliance/eu-ai-act/annex-iv-technical-documentation/ | prose | report | 4377 | 8005 |\n78\t| /rfcs/proposals/oasf-safety-extensions/ | rfc | report | 4128 | 5690 |\n79\t| /compliance/iso-42001/competency-framework/ | prose | report | 4094 | 6695 |\n80\t| /compliance/iso-42001/internal-audit-checklist/ | prose | report | 4005 | 6241 |\n81\t| /compliance/eu-ai-act/post-market-monitoring/ | prose | report | 3803 | 6016 |\n82\t| /background/research/benchmarks/ | prose | report | 3665 | 4791 |\n83\t| /compliance/iso-42001/stakeholder-analysis/ | prose | report | 3587 | 5766 |\n84\t| /guides/skills/perspective-validation/checklist/ | prose | report | 3376 | 5360 |\n85\t| /spec/1.0.0/ | spec | report | 3312 | 5017 |\n86\t| /background/grounded-agency/ | prose | report | 3218 | 5225 |\n87\t| /compliance/iso-42001/management-review/ | prose | report | 3218 | 4687 |\n88\t| /guides/modality-handling/ | prose | report | 3132 | 3201 |\n89\t| /workflows/roadmap/ | prose | report | 3125 | 4939 |\n90\t| /guides/skills/discover-capabilities/ | skill | report | 3116 | 4264 |\n91\t| /compliance/iso-42001/nonconformity-procedure/ | prose | report | 3101 | 5009 |\n92\t| /guides/skills/ | prose | report | 3010 | 4232 |\n93\t| /compliance/eu-ai-act/risk-classification/ | prose | report | 2983 | 4400 |\n94\t| /start/quickstart/ | prose | report | 2876 | 3944 |\n95\t| /compliance/eu-ai-act/notified-body-assessment/ | prose | report | 2829 | 5166 |\n96\t| /background/research/validator-engine-disagreements-1-0/ | prose | report | 2562 | 2956 |\n97\t| /background/whitepaper/ | prose | report | 2500 | 3800 |\n98\t| /start/tutorial/ | prose | report | 2487 | 2576 |\n99\t| /guides/skills/perspective-validation/ | skill | report | 2396 | 2526 |\n100\t| /guides/orchestration-extensions/ | prose | report | 2311 | 3550 |\n101\t| /community/release-notes/ | prose | report | 2258 | 3988 |\n102\t| /background/methodology/first-principles-reassessment/ | prose | report | 2107 | 3060 |\n103\t| /guides/hooks/ | prose | report | 2050 | 2807 |\n104\t| /background/methodology/agent-architecture-research/ | prose | report | 2012 | 2655 |\n105\t| /compliance/iso-42001/ai-policy-template/ | prose | report | 1968 | 3169 |\n106\t| /community/code-of-conduct/ | prose | report | 1921 | 2758 |\n107\t| /guides/skill-authoring/verification-patterns/ | prose | report | 1911 | 2069 |\n108\t| /spec/security/ | prose | report | 1873 | 2405 |\n109\t| /background/methodology/skills-alignment-evaluation/ | prose | report | 1833 | 2467 |\n110\t| /spec/extending/ | prose | report | 1831 | 2203 |\n111\t| /start/faq/ | prose | report | 1830 | 2530 |\n112\t| /compliance/iso-42001/risk-treatment-plan/ | prose | report | 1808 | 2494 |\n113\t| /start/glossary/ | prose | report | 1786 | 2460 |\n114\t| /compliance/eu-ai-act/ | prose | report | 1777 | 2814 |\n115\t| /workflows/patterns/ | prose | enforced | 1769 | 2012 |\n116\t| /background/research/replanning-capabilities/ | prose | report | 1768 | 2557 |\n117\t| /spec/edge-types/ | edge-types | enforced | 1765 | 2267 |\n118\t| /background/research/oasf-comparison/ | prose | report | 1735 | 2866 |\n119\t| /guides/claude-agent-sdk/ | prose | enforced | 1710 | 2708 |\n120\t| /workflows/digital-twin-sync-loop/ | workflow | enforced | 1678 | 2908 |\n121\t| /community/contributing/ | prose | report | 1667 | 2000 |\n122\t| /spec/1.1.0/ | spec | enforced | 1653 | 3278 |\n123\t| /workflows/ | workflows-index | enforced | 1650 | 2963 |\n124\t| / | home | enforced | 1625 | 4030 |\n125\t| /community/press-kit/ | prose | report | 1615 | 2395 |\n126\t| /guides/oasf-coverage/ | prose | report | 1609 | 2051 |\n127\t| /guides/ | listing | enforced | 1607 | 2757 |\n128\t| /background/research/capability-mapping/ | prose | report | 1595 | 2439 |\n129\t| /background/methodology/rejected-candidates/ | prose | report | 1557 | 2212 |\n130\t| /background/ | listing | enforced | 1555 | 2825 |\n131\t| /capabilities/ | capabilities-index | enforced | 1541 | 2480 |\n132\t| /capabilities/audit/ | capability | enforced | 1537 | 2965 |\n133\t| /capabilities/invoke/ | capability | enforced | 1513 | 2647 |\n134\t| /capabilities/synchronize/ | capability | enforced | 1508 | 2384 |\n135\t| /domains/ | domains-index | enforced | 1493 | 2058 |\n136\t| /capabilities/search/ | capability | enforced | 1492 | 2119 |\n137\t| /start/overview/ | prose | enforced | 1457 | 2045 |\n138\t| /domains/data-analysis/ | domain | enforced | 1450 | 1690 |\n139\t| /layers/understand/ | layer | enforced | 1445 | 1526 |\n140\t| /spec/changelog/ | prose | report | 1442 | 2988 |\n141\t| /domains/multimodal/ | domain | enforced | 1425 | 2258 |\n142\t| /community/governance/ | prose | report | 1415 | 1675 |\n143\t| /guides/skill-authoring/output-contracts/ | prose | report | 1414 | 1580 |\n144\t| /capabilities/verify/ | capability | enforced | 1404 | 1813 |\n145\t| /spec/ | listing | enforced | 1403 | 2136 |\n146\t| /compliance/ | listing | enforced | 1390 | 2223 |\n147\t| /spec/diagnostics/ | diagnostics | enforced | 1389 | 2978 |\n148\t| /guides/running-workflows/ | prose | report | 1381 | 2521 |\n149\t| /background/methodology/workflow-coverage/ | prose | report | 1346 | 1708 |\n150\t| /capabilities/rollback/ | capability | enforced | 1298 | 2084 |\n151\t| /guides/examples/ | prose | report | 1297 | 1698 |\n152\t| /background/research/failure-taxonomy/ | prose | report | 1295 | 1929 |\n153\t| /layers/model/ | layer | enforced | 1283 | 1392 |\n154\t| /layers/verify/ | layer | enforced | 1283 | 1436 |\n155\t| /domains/personal-assistant/ | domain | enforced | 1266 | 1550 |\n156\t| /domains/healthcare/ | domain | enforced | 1237 | 1817 |\n157\t| /workflows/production-line-monitoring/ | workflow | enforced | 1232 | 1876 |\n158\t| /capabilities/recall/ | capability | enforced | 1207 | 1700 |\n159\t| /capabilities/integrate/ | capability | enforced | 1190 | 2207 |\n160\t| /capabilities/persist/ | capability | enforced | 1187 | 1803 |\n161\t| /spec/conformance/ | prose | report | 1168 | 1985 |\n162\t| /capabilities/receive/ | capability | enforced | 1149 | 1882 |\n163\t| /community/roadmap/ | prose | report | 1147 | 1529 |\n164\t| /workflows/rag-pipeline/ | workflow | enforced | 1145 | 1250 |\n165\t| /capabilities/inquire/ | capability | enforced | 1140 | 1598 |\n166\t| /capabilities/transform/ | capability | enforced | 1127 | 1814 |\n167\t| /layers/coordinate/ | layer | enforced | 1121 | 1258 |\n168\t| /layers/perceive/ | layer | enforced | 1121 | 1230 |\n169\t| /layers/reason/ | layer | enforced | 1121 | 1230 |\n170\t| /guides/skill-authoring/ | prose | report | 1114 | 1787 |\n171\t| /domains/vision/ | domain | enforced | 1103 | 1731 |\n172\t| /workflows/patient-monitoring/ | workflow | enforced | 1092 | 1719 |\n173\t| /capabilities/transition/ | capability | enforced | 1091 | 1532 |\n174\t| /workflows/handoff-preparation/ | workflow | enforced | 1090 | 1535 |\n175\t| /workflows/world-model-build/ | workflow | enforced | 1082 | 1747 |\n176\t| /capabilities/plan/ | capability | enforced | 1080 | 1830 |\n177\t| /capabilities/retrieve/ | capability | enforced | 1077 | 1673 |\n178\t| /domains/audio/ | domain | enforced | 1075 | 1759 |\n179\t| /capabilities/constrain/ | capability | enforced | 1063 | 1630 |\n180\t| /capabilities/simulate/ | capability | enforced | 1063 | 1303 |\n181\t| /capabilities/state/ | capability | enforced | 1058 | 1629 |\n182\t| /workflows/schedule-management/ | workflow | enforced | 1055 | 1633 |\n183\t| /workflows/information-research/ | workflow | enforced | 1053 | 1575 |\n184\t| /workflows/data-pipeline-validation/ | workflow | enforced | 1048 | 1495 |\n185\t| /workflows/model-monitoring/ | workflow | enforced | 1042 | 1586 |\n186\t| /capabilities/critique/ | capability | enforced | 1036 | 1899 |\n187\t| /workflows/clinical-alert-triage/ | workflow | enforced | 1029 | 1453 |\n188\t| /workflows/care-plan-review/ | workflow | enforced | 1024 | 1469 |\n189\t| /capabilities/generate/ | capability | enforced | 1008 | 1770 |\n190\t| /capabilities/explain/ | capability | enforced | 1005 | 1589 |\n191\t| /workflows/anomaly-investigation/ | workflow | enforced | 1005 | 1427 |\n192\t| /workflows/model-deployment/ | workflow | enforced | 991 | 1565 |\n193\t| /capabilities/send/ | capability | enforced | 982 | 1914 |\n194\t| /workflows/report-generation/ | workflow | enforced | 981 | 1456 |\n195\t| /capabilities/execute/ | capability | enforced | 976 | 1361 |\n196\t| /capabilities/delegate/ | capability | enforced | 969 | 1730 |\n197\t| /capabilities/compare/ | capability | enforced | 968 | 1658 |\n198\t| /capabilities/discover/ | capability | enforced | 960 | 1669 |\n199\t| /layers/execute/ | layer | enforced | 959 | 1221 |\n200\t| /layers/synthesize/ | layer | enforced | 959 | 1040 |\n201\t| /capabilities/mutate/ | capability | enforced | 951 | 1314 |\n202\t| /capabilities/decompose/ | capability | enforced | 938 | 1533 |\n203\t| /capabilities/attribute/ | capability | enforced | 934 | 1564 |\n204\t| /capabilities/classify/ | capability | enforced | 934 | 1378 |\n205\t| /capabilities/measure/ | capability | enforced | 934 | 1400 |\n206\t| /capabilities/predict/ | capability | enforced | 934 | 1403 |\n207\t| /compliance/iso-42001/ | prose | report | 918 | 1738 |\n208\t| /domains/manufacturing/ | domain | enforced | 918 | 1484 |\n209\t| /workflows/debug-code-change/ | workflow | enforced | 909 | 1399 |\n210\t| /capabilities/checkpoint/ | capability | enforced | 906 | 1403 |\n211\t| /capabilities/detect/ | capability | enforced | 906 | 1340 |\n212\t| /capabilities/ground/ | capability | enforced | 906 | 1378 |\n213\t| /community/ | listing | enforced | 905 | 1327 |\n214\t| /workflows/data-quality-pipeline/ | workflow | enforced | 900 | 1348 |\n215\t| /workflows/supply-chain-sync/ | workflow | enforced | 885 | 1452 |\n216\t| /capabilities/observe/ | capability | enforced | 865 | 1312 |\n217\t| /workflows/security-assessment/ | workflow | enforced | 852 | 1303 |\n218\t| /workflows/multi-agent-orchestration/ | workflow | enforced | 828 | 1252 |\n219\t| /workflows/communication-drafting/ | workflow | enforced | 819 | 1285 |\n220\t| /layers/remember/ | layer | enforced | 797 | 903 |\n221\t| /workflows/clarify-intent/ | workflow | enforced | 772 | 1104 |\n222\t| /workflows/predictive-maintenance/ | workflow | enforced | 771 | 1214 |\n223\t| /spec/schemas/ | schemas | report | 757 | 961 |\n224\t| /workflows/monitor-and-replan/ | workflow | enforced | 740 | 1138 |\n225\t| /workflows/quality-control-loop/ | workflow | enforced | 729 | 1116 |\n226\t| /workflows/task-delegation/ | workflow | enforced | 716 | 1020 |\n227\t| /workflows/capability-gap-analysis/ | workflow | enforced | 700 | 1035 |\n228\t| /spec/conformance/contributed-fixtures/ | prose | report | 696 | 1481 |\n229\t| /workflows/digital-twin-bootstrap/ | workflow | enforced | 648 | 699 |\n230\t| /start/ | listing | enforced | 640 | 1072 |\n231\t| /rfcs/ | rfcs-index | enforced | 461 | 415 |\n232\t| /community/citation/ | citation | report | 0 | 0 |\n233\t| /rfcs/0001/ | rfc | report | 0 | 0 |\n234\t| /rfcs/0002/ | rfc | report | 0 | 0 |\n235\t| /rfcs/0003/ | rfc | report | 0 | 0 |\n236\t| /rfcs/0004/ | rfc | report | 0 | 0 |\n237\t\n238\tThe citation page and the RFC bodies show 0 because their whole body is exempt. The table is also saved at REDACTED.md.\n239\t\n240\t## Still open from the builders' reports\n241\tThese items still need a decision; I did not change any of them.\n242\t- **Prose-b's five pair-style diagrams:** keep or cut. They are the ISO treatment options and residual risk, the EU framework-to-EU risk tiers, the press-kit failures, and the whitepaper fixture kinds.\n243\t- **Skill template page:** left without diagrams, at 5,276px. A diagram there would be copied into every new skill.\n244\t- **`benchmarks/README.md`:** left unedited, at 3,665px.\n245\t- **Identity-resolution figure:** it is 52px tall, below the 64px a figure needs to count toward runs.\n246\t- **Audit notes:**\n247\t  - At 360px, the workflow spine cuts capability names off slightly earlier than before.\n248\t  - The /spec/ figure does not name the six untested codes; the Conformance page lists them.\n249\t===== review\n250\t# Visual review of feature/issue-125-site-visuals at 6e33b5a\n251\t\n252\tI built and checked the pushed head, 6e33b5a, which is local HEAD and matches `git ls-remote`. Commit 045c0cc, named in the task, is not in this worktree, so this review does not cover it. I did not edit any repository file.\n253\t\n254\t## Check results at 6e33b5a\n255\t- `npm ci` and `npm run check`: 0 errors, 0 warnings. Contrast: 412 pairs pass. Design-data check passes.\n256\t- `npm test`: 36 files, 834 tests pass.\n257\t- `npm run build`: passes, with every check-dist check: 168 pages and 27,270 internal links.\n258\t- `npm run check:axe`: 168 pages and 672 runs with no violations and no sideways scroll at 360px. No enforced page has a run over 1,800px.\n259\t\n260\t## How I looked\n261\tI served a copy of `dist` on 127.0.0.1 and took shots of the 16 required pages at 1440 light, 1440 dark and 360 light, with reduced motion. The compliance document was the ISO internal audit checklist and the composed-skill guide was digital-twin-sync-loop. For each page I took a full-page shot, page slices and one shot per figure. I opened every full-page shot, as a contact sheet. I also opened about 45 slices and figure shots in detail, mostly 1440 light, plus the 360 shots of the diagnostics, background, workflow and spec pages and dark shots of the workflow and domain pages.\n262\t\n263\tA script measured each figure for sideways overflow, internal scrollers and text under 12px. It is a proxy, and the findings below come from the opened images unless I say otherwise.\n264\t\n265\tThree capture artifacts are not page bugs:\n266\t- Full-page shots of pages taller than 16,384px repeat from the top. Chromium does this. The slices are clean.\n267\t- Some per-figure shots show the sticky header across them.\n268\t- A figure taller than the window is cut off in its own shot.\n269\t\n270\t## Figures compared with Markdown-copy figure blocks\n271\tOn every page I counted, the number of figures in the HTML equals the number of figure blocks in the page's Markdown copy:\n272\t\n273\t| Page | Figures |\n274\t|---|---:|\n275\t| rollback | 8 |\n276\t| audit | 9 |\n277\t| /layers/remember/ | 3 |\n278\t| /spec/1.0.0/ | 12 |\n279\t| /spec/diagnostics/ | 7 |\n280\t| /spec/, /start/, /background/ | 1 each |\n281\t| workflow digital-twin-sync-loop | 3 |\n282\t| /domains/multimodal/ | 13 |\n283\t| glossary | 15 |\n284\t| FAQ | 14 |\n285\t| ISO internal audit checklist | 7 |\n286\t| skill digital-twin-sync-loop | 4 |\n287\t| release notes | 18 |\n288\t\n289\tOn the Mermaid pages the number of `mermaid` fences in the copy also equals the figure count.\n290\t\n291\t## P1: wrong or broken\n292\t\n293\t**1. The /spec/1.0.0/ step figure says \"A step has 3 fields, 3 required.\"**\n294\t- Screenshot: `REDACTED.png`\n295\t- Cause: §5.2 of STANDARD-v1.0.0 has two tables, 3 required fields and 14 optional fields (\"Each step MAY define\"). The figure reads only the first table. The Markdown copy says the same thing.\n296\t- The /spec/1.1.0/ figure gets this right: \"A step has 26 fields in 5 groups; 3 are required\".\n297\t- Change: read both §5.2 tables, so the figure shows 17 fields with 3 required, or retitle it \"Required step fields\".\n298\t\n299\t**2. The composition-pattern figure on capability pages drops capabilities listed after a slash.**\n300\t- Screenshot: `REDACTED.png`\n301\t- Rollback's SKILL.md lists `` `mutate` / `execute` `` under \"Commonly follows\". The figure shows mutate only and says \"The skill lists 6 capabilities\"; the list names 7.\n302\t- The same happens on audit (`` `execute` / `mutate` ``, so mutate is dropped; fig 9) and on verify (`` `execute` / `mutate` ``).\n303\t- Cause: in `site/src/lib/capability-figures.ts`, the parser takes only the first backticked id of each list item.\n304\t- Change: take every backticked capability id in the item. The captions will then read 7 for rollback.\n305\t\n306\t## P2: clearly worse than it should be\n307\t\n308\t**3. Five /spec/1.0.0/ figures repeat the table directly below them.**\n309\t- The figures: §4.1 capability fields, §5.1 workflow fields, §5.2 step fields, §6.2 event fields and §6.3 world-state fields.\n310\t- Each one is the field and type list from the table that follows it, without the descriptions. They add nothing to the table and appear to exist to break up long runs.\n311\t- Screenshots:\n312\t  - `REDACTED.png`\n313\t  - `REDACTED.png`\n314\t- The §10 conformance figure (fig 8) also repeats the §10.2 bullet lists word for word, and its title cites §10.1 although it draws §10.2: `REDACTED.png`\n315\t- Change: replace these with figures that add something, as 1.1.0 does (the step anatomy groups and the safety defaults). Otherwise, show the tables as figures instead of drawing the same data twice.\n316\t\n317\t**4. At 360px, matrix figures show about a third of their columns, and the hidden part looks empty.**\n318\t- **Diagnostics §5 matrices**: about 7 of 13 columns show, and column headers are cut mid-label (\"5.\"). Screenshots:\n319\t  - `REDACTED.png`\n320\t  - `REDACTED.png`\n321\t- **Background layer heat map**: 3 of 9 layers show. Screenshot: `REDACTED.png`\n322\t- **Workflow data-flow matrix**: 7 of 21 columns show, so rows 11 to 21 look empty. Screenshot: `REDACTED.png`\n323\t- Cause: each matrix is inside a scrolling table container that is 308px wide while the table is 483 to 667px wide. There is no visible sign that it scrolls.\n324\t- Change: below about 480px, switch to a per-row list (code, then section chips; or step, then the steps it reads), or shrink the cells to fit 308px. At the least, add a visible scroll cue.\n325\t\n326\t**5. The \"used in workflows\" step strips on capability pages have no key.**\n327\t- Screenshot: `REDACTED.png`\n328\t- The black squares with a check, flag or pencil and the underline gate marks are not explained. The caption covers only the page's own symbol.\n329\t- Most squares are empty: on the home gallery a plain step shows its capability's two-letter symbol, but on capability pages it does not.\n330\t- The digital_twin_sync_loop strip wraps onto a second line while the others do not, so the rows look uneven.\n331\t- Change: add the role and gate key used on workflow pages, show the two-letter symbols as the home gallery does, and stop the strip wrapping (scale it, or move the step label onto its own line).\n332\t\n333\t**6. The examples figure on capability pages says nothing when every example has every field.**\n334\t- On rollback, the two examples show the same 11 green chips. Screenshot: `REDACTED.png`\n335\t- On audit, the same happens.\n336\t- Change: when every example has every field, state that in one sentence and drop the drawing. Draw the figure only when the examples differ, as on synchronize, where sender and sender_identity are absent.\n337\t\n338\t**7. The audit procedure figure says 4 output fields are \"used by no step\", although step titles name them.**\n339\t- Example: step 3 is titled \"Extract decision rationale\", yet the figure lists `decision_rationale` as unused.\n340\t- Screenshot: `REDACTED.png`\n341\t- The maintainer decided to keep the word-match figure, so the figure stays. The fix is to the matching inside it.\n342\t- Change: treat `_` and a space as the same when matching field names, so \"decision rationale\" matches `decision_rationale`.\n343\t\n344\t**8. At 360px, the workflow step map has text below 12px and cuts step names.**\n345\t- The context_gathering chips are 10.8px, which the script measured.\n346\t- Step names are cut: \"transiti…\".\n347\t- Screenshot: `REDACTED.png`\n348\t- This is the audit note \"the spine cuts names earlier\"; I confirmed it is a real problem.\n349\t- Change: keep the chips at 12px or more, and let the name column take the space the purpose column frees up at narrow widths.\n350\t\n351\t**9. The composed-skill guide's longest run is still an open YAML block, about 9,174px at 1440.**\n352\t- Screenshot: `REDACTED.png`\n353\t- It is the longest run on the site, made of code rather than prose.\n354\t- Change: collapse the output-contract and example YAML, as the capability pages do with examples (\"The output as the skill writes it, in YAML\").\n355\t\n356\t## P3: polish\n357\t\n358\t- **Relationship figure on capability pages** (`REDACTED.png`): the tree uses only the left third of a 632px-tall panel. A two-column layout (in and out on either side of the capability) would halve its height.\n359\t- **Layer page edge figure** (`REDACTED.png`):\n360\t  - Every bar is full width with a count of 1, so the bars carry no information. Hide the bars when every count is equal.\n361\t  - The symmetric VERIFY conflicts_with edge is listed under both \"Into\" and \"Out of\", while capability pages use \"Either way\". Use the same grouping on both.\n362\t- **Layer workflow-share figure**: \"1 of the 277 steps … (0%)\" should print \"<1%\".\n363\t- **/spec/ and /background/ cards** (`REDACTED.png`, `REDACTED.png`):\n364\t  - The Diagnostics and Schemas cards have no description.\n365\t  - The Standard excerpts stop at \"…; A…\".\n366\t  - The Skills alignment card stops at \"we find:\".\n367\t- **/spec/ figure**: it does not name the six codes the suite does not expect (the audit note). Naming them would make it more useful.\n368\t- **Background heat map**: counting how often each page names a capability as code describes the pages' formatting more than their content, and the Benchmarks row is all zeros.\n369\t- **Reading-time figure on /start/**: correct (7+4+6+9+10 = 36 min) but low in value. It is acceptable on an index page.\n370\t- **Mermaid figures, in general**: the ones on glossary, ISO and release notes are mostly monochrome boxes in a vertical chain. Some say only one sentence: release notes fig 17 (\"99 capabilities → 36\") and fig 18 (the skills path). Nodes that are capabilities do carry their layer colour and symbol (FAQ fig 2, skill fig 4), and those are the strongest.\n371\t- **Mermaid edge routing**: in FAQ fig 2, edges from coordinate and compress run side by side and meet at integrate, which makes them hard to trace. Screenshot: `REDACTED.png`\n372\t- **Diagnostics matrix column headers at 1440**: \"5.10\" and \"5.11\" have almost no gap between them.\n373\t- **Spec 1.0.0 conformance boxes**: the L1 and L2 boxes start about 4px apart vertically.\n374\t- **Domain proposed-workflow figures**: figs 10 to 13 put a one-row strip in a large dashed panel. Two per row, or a tighter panel, would cut empty space.\n375\t\n376\t## What looks good\n377\tThese figures draw from the page's data, agree with their sources where I checked them, and read well in both themes:\n378\t- the workflow step map at 1440 (`REDACTED.png`, and the dark shot `REDACTED.png`);\n379\t- the diagnostics family tiles;\n380\t- the spec 1.0.0 requirements-by-chapter bars (their totals are 40 MUST, 8 SHOULD and 1 MAY);\n381\t- the decision tree;\n382\t- the domain risk, checkpoint and evidence figures (`REDACTED.png`);\n383\t- the skill guide's branching flow (`REDACTED.png`).\n384\t\n385\tThe data checks I made by hand: the rollback edges against the ontology, the parallel group in digital_twin_sync_loop (one step, as drawn), the uses of persist and recall in the catalogs, and FAQ fig 2 against FAQ.md.\n386\t\n387\t## Files\n388\tAll screenshots are in `REDACTED`, in the `full/`, `tiles/` and `figs/` folders. The per-figure measurements are in `report.json` and `issues.txt` there. The build log is `REDACTED.log` and the axe log is `REDACTED.log`. The review server is stopped.\n389\t===== fixed\n390\tI fixed every P1 and P2 finding and all but two P3 items, which I left with reasons. The branch is pushed at **7709d36**, and local HEAD matches `git ls-remote`. All four checks pass at that commit.\n391\t\n392\t**Branch state.** The pushed head before my work was 6e33b5a. Commit 045c0cc, which the task named, is an ancestor of 6e33b5a, so it was already included. I pushed normally, with no force, as the closing step asked; that overrides the opening line that said not to push. There are 17 new commits, 01f246a through 7709d36. I made no change to the run-length exemptions.\n393\t\n394\t## Findings and what was done\n395\t**P1**\n396\t1. **/spec/1.0.0/ step figure:** the drawn field list is gone. §5.2's first table is now itself the figure, titled \"Required step fields\". Its caption reads both tables: \"A step must define 3 fields; the second table of §5.2 lists 14 more that a step may define, 17 fields in all.\"\n397\t2. **Composition figure dropped capabilities after a slash:** the parser now takes every capability in an item's opening run (`` `mutate` / `execute` ``). It does not pick up ids from the description, such as plan's \"(`plan` precedes both)\". Rollback now reads 7, and audit and verify get mutate back.\n398\t\n399\t**P2**\n400\t3. **1.0.0 figures that repeated their tables:** the §4.1, §5.1, §5.2, §6.2 and §6.3 tables are now the figures, so nothing is drawn twice. The 1.0.0 conformance figure is now the §10.1 table, with a caption that counts the §10.2 requirements per level. On 1.1.0 the conformance figure moved under §10.2, so its title now cites the section it draws. The same repeat existed on 1.1.0's §4.1 and §6.3, so those tables are figures too.\n401\t4. **Matrices at 360px:** below 480px, the diagnostics matrices, the background heat map and the workflow data-flow grid each show one line per row. Each line lists the cells that row has, named by column. This is CSS only, with no second copy of the table.\n402\t5. **Workflow strips on capability pages:**\n403\t   - Plain steps show their two-letter symbol, and the page's own capability is drawn with an ink ring.\n404\t   - A key names every tile the strips use: the role tiles in the workflow page's wording, and the gate bar.\n405\t   - The workflow name and step numbers sit on one line and the strip on the next, so the strip no longer wraps at 1440.\n406\t6. **Examples figure:** when every example writes out the same fields, one sentence says so and nothing is drawn. Synchronize falls under this rule too: both of its examples leave out the same two fields, so they do not differ.\n407\t   - This removed the figure from 33 pages and pushed recall and transform over the run limit.\n408\t   - To fix that, the chip figure for the output contract is gone (it listed the same field names as the Field Definitions table under it). That table now has an \"In the output contract\" column: required, optional, or the skill's own.\n409\t   - The sentence above the table names the fields the contract requires and any contract field the skill leaves out.\n410\t7. **Audit word match:** a space now counts as an underscore, case-insensitively, so \"Extract decision rationale\" matches `decision_rationale`. This changed the procedure and verification captions on most capability pages; I read the before-and-after list and the new matches look right.\n411\t8. **Step map at 360px:** step names are 13px and take the space the purpose column frees, and the parallel-group ids stay at 12px. A check across all 30 workflow pages found no names cut and no text under 12px.\n412\t9. **Composed-skill guides:** the output YAML and each example fold under a summary, as on capability pages. The digital-twin-sync-loop guide's longest run went from 9,174px to 2,718px.\n413\t\n414\t**P3**\n415\t- **Relationship figure:** two columns at 640px and wider, about half the height; narrow screens keep the single stack.\n416\t- **Layer edge figure:**\n417\t  - Symmetric edges go in an \"Either way\" row, so REMEMBER shows VERIFY once.\n418\t  - When every row has the same count, the figure prints the count and draws no bars.\n419\t  - The caption leaves out directions with no edges.\n420\t- **Layer step share:** prints \"<1%\".\n421\t- **Cards:**\n422\t  - Diagnostics, Schemas and also Cite this standard now have descriptions.\n423\t  - A description built from a list now ends after its last whole item.\n424\t  - Skills alignment now uses its Purpose line.\n425\t- **/spec/ figure:** the caption names the six codes no fixture expects: V103, S301, S302, F505, W607 and W612.\n426\t- **Background heat map:** Benchmarks, which names no capability as code, no longer has an empty row; the caption names it. I kept counting code-formatted names because a plain word such as \"plan\" may not mean the capability.\n427\t- **Mermaid:**\n428\t  - Release notes figures 17 and 18 are removed. That page now has a 4,595px run; it is report-only and the checks pass.\n429\t  - In left-to-right diagrams, a box with three or more edges on one side is at least 16px tall per edge, so FAQ figure 2's edges now leave its boxes apart.\n430\t- **Diagnostics matrix headers** have a gap between them.\n431\t- **Conformance boxes** now start level with each other.\n432\t- **Proposed-workflow cards:** the duplicate workflow id is gone. I tried putting the badge and tiles on one row, but that made the drawing shorter than 64px, so the run check stopped counting it and three domain pages failed. That change is reverted.\n433\t- **Not changed:**\n434\t  - The reading-time figure: the review rated it acceptable.\n435\t  - The general \"monochrome Mermaid boxes\" point: only boxes that are capabilities have a layer to colour them by, so other boxes have no colour that comes from the data.\n436\t\n437\t## Check results at 7709d36\n438\t- **`npm run check`:** 0 errors, 0 warnings; contrast check passes on 412 colour pairs; design-data check passes.\n439\t- **`npm test`:** 36 files, 846 tests pass.\n440\t- **`npm run build`:** passes, with 168 pages and 27,261 internal links checked.\n441\t- **`npm run check:axe`:** 168 pages in 672 runs, no violations and no sideways scroll at 360px. No enforced page has a run over 1,800px.\n442\t\n443\t## Longest runs and screenshots\n444\tThe longest run at 1440 and 360 for all 168 pages is in `REDACTED.md` (columns: page, template, enforced or report, 1440px, 360px). The raw output is `REDACTED.txt`. The highest enforced runs at 1440 are:\n445\t\n446\t| Page | 1440px | 360px |\n447\t|---|---:|---:|\n448\t| /capabilities/synchronize/ | 1,724 | 2,685 |\n449\t| /capabilities/audit/ | 1,717 | 3,237 |\n450\t| /capabilities/invoke/ | 1,685 | 2,904 |\n451\t| /workflows/digital-twin-sync-loop/ | 1,678 | 2,908 |\n452\t| /spec/1.1.0/ | 1,653 | 3,278 |\n453\t\n454\tThe final screenshots are in `REDACTED`. There are 23 targets, each as `<name>-1440-light.png`, `<name>-1440-dark.png` and `<name>-360-light.png`, plus a `sheet-<name>.png` with the three side by side; I opened every sheet.\n455\t- The targets cover rollback, audit, both Standard versions, the diagnostics page, /spec/, /background/, the workflow and composed-skill guide, the REMEMBER layer, the multimodal domain, FAQ, release notes, glossary, the ISO internal audit checklist and the citation card.\n456\t- `background-heat-1440-light-clip.png` re-checks the heat map at 1440: the per-element shot cut off its caption, and the clip shows the page itself is fine.\n457\t- Opening the sheets turned up one more bug: at 360px the table figures split field names mid-word (\"capa/bili/ty\"). Commit 7709d36 fixes it, and I re-took and re-opened those two sheets.\n458\t\n459\tOne thing is left as it was: at 360px the skill Field Definitions table, including its new contract column, scrolls sideways inside its frame, as other tables on the site do.\n460\t===== audit\n461\tFixes 1 to 3 are built and committed. Fix 4 needed no change: the deploy job already removes the review sheet before publishing. All four checks pass at head 30c1a14.\n462\t\n463\t**Worktree:** /Users/danielbentes/agent-capability-standard/.claude/worktrees/i125s-audit, branch `feature/issue-125-s-audit`, four commits on 045c0cc. Nothing is pushed.\n464\t\n465\t**Commits:**\n466\t- 34966b4 fix(site): every numbered figure has a figure block in the page's Markdown copy\n467\t- 1fad9e4 fix(site): the workflow key tells a step's rollback from a gate's and a failure's\n468\t- 288cc19 fix(site): the Specification and Get started indexes show their own data\n469\t- 30c1a14 fix(site): equal bar tracks, the failure cross at 360, link-aware reading times\n470\t\n471\t**1. Figure blocks in the Markdown copies**\n472\t- A new sitewide check in `site/scripts/check-dist.mjs` runs on every build. For each page it takes every figure with a \"Fig n\" eyebrow and its name, and matches it against the \"**Figure: {title}.**\" blocks in the page's Markdown copy, in both directions. Blocks inside list items count; text inside code fences does not.\n473\t- On 045c0cc it found 58 figures with no block and one block with no figure. They were on 9 compliance pages, 4 methodology and research pages, 4 domain pages, the edge types page, the overview, the SDK guide and the workflow patterns page.\n474\t- How each page type was fixed:\n475\t  - **Prose, RFC and skill pages** (new file `site/src/twins/prose-blocks.ts`): the copy puts a block directly before each fence the page draws. That covers box diagrams, directory trees and pattern chains. The fence follows the block, and a chain's block also lists its steps in order. Fences are picked by the same tests the drawing step uses, and the overview's folded box is skipped because it has no number.\n476\t  - **Domain pages:** each workflow card now has a \"Steps of …\" block listing its steps. The existing domain test no longer leaves the cards out; the reason is written in the test.\n477\t  - **Edge types page:** one block per figure, 15 in all, in page order. Before, one block covered all seven type cards.\n478\t- Tests in `site/test/check-dist-script.test.ts` use small hand-written pages: a missing block, a block with no figure, a box diagram named by its label, a block written inside a fence, and a figure whose label is not a number.\n479\t\n480\t**2. The workflow figure key**\n481\t- Every workflow page's key has the same layout. Three workflow pages listed one glyph with two meanings:\n482\t  - model-deployment and debug-code-change: \"step rolls back\" and \"on failure, roll back\" both used the undo glyph;\n483\t  - digital-twin-sync-loop: that pair, and also \"gate stops the run\" and \"on failure, stop\".\n484\t- I kept the separate meanings and made the entries look different. The failure column now starts with a cross, as the gate column starts with the diamond. In the key, each gate action is drawn after the diamond and each failure action after the cross, and the cross has its own entry.\n485\t- The cross stays visible at 360px, unlike the diamond.\n486\t- A new build check fails any legend or key (a class ending in \"legend\" or \"key\") that draws the same glyph, or glyph pair, for two entries with different words.\n487\t- A unit test builds a workflow with a rollback step and every gate and failure action; it fails without the fix.\n488\t\n489\t**3. The heat map on /start/, /spec/ and /background/**\n490\t- **/spec/: replaced.** Most cells were 0. The new figure shows, for each diagnostic family, how many of its codes the conformance suite expects: 40 of the 46 codes. The caption gives the number of fixtures and cases of each kind, 606 in all. The six codes it shows as untested (V103, S301, S302, F505, W607, W612) are the ones the Conformance page itself lists as coverage gaps, so the figure agrees with the page.\n491\t- **/start/: replaced.** The map was misleading there: it scored the Overview 0 in eight layers, although its periodic table names all 36 capabilities in a drawing. The new figure shows how long each page takes to read at 200 words a minute, with its number of code blocks; diagrams and link addresses are not counted.\n492\t- **/background/: kept.** Each paper's layers differ and the rows read true. The caption already says only names written as code are counted.\n493\t- Each bar row now reserves the same width for its text, so the bars are the same length and a share reads correctly. The release-notes bars on /community/ also changed with this.\n494\t- The run-length check still passes.\n495\t\n496\t**4. Glyph review sheet: confirmed, no workflow change**\n497\t- `site.yml` is the only workflow that deploys. Its deploy job removes `dist/_review` before `pages deploy dist`, and an existing test checks that order.\n498\t- The search index and the sitemap list the same 168 pages, with no review page.\n499\t- I added a check that fails if any built file outside `dist/_review` links to it; it passes.\n500\t\n501\t**Check results at 30c1a14:**\n502\t- `npm run check`: passes.\n503\t- `npm test`: 36 files, 788 tests pass.\n504\t- `npm run build`: passes, including the figures, legends and review checks.\n505\t- `npm run check:axe`: 168 pages, 672 runs, no violations and no sideways scroll at 360px. The run-length check finds no enforced page with a run over 1800px.\n506\t\n507\t**Screenshots I opened** (all under `REDACTED`):\n508\t- Before: `before-spine-1440-light.png`, `before-spec-index-1440-light.png`, `before-start-1440-light.png`, `before-background-1440-light.png`.\n509\t- After commit 2: `spine-model-deployment-1440-light.png`, `spine-model-deployment-360-light.png`, `spine-digital-twin-1440-dark.png`.\n510\t- After commit 3: `spec-index-1440-light.png`, `spec-index-1440-dark.png`, `spec-index-360-light.png`, `start-index-360-light.png`.\n511\t- Final: `r2-spine-digital-twin-360-light.png`, `r2-spec-index-1440-light.png`, `r2-start-index-1440-dark.png`, `r2-community-360-light.png`.\n512\t- I also read the edge types copy's new section and the healthcare domain copy.\n513\t\n514\t**Not finished, or open:**\n515\t- At 360px the spine's capability names cut off a little earlier (\"transiti…\", \"checkpoi…\"). The failure column is 16px wider so the cross stays visible.\n516\t- A box diagram's copy uses one fixed caption sentence, because the page shows these diagrams with a name but no caption.\n517\t- The /spec/ figure does not name the six untested codes. The Conformance page lists them.\n518\t- Screenshots I did not open: `r2-start-index-1440-light.png`, `start-index-1440-light.png` and `start-index-1440-dark.png`, the background screenshots taken after the change (the background figure did not change), and the r2 spine and spec shots other than the ones listed above.\n519\t"}]}}
