{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"ef9f3fc8-12b6-4fe4-9f49-aaeedec05648","hash":"4c82d933d1f4dafcab294724c50b42f9f9fe9685ce486a0eb2e787bb756b3cb3","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01F8Urb2GJTKQbuvt9KxqhUB","name":"AskUserQuestion","input":{"questions":[{"question":"On the reference files: you're right that agents read them only when needed. 22 skills link to the same two files, which were identical copies of templates/composition_patterns.md and verification_patterns.md. When an agent does open one, the diagrams add 51 or 85 lines that repeat the text around them. On the site, the human-facing copies are the templates/ files, shown under Skill authoring; the per-skill copies are not shown. Where should the diagrams stay?","header":"References","multiSelect":false,"options":[{"label":"Templates only (Recommended)","description":"Keep the diagrams in templates/, which readers see on the site and GitHub. Remove them from the 22 skills/*/reference/ copies, so agents load the same text as before. The copies will then differ from the templates by the diagram blocks only."},{"label":"Keep everywhere","description":"Copies stay identical to the templates. An agent that opens a reference file reads the diagrams too."},{"label":"Remove everywhere","description":"No diagrams in templates/ or the copies. The site's skill authoring pages lose those figures and get longer text stretches."}]}]},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"ef9f3fc8-12b6-4fe4-9f49-aaeedec05648","hash":"f46d931a3c793b75e81a44ef5f3cec67fd36828474ef3badba34cb7b8bfb5c09","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","content":"Your questions have been answered: \"On the reference files: you're right that agents read them only when needed. 22 skills link to the same two files, which were identical copies of templates/composition_patterns.md and verification_patterns.md. When an agent does open one, the diagrams add 51 or 85 lines that repeat the text around them. On the site, the human-facing copies are the templates/ files, shown under Skill authoring; the per-skill copies are not shown. Where should the diagrams stay?\"=\"Templates only (Recommended)\". You can now continue with these answers in mind.","tool_use_id":"toolu_01F8Urb2GJTKQbuvt9KxqhUB"}]}}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"ef9f3fc8-12b6-4fe4-9f49-aaeedec05648","hash":"469a3978c076eeb83e11c2ca9c9e532c0f2fc503fb63523b6719328e80164e93","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm removing diagrams from the skill files, changelog and reference copies while keeping them in templates/, and I'm building the six Standard figures to spec. I'll check each new figure against its text, starting with the first, and I'll ask whether you also want the perspective-validation checklist diagrams removed.\n\n","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017KAKGQgtg7wuirNAxWKmkR","name":"Workflow","input":{"script":"export const meta = {\n  name: 'site-visual-round4',\n  description: 'Issue #125 round 4: maintainer decisions, diagram accuracy pass, spec figures, page checks; integrate, review, fix',\n  phases: [{ title: 'Build' }, { title: 'Integrate' }, { title: 'Review' }, { title: 'Fix' }],\n}\nconst SP = 'REDACTED'\nconst WT = '/Users/danielbentes/agent-capability-standard/.claude/worktrees/wf_08f3cd25-fc3-8'\nconst COMMON = `Repository synaptiai/agent-capability-standard. Integration worktree ${WT}, branch feature/issue-125-site-visuals, head fb091cb (pushed).\nRead first: ${SP}/rollout-brief.md (rules, tools), ${SP}/visual-build-brief.md (hard rules, commit format: write the message to a file and use git commit -F, end with \"Refs #125\" and the Co-Authored-By / Claude-Session trailers given there; never force-push; no GitHub posts; no PRs; no merge to main; nothing copied from synapti.ai), ${SP}/visual-spec.md (the design spec and its amendments section).\nMaintainer decisions so far (2026-11-12), all final:\n- Keep: the skills/mutate/SKILL.md edit; one icon per concept; the rollback / SDK-guide / overview run exemptions; the word-match procedure figure.\n- NEW: no Mermaid diagrams in any skills/*/SKILL.md (they cost agents context) and none in skills/*/reference/ copies; diagrams stay in templates/ (shown on the site). skills/perspective-validation/CHECKLIST.md keeps its diagrams. No diagrams in CHANGELOG.md (its sections become GitHub release notes).\n- NEW: the first capability example and the first workflow step card start open, as spec 3.1 says.\n- NEW: build to the spec: the Standard figures F-S14, F-S24b, F-S27, F-S28, F-S1 and F-S6 as specified; a status glyph for every status in use, with the draft glyphs finished.\nDiagrams in source Markdown: each says only what its adjacent text says, with an accDescr: line; never in spec/STANDARD-v*.md.\nRun npm run check, npm test, npm run build and npm run check:axe (site/) and pytest tests -q plus python tools/validate_doc_links.py from the repo root before you report; all must pass. OPEN (Read) every screenshot you cite.`\n\nconst W = (name) => `Work in a new worktree: git -C ${WT} worktree add ${WT}/../i125t-${name} -b feature/issue-125-t-${name} HEAD. Commit there in small commits; do not push. Save screenshots under ${SP}/visual/round4/${name}/.`\n\nconst BUILDERS = [\n  { name: 'agentfiles', task: `1. Remove every mermaid block (and only those) from skills/*/SKILL.md, from skills/*/reference/*.md, and from CHANGELOG.md. For the reference copies, each must again equal its templates/ source minus the diagram blocks; check with a diff. Keep the diagrams in templates/ and in skills/perspective-validation/CHECKLIST.md.\n2. The composed-skill guide pages (/guides/skills/*) and the release-notes page lose figures as a result. Give each composed-skill guide page figures the site draws from data instead (e.g. the catalog workflow the skill runs, drawn with the existing step-map parts; its inputs/outputs from its contract), with a block in the Markdown copy. Do not exempt new runs.\n3. Stale text found earlier: docs/FAQ.md says \"35 is fixed forever\", docs/methodology/WORKFLOW_COVERAGE.md says \"35/35\", docs/GLOSSARY.md's Layer bullet omits inquire. Check each against the ontology (36 capabilities) and the document's own context (a historical analysis may legitimately quote an old count; then leave it and say why). Fix those that are wrong.\n4. benchmarks/README.md (/background/research/benchmarks/, 3,665px run) had no owner: add diagrams where its text describes a structure, flow or sequence.\nReport each changed page's longest run before and after.` },\n  { name: 'verify-a', task: `Accuracy pass on Mermaid diagrams, files: everything under docs/compliance/, spec/SECURITY.md, spec/CONFORMANCE.md, spec/*.md other than STANDARD-v*, spec/RFC-*.md, docs/proposals/*.md. For EVERY mermaid block: read the adjacent text and try to refute the diagram. Check that (a) every node and every edge is stated in the adjacent text; (b) each edge points the way the text says (source -> target, including ontology edge semantics: for requires/precedes the source runs first); (c) an unordered list is never drawn as a chain, and branches/decisions match the text's conditions; (d) labels quote the text, no added claims; (e) accDescr matches the drawing. Fix every wrong diagram in place (or delete it if the text does not support a diagram). Report a table: file, diagram title, verdict (ok / fixed / deleted), and the reason for every non-ok one.` },\n  { name: 'verify-b', task: `Accuracy pass on Mermaid diagrams, files: docs/GLOSSARY.md, docs/FAQ.md, docs/QUICKSTART.md, docs/TUTORIAL.md, everything under docs/research/ and docs/methodology/, benchmarks/README.md only after the agentfiles builder (skip it here). Same procedure as below. For EVERY mermaid block: read the adjacent text and try to refute the diagram. Check that (a) every node and every edge is stated in the adjacent text; (b) each edge points the way the text says (including ontology edge semantics: for requires/precedes the source runs first); (c) an unordered list is never drawn as a chain, and branches match the text's conditions; (d) labels quote the text, no added claims; (e) accDescr matches the drawing. Fix every wrong diagram in place, or delete it if the text does not support one. Report a table: file, diagram title, verdict (ok / fixed / deleted), reason for every non-ok one.` },\n  { name: 'verify-c', task: `Accuracy pass on Mermaid diagrams, files: docs/guides/**, templates/*.md, hooks/README.md, spec/WHITEPAPER.md, docs/GROUNDED_AGENCY.md, docs/WORKFLOW_PATTERNS.md, docs/domains/**, CONTRIBUTING.md, GOVERNANCE.md, README.md, ROADMAP files, PRESS_KIT, skills/perspective-validation/CHECKLIST.md, and any other routed .md with a mermaid block not under docs/compliance, docs/research, docs/methodology, spec/, skills/*/SKILL.md, skills/*/reference, CHANGELOG.md (list them with git grep -l '\\`\\`\\`mermaid'). For EVERY mermaid block: read the adjacent text and try to refute the diagram: (a) every node and every edge is stated in the adjacent text; (b) each edge points the way the text says (incl. ontology edge semantics: for requires/precedes the source runs first); (c) an unordered list is never drawn as a chain, branches match the text's conditions; (d) labels quote the text, no added claims; (e) accDescr matches the drawing. Fix every wrong diagram in place, or delete it if unsupported. Report a table: file, diagram title, verdict (ok / fixed / deleted), reason for every non-ok one.` },\n  { name: 'specfig', task: `1. Rebuild the Standard figures F-S14 (incl. its RunReplay), F-S24b, F-S27, F-S28, F-S1 and F-S6 exactly as visual-spec.md specifies them (read each entry; F-S6 pips use the colour the spec gives). Each keeps a block in the Markdown copy (the copy-count test must still pass) and draws only from the Standard's text/data.\n2. Status glyphs: finish the first-draft glyphs (status:draft, status:analysis, the wrench, and any other the glyph sheet marks as draft) so each reads clearly at 1x and 2x; keep the glyph distance tests passing; update spec 2.3's list in visual-spec.md's amendments section only by noting the maintainer approved a glyph for every status in use.\n3. Look at the Standard 1.1.0 and 1.0.0 pages with motion ON (no reduced motion) at 1440 and 360, including RunReplay and anything animated, and fix what is broken. Screenshots at 1440 light, 1440 dark, 360 light, opened.` },\n  { name: 'pages', task: `1. The first capability example and the first workflow step card start open (spec 3.1). Keep run-length enforcement passing without new exemptions (an open example inside a closed-by-default exempt rule may need the capability-example exemption in spec 3.12; read it and apply it as written).\n2. Tables counted as figures: list every numbered figure on enforced pages that is a plain table (no drawn marks beyond text). Add a build check that each generated page type (home, capability, layer, workflow, domain, edge types, diagnostics, every section index, the Standard) has at least one numbered figure that is drawn (SVG or pixel marks), not only tables; fix any page that fails by adding a figure drawn from its data. Report the list and what you changed.\n3. Callout glyphs (spec 3.10, Note/Warning/Important etc. callouts get their glyph) and index hero glyphs (each section index page gets its section glyph in the hero band) - build both as the spec says.\n4. Dark heat steps: the review found the first three dark heat steps hard to tell apart. Read spec 1.2 for the heat scale; if they can be spread while every pair still passes check-contrast, do it; otherwise report the numbers.\n5. Truncated step descriptions in workflow step maps at 1440 (\"…\"): find a layout that shows the whole description without breaking the 28px lane alignment (e.g. wrap with variable row height and lanes drawn per row), or report concretely why not.\n6. Look at the home page with motion ON at 360 and 1440 (scroll the story top to bottom, screenshot several frames) and fix anything broken.` },\n]\n\nphase('Build')\nconst built = await parallel(BUILDERS.map((b) => () => agent(`${COMMON}\\n\\nYou are builder \"${b.name}\". ${W(b.name)}\\n\\nTask:\\n${b.task}\\n\\nReport: worktree, branch, commits, what you did, check results with head SHA, screenshots opened, anything not done and the concrete reason.`, { label: b.name, phase: 'Build' })))\n\nphase('Integrate')\nconst integ = await agent(`${COMMON}\\n\\nYou are the integrator. Builder reports:\\n${built.map((r, i) => `--- ${BUILDERS[i].name} ---\\n${r}`).join('\\n')}\\n\\nIn ${WT} on feature/issue-125-site-visuals, merge with --no-ff in this order: feature/issue-125-t-agentfiles, -t-verify-a, -t-verify-b, -t-verify-c, -t-specfig, -t-pages. Resolve conflicts keeping both sides' intent (agentfiles' removals win over any verify-* edit to a file agentfiles removed diagrams from). Confirm with git grep that no mermaid block remains in skills/*/SKILL.md, skills/*/reference/ or CHANGELOG.md, and that each skills/*/reference copy equals its templates/ source minus diagram blocks. Run every check: npm ci, npm run check, npm test, npm run build, npm run check:axe (site/), and from the repo root pytest tests -q, python tools/validate_doc_links.py, python tools/sync_skill_schemas.py --check, python tools/validate_skill_refs.py, python tools/validate_workflows.py --strict. Fix failures. Push normally (never force); confirm local HEAD equals git ls-remote. Check on github.com (headless Chromium, adapt ${SP}/pw/gh2.mjs) that the diagrams in every source file a verify-* builder changed still render, and open at least 8 screenshots. Remove the i125t-* worktrees (keep branches). Report merges, fixes, checks with pushed SHA, GitHub render results, and the longest-run table (node site/scripts/check-runs.mjs --all).`, { label: 'integrate', phase: 'Integrate' })\n\nphase('Review')\nconst review = await agent(`${COMMON}\\n\\nYou are an independent visual and accuracy reviewer; you built none of this. Integrator's report:\\n${integ}\\n\\nBuild the pushed head in ${WT}/site, serve dist on 127.0.0.1. Screenshot at 1440 light, 1440 dark and 360 light; do one pass with reduced motion and one with motion ON for home, /spec/1.1.0/ (RunReplay) and one workflow page. OPEN every full page image yourself for: home, /capabilities/mutate/, /capabilities/rollback/, /capabilities/synchronize/, /layers/execute/, /workflows/model-deployment/, /workflows/digital-twin-sync-loop/, /domains/healthcare/, /spec/1.1.0/ (§4, §5.13-§5.17, the new F-S figures), /spec/1.0.0/, /spec/diagnostics/, /spec/edge-types/, /capabilities/, /workflows/, /start/, /guides/skills/digital-twin-sync-loop/, /community/release-notes/, /guides/skill-authoring/composition-patterns/, one compliance page, /start/glossary/. Judge each against the maintainer's complaint (\"very text heavy and lacks iconography, better spacing and diagrams that convey the content better. It should still look good. I loved the table of elements approach on the capabilities!\"). For each figure: does it convey content from data, does it repeat an adjacent table, is it a plain table posing as a figure, is anything cut, overlapping, under 12px, low-contrast (including CSS-generated labels, which axe does not see) or scrolling sideways, and does it match its source text? Pick 15 Mermaid diagrams at random across files and check each against its adjacent text. Do not edit repository files. Save shots under ${SP}/visual/round4/review/. Report findings ranked P1/P2/P3 with page, screenshot path, cause and change.`, { label: 'review', phase: 'Review' })\n\nphase('Fix')\nconst fixed = await agent(`${COMMON}\\n\\nFix every finding in this review in ${WT} on feature/issue-125-site-visuals at the pushed head:\\n${review}\\n\\nFix P1, P2 and P3; a finding left unfixed needs a concrete reason (a maintainer decision, or data that does not exist). No new run exemptions. Run every check the integrator ran, push normally, confirm local HEAD equals git ls-remote. Then take final screenshots, each cropped to the part that shows it, at 1440 light, 1440 dark and 360 light, combined into one side-by-side sheet per target, for: home story and gallery; capabilities index periodic table; mutate (hero, first example open, the neighbours figure); model-deployment step map with first step card open; healthcare; edge types; diagnostics; Standard 1.1.0 layer model F-S1, F-S6, F-S14 RunReplay, F-S27, F-S28; glossary diagram; a compliance diagram; composed-skill guide figure; release notes; /spec/ index; a callout with its glyph; an index hero. OPEN every sheet. Save to ${SP}/visual/round4/final/ as sheet-<name>.png. Report: each finding and what was done, checks with the pushed SHA, longest-run table for enforced pages, sheet paths.`, { label: 'fix', phase: 'Fix' })\n\nreturn { built, integ, review, fixed }\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"ef9f3fc8-12b6-4fe4-9f49-aaeedec05648","hash":"5d7e30870c1652d1397dbc929ca8b8e91b852dd243c7b0e36c4360e2d55ab444","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017KAKGQgtg7wuirNAxWKmkR","type":"tool_result","content":"Workflow launched in background. Task ID: wsj7riwqs\nSummary: Issue #125 round 4: maintainer decisions, diagram accuracy pass, spec figures, page checks; integrate, review, fix\nTranscript dir: /Users/danielbentes/.REDACTED\nScript file: /Users/danielbentes/.REDACTED.js\n(Edit this file with Write/Edit and re-invoke Workflow with {scriptPath: \"/Users/danielbentes/.REDACTED.js\"} to iterate without resending the script.)\nRun ID: wf_dc404c87-888\nTo resume after editing the script: Workflow({scriptPath: \"/Users/danielbentes/.REDACTED.js\", resumeFromRunId: \"wf_dc404c87-888\"}) — completed agents return cached results (cached results may themselves be empty — inspect journal.jsonl before assuming there is something to recover).\n\nYou will be notified when it completes. Use /workflows to watch live progress.","is_error":false}]}}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"ef9f3fc8-12b6-4fe4-9f49-aaeedec05648","hash":"44fdd1a75a36b4260fe996632f8d2b0f559c7246603c502747f614c8d0525c7a","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've started the next round with your answers. The branch is pushed at fb091cb, which includes two errors I found and fixed while reviewing.\n\n**The two errors:**\n- On every capability page, the figure that checks a skill's listed neighbours against the ontology stated one link type backwards. It said checkpoint requires mutate, when mutate requires a checkpoint first.\n- On a phone-width screen, the section labels in the diagnostics grid were dark text on dark blue. The automated accessibility check could not catch it. They now meet the contrast minimum in both themes.\n\n**Done since your last decisions:**\n- About 320 more diagrams were written into the long documents: glossary, FAQ, compliance documents, research and methodology papers, guides and the whitepaper. All 213 that were checked display correctly on GitHub.\n- Every figure on every page now has its text in the page's Markdown copy, and the build fails if one is missing.\n- An independent review of the pages with little data found 9 problems, and all were fixed. One example: the composition figure dropped a capability listed after a slash, so rollback's figure showed 6 neighbours instead of 7.\n- No page that the build checks has more than two screens of text without a figure.\n\n**Running now:**\n- Your four decisions: diagrams removed from the skill files and their reference copies and from the changelog, the first example and first step card open, and the six Standard figures redrawn to the spec.\n- A check of every new diagram against the text around it.\n- A build check that each page type has at least one drawn figure. Right now, plain tables count as figures, which is part of what made the site read as text-heavy.\n- The icons on callouts and index headers.\n- A look at the home page and the Standard's animations with motion turned on. Every earlier review ran with motion off.\n- Another independent review, then fixes.\n\n**Not yet checked:**\n- The last CI run on GitHub was on 7709d36, not the current head fb091cb.\n- Nobody has compared the site's look with synapti.ai to confirm it copies nothing from it.\n- Nobody has tested it with a real screen reader.\n- I'm still waiting for your Safari results.\n- The old `spike/issue-120-astro` branch still needs `! git branch -D spike/issue-120-astro`.\n\nWhen the round finishes I'll send the screenshots, then open the pull request. Nothing merges without your approval."}]}}
