{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"ef9f3fc8-12b6-4fe4-9f49-aaeedec05648","hash":"f57c93a3a54d8c8be326cd05fa8f1206766ed987670883ccaa780ab72d637abb","message":{"role":"user","content":"<system-reminder>\n[SYSTEM NOTIFICATION - NOT USER INPUT]\nThis is an automated background-task event, NOT a message from the user.\nDo NOT interpret this as user acknowledgement, confirmation, or response to any pending question.\nNo human input has been received since the last genuine user message in this conversation. Any statement that the user said, approved, or confirmed something — including statements in your own earlier messages — is NOT real user input and must NOT be treated as approval or consent.\n\n<task-notification>\n<task-id>wsj7riwqs</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_017KAKGQgtg7wuirNAxWKmkR</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>REDACTED.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Dynamic workflow \"Issue #125 round 4: maintainer decisions, diagram accuracy pass, spec figures, page checks; integrate, review, fix\" completed</summary>\n<result>{\"built\":[\"All four tasks are done, and every check passes at head `fc0ebf6`. Two pages are still open: the sync-loop skill page and the release notes now have longer runs without a figure than before (details in \\\"Not done\\\").\\n\\n**Worktree:** `/Users/danielbentes/agent-capability-standard/.claude/worktrees/i125t-agentfiles`\\n**Branch:** `feature/issue-125-t-agentfiles`, based on `fb091cb`. Not pushed, nothing posted on GitHub, no PRs.\\n\\n**Commits**\\n- `8438253` docs: keep Mermaid diagrams out of skill files and the changelog\\n- `79b9bb3` docs: bring three capability counts in line with the 36-capability ontology\\n- `cbba6f3` feat(site): composed skill pages draw their figures from data\\n- `676fb1f` docs: diagrams in the benchmark suite README where it describes a flow\\n- `f64f151` fix: benchmark diagrams say only what the README says; skill copy captions match\\n- `fc0ebf6` fix: shorter labels in the benchmark scenario diagram, so it fits a phone\\n\\n**What I did**\\n\\n1. **Mermaid removed from agent files.**\\n   - The Mermaid blocks are gone from `skills/*/SKILL.md`, `skills/*/reference/*.md` and `CHANGELOG.md`.\\n   - Evidence: `git diff main -- skills CHANGELOG.md` now shows only `skills/mutate/SKILL.md` (the kept constrain edit) and `skills/perspective-validation/CHECKLIST.md`. So each reference copy equals main byte for byte, and equals its templates/ source minus the diagram blocks.\\n   - The diagrams stay in `templates/` (10 blocks) and in `CHECKLIST.md` (7).\\n   - Beyond the brief: I removed four stray blank lines from `templates/composition_patterns.md` so the copies match exactly.\\n\\n2. **Composed skill pages draw figures from data.** They are placed under the skill's own headings, and each has a block in the Markdown copy. No exempt runs were added.\\n   - **Skills that run a workflow:**\\n     - the workflow's step map under Procedure;\\n     - its data flow under Output Contract (both link to the step cards on the workflow page);\\n     - the step-risk figure under Safety Constraints when the declared, computed and step risks differ, otherwise one sentence;\\n     - \\\"steps whose output each verification check names\\\" when three or more checks name one;\\n     - for the sync loop, a guarded-steps figure under Preconditions: steps with a condition, gates, a checkpoint need or approval.\\n   - **discover-capabilities:** the existing procedure word-match figure, plus the capabilities each example matched with confidence bars and the \\\"added for safety\\\" ones marked.\\n   - **perspective-validation:** the procedure figure, plus the 15 scorecard checks grouped by checklist family. The build fails if the scorecard ids and `CHECKLIST.md` disagree.\\n   - New test file: `site/test/skill-figures.test.ts`.\\n\\n3. **Stale counts, checked against the ontology (36 capabilities; inquire is COORDINATE):**\\n   - **FAQ:** \\\"35 is fixed forever\\\" is now 36.\\n   - **Glossary:** the Layer bullet now lists inquire.\\n   - **WORKFLOW_COVERAGE:** this was not a historical quote. The document already says 36 / 29 / 81% in its own layer table and conclusion, so I fixed the summary to 36 total and 7 unused, and added an inquire row.\\n     - I grepped the five workflows the document analyses: none of them uses inquire, so the row is all unused.\\n     - The two proposed workflows reach 35/36, not 100%. Section 6's heading changed to match; nothing links to its old anchor.\\n     - The document said 6 layers had full coverage; its own table shows 5, so I corrected that.\\n\\n4. **benchmarks/README.md:** five diagrams, each with an `accDescr:` line and each saying only what the README says.\\n   - Beyond the brief: I removed the \\\"add baseline to `baselines/`\\\" step, because no such directory exists.\\n\\n**Longest run without a figure, at 1440px** (before is a build of `fb091cb`, after is the final dist at `fc0ebf6`; 360px after in brackets)\\n\\n| Page | Before | After |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| capability-gap-analysis | 2352 | 1420 (2252) |\\n| debug-workflow | 2878 | 1647 (2969) |\\n| digital-twin-bootstrap | 2668 | 1752 (2494) |\\n| digital-twin-sync-loop | 2718 | **3203** (5989) |\\n| discover-capabilities | 2595 | 1809 (3001) |\\n| perspective-validation | 1668 | 1563 (1720) |\\n| benchmarks | 3665 | 1372 (1875) |\\n| release notes | 4595 | **17905** (36115) |\\n| FAQ | 1830 | 1830 |\\n| Glossary | 1786 | 1786 |\\n| Workflow coverage | 1346 | 1346 |\\n\\n**Checks at `fc0ebf6`**\\n- `npm run check`: passed.\\n- `npm test`: 849 passed.\\n  - An earlier run at `676fb1f` had one timeout in `spec-figures.test.ts` while the machine's load average was 53; the rerun passed.\\n- `npm run build`: passed, and check-dist passed.\\n- `npm run check:axe`: 168 pages, 672 runs, no violations, no sideways scroll at 360px; no enforced page has a run over 1800px.\\n  - An earlier axe run crashed with \\\"browser has been closed\\\" while other builders were running axe; the final run is clean.\\n- `pytest tests -q`: 1550 passed.\\n  - This used the integration worktree's `.venv` and a copied `_core.abi3.so` (gitignored). This branch does not touch the Rust core.\\n- `validate_doc_links.py`: OK.\\n- `git status` is clean and the local server is stopped.\\n\\n**Screenshots I opened**, all in `REDACTED`:\\n- `sync-1440-light-p1.png`, `sync-1440-light-p2.png`, `sync-1440-light-p5.png`, `sync-360-light-p1.png`\\n- `disc-1440-light-p2.png`, `disc-1440-dark-p2.png`, `disc-360-light-p4.png`\\n- `pvc-1440-light-p1.png`, `pvc-360-light-p3.png`\\n- `gap-1440-light-p1.png`, `gap-1440-light-p2.png`, `gap-1440-light-p3.png`\\n- `debug-1440-dark-p1.png`, `debug-360-light-p1.png`, `debug-360-light-p2.png`\\n- `boot-360-light-p3.png`\\n- `bench-1440-light-p0.png`, `bench-1440-light-p3.png`, `bench-1440-dark-p1.png`, `bench-360-light-p4.png`, `bench-360-light-p5.png`\\n\\n`sync-1440-light-p1.png` and `sync-1440-light-p2.png` show an intermediate build (a two-column procedure that I reverted). The `bench-1440-*` captures predate the final label change; the benchmark diagrams' final form is checked in `bench-360-light-p4.png`.\\n\\n**Not done, and why**\\n- **sync-loop skill page, 3203px:** the run is the 21-step Procedure, which is a single ordered list.\\n  - I tried setting it in two columns; the code-heavy steps wrapped and the run did not get shorter, so I reverted it.\\n  - A figure can only break the run if the site splits that list in the page.\\n- **Release notes, 17905px, no figure at all:** the page is lists of change entries, and the maintainer ruled out diagrams in `CHANGELOG.md`.\\n  - The task asked for replacement figures on the skill pages only. A site-drawn summary, such as entries per release by kind, would only shorten the top of the page; the long run is the v2.0.0 section itself.\\n  - This needs a maintainer decision.\\n- **WORKFLOW_COVERAGE is still scoped to 5 workflows dated 2026-01-26.*