{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"ef9f3fc8-12b6-4fe4-9f49-aaeedec05648","hash":"7afe39d7201bcf8fbe080d88bb701657d8c1d8ef76f0b21afa557acf8aa2881a","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TJ7oLPEmgNYdXF4GB4Didy","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tAll 25 findings were dealt with: 19 are fixed and 6 need a decision from you or have a concrete reason they stay. The pushed head is `be4eb0b`, and local HEAD matches `git ls-remote`. The task named `fb091cb`, which was stale; the work started from `fa16612`, the head the reviewer checked.\n2\t\n3\t## Checks at `be4eb0b`\n4\tAll pass:\n5\t- `npm run check`: 0 errors; colour contrast 412 pairs; design data reports 20 status values, each with a style.\n6\t- `npm test`: 864 of 864.\n7\t- `npm run build`: every check-dist check passes.\n8\t- `npm run check:axe`: 168 pages, 672 runs, no violations, no sideways scroll at 360px, and no data-flow grid scrolls at 1440px. The figure-gap check finds no enforced page over 1800px.\n9\t- `pytest tests -q`: 1550 passed. `validate_doc_links.py`: 315 references resolve.\n10\t\n11\t## P1\n12\t**Sync-loop data-flow grid cut at 1440px.** Fixed. The narrow-padding rule for figure tables now skips `table.flow-grid`. `check:axe` now fails if any data-flow grid scrolls at 1440px; it reported 285px on that page before the fix.\n13\t\n14\t## P2\n15\t- **2. Rollback in §5.2.1.** Fixed. Rollback's \"Needs checkpoint\" cell shows the requires mark on an outlined cell, with its own key entry and a caption that says so. The Markdown copy says \"Yes, via requires edge\". This key entry is an addition to the visual spec.\n16\t- **3. §5.12 recovery loop.** Redrawn as one step tile with three branches:\n17\t  - the loop back to its `goto_step` target, with the `max_loops` cells;\n18\t  - \"Loops exhausted\", leading to the `on_exhausted` handler with R404;\n19\t  - \"No loop\", leading to \"The run ends with the step's code\".\n20\t\n21\t  The two exits hang side by side because they are alternatives. Labels are the first clause of each table cell. I dropped R402 from the \"No loop\" tile, because §5.12 gives R402 only for a failure mode fired by `when` on a step that did not fail.\n22\t- **4. §5.14 approval.** Fixed. Stage 1 is now a 2×2 grid of tiles that wraps to one column on a phone. Stage 3 adds the three `when_unattended` plans from the schema: `fail` → F502, `skip`, and `defer_to_queue` → a planned action record.\n23\t- **5. §3.3 safety ordering.** Fixed with the option that keeps the specified layout. Sources now sit over the gaps between target columns, so constrain no longer sits on rollback's column. Each lane is labelled with its source's two-letter symbol.\n24\t- **6. Plain tables framed as figures.** On 1.1.0, §4.1 and §6.3 are now Port columns with descriptions, and the source table is folded under each. 1.0.0 gets the same two; its §5.1, §5.2, §6.2 and §10.1 tables are plain tables again. The 1.1.0 page still passes the enforced check (longest run 1653px).\n25\t- **7. Status glyphs.** Fixed. Every status line in the sources is now collected, and the badge draws its glyph. There are five new 7×7 glyphs: template, implementation, ready, guide and integrated. Two mappings are my choice and easy to reverse: Standard uses the normative style and Reference analysis uses the analysis style. One follow-up fix: the long \"Reference implementation\" badge overflowed at 360px, so it now wraps.\n26\t- **8. Mermaid diagrams that repeat their neighbour.** I removed 98 of the 363 diagrams.\n27\t  - I scored all 363 by how many of their labels appear in the table, list or code block next to them.\n28\t  - The cut covered diagrams with 80% or more overlap, up to 25 lines, outside the workflow pattern flows, `spec/CHANGELOG.md`, `templates/` and `skills/`.\n29\t  - I read the summary of about 70 of them. About 45 were cut on their score alone, without reading them; `git show f5b1243` lists them all for you to check or restore.\n30\t  - Also cut: the analyze flow (the page now draws its six steps in order), the act split with its act-to-send edge, D17, and the glossary's derivation diagram.\n31\t  - Redrawn: the evidence diagram on the workflow patterns page, now one capability output after another feeding the pattern output.\n32\t  - Kept: the SDK guide's multi-agent diagram, because it sums up a 40-line code block.\n33\t- **9. Long open first example.** I followed the reviewer's recommendation: the example stays open, and an Output block over 100 lines folds under \"Show the whole output, N lines\". This folds decompose (207 lines) and compare. I first set the limit at 40 lines, but folding integrate (94 lines) left it with a 1923px run and no exemption. I raised it to 100, so integrate stays as before and is still exempt. **Decision for you:** keep the 100-line limit, or fold integrate too and give that page another figure.\n34\t\n35\t## P3\n36\t1. **§10.1 conformance figure: unchanged.** You asked for F-S28 as specified, and it is.\n37\t2. **§9.6 heat grid at 360px:** rows now show \"§5.n\" alone, and all six columns fit.\n38\t3. **§5.15 delegate figure:** inputs and outputs sit side by side when the frame is 600px or wider.\n39\t4. **mutate verification figure:**\n40\t   - The checklist below it now folds into a \"Text version\".\n41\t   - A check that names no field now says so instead of showing empty cells.\n42\t5. **Blank cells in Field Definitions:** dotted names are looked up by their whole path, and a row naming two fields gets a mark for each.\n43\t6. **Workflow inputs at 360px:** the type glyph and the name stay together.\n44\t7. **Periodic table at 360px:** IDs are 12px with tighter padding, so \"transition\", \"checkpoint\" and \"synchronize\" show in full.\n45\t8. **Mermaid label wrapping:** labels now wrap at 34 characters before falling back to 22.\n46\t9. **Tables scrolling at 1440px:** long code in a table cell may break after \"/\", \".\" or \"_\". None of the three tables scrolls now.\n47\t10. **Composition patterns page:** step tables now get a capability tile for IDs written with their parameters, so these tables now count as figures.\n48\t11. **`spec/CHANGELOG.md` diagrams: left as they are.** This is your decision; your rule named only the root `CHANGELOG.md`.\n49\t\n50\tAlso left for you: a release-notes timeline drawn from the version headings. The release notes page still has no figure.\n51\t\n52\tOne defect I found that predates this round and is not fixed: in the edge-type summary table at 360px, the first column breaks IDs letter by letter. It comes from a phone-width rule added in commit `4a1ccd1`.\n53\t\n54\t## Longest runs on enforced pages (1440px; limit 1800px)\n55\t| Page | Longest run |\n56\t|---|---|\n57\t| /workflows/patterns/ | 1769px |\n58\t| /workflows/digital-twin-sync-loop/ | 1767px |\n59\t| /spec/edge-types/ | 1765px |\n60\t| /capabilities/rollback/ | 1765px |\n61\t| /capabilities/synchronize/ | 1724px |\n62\t| /capabilities/audit/ | 1717px |\n63\t| /guides/claude-agent-sdk/ | 1710px |\n64\t| /capabilities/invoke/ | 1685px |\n65\t| /spec/1.1.0/ | 1653px |\n66\t| /workflows/ | 1650px |\n67\t| / | 1625px |\n68\t| every other enforced page | 1607px or less |\n69\t\n70\t12 pages meet the 900px target.\n71\t\n72\t## Sheets\n73\tI opened every sheet. Each is cropped to its target at 1440 light, 1440 dark and 360 light. They are in `REDACTED`:\n74\t- sheet-home.png (story and gallery)\n75\t- sheet-capabilities-index.png\n76\t- sheet-mutate.png (hero, first example open, neighbours figure)\n77\t- sheet-model-deployment.png (step map and the first step card open)\n78\t- sheet-healthcare.png\n79\t- sheet-edge-types.png\n80\t- sheet-diagnostics.png\n81\t- sheet-spec-layer-model.png, sheet-spec-fs1.png, sheet-spec-fs6.png, sheet-spec-fs14.png (with its RunReplay), sheet-spec-fs17.png, sheet-spec-fs27.png, sheet-spec-fs28.png, sheet-spec-fs2.png\n82\t- sheet-glossary.png\n83\t- sheet-compliance.png\n84\t- sheet-composed-skill.png\n85\t- sheet-release-notes.png\n86\t- sheet-spec-index.png\n87\t- sheet-callout.png\n88\t- sheet-index-hero.png\n89\t- sheet-status-badges.png (Template, Ready for use, Guide, SDK-integrated, Reference analysis)\n90\t\n91\tThe local server is stopped. `.decisions/` was already untracked and was left out of every commit.\n92\t"}]}}
