{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"ef9f3fc8-12b6-4fe4-9f49-aaeedec05648","hash":"8929b822cc05589cf25469a760456410000ba3fa978185bfc8653f1c1bf073af","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01FdAMtredWvtxSvTcTMBfEx","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/danielbentes/agent-capability-standard/.claude/worktrees/i125-relnotes && sed -n 280,330p site/src/lib/index-figures.ts; grep -n \"^## \\|^### \" CHANGELOG.md | head -60; grep -n \"^## \" CHANGELOG.md | wc -l","description":"Read the release parser and changelog structure"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"ef9f3fc8-12b6-4fe4-9f49-aaeedec05648","hash":"331f220d659a38d76b4ce068d8b2430e2beae190729cf26ce657c161c8f489d8","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FdAMtredWvtxSvTcTMBfEx","type":"tool_result","content":"  head: [string, string];\n  rows: { label: string; url?: string; value: number; max?: number; words: string }[];\n}\n\n/**\n * The releases in CHANGELOG.md, newest first: each \"## [vX.Y.Z] — date\"\n * section with the number of change items (list lines) under it.\n */\nexport function releaseBars(changelog: string): BarList {\n  const lines = changelog.split('\\n');\n  const rows: { label: string; value: number; words: string }[] = [];\n  let cur: { label: string; value: number; date: string } | null = null;\n  const flush = () => cur && rows.push({ label: cur.label, value: cur.value, words: `${plural(cur.value, 'change', 'changes')}, ${cur.date}` });\n  for (const l of lines) {\n    const h = /^## \\[(v\\d+\\.\\d+\\.\\d+[^\\]]*)\\]\\s+—\\s+(\\d{4}-\\d{2}-\\d{2})/.exec(l);\n    if (h) {\n      flush();\n      cur = { label: h[1]!, value: 0, date: h[2]! };\n      continue;\n    }\n    if (/^## /.test(l)) {\n      flush();\n      cur = null;\n      continue;\n    }\n    if (cur && /^\\s*[-*] /.test(l)) cur.value += 1;\n  }\n  flush();\n  if (rows.length === 0) throw new Error('CHANGELOG.md: no \"## [vX.Y.Z] — date\" section');\n  const top = [...rows].sort((a, b) => b.value - a.value)[0]!;\n  return {\n    title: 'Changes in each release, newest first',\n    head: ['Release', 'Changes'],\n    caption: `${plural(rows.length, 'release', 'releases')} from ${rows.at(-1)!.label} to ${rows[0]!.label}; ${top.label} has the most changes (${top.value}), counted as list items in the release notes.`,\n    rows,\n  };\n}\n\n// ------------------------------------------------------------ /start/\n\n/** The reading speed the start pages' reading times assume. */\nexport const WORDS_PER_MINUTE = 200;\n\n/**\n * A page's words outside fenced blocks, and its fenced blocks other than\n * diagrams (mermaid, or two or more lines of box-drawing characters): the\n * commands and code to read or run.\n */\nexport function pageSize(text: string): { words: number; codeBlocks: number } {\n  let codeBlocks = 0;\n  const prose = text\n33 matches in 1 files:\n\n7:## [Unreleased]\n15:### Changed\n53:### Fixed\n61:## [v2.0.0] — 2026-10-29\n79:### Added\n252:### Changed\n365:### Fixed\n542:## [v1.2.0] — 2026-02-04\n547:### Added\n566:### Changed\n569:### Fixed\n575:## [v1.1.1] — 2026-01-27\n577:### Changed\n582:## [v1.1.0] — 2026-01-27\n584:### Added\n595:### Fixed\n598:### Changed\n603:## [v1.0.5] — 2026-01-25\n605:### Changed\n609:### Fixed\n613:## [v1.0.4] — 2026-01-25\n615:### Fixed\n619:## [v1.0.3] — 2026-01-25\n621:### Fixed\n625:### Changed\n  +8 more in CHANGELOG.md [see remaining: tail -n +26 \"$HOME/Library/Application REDACTED.log\"]\n      11","is_error":false}]}}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"ef9f3fc8-12b6-4fe4-9f49-aaeedec05648","hash":"9cf9a63a2af77235585a2046f5998e4b7eaa43b008f136e6ab01d6f8f0462caf","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XjgGsMmFKXeqvkuJg137AG","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/danielbentes/agent-capability-standard/.claude/worktrees/i125-relnotes && sed -n 61,100p CHANGELOG.md | cut -c1-200; grep -c \"^- \" CHANGELOG.md; awk 'NR>=79 && NR<252 && /^- /' CHANGELOG.md | cut -c1-90 | head -40","description":"Read the v2.0.0 section structure"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"ef9f3fc8-12b6-4fe4-9f49-aaeedec05648","hash":"e070aaffa556b42769cdd20ea9085a6e30b3ec2721247eeac8750cd875641fb7","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XjgGsMmFKXeqvkuJg137AG","type":"tool_result","content":"## [v2.0.0] — 2026-10-29\n\nImplements Standard v1.1.0 (Candidate Standard) with RFC-0003 and RFC-0004\n(#114, #116) and replaces the 1.0 validator and engine with one Rust core\n(#115). The Standard's version (v1.1.0; v1.0.0 still supported) is separate\nfrom this plugin release.\n\n**Upgrading from v1.2.0:**\n- Building from source needs a Rust toolchain (rustc >= 1.86): the validator\n  and executor are the `grounded_agency._core` extension, built by maturin\n  with `pip install -e \".[dev]\" -c constraints.txt`.\n- `transform.output` is `object|array` (ontology 2.1.0); a reference to it\n  without an annotation is now B204.\n- Validation is stricter: catalogs that passed 1.0 may now get errors or\n  warnings (unknown fields W604, unbound required inputs W615, literal type\n  mismatches B203, among others listed below).\n- A quorum's model families count only when the host attests them.\n\n### Added\n- **Release workflow.** `.github/workflows/release.yml` publishes a GitHub\n  Release with the tag's CHANGELOG section as its notes, for a pushed `v*`\n  tag or, run by hand on `main`, for a tag it creates there;\n  `scripts/release_notes.py` refuses a tag that does not match `plugin.json`\n  or has no section\n- **Delegate identity (#114, RFC-0004 amendment).** With `identity@1` a\n  host may attest who took a delegation (`effective.identity`); a waiting\n  delegate keeps only results from that principal (others dropped as\n  `delegate_identity`), a malformed or contradicting identity is R402, and\n  `quorum.require_distinct_identities` counts one verdict per attested\n  principal. Quorum model families now count only as attested. Validator,\n  executor, schema, eleven runtime fixtures and docs\n- **Standard changes from the orchestrator fixtures (#114).** Gates can\n  `end` a run successfully (`RunResult.ended`); a step can `delay` before\n  it goes on (`wait@1`), without a fake event to wait on; an `accept_from`\n  or `correlate` built from a missing value fails the step at once (R402)\n  instead of dropping every sender, or matching every event that lacks the\n  key; and\n  `after_deferral: run` (`approval@1`) lets a step that does not depend on\n  a deferred one, such as an escalation, run anyway. Validator, executor,\n  Python runner, schema, runtime fixtures and docs\n151\n- **Release workflow.** `.github/workflows/release.yml` publishes a GitHub\n- **Delegate identity (#114, RFC-0004 amendment).** With `identity@1` a\n- **Standard changes from the orchestrator fixtures (#114).** Gates can\n- **W616 `VERSION_FEATURE_MISMATCH`.** A workflow that declares standard\n- **The #114 author's orchestrator workflows as conformance fixtures.** The\n- **Contributed runtime fixtures.** Twenty scripted runs the #114 author\n- **Read-only reviewers and per-reviewer waits (#114).** `delegate` takes\n- **Agent identity, `identity@1` (RFC-0004, #114).** A new\n- **`in` in condition expressions (#114).** `x in y` tests membership in a\n- **Rust core (`core/`, #114).** The workflow validator now lives in a Rust\n- **Orchestration extensions, first part (#114):** `workflow_extensions.requires`\n- **Reference executor (#114).** A deterministic, sans-IO executor in the\n- `docs/research/analysis/validator-engine-disagreements-1.0.md`: minimal\n- A step that raises `requires_checkpoint` above the ontology is now held to\n- `world_state_schema.yaml` 1.1.0: action records gain status `rejected`\n- `schemas/review_verdict_schema.yaml` for quorum verdicts; ontology inputs\n- `spec/STANDARD-v1.1.0.md` (Candidate Standard) and `spec/RFC-0003-orchestration-extensio\n- Validator warnings: `tools/validate_workflows.py` reports warnings (W6xx)\n- `WorkflowEngine.validate_report()`, `add_workflow()` and `effective_flags()`;\n- `python tools/sync_skill_schemas.py --check`, run in CI, fails when a\n- Conformance fixtures for the v1.1 edge, flag, unknown-field and version\n- `tools/validate_canonical_schemas.py` and a CI job covering the five canonical\n- `spec/RFC-0002-agent-reliability-profile.md` proposing cross-session agent\n- `tools/validate_rfcs.py` and a CI job enforcing what `spec/GOVERNANCE.md`\n- `tools/validate_constraints.py` and a CI job asserting that every pin in\n- `tools/validate_doc_links.py` and a CI job asserting that documentation","is_error":false}]}}
