{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"ef9f3fc8-12b6-4fe4-9f49-aaeedec05648","hash":"5832fb1ec7f73865db5dab9065257c65440d72920faf23856b922d68731f7dae","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The diagram review is done: 19 of the 98 are back, 3 of them corrected, and the branch is at ec5f68d. Next I'll commit the release notes work and merge it into the branch."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016iqQNANSrqWLaojktasuRU","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"REDACTED.txt","content":"feat(site): release notes get a timeline, section figures and folds\n\nThe release notes page had no figure and an 18,000px run of entries. The\nmaintainer ruled out diagrams in CHANGELOG.md (its sections become GitHub\nrelease notes), so the site draws them from the changelog's own structure:\n\n- a timeline: each release, its date, and a bar per kind of change\n  (Added, Changed, Removed, Fixed) counting its top-level entries;\n- under a section of 8 or more entries that cites issues or names\n  diagnostic codes: the issues with the number of entries citing each,\n  and the codes as tiles linked to the diagnostics page;\n- every section of 8 or more entries shows its first 5 and folds the\n  rest under \"Show the other N entries\". The Markdown copy keeps them all.\n\nBelow 480px the timeline puts each release on its own lines, so it never\nscrolls sideways. The longest run on the page falls from 17,905px to\n2,633px at 1440. Tests count from a hand-written changelog fixture.\n\nRefs #125\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Jea2Va3FATnCydAsWsbLXR\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01AZeo5sCycF3PGFdd5MZHcB","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/danielbentes/agent-capability-standard/.claude/worktrees/i125-relnotes && git add site/src/lib/release-figures.ts site/src/plugins/release-figures-hast.ts site/src/plugins/rehype-prose-figures.ts site/src/twins/release-blocks.ts site/src/twins/index.ts site/src/styles/figures-prose.css site/test/release-figures.test.ts && git status --short | head && git commit -q -F REDACTED.txt && git log --oneline -1","description":"Commit the release notes work"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
