{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"ef9f3fc8-12b6-4fe4-9f49-aaeedec05648","hash":"df60dc594117675b3f40cb7d1aaee7a03e4b7e2c2ce4bb9f18981648f94da6de","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The release notes page is improved, and the branch is pushed at f254598. I've sent you four screenshots of it.\n\n**What's on the page now** (drawn from the structure of `CHANGELOG.md`; the file itself is unchanged, so GitHub release notes stay plain text):\n- **A timeline at the top:** every release with its date and a bar for each kind of change (Added, Changed, Removed, Fixed), counting its entries. On a phone, each release gets its own short block, so nothing scrolls sideways.\n- **Figures for big sections:** for v2.0.0's Added, Changed and Fixed, and v1.2.0's Added, the issues the entries cite with how many entries cite each. The diagnostic codes they introduce or change are shown as tiles linked to the diagnostics page.\n- **Folded long sections:** any section with 8 or more entries shows its first 5, and the rest sit behind \"Show the other N entries\". The page's Markdown copy still lists every entry.\n- **Shorter stretches of text:** the longest stretch without a figure went from 17,905px to 2,633px at desktop width.\n\n**The removed diagrams:** all 98 were reviewed against their text. 19 are back, because they show a branch, a loop, a parallel step or an order that the text doesn't make visible. Three of those were corrected first. The other 79 stay out, because each one redrew its table or list in the same shape.\n\nThe reviewer also noticed something outside those 98: the Annex VI procedure, and the four workflow diagrams in sections 5.1 to 5.4 of the OASF comparison, are still plain copies of the list beside them, while similar ones were removed. I can remove those too if you want them treated the same way.\n\n**Checks at f254598, on my machine:** all pass.\n- Type check and contrast check.\n- 875 site tests.\n- Build checks.\n- Accessibility: 168 pages, both themes, desktop and phone width.\n- The long-text check: no checked page goes over the limit.\n- The repository's link check.\n\nGitHub's checks haven't run on this commit yet. They'll run when I open the pull request.\n\nNext I'll open the pull request, which closes #125. Merging it publishes the site, so that step is yours."}]}}
