{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"ef9f3fc8-12b6-4fe4-9f49-aaeedec05648","hash":"3bddf028b2ad57b67b510ebab785c0432a9bb2a2d6d21af71c0cefa83b785a11","message":{"role":"user","content":"<system-reminder>\n[SYSTEM NOTIFICATION - NOT USER INPUT]\nThis is an automated background-task event, NOT a message from the user.\nDo NOT interpret this as user acknowledgement, confirmation, or response to any pending question.\nNo human input has been received since the last genuine user message in this conversation. Any statement that the user said, approved, or confirmed something — including statements in your own earlier messages — is NOT real user input and must NOT be treated as approval or consent.\n\n<task-notification>\n<task-id>a6199c2d270c6660b</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01NajjYTeuZBoFm4rA6sm9Tf</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>REDACTED.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Security review of the branch\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>I found no security findings in this change, so the security facet's decision is **APPROVE**. This covers `origin/main` at 824eea1 to HEAD f254598, read on 2026-11-13.\n\n## Security Review Findings\n\n### P1 — Critical Security Issues (Blocks Merge)\n| Finding | Suggested Fix |\n|---------|---------------|\n\n### P2 — Security Concerns\n| Finding | Suggested Fix |\n|---------|---------------|\n\n### P3 — Security Improvements\n| Finding | Suggested Fix |\n|---------|---------------|\n\n### Dependency Audit (separate from finding schema — no file:line)\n| Package | Severity | Advisory | Fix |\n|---------|----------|---------|-----|\n| (none) | — | `npm audit` in `site/`: 0 info, 0 low, 0 moderate, 0 high, 0 critical | — |\n\n### Summary\n- Security findings: P1: 0, P2: 0, P3: 0\n- Dependency findings (`DEP-`, in the tables above): 0\n- Dependency read: ok (both changed manifests read: `site/package.json` and `site/package-lock.json`)\n- Advisory audit: ran (`npm audit --json` in `site/`, this is your own PR); 0 advisories\n- Secrets scan: none (37,704 added lines checked; no keyword or high-entropy hits apart from lockfile integrity hashes; no `.env` files)\n- Overall risk: Low\n\n## What was checked\n\n**HTML built from Markdown, YAML and diagram text**\n- **One processor for all Markdown.** Every Markdown page goes through the same processor (`site/src/lib/markdown.ts:71`, wired in `site/astro.config.mjs:40`). It includes the existing raw-HTML allowlist (`site/src/plugins/remark-html-allowlist.ts`), which only lets through `details`, `summary`, `br`, `sup`, `sub` and `&lt;a name|id&gt;`. No changed plugin adds raw HTML of its own; a search of `plugins/`, `lib/`, `components/`, `templates/` and `pages/` found none.\n- **The new `set:html` calls are safe.** The roughly 25 new calls (in `SpecFigure.astro`, `SpecPage.astro`, `ProsePage.astro`, `RfcPage.astro`, `SkillPage.astro`, `capabilities/[id].astro`, `domains/*.astro`, `spec/edge-types.astro`) only re-insert pieces of that processor's output.\n- **The fold helpers are safe.** `foldFirstTable`, `foldFirstTaskList` and `foldFirstBox` (`site/src/lib/inject.ts:78-94`, `site/src/lib/prose-figures.ts:26-34`) and `foldCapabilityList` (`site/src/lib/domain-figures.ts:368`) wrap already-rendered HTML. Their summary text is a fixed string and is HTML-escaped. `h2Section` (`site/src/lib/domain-figures.ts:309`) builds its regex from constant anchors only.\n- **Mermaid diagrams.** `site/src/lib/mermaid/render.ts` builds the SVG as a structured element tree. Every label, title, caption and text-version item is a text node, so it is escaped when written out. The Markdown copy escapes `\\ * [ ] &lt;` and backticks (`site/src/lib/mermaid/text.ts:52`).\n- **Links.** Every `href` in the new figure components comes from a route helper (`workflowHref`, `layerHref`, `domainHref`, `sectionLink`, `githubBlobUrl`) or from internal route URLs. Astro escapes attribute values. I searched for these rather than reading all 9 changed plugins line by line; I read `remark-mermaid.ts` and `remark-html-allowlist.ts` in full.\n\n**One case I looked at but did not raise.** `site/src/components/fig/WorkflowSpine.astro:81` puts the workflow id, unescaped, into a CSS selector, which line 228 writes into `&lt;style set:html&gt;`. Nothing limits the characters in an id: the catalog schema allows any key, and `parseCatalog` in `site/src/data/workflows.ts` does not check them. However, ids come only from catalog files in this repository, which go through the same review as the component itself. Someone who could plant a bad id could edit the component directly, so it is outside the review scope. A rule in the site loader limiting ids to `^[a-z0-9_]+$` would close it cheaply if you want that.\n\n**CI workflow (`.github/workflows/site.yml`)**\n- Permissions stay at `contents: read`.\n- Deploy still runs only on a push to `main` with `SITE_DEPLOY_ENABLED`. It uses the action pinned to a commit and takes the build output from the same run.\n- No step interpolates pull-request text into a shell command; the deploy step uses only `github.sha`.\n- The new steps run in the build job, which has no secrets:\n  - `npx playwright install --with-deps chromium` uses the `playwright` 1.64.1 installed from the lockfile.\n  - `npm run check:axe` starts a local server that listens only on `127.0.0.1` on a random port and refuses `..` paths (`site/scripts/check-axe.mjs:47-68`).\n- The new step that removes `dist/_review` runs before deploy. Those review pages are not in the search index, because they lack `data-pagefind-body` and every published page template has it. They are also absent from `sitemap.xml`. That last check was on a local `dist/` built at 07:43 today from an unknown commit.\n\n**Dependencies, one judgment per package**\n\n| Package | Advisory | License | Install hook | Imported | Near-name |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `elkjs@0.12.0` (runtime dependency) | none | EPL-2.0 OR GPL-3.0-or-later | none | yes, `site/src/lib/mermaid/layout.ts:11` | none |\n| `playwright@1.64.1` (dev) | none | Apache-2.0 | none | yes, `site/scripts/check-axe.mjs:88`, `site/scripts/check-runs.mjs:153` | none |\n| `@axe-core/playwright@4.14.0` (dev) | none | MPL-2.0 | none | yes, `site/scripts/check-axe.mjs:89` | none |\n| `axe-core@4.14.0`, `playwright-core@1.64.1` and `@1.65.0` (pulled in by the above) | none | MPL-2.0 / Apache-2.0 | none | — | none |\n\n- **elkjs license.** It does not conflict with the project's Apache-2.0 licence. elkjs runs only at build time:\n  - At HEAD, only `remark-mermaid.ts` imports it, through `layout.ts`.\n  - No browser `&lt;script&gt;` imports anything under `lib/mermaid`.\n  - The local `dist/_astro` (same build-vintage caveat as above) contains no elkjs code.\n  - `site/package.json` is marked private.\n\n  So the site does not redistribute elkjs, and the SVGs it draws are output, not a derived work. This would change if elkjs were ever imported by browser code.\n- **Install hooks.** The only `hasInstallScript` entry is `fsevents`, which was already in the lockfile before this change; CI still runs `npm ci --ignore-scripts`.\n- **`playwright-core@1.65.0`** is installed at the top level because `@axe-core/playwright` asks for it, while `playwright` uses its own 1.64.1. Both are locked with integrity hashes. This is a duplicate copy, not a security problem.\n\nNo `.md` report file was written.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>98753</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>39</tool_uses><duration_ms>339087</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>\n</system-reminder>"}}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"ef9f3fc8-12b6-4fe4-9f49-aaeedec05648","hash":"5c0895cba7a3c36599e085eda051e49cea8cc07869d1c6448973219680e05ce5","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The security review found nothing. It suggested one cheap hardening step: the site's catalog loader should reject workflow IDs with unexpected characters. I'll include that in the fix batch. Three reviewers are still running."}]}}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"ef9f3fc8-12b6-4fe4-9f49-aaeedec05648","hash":"fb15452b9c0af32d5b572dd4f0b25fcaaadc7f732147abe4e9779a812465c179","message":{"role":"user","content":"<system-reminder>\n[SYSTEM NOTIFICATION - NOT USER INPUT]\nThis is an automated background-task event, NOT a message from the user.\nDo NOT interpret this as user acknowledgement, confirmation, or response to any pending question.\nNo human input has been received since the last genuine user message in this conversation. Any statement that the user said, approved, or confirmed something — including statements in your own earlier messages — is NOT real user input and must NOT be treated as approval or consent.\n\n<task-notification>\n<task-id>a51ed6eadc0b80762</task-id>\n<output-file>REDACTED.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Run all quality commands\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>All 20 commands passed on commit f254598, the head of `feature/issue-125-site-visuals`, on 2026-11-13. Every one exited with code 0, so there is no error output to include. I edited no files. The only file the commands wrote is `tools/validator_suggestions.json`, which `.gitignore` excludes, and `git status` afterwards showed only the `.decisions/` folder that was already untracked.\n\n### Site (in `site/`, Node v26.13.0, matching `.nvmrc`)\n\n| Command | Status | Summary line it printed |\n|---|---|---|\n| `npm ci` | Pass | `added 422 packages, and audited 423 packages in 5s` / `found 0 vulnerabilities` |\n| `npm run check` | Pass | `Result (286 files): - 0 errors - 0 warnings - 0 hints`; `check-contrast: 412 pairs in light and dark meet 4.5:1 (text) and 3:1 (edges)`; `check-design-data: 9 layers have light and dark tokens and a glyph; 207 grids parse; 48 glyph keys from the data have a grid; 20 status values have a style; no hand-typed counts in 263 source files` |\n| `npm test` | Pass | `Test Files  38 passed (38)` / `Tests  875 passed (875)` |\n| `npm run build` | Pass | Pagefind: `Indexed 168 pages`; `check-dist: every check passed (files, links, md-links, copies, sitemap, figures, drawn, legends, review)`; `check-dist: links: 27598 internal links checked` |\n| `npm run check:axe` | Pass | `check-axe: 168 pages, 672 runs (light and dark at 1440 and 360px): no axe violations, no sideways scroll at 360px, no data-flow grid scrolls at 1440px`; `check-runs: 168 pages; 12 meet the 900px target; 0 enforced page(s) have a run over 1800px (enforced)` |\n\n`npm ci` printed one warning, which did not stop it: `fsevents@2.3.3` has install scripts that `allowScripts` does not cover yet.\n\n### Repo root (with `/Users/danielbentes/agent-capability-standard/.venv` active)\n\nThe active `grounded_agency` package was the one in this worktree, not the main checkout's.\n\n| Command | Status | Summary line it printed |\n|---|---|---|\n| `pytest tests -q` | Pass | `1550 passed in 82.31s (0:01:22)` |\n| `validate_workflows.py --strict` | Pass | `VALIDATION PASS` |\n| Catalog loop (5 catalogs) | Pass | `VALIDATION PASS` for each: data_analysis, healthcare, manufacturing, personal_assistant, digital_twin_sync_loop |\n| `validate_profiles.py` | Pass | `PROFILE VALIDATION PASS: 7 profiles validated` |\n| `validate_skill_refs.py` | Pass | `SKILL REFERENCE VALIDATION PASS: 42 skills validated` |\n| `validate_ontology.py` | Pass | `VALIDATION PASSED` (34 of 36 capabilities have incoming edges; 0 orphan capabilities) |\n| `validate_canonical_schemas.py` | Pass | `CANONICAL SCHEMA VALIDATION PASS: 5 schemas validated` |\n| `validate_rfcs.py` | Pass | `RFC VALIDATION PASS: 4 RFCs validated` |\n| `validate_constraints.py` | Pass | `OK: 1 pin(s) in constraints.txt agree with pyproject.toml` |\n| `validate_doc_links.py` | Pass | `OK: 315 reference(s) across 164 file(s) resolve` |\n| `validate_yaml_util_sync.py` | Pass | `YAML util sync OK — 4 definitions match` |\n| `validate_transform_refs.py` | Pass | `TRANSFORM REFERENCE VALIDATION PASS: 5 refs validated` |\n| `validate_benchmark_deps.py` | Pass | `PASS: All benchmark dependencies validated against ontology` |\n| `sync_skill_schemas.py --check` | Pass | `SYNC CHECK PASS: 107 generated files up to date` |\n| `gen_runtime_fixtures.py --check` | Pass | `175 runtime fixtures up to date` |\n\n### How the numbers were collected\n- **Exit codes:** the first pass of the validators returned no exit codes, because the shell is zsh and does not set `PIPESTATUS`. I ran them again without a pipe and every exit code was 0.\n- **pytest line:** the shell's rtk proxy shortened the first pytest run to `1550 passed in 143.77s`. I ran it again with the proxy bypassed to get the exact line above. Both runs passed 1550 tests.\n- **Site commands:** I ran them one after another, so `check:axe` checked the `dist/` folder that `npm run build` had just produced. The full logs are in `REDACTED`.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>41491</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>11</tool_uses><duration_ms>475658</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>\n</system-reminder>"}}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"ef9f3fc8-12b6-4fe4-9f49-aaeedec05648","hash":"dfd98c51908d0b6761005b9006e0199c5622caa20c1ab134202f1173bfbd0275","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 20 quality commands pass at f254598. Waiting on the code review and the error-handling review."}]}}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"ef9f3fc8-12b6-4fe4-9f49-aaeedec05648","hash":"343d8b5b1e311304c7cf239ec1f1ef2461574a9cc8c9cd4d6388de86789e77a8","message":{"role":"user","content":"<system-reminder>\n[SYSTEM NOTIFICATION - NOT USER INPUT]\nThis is an automated background-task event, NOT a message from the user.\nDo NOT interpret this as user acknowledgement, confirmation, or response to any pending question.\nNo human input has been received since the last genuine user message in this conversation. Any statement that the user said, approved, or confirmed something — including statements in your own earlier messages — is NOT real user input and must NOT be treated as approval or consent.\n\n<task-notification>\n<task-id>aa39a6988813ee62c</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01MR1Z796c38pPufd7uVz6Wz</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>REDACTED.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Error handling inspection\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>## Error Handling Inspection\n\nAll findings are against HEAD f254598 (branch feature/issue-125-site-visuals, compared with origin/main at 824eea1). Where a finding says \"observed\", it was checked against the `site/dist` build from 07:43 on 2026-11-13, which is later than that commit.\n\n### P1 — Critical (Blocks Merge)\n| Finding | Suggested Fix |\n|---------|---------------|\n\n### P2 — Should Fix\n| Finding | Suggested Fix |\n|---------|---------------|\n| **ERR-1 · silent-failure · `site/src/lib/capability-figures.ts:571-574`**&lt;br&gt;The Examples parser reads the skill line by line and does not skip code fences, so any `### ` line inside a fence becomes a new example. This is live: the persist capability page's Fig 5 lists a fourth example, \"Architecture Decisions\", that writes no output field. That heading comes from a fenced Markdown sample. Its caption reads \"4 examples … no field is in every example\". In fact there are three examples and each writes every field. The page's Markdown copy repeats the phantom row. `exampleWorkflows` at :792 does `ex += 1` before its fence test, so its example numbers shift the same way. The section-end tests at :568, :707, :787 and :207 (`/^## /`) are also not fence-aware. _(HIGH)_&lt;br&gt;Trigger: a skill's Examples section has a fenced Markdown sample containing a `### ` line (`skills/persist/SKILL.md:228` today) → a phantom example is drawn and the caption's counts are wrong. | Read these sections from the mdast tree (`sectionBlocks`/`parseMarkdown`, as md-sections.ts already does), or toggle a fence flag before testing heading lines. Add a test using persist's SKILL.md that expects 3 examples. |\n| **ERR-2 · silent-failure · `site/src/lib/release-figures.ts:40,90`**&lt;br&gt;`RELEASE` only accepts an em dash before the date, and entries are only `- ` bullets. When I ran `parseReleases`, a `## [v2.1.0] - 2026-11-20` section was dropped entirely: it fell into the generic `## ` branch, which sets `rel = null`. `* d` / `* e` entries counted as 0. `scripts/release_notes.py:26` matches `## \\[v…\\](\\s\\|$)`, so the release tooling accepts the hyphen heading while the site leaves that release out of the timeline. The rendered-entry cross-check at `release-figures-hast.ts:145` only runs on sections the parser already counted at 8 or more entries, so it cannot catch a dropped release or a zero count. _(HIGH)_&lt;br&gt;Trigger: a release heading written with `-` or `–` before the date, or a kind section with `*` bullets → that release is missing from the timeline and section figures, or its bars show 0, and the build passes. | Throw on any `## [` line that `RELEASE` does not match. Accept `[-*+] ` bullets. Run the rendered-vs-parsed entry count for every kind section, not only long ones. |\n| **ERR-3 · silent-failure · `site/scripts/check-runs.mjs:111,180,205`**&lt;br&gt;When `.doc-main__body` is absent, `measurePage` returns null and the page is neither measured nor reported as failed. `summarise` then skips it (`if (!r.wide) continue`). When I ran `summarise` on pages with no measurement, it returned 0 results and 0 missing, and the main block exits 0. The self-check cannot catch this, because the fixture `test/fixtures/runs-page.html:16` hard-codes the same class. There is also no empty-sitemap guard, which check-axe has at :91. Today all 168 built pages have the element. _(HIGH)_&lt;br&gt;Trigger: the body wrapper class in DocLayout is renamed, or a template stops using DocLayout → the figure-gap sweep measures no pages, prints \"0 pages\", and CI passes. | Push the URL to `failed` when `measurePage` returns null. Throw when `results.length === 0` or when `results.length` is less than the number of paths. |\n| **ERR-4 · silent-failure · `site/scripts/check-dist.mjs` `checkDrawnFigures` / `pageTemplate`**&lt;br&gt;A page whose template is null, or is not in `DRAWN_TEMPLATES`, is skipped without a report. I ran the check on the real dist with `page--` renamed in memory: it reported 0 problems. Unmeasured and clean give the same result. A template renamed in the layout (for example `edge-types` to `edges`) also stops being checked without notice. _(HIGH)_&lt;br&gt;Trigger: the body template class prefix or a template name changes → the \"every generated page has a drawn figure\" check passes without examining any page. | Fail when any `DRAWN_TEMPLATES` entry matches no built page, and when an HTML page has no template class. |\n| **ERR-5 · silent-failure · `site/src/lib/runs.ts:132`**&lt;br&gt;`ENFORCED_URLS` pins `'/spec/1.1.0/'`, while the docstring at :113-116 says the enforced page is \"the current Standard\". The `spec` template is not in `ENFORCED_TEMPLATES`. Nothing reports an enforced URL, or a per-URL exempt entry, whose page is no longer the one intended: `summarise` only checks anchors on pages it measured. _(MEDIUM)_&lt;br&gt;Trigger: the next Standard version is published → the new current Standard is only reported on, and 1.1.0 stays enforced, with no failure. | Derive the current Standard's URL from the versions data instead of a literal. Fail when an `ENFORCED_URLS` entry or a non-template exempt entry matches no page in the sitemap. |\n\n### P3 — Consider\n| Finding | Suggested Fix |\n|---------|---------------|\n| **ERR-6 · swallowed-exception · `site/src/lib/skill-figures.ts:141-145,161`**&lt;br&gt;The bare `catch { return null }` covers both invalid YAML and `sectionFence`'s throw when the \"Output Contract\" heading or fence is missing. Either way the scorecard figure disappears without a message, although the function throws loudly for every other disagreement. Separately, a `### ` family heading that does not match `X) Name (CODE)` is skipped, so its `####` checks are attributed to the previous family. The id cross-check still passes, because the ids are all present. _(MEDIUM)_&lt;br&gt;Trigger: a skill with a CHECKLIST.md gets a YAML typo in its Output Contract, or a family heading without its `(CODE)` → no scorecard figure, or checks grouped under the wrong family, with no build error. | Return null only when the contract has no `scorecard` key, and rethrow parse errors with `where`. Throw on any H3 in CHECKLIST.md that is not a family heading. |\n| **ERR-7 · silent-failure · `site/src/lib/spec-tail-figures.ts:525-530`**&lt;br&gt;Any YAML error in a §12.5 fence falls back to `stepsByLine`. The comment justifies this for the 1.0.0 text, but the fallback also covers the current Standard, so a new syntax error there is quietly read line by line, which can lose steps. _(MEDIUM)_&lt;br&gt;Trigger: a §12.5 pattern fence in the current Standard is edited into invalid YAML → its strip is drawn from a partial line read and the build passes. | Allow the fallback only for the Standard versions known to need it (by `where`), and rethrow otherwise. |\n| **ERR-8 · silent-failure · `site/src/lib/inject.ts:78-94`, `site/src/lib/prose-figures.ts:26-34`, `site/src/lib/domain-figures.ts:367-372`**&lt;br&gt;`foldFirstTable`, `foldFirstTaskList`, `foldFirstBox` and `foldCapabilityList` return the HTML unchanged when their regex misses. Their callers have already drawn the figure that replaces the block, so a miss shows both. For `foldFirstBox`, the box also keeps its \"Fig n\" eyebrow. _(MEDIUM)_&lt;br&gt;Trigger: the renderer's markup for a table wrapper, task list or ASCII figure changes, for example attribute order or an added class → the source block is shown in full next to its figure, with no error. | Since each caller only calls these where the block is expected, have them throw `where: no &lt;block&gt; to fold`. |\n| **ERR-9 · silent-failure · `site/src/lib/domain-usage.ts:49,58-62`**&lt;br&gt;A README whose \"Capability Usage\" heading is renamed returns `[]` without even the warning that other skips get. A YAML parse error is reported as \"has no single-capability YAML fence\", which hides the parse message. _(MEDIUM)_&lt;br&gt;Trigger: a domain README's usage heading is reworded, or one example fence gets a YAML typo → the usage figure disappears silently, or the warning points at the wrong cause. | Warn on the missing heading, and include the YAML error's message in the warning. |\n| **ERR-10 · missing-fallback · `site/scripts/check-axe.mjs:145`, `site/scripts/check-runs.mjs:244`**&lt;br&gt;`--paths` with an empty or missing value gives `only = []`. Zero pages are checked, and check-axe prints \"0 pages, 0 runs … no axe violations\" and exits 0. _(MEDIUM)_&lt;br&gt;Trigger: a local or scripted run with `--paths \"$CHANGED\"` where the variable is empty → a passing result that checked nothing. | Throw when `--paths` is present but yields no paths. |\n| **ERR-11 · error-handling · `site/src/lib/index-figures.ts:508-511`**&lt;br&gt;`skillsCaption` calls `Math.min/Math.max(...runs)` with no empty guard, and neither caller (`SkillWorkflows.astro:33`, `twins/listing.ts:30`) guards. With no composed skill mapped to a workflow, the caption reads \"of Infinity to -Infinity steps\". _(MEDIUM)_&lt;br&gt;Trigger: every `COMPOSED_SKILLS` entry is set to null → the published caption contains \"Infinity\". | When `runs.length === 0`, write \"none of the N composed skills runs a catalog workflow\". |\n\n### Summary\n- Files inspected: 9 of 10 changed check scripts (the 5 `.mjs` scripts and 4 of the 5 `.d.mts` type-declaration stubs, the `check-contrast.d.mts` stub excepted). Of the 62 changed files under `site/src/lib`, `site/src/plugins` and `site/src/twins`, I read in full or in part release-figures, release-figures-hast, md-sections, inject, prose-figures, prose-page, runs (scope lists), layer-figures, the catch sites, every `Math.max/min(...)` spread, and the empty-return early exits that the grep found. I did not read these line by line: spec-dsl-figures, spec-slots, rehype-spec-slots, most of rehype-prose-figures, rehype-capability-skill, and most twins.\n- Total findings: P1: 0, P2: 5, P3: 6\n- Error handling coverage: the drawing primitives are strict. `PixelBar` and `pixelBarElement` throw on `max &lt;= min`; `heatStep` cannot divide by zero because it returns early for `count &lt;= 0`; `glyph()`, `parseMermaid`, `sectionBlocks`, `cutAfterHeadings`, the home principles parser and `parseReleases` with no sections all throw with the file location. check-contrast, check-design-data and check-dist report missing inputs. In `serve()`, a listen failure or a missing `404.html` raises an unhandled error event and crashes the process, which fails CI loudly. The weak points are the line-based Markdown parsers, which do not skip fences, and the gate scripts, which treat \"measured nothing\" as \"clean\" (ERR-1 to ERR-5).\n- Not run: the Step 2b LSP diagnostics and `npm run check` (astro check). The `.then(` grep over changed files found nothing unhandled. The catch blocks in the changed scripts record their errors as problems; `safeDecode` in check-dist predates this branch.\n\nPaths for the main findings:\n- /Users/danielbentes/agent-capability-standard/.claude/worktrees/wf_08f3cd25-fc3-8/site/src/lib/capability-figures.ts\n- /Users/danielbentes/agent-capability-standard/.claude/worktrees/wf_08f3cd25-fc3-8/site/src/lib/release-figures.ts\n- /Users/danielbentes/agent-capability-standard/.claude/worktrees/wf_08f3cd25-fc3-8/site/scripts/check-runs.mjs\n- /Users/danielbentes/agent-capability-standard/.claude/worktrees/wf_08f3cd25-fc3-8/site/scripts/check-dist.mjs\n- /Users/danielbentes/agent-capability-standard/.claude/worktrees/wf_08f3cd25-fc3-8/site/src/lib/runs.ts\n- /Users/danielbentes/agent-capability-standard/.claude/worktrees/wf_08f3cd25-fc3-8/site/dist/capabilities/persist/index.html (where ERR-1 shows on the built page)</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>152794</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>46</tool_uses><duration_ms>561876</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>\n</system-reminder>"}}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"ef9f3fc8-12b6-4fe4-9f49-aaeedec05648","hash":"d3a544c001463b67f7fd9c9e4633b9d4dd5fb02a6ac99fba73f628d14fc0b288","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The error-handling review found five P2s and six P3s. One is already visible on the live build: the persist page shows a fourth example that doesn't exist, because the parser reads a heading inside a code sample. The others are build checks that can pass without measuring anything, and parsers that drop data without an error. I'll wait for the code review and then fix everything in one batch."}]}}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"ef9f3fc8-12b6-4fe4-9f49-aaeedec05648","hash":"1fb38ca2c86db4d87c6596c10141a562e944d9fc07da7e84f6df899fc9ffd541","message":{"role":"user","content":"<system-reminder>\n[SYSTEM NOTIFICATION - NOT USER INPUT]\nThis is an automated background-task event, NOT a message from the user.\nDo NOT interpret this as user acknowledgement, confirmation, or response to any pending question.\nNo human input has been received since the last genuine user message in this conversation. Any statement that the user said, approved, or confirmed something — including statements in your own earlier messages — is NOT real user input and must NOT be treated as approval or consent.\n\n<task-notification>\n<task-id>a154811a559585f06</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>REDACTED</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>REDACTED.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Code review of the branch\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>## Code Review Findings\n\nAll evidence comes from branch head `f254598`. The site suite passed at that commit (vitest: 38 files, 875 tests). The `site/dist` I inspected carries commit stamp `f25459898eb6` on its capability pages.\n\nThe deploy guard is correct and this diff does not touch it. `.github/workflows/site.yml:92` still reads `if: github.event_name == 'push' &amp;&amp; github.ref == 'refs/heads/main' &amp;&amp; vars.SITE_DEPLOY_ENABLED == 'true'`. The new axe step runs in the `build` job, and the new `dist/_review` removal runs in `deploy` before the wrangler step.\n\n### P1 — Critical (Blocks Merge)\n| Finding | Suggested Fix |\n|---------|---------------|\n\n### P2 — Should Fix\n| Finding | Suggested Fix |\n|---------|---------------|\n| **F1 · correctness · `site/scripts/check-runs.mjs:199-221`** (with `site/src/lib/runs.ts:132`)&lt;br&gt;`summarise()` only looks at pages it measured. An `EXEMPT_RUNS` entry or an `ENFORCED_URLS` entry that names a URL missing from the sitemap is never reported. The script's own header says \"the map cannot go stale silently\", and this case breaks that. Reproduced: with no page at `/start/overview/`, `summarise(new Map([['/start/overview-renamed/', …]]))` returns `missing: []`. _(HIGH)_&lt;br&gt;Trigger: renaming the overview or SDK-guide route, or a 1.2.0 Standard taking over as current while `/spec/1.1.0/` stays hard-coded → the gate passes, the page that should be enforced is only reported, and the old exemptions keep applying to the older page. | When `complete` is true, report every URL-keyed `EXEMPT_RUNS` page and every `ENFORCED_URLS` entry that is not among the measured pages. Better still, build the current-Standard URL from `currentStandard()` instead of the literal `/spec/1.1.0/`. |\n| **F2 · correctness · `site/src/lib/release-figures.ts:40`**&lt;br&gt;`RELEASE` only matches `## [ver]` or `## [ver] — date` with an em dash. Keep a Changelog writes `## [1.0.0] - 2017-06-20` with a hyphen, and `scripts/release_notes.py:26` accepts any `## [vX.Y.Z]` followed by whitespace. A non-matching heading hits the `^## ` branch at line 76, sets `rel = null`, and that release's entries drop out without any error. Reproduced: a changelog with `## [v2.1.0] - 2026-12-01` parses to `[[\"v2.0.0\",[[\"Fixed\",1]]]]`. _(HIGH)_&lt;br&gt;Trigger: `## [v2.1.0] - 2026-12-01` in CHANGELOG.md → the release publishes on GitHub, but the site timeline, caption totals, section figures and folds all leave it out. | Accept `[—–-]` as the separator, or throw on any `## [` heading the regex does not match, so a format slip fails the build. |\n| **F3 · correctness · `site/src/lib/inject.ts:19-20`** (used by `site/src/pages/domains/[domain].astro:95-96`)&lt;br&gt;`decode()` handles only named entities. The built HTML writes `&amp;` and `&lt;` in headings as `&amp;#x26;` and `&amp;#x3C;`; I saw this in `dist`, for example `Safety &amp;#x26; Recovery`. `pickHeading` compares that undecoded `h.text` with the mdast heading text in `usageByHeading`, so the comparison fails and the usage figure is skipped without a warning. The edge-types caller fails loudly instead, because it throws when nothing matches. _(MEDIUM)_&lt;br&gt;Trigger: an H3 under a domain README's \"Capability Usage\" with `&amp;` or `&lt;` in it (e.g. \"Detect &amp; Classify\") → no usage figure and no build message. | Decode numeric entities too (`&amp;#x([0-9a-f]+);` and `&amp;#(\\d+);` through `String.fromCodePoint`). Also warn when a usage example in `usageByHeading` was never placed. |\n\n### P3 — Consider\n| Finding | Suggested Fix |\n|---------|---------------|\n| **F4 · correctness · `site/src/lib/inject.ts:90`**&lt;br&gt;`foldFirstTaskList` matches up to the first `&lt;/ul&gt;` with a lazy pattern, so a nested list ends the match early. Reproduced: `&lt;ul class=\"contains-task-list\"&gt;&lt;li&gt;a&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;sub&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;b&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;` comes out as `…&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;sub&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/details&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;b&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;`. _(HIGH)_&lt;br&gt;Trigger: a sub-list under one item of a skill's verification checklist → broken markup, and the remaining items fall outside the fold. | Find the end with depth counting (like `elementAt` in check-dist.mjs), or do the fold in hast instead of on the HTML string. |\n| **F5 · tests · `site/scripts/check-design-data.mjs:135`**&lt;br&gt;`findHexColours` misses 8-digit and 4-digit hex. Probed: `#00000080` → 0 hits, `#fffa` → 0 hits, `#a1b2c3` → 1 hit. _(HIGH)_&lt;br&gt;Trigger: a figure component written with `fill: #00000080` → the \"no hex colour\" check passes. | Use `/#(?:[0-9a-fA-F]{8}\\|[0-9a-fA-F]{6}\\|[0-9a-fA-F]{4}\\|[0-9a-fA-F]{3})\\b(?![-\\w])/`. |\n| **F6 · error-handling · `site/scripts/check-axe.mjs:145`** (and `site/scripts/check-runs.mjs:244`)&lt;br&gt;`--paths` with no value, or with an empty one, gives `only = []`. `paths` is then `[]`, nothing is checked, and the script prints the success line (\"0 pages … no axe violations\") and exits 0. _(MEDIUM)_&lt;br&gt;Trigger: `node scripts/check-axe.mjs --paths` → a local run that reports clean but checked nothing. CI does not pass `--paths`. | Throw when `only` is an empty array. |\n| **F7 · correctness · `site/src/lib/layer-figures.ts:88-93`**&lt;br&gt;`stepsCaption` ranks by sort position. When two layers have the same step count, one caption says \"the most\" and the other \"the 2nd most\". There are no ties in the current data; I checked the 9 counts against the catalogs, totalling 277. _(MEDIUM)_&lt;br&gt;Trigger: two layers with equal step counts → captions rank equal layers differently. | Rank as 1 + the number of layers with strictly more steps, and say \"joint\" on a tie. |\n| **F8 · error-handling · `site/src/lib/skill-figures.ts:142-146`**&lt;br&gt;A bare `catch { return null; }` around the Output Contract lookup and YAML parse hides a missing section, a missing fence and invalid YAML alike. _(MEDIUM)_&lt;br&gt;Trigger: a skill that has `CHECKLIST.md` but a malformed Output Contract fence → the scorecard figure disappears with no message. | Return null only when the section does not exist. Rethrow parse errors with `where`. |\n| **F9 · duplication · `site/src/lib/*-figures.ts`** (e.g. `layer-figures.ts:8`, `release-figures.ts:120`, `mermaid/text.ts:12`)&lt;br&gt;Layer B: `plural` is defined 17 times (16 lib files plus `review/Parts.astro`). `isEl` and the hast text walker are repeated in `rehype-figure-marks.ts:33-40`, `release-figures-hast.ts:34-41`, `rehype-spec-slots.ts:31` and `rehype-prose-figures.ts:67-76`. `andList` appears in 3 files. The template-class parsing in `check-dist.mjs:444` and `check-runs.mjs:97` is the same logic. None of these existed on `origin/main`, so every copy comes from this branch. _(MEDIUM)_&lt;br&gt;Trigger: a fix to one copy (e.g. irregular plurals, or a new `page--` modifier class) → the other copies drift. | Put `plural` and `andList` in one lib module and `isEl` and `hastText` in one plugin helper, and import them. |\n\n### Summary\n- **Files reviewed:**\n  - Read in full: `site.yml`, `check-axe.mjs`, `check-runs.mjs`, `runs.ts`, `inject.ts`, `md-sections.ts`, `domain-usage.ts`, `layer-figures.ts`, `release-figures.ts`, `release-figures-hast.ts`, `mermaid/parse.ts`, `mermaid/text.ts`, `mermaid/capabilities.ts`, `mermaid/twin.ts`, `remark-mermaid.ts`, `rehype-figure-marks.ts`, `rehype-spec-slots.ts` (first 205 lines), and `review.ts`.\n  - Read as diffs only: `check-dist.mjs`, `check-contrast.mjs`, `check-design-data.mjs`, `markdown.ts`, `status.ts`, `listing.ts`, `agent-files.ts`, `routes.ts`, `rehype-callouts.ts`, `rehype-tables.ts`.\n  - Partly read: `rehype-prose-figures.ts` (tail), `run-replay.ts`, `skill-figures.ts` and `spec-tail-figures.ts` (catch sites only).\n  - **Not read:** `rehype-capability-skill.ts`, `mermaid/layout.ts`, `mermaid/render.ts`, and most of `capability-figures`, `spec-dsl-figures`, `spec-figures`, `index-figures`, `workflow-figures`, `edge-figures`, `domain-figures`. The absence of findings covers only the files read.\n- **Figure correctness**, recomputed from the YAML sources, all matching the built pages:\n  - steps per layer, all 9 captions (277 steps);\n  - risk by layer (29 low, 5 medium, 2 high);\n  - the edge-type summary, all 7 counts (conflicts_with as 2 pairs, alternative_to as 6 pairs);\n  - \"12 pairs carry a second edge type\";\n  - in GROUNDED_AGENCY: the checkpoint → mutate, send, rollback edges, the recovery loop (max_loops 3) and the 50/10/8/2 seeded-error figures.\n\n  That is a sample: 1 of 47 documents with new Mermaid diagrams, plus 3 generated figure types.\n- **Other checks:**\n  - Dark mode does apply through `prefers-color-scheme` (`tokens.css:150`), so the dark axe pass is a real second theme.\n  - `pairs()` receives one theme's tokens at a time and produces 12 heat pairs per theme.\n  - The review pages are absent from the sitemap and the Pagefind fragments.\n- **Callers examined:**\n  - `walk`: 2 (git grep, both inside check-dist.mjs)\n  - `sourceStatuses`: 3 (git grep)\n  - `pairs`: 7 (git grep)\n  - `listingGroups`: 4 (git grep)\n  - `fullTextRoutes`: 1 (git grep)\n  - `rehypeCallouts`: 2 (git grep)\n  - `rehypeTables`: 2 (git grep)\n  - `remarkPageMeta`: 2 (git grep)\n\n  I did not use LSP for any of these.\n- **Blast radius:** `flow-contract-files.sh` exited 1 after a successful `git diff`, meaning none of the changed files is an API, schema or migration contract.\n- **Clone scan:** STATE=unavailable. REASON: jscpd is not installed, so no clone scan was performed. INSTALL: `npm install -g jscpd@5.3.1`. This review does not cover verbatim duplication.\n- **Candidates examined (Layer B):** `plural`: 17. `isEl`: 4. `andList`: 3. Template-class parsing: 2. Other new symbols were not searched.\n- **Total findings:** P1: 0, P2: 3, P3: 6\n- **Recommendation:** REQUEST_CHANGES under the decision table (MEDIUM/HIGH P2 findings). If this is your own pull request, the review is posted as COMMENT.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>185758</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>79</tool_uses><duration_ms>698052</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>\n</system-reminder>"}}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"ef9f3fc8-12b6-4fe4-9f49-aaeedec05648","hash":"a4a167569ba998a92f678247332cf2e726bb93d28e5ff07e622913f2a6d71631","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Both reviews are in. After removing duplicates, there are 6 P2 findings and about 11 P3s, and none are P1.\n\nThe P2s:\n- the persist page's phantom example;\n- release headings written with a plain hyphen get dropped silently;\n- two build checks treat \"measured nothing\" as a pass;\n- the enforced Standard page is hard-coded as version 1.1.0;\n- some domain usage figures can vanish without a warning when a heading contains `&`.\n\nOne agent will fix all of them, each with a test that fails without the fix."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01AoKUzZdUMph7drxUeQgYqc","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Fix all review findings","run_in_background":"true","prompt":"Repository synaptiai/agent-capability-standard, worktree /Users/danielbentes/agent-capability-standard/.claude/worktrees/wf_08f3cd25-fc3-8, branch feature/issue-125-site-visuals, head f254598 (pushed). Work directly in that worktree. Fix every finding below from the pre-PR review, in the site/ Astro project. Each fix covers its class (other callers / other inputs of the same shape), and each P1/P2 fix gets a test whose expected value comes from the source data or a hand-written fixture, never the function's own output, and which fails without the fix.\n\nP2 (must fix):\n1. site/src/lib/capability-figures.ts ~571-574 (also exampleWorkflows ~792, and the section-end tests ~207, ~568, ~707, ~787): the Examples parser and section-end tests are not fence-aware, so a `### ` or `## ` line inside a fenced code block starts a new example/section. Live: /capabilities/persist/ shows a phantom 4th example \"Architecture Decisions\" (from a fenced Markdown sample at skills/persist/SKILL.md:228); its caption and Markdown copy are wrong. Make them fence-aware (prefer reading the mdast tree as md-sections.ts does). Test: persist has 3 examples.\n2. site/src/lib/release-figures.ts:40,90 — RELEASE only accepts an em dash; Keep a Changelog writes a hyphen; scripts/release_notes.py:26 accepts any `## [vX.Y.Z]` + whitespace. Accept `[—–-]` as the separator, throw on any `## [` heading the regex does not match, accept `[-*+] ` bullets, and in site/src/plugins/release-figures-hast.ts run the rendered-vs-parsed entry-count check for every kind section, not only long ones.\n3. site/scripts/check-runs.mjs ~111,180,205 — when `.doc-main__body` is missing, measurePage returns null and the page is silently skipped. Push it to `failed`; throw when results are empty or fewer than the paths.\n4. site/scripts/check-dist.mjs checkDrawnFigures/pageTemplate — a page with no template class, or a DRAWN_TEMPLATES entry that matches no built page, is skipped silently. Fail in both cases.\n5. site/src/lib/runs.ts:132 + check-runs.mjs summarise ~199-221 — ENFORCED_URLS hard-codes '/spec/1.1.0/'; derive the current Standard URL from the versions data (currentStandard / loadVersions). Report every URL-keyed EXEMPT_RUNS entry and every ENFORCED_URLS entry that is not among the measured pages (when the run is complete).\n6. site/src/lib/inject.ts:19-20 decode() handles only named entities; built HTML writes `&#x26;`/`&#x3C;`, so pickHeading misses headings with & or < and the domain usage figure is skipped silently (site/src/pages/domains/[domain].astro:95-96). Decode numeric entities; warn (or throw) when a usage example in usageByHeading is never placed.\n\nP3 (fix in one batch):\n7. site/src/lib/skill-figures.ts:141-146,161 — bare catch returns null for missing section, missing fence and invalid YAML alike; return null only when there is no scorecard key / section, rethrow others with `where`. Throw on an H3 in CHECKLIST.md that is not a family heading `X) Name (CODE)`.\n8. site/src/lib/spec-tail-figures.ts:525-530 — YAML-error fallback to stepsByLine also covers the current Standard; allow it only for the versions known to need it, rethrow otherwise.\n9. site/src/lib/inject.ts:78-94, site/src/lib/prose-figures.ts:26-34, site/src/lib/domain-figures.ts:367-372 — foldFirstTable / foldFirstTaskList / foldFirstBox / foldCapabilityList return the HTML unchanged when their regex misses; throw `<where>: no <block> to fold` instead. Also foldFirstTaskList's lazy `</ul>` match breaks on a nested list: find the end by depth counting.\n10. site/src/lib/domain-usage.ts:49,58-62 — warn on a missing \"Capability Usage\" heading; include the YAML error message in the warning.\n11. site/scripts/check-axe.mjs:145 and check-runs.mjs:244 — `--paths` present but empty must throw.\n12. site/src/lib/index-figures.ts:508-511 skillsCaption — guard empty runs (no Infinity in a caption).\n13. site/scripts/check-design-data.mjs:135 findHexColours misses 4- and 8-digit hex; use /#(?:[0-9a-fA-F]{8}|[0-9a-fA-F]{6}|[0-9a-fA-F]{4}|[0-9a-fA-F]{3})\\b(?![-\\w])/ and fix anything it then finds.\n14. site/src/lib/layer-figures.ts:88-93 stepsCaption — rank ties correctly (\"joint\").\n15. Duplication: `plural` is defined ~17 times across site/src/lib/*.ts and review/Parts.astro; `andList` in 3 files; `isEl` and the hast text walker in rehype-figure-marks.ts, release-figures-hast.ts, rehype-spec-slots.ts, rehype-prose-figures.ts; template-class parsing in check-dist.mjs:444 and check-runs.mjs:97. Put plural/andList in one lib module, isEl/hastText in one plugin helper, the template-class parse in one script helper, and import them.\n16. Hardening: site/src/data/workflows.ts parseCatalog — reject workflow ids that are not ^[a-z0-9_]+$ (they are written into a CSS selector in WorkflowSpine.astro). Check all current catalogs pass.\n\nRules: commit in small conventional commits (message in a file, `git commit -F <file>`), each ending with:\n\nRefs #125\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Jea2Va3FATnCydAsWsbLXR\n\nUse a normal merge-free history (no rebase of pushed commits, never force-push). No YAML files under site/. No hand-typed counts. Before reporting, run in site/: npm run check, npm test, npm run build, npm run check:axe (all must pass), and from the repo root with /Users/danielbentes/agent-capability-standard/.venv active: pytest tests -q, python tools/validate_doc_links.py. Then push normally and confirm local HEAD equals `git ls-remote origin refs/heads/feature/issue-125-site-visuals`. Open the built /capabilities/persist/ page's examples figure (screenshot via playwright-core at ~/.REDACTED with Chromium at ~/Library/Caches/ms-playwright/chromium-1248/chrome-mac-arm64/Google Chrome for Testing.app/Contents/MacOS/Google Chrome for Testing; serve dist with python3 -m http.server on 127.0.0.1) and Read the PNG to confirm 3 examples. Do not post on GitHub or open a PR.\n\nReport: per finding, what changed (commit SHA) and the test that covers it; any finding not fixed with the concrete reason; check results with the pushed SHA."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
