{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"ef9f3fc8-12b6-4fe4-9f49-aaeedec05648","hash":"0a0abcd2e44bc7ec2443e5ed156c18a95622797f7241d62daaaeb9653067a9d0","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Everything passes. I'm committing the five regression fixes and pushing."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01CDbtLp72ibQsckWSMBxez8","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"REDACTED.txt","content":"fix(site): five regressions from the review fixes\n\n- Release notes: a list line inside a code fence no longer counts as an\n  entry or extends one, matching the release bars, so the rendered-count\n  check cannot fail on a valid changelog.\n- decodeEntities: only \"&#x…;\" is a hex reference; \"&excl;\" and \"&exist;\"\n  are left as they are instead of decoding wrongly or throwing.\n- Domain usage: the four domain READMEs written without a \"Capability\n  Usage\" section are listed in NO_USAGE_SECTION; any other README without\n  one, or a listed one that gains one, fails the build. No warning on\n  every build for an allowed state. A test reads the list from the files.\n- Workflow ids: the Standard names no pattern for workflow names, so the\n  site no longer restricts them; the workflow page escapes the id where\n  it writes it into a quoted CSS string inside <style>.\n- check-design-data skips code blocks with the same codeLines the figure\n  code uses, now in anchors.ts so plain Node can load it, instead of a\n  second hand-written fence parser.\n\nRefs #125\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Jea2Va3FATnCydAsWsbLXR\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0137V76W4ox1NbGAmkb3tWn1","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/danielbentes/agent-capability-standard/.claude/worktrees/wf_08f3cd25-fc3-8 && git add site/scripts/check-design-data.mjs site/src/components/fig/WorkflowSpine.astro site/src/data/workflows.ts site/src/lib/anchors.ts site/src/lib/domain-usage.t