{"parentUuid":"ddb56c9d-255c-4474-8031-6865e5e25d1d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgzz8XxE5vj4rQZoB3tVZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Cp3gVdo7aiZyAFDsyvYqNk","name":"AskUserQuestion","input":{"questions":[{"question":"How far should the site go beyond being a static site? Today Cloudflare Pages serves plain files. Some checks need code that runs on each request: returning Markdown when an agent sends Accept: text/markdown, a Markdown 404 page, and Markdown for AI bot user agents. A docs MCP server (tools such as search_standard and get_capability) is worth about 10 more points and is the most useful item for coding agents.","header":"Scope","multiSelect":false,"options":[{"label":"Static + Pages Functions + docs MCP (Recommended)","description":"Do all the static fixes, add a few Pages Functions for Markdown negotiation and 404s, and run a read-only docs MCP server on Cloudflare at acs.synapti.ai/mcp. More moving parts on the deploy, and it is the biggest score gain."},{"label":"Static + Pages Functions","description":"Static fixes plus per-request Markdown negotiation and Markdown 404s. No MCP server."},{"label":"Static only","description":"Only files the build writes: discovery files, JSON-LD, Link headers in _headers, the .md fallbacks, a shorter llms.txt, frontmatter, the skills index. The smallest and safest change."}]},{"question":"Should the site publish the standard's data as a read-only JSON API with an OpenAPI description? This would cover the capabilities, edges, workflows, profiles and diagnostic codes, as static files such as /api/v1/capabilities.json, plus /openapi.json. The checks give an API and OpenAPI the most points, and agents could read the ontology without parsing YAML from GitHub.","header":"Data API","multiSelect":false,"options":[{"label":"Yes, static JSON + OpenAPI (Recommended)","description":"Built from the same loaders as the pages and versioned under /api/v1/. GET only, no keys, so the OAuth checks don't apply (the API is open)."},{"label":"No","description":"Agents keep using the Markdown copies and llms.txt."}]},{"question":"Should the site register in-page WebMCP tools (navigator.modelContext / document.modelContext), so a browser agent can call search, open a capability, or open a workflow on the page instead of clicking through it? This is an emerging browser API. The script does nothing in browsers that lack it.","header":"WebMCP","multiSelect":false,"options":[{"label":"Yes, read-only tools (Recommended)","description":"search_docs (Pagefind), get_capability, get_workflow and get_page_markdown, all read-only and marked readOnlyHint. A small script, loaded on every page."},{"label":"No","description":"Skip it until the API settles."}]},{"question":"The trust checks want /about, /contact and /privacy pages, and Organization JSON-LD with a contact point. I can write /about from the README. For /contact and /privacy I need facts I don't have: who to contact and what the site collects (as far as I can tell it sets no cookies and runs no analytics; Cloudflare logs requests). What should these pages use?","header":"Trust pages","multiSelect":false,"options":[{"label":"GitHub-only contact, no-tracking privacy note (Recommended)","description":"Contact goes through GitHub issues and discussions. The privacy page says the site sets no cookies and runs no analytics, and that Cloudflare processes request logs. The Organization is Synapti with the GitHub org as sameAs. No email or postal address."},{"label":"I'll give you an email","description":"Add a contact email (and an address if you want one) to /contact and the JSON-LD. Type it in the notes."},{"label":"Skip trust pages","description":"Leave out /about, /contact and /privacy."}]}]},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3371,"cache_read_input_tokens":551989,"output_tokens":2143,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":819},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3371,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2143,"cache_read_input_tokens":551989,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3371,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3371},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":11707,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01Cp3gVdo7aiZyAFDsyvYqNk":{"questions":[{"question":"How far should the site go beyond being a static site? Today Cloudflare Pages serves plain files. Some checks need code that runs on each request: returning Markdown when an agent sends Accept: text/markdown, a Markdown 404 page, and Markdown for AI bot user agents. A docs MCP server (tools such as search_standard and get_capability) is worth about 10 more points and is the most useful item for coding agents.","header":"Scope","multiSelect":false,"options":[{"label":"Static + Pages Functions + docs MCP (Recommended)","description":"Do all the static fixes, add a few Pages Functions for Markdown negotiation and 404s, and run a read-only docs MCP server on Cloudflare at acs.synapti.ai/mcp. More moving parts on the deploy, and it is the biggest score gain."},{"label":"Static + Pages Functions","description":"Static fixes plus per-request Markdown negotiation and Markdown 404s. No MCP server."},{"label":"Static only","description":"Only files the build writes: discovery files, JSON-LD, Link headers in _headers, the .md fallbacks, a shorter llms.txt, frontmatter, the skills index. The smallest and safest change."}]},{"question":"Should the site publish the standard's data as a read-only JSON API with an OpenAPI description? This would cover the capabilities, edges, workflows, profiles and diagnostic codes, as static files such as /api/v1/capabilities.json, plus /openapi.json. The checks give an API and OpenAPI the most points, and agents could read the ontology without parsing YAML from GitHub.","header":"Data API","multiSelect":false,"options":[{"label":"Yes, static JSON + OpenAPI (Recommended)","description":"Built from the same loaders as the pages and versioned under /api/v1/. GET only, no keys, so the OAuth checks don't apply (the API is open)."},{"label":"No","description":"Agents keep using the Markdown copies and llms.txt."}]},{"question":"Should the site register in-page WebMCP tools (navigator.modelContext / document.modelContext), so a browser agent can call search, open a capability, or open a workflow on the page instead of clicking through it? This is an emerging browser API. The script does nothing in browsers that lack it.","header":"WebMCP","multiSelect":false,"options":[{"label":"Yes, read-only tools (Recommended)","description":"search_docs (Pagefind), get_capability, get_workflow and get_page_markdown, all read-only and marked readOnlyHint. A small script, loaded on every page."},{"label":"No","description":"Skip it until the API settles."}]},{"question":"The trust checks want /about, /contact and /privacy pages, and Organization JSON-LD with a contact point. I can write /about from the README. For /contact and /privacy I need facts I don't have: who to contact and what the site collects (as far as I can tell it sets no cookies and runs no analytics; Cloudflare logs requests). What should these pages use?","header":"Trust pages","multiSelect":false,"options":[{"label":"GitHub-only contact, no-tracking privacy note (Recommended)","description":"Contact goes through GitHub issues and discussions. The privacy page says the site sets no cookies and runs no analytics, and that Cloudflare processes request logs. The Organization is Synapti with the GitHub org as sameAs. No email or postal address."},{"label":"I'll give you an email","description":"Add a contact email (and an address if you want one) to /contact and the JSON-LD. Type it in the notes."},{"label":"Skip trust pages","description":"Leave out /about, /contact and /privacy."}]}]}},"serverClassifierRequest":"caabad6a-b37a-432a-94b7-9cd2e21b8a18","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011Cgzz8UxeiEygrqM7wA5pB","requestRef":"ba2fc049-7860-4f7d-8356-450acd3917dd","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"f6c7f3e3-5072-4a82-abf6-3eecfbe9de48","timestamp":"2026-11-13T13:13:17.522Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-2","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ef9f3fc8-12b6-4fe4-9f49-aaeedec05648","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/danielbentes/agent-capability-standard/.claude/worktrees/wf_08f3cd25-fc3-8","sessionId":"ef9f3fc8-12b6-4fe4-9f49-aaeedec05648","version":"2.1.322","gitBranch":"feature/issue-125-site-visuals","slug":"i-just-came-across-imperative-newell"}
