about 10 more points and is the most useful item for coding agents.":"Static + Pages Functions + docs MCP (Recommended)","Should the site publish the standard's data as a read-only JSON API with an OpenAPI description? This would cover the capabilities, edges, workflows, profiles and diagnostic codes, as static files such as /api/v1/capabilities.json, plus /openapi.json. The checks give an API and OpenAPI the most points, and agents could read the ontology without parsing YAML from GitHub.":"Yes, static JSON + OpenAPI (Recommended)","Should the site register in-page WebMCP tools (navigator.modelContext / document.modelContext), so a browser agent can call search, open a capability, or open a workflow on the page instead of clicking through it? This is an emerging browser API. The script does nothing in browsers that lack it.":"Yes, read-only tools (Recommended)","The trust checks want /about, /contact and /privacy pages, and Organization JSON-LD with a contact point. I can write /about from the README. For /contact and /privacy I need facts I don't have: who to contact and what the site collects (as far as I can tell it sets no cookies and runs no analytics; Cloudflare logs requests). What should these pages use?":"GitHub-only contact, no-tracking privacy note (Recommended)"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"f6c7f3e3-5072-4a82-abf6-3eecfbe9de48","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"user_temporary","grantScope":"once","reasonCode":"unknown"},"session_id":"ef9f3fc8-12b6-4fe4-9f49-aaeedec05648","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/danielbentes/agent-capability-standard/.claude/worktrees/wf_08f3cd25-fc3-8","sessionId":"ef9f3fc8-12b6-4fe4-9f49-aaeedec05648","version":"2.1.322","gitBranch":"feature/issue-125-site-visuals","slug":"i-just-came-across-imperative-newell"}
