loper portal with API keys).\nWhere a check does not apply (payments, OAuth for an open read-only API), leave\nit and say so.\n\n## Live facts (2026-11-13)\n- robots.txt allows all; sitemap at /sitemap.xml has no lastmod.\n- /llms.txt is 31,727 chars (limit 30,000); /llms-full.txt 1.27 MB.\n- Home has canonical, lang, og:title/description/image, `<link rel=alternate type=text/markdown href=/index.md>`, one <main>; no og:type, no JSON-LD.\n- Markdown copies at <route>index.md (text/markdown via public/_headers). `<route-without-slash>.md` returns 404. Accept: text/markdown on / returns HTML.\n- No /.well-known files, no /about /contact /privacy, 404s are HTML only.\n- /spec/1.1.0/ has ~125K chars of text (page-token-budget check wants < ~100K).\n\n## Shared contract (all builders use exactly these paths)\n- Data API, static JSON, GET only, built from the site's existing loaders (src/data/*):\n  - /api/v1/index.json (list of resources, versions: standard, ontology, plugin)\n  - /api/v1/capabilities.json and /api/v1/capabilities/{id}.json\n  - /api/v1/layers.json\n  - /api/v1/edges.json\n  - /api/v1/workflows.json and /api/v1/workflows/{id}.json (id = catalog key)\n  - /api/v1/profiles.json and /api/v1/profiles/{domain}.json\n  - /api/v1/diagnostics.json\n  - /api/v1/pages.json (every page: url, markdown url, title, description, section, headings) — the MCP server and WebMCP search use it\n- /openapi.json (OpenAPI 3.1) describing those operations.\n- /.well-known/api-catalog (RFC 9727 linkset), /.well-known/ard.json and /.well-known/ai-catalog.json, /.well-known/agent-skills/index.json (+ skill files), /.well-known/mcp/server-card.json.\n- MCP endpoint: https://acs.synapti.ai/mcp (Streamable HTTP, stateless, read-only). Server card also at /mcp/server-card.\n- Markdown copies stay at <route>index.md; additionally <route-without-trailing-slash>.md and Accept: text/markdown on <route> serve the same copy.\n\n## Rules (all builders)\n- Original work; nothing from synapti.ai. Commits: conventional, message in a file with `git commit -F`, each ending with:\n\n      Refs #127\n\n      Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n      Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Jea2Va3FATnCydAsWsbLXR\n\n- Never force-push; no GitHub posts; no PRs; no merge to main.\n- Tests take expected values from the repository data or hand-written fixtures, never from the code under test.\n- Before reporting, in site/: npm ci (if needed), npm run check, npm test, npm run build, npm run check:axe — all pass. Repo root (activate /Users/danielbentes/agent-capability-standard/.venv): pytest tests -q, python tools/validate_doc_links.py.\n- Disk is tight (~12 GB free): remove your worktree's node_modules and dist when you are done; never copy the repo.\n- Report: commits, what you built, how you verified it (commands and their summary lines), what you did not do and why.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"0c7b1457-2492-4a42-9429-76a2bc10f040","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"session_id":"ef9f3fc8-12b6-4fe4-9f49-aaeedec05648","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/danielbentes/agent-capability-standard/.claude/worktrees/i127","sessionId":"ef9f3fc8-12b6-4fe4-9f49-aaeedec05648","version":"2.1.322","gitBranch":"feature/issue-127-agent-ready","slug":"i-just-came-across-imperative-newell"}
