{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-11-13T15:26:39.327Z","sessionId":"ef9f3fc8-12b6-4fe4-9f49-aaeedec05648","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>whwk5ko2x</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>REDACTED</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>REDACTED.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Dynamic workflow \"Issue #127: data API + OpenAPI, discovery files, Pages worker with Markdown negotiation and docs MCP server, WebMCP; integrate, review, fix\" completed</summary>\n<result>{\"built\":[\"I built the static data API, its OpenAPI 3.1 description, the RFC 9727 API catalog and a `/developers/` page. All required checks pass. The only exception is pytest, which needed the main checkout's compiled Rust core (details under Verification). Everything is committed locally and not pushed.\\n\\n**Worktree** `/Users/danielbentes/agent-capability-standard/.claude/worktrees/i127-api`, branch `feature/issue-127-api`, based on a4c00cd.\\n\\n**Commits**\\n- `a10e53c` feat(site): static JSON data API, OpenAPI 3.1 and an API page\\n- `0599b3e` fix(site): describe search_standard as the MCP server runs it\\n\\n**`/api/v1/pages.json` shape (the worker and WebMCP read this):**\\n```\\n{ api_version: \\\"v1\\\",\\n  version: {standard, standard_status, ontology, plugin},\\n  generated_from: {repository, commit, sources[]},\\n  count,\\n  pages: [ { url, markdown_url, title, description|null, section, section_label, group|null, source|null,\\n             headings: [ {level: 2|3, text} ] } ] }\\n```\\n- **Envelope:** every other file starts with the same envelope.\\n- **Collections:** these carry `count` plus a key named after the resource: `capabilities`, `layers`, `edges` (plus `edge_types`), `workflows`, `profiles` or `diagnostics`.\\n- **Single-item files:** these use `capability`, `workflow` or `profile`.\\n- **Field names:** snake_case; a field the source leaves unset is `null`, not missing.\\n- **URLs:** absolute (`page_url`, `markdown_url`, `api_url`).\\n- **Worker compatibility:** I read the worker worktree at 5d8eed6. Its `toPageEntry` reads `url`, `markdown_url` and `headings[].text`, and `unwrap(..., 'capability')` matches the single-capability key.\\n\\n**What I built**\\n- **Data API:** one registry in `site/src/lib/api.ts` lists the endpoints. The endpoint files, `/openapi.json` and the endpoint table on the page all read it.\\n  - The endpoints are the 11 in the shared contract.\\n  - The pages index is built in `site/src/lib/api-pages.ts`.\\n  - The paths that need no other code are in `site/src/lib/api-paths.ts`.\\n  - The build writes 79 JSON files.\\n- **`/openapi.json`** (`site/src/lib/openapi.ts`):\\n  - Each operation has a unique verb-led camelCase operationId, a summary and a description.\\n  - Path parameters are typed with an enum of the ids (36 capabilities, 28 workflows, 7 domains).\\n  - Response schemas are complete and set `additionalProperties: false`. All `$ref`s point inside the file.\\n  - The three operations with a path parameter declare an RFC 9457 problem+json 404. The fixed paths have no 404, since they cannot miss.\\n  - `info.description` says the API is open, needs no authentication, is read-only, is not paginated, and is versioned by path. It states the deprecation policy: a new major path, the old one kept for at least one minor version of the Standard, and Deprecation and Sunset headers sent first. There are no securitySchemes.\\n- **`/.well-known/api-catalog`:**\\n  - The linkset anchors the API at `https://acs.synapti.ai/api/v1/`, with a service-desc link to the OpenAPI file and a service-doc link to `/developers/`. A second entry lists the API as an item of the catalog. There is no `status` link, because no status endpoint exists.\\n  - `_headers` serves it as `application/linkset+json; profile=\\\"https://www.rfc-editor.org/info/rfc9727\\\"`.\\n  - `/api/v1` and `/api/v1/` redirect (302) to `index.json`.\\n  - `/api/*` and `/openapi.json` get `Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *`.\\n- **`/developers/` page:** titled \\\"Agent Capability Standard API and agent access\\\", in the Get started section with a new glyph.\\n  - It has three figures: ways to read the site, the endpoint table, and the MCP tools.\\n  - It has a Markdown copy, curl examples and the error and versioning rules.\\n  - It covers the Markdown copies and llms.txt, the MCP server at `https://acs.synapti.ai/mcp` with its four tools named exactly, and WebMCP.\\n  - It is linked from the home page's agent block and its Markdown copy, from every page's footer (with an OpenAPI link beside it), and from llms.txt through its route.\\n  - The run-length check now covers this page. The curl examples section is exempt as commands, which leaves a longest gap of 1290px against the 1800px limit.\\n- **check-dist:** a new `api` check requires the OpenAPI paths, expanded by their enums, to equal the JSON files in dist exactly. It also checks that every file parses, that the catalog's links resolve, and that the catalog header is present.\\n\\n**Verification** (on the tree that became a10e53c, re-run after 0599b3e; the built files carry commit a4c00cd because the build ran before the commit)\\n- `npm run check`: 0 errors; contrast passes (412 pairs); design-data reports no hand-typed counts.\\n- `npm test`: 950 passed in 40 files. This includes the new `test/api.test.ts`, which compares the payloads with line scans of the YAML and Markdown sources and checks the OpenAPI structure. It validates every payload against its schema with a small checker that throws on any keyword it does not know. `dist.test.ts` validates every built file, `pages.json` included, against the built `openapi.json`. `check-dist-script.test.ts` gained four defect cases.\\n- `npm run build`: \\\"check-dist: every check passed (files, links, md-links, copies, sitemap, figures, drawn, legends, review, api)\\\".\\n- `npm run check:axe`: 169 pages, 676 runs, no axe violations, no sideways scroll at 360px; no enforced page has a gap over 1800px.\\n- `python tools/validate_doc_links.py`: 315 references resolve.\\n- `pytest tests -q`: 1550 passed. This worktree has no compiled Rust core, so I symlinked the main checkout's `_core.abi3.so` (built from the same base) for the run and then removed it. I did not rebuild the core here.\\n- **Page and API viewed directly:** I opened a screenshot of `/developers/` at 1440px. On `npm run preview`, `/api/v1/capabilities/checkpoint.json` returned 200 and `index.json` returned the expected JSON. At 390px the screenshot was too small to read; that width rests on axe and the page width check. At that width the endpoint table scrolls inside its own frame.\\n\\n**Not done, and notes for the integrator**\\n- **The 404 claim depends on the worker.** Static Pages cannot return problem+json. The page's Errors paragraph (`ERRORS` in `developers.ts`) and the Errors bullet in the OpenAPI description are true only once the worker is deployed. The worker worktree at 5d8eed6 does serve it (`problemNotFound` in `site/src/worker/site.ts`).\\n- **WebMCP tool names are left out on purpose.** The webmcp builder's names (`search_docs`, `read_capability`, `read_workflow`, `read_page_markdown`) were still uncommitted, so the page describes the tools without naming them.\\n- **llms.txt is 31.2 KB, over the 30,000-character limit.** I left it to the discovery builder, who is reworking that file.\\n- **Shared files I edited** (small, additive): `public/_headers`, `routes.ts`, `DocLayout.astro`, `check-dist.mjs`, `redirects.ts`, `runs.ts`, `generated.ts`, `home.ts`, `index.astro`, `glyphs-pages.ts`, `twins/index.ts`.\\n- **Cleanup:** the worktree's `site/node_modules` and `site/dist` are deleted. The two screenshots are still in the scratchpad: `REDACTED.png` and `REDACTED.png`.\",\"I built 10 of the 11 discovery items. All checks pass on the final commit `bbf351a`. Item 11 (the size of the Standard's page) is reported below with no change, because every way to shrink it removes information.\\n\\n**Worktree:** `/Users/danielbentes/agent-capability-standard/.claude/worktrees/i127-discovery`\\n**Branch:** `feature/issue-127-discovery` (not pushed; `site/node_modules`, `site/dist` and a temporary link to the built Rust core are removed)\\n\\n**Commits**\\n- `dc811e9` feat(site): about, contact and privacy pages; AGENTS.md\\n- `c48\n... (truncated 48908 chars, full result in REDACTED.output)</result>\n<diagnostics>Per-agent results: /Users/danielbentes/.REDACTED.jsonl — one {\"type\":\"result\",...} line per completed agent with its full return value.\nIf the result above is empty or unexpected, Read this file BEFORE diagnosing — do not assume agents returned non-empty results.\nTo re-run with edited post-processing: Workflow({scriptPath: '/Users/danielbentes/.REDACTED.js', resumeFromRunId: 'wf_902fc277-7ab'}) — agents whose (prompt, opts) are unchanged replay from cache.</diagnostics>\n<usage><agent_count>7</agent_count><agents_done>7</agents_done><agents_error>0</agents_error><agents_skipped>0</agents_skipped><agents_empty_result>0</agents_empty_result><subagent_tokens>1606709</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>698</tool_uses><duration_ms>7236289</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
