{"parentUuid":"e86267b4-a41d-47b8-9f25-36cfd5adc2e2","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch1BMwnLrfgaCEy6sejwN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0117RTFzsCDypTrjpEE5eLC2","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='src/worker/entry.ts'; s=open(p).read()\na=\"\"\"// Cloudflare's documentation says _headers and _redirects are not applied to\n// responses a worker generates. The worker reads every file through\n// env.ASSETS.fetch, and under `wrangler pages dev` (4.160.0) those responses\n// do carry the _headers rules and the /spec/ redirect; that was checked\n// locally, not on the production project. The worker sets the headers of the\n// responses it builds itself.\"\"\"\nb=\"\"\"// Cloudflare's documentation says _headers and _redirects are not applied to\n// responses a worker returns, so the worker applies the same rules itself\n// (static-rules.ts).\"\"\"\nassert a in s; s=s.replace(a,b); open(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ncd .. && REDACTED && cat > $S/msg-rules.txt <<'EOF'\nfix(site): apply the _headers and _redirects rules in the worker\n\nCloudflare's documentation says _headers and _redirects are not applied\nto responses a Pages worker returns. Every page now goes through the\nworker, so on production the pages.dev noindex header, the API's CORS\nand JSON types, the API catalog's linkset type and the /spec/ redirect\ncould all be lost. The worker now applies the same rules to every file\nit passes through, and serves the redirects from the table that writes\n_redirects. A test checks the worker's rules equal public/_headers, and\nthree tests against an asset server that applies no rules failed before\nthis change.\n\nRefs #127\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Jea2Va3FATnCydAsWsbLXR\nEOF\ngit add -A site && git status --short && git commit -q -F $S/msg-rules.txt && git push -q origin feature/issue-127-agent-ready && git rev-parse HEAD && git ls-remote origin feature/issue-127-agent-ready","description":"Commit and push the worker static-rules fix"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":339,"cache_read_input_tokens":187905,"output_tokens":916,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":60},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":339,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":916,"cache_read_input_tokens":187905,"cache_creation_input_tokens":339,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":339},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":7030,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_0117RTFzsCDypTrjpEE5eLC2":{"command":"cd /Users/danielbentes/agent-capability-standard/.claude/worktrees/i127/site && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='src/worker/entry.ts'; s=open(p).read()\na=\"\"\"// Cloudflare's documentation says _headers and _redirects are not applied to\n// responses a worker generates. The worker reads every file through\n// env.ASSETS.fetch, and under `wrangler pages dev` (4.160.0) those responses\n// do carry the _headers rules and the /spec/ redirect; that was checked\n// locally, not on the production project. The worker sets the headers of the\n// responses it builds itself.\"\"\"\nb=\"\"\"// Cloudflare's documentation says _headers and _redirects are not applied to\n// responses a worker returns, so the worker applies the same rules itself\n// (static-rules.ts).\"\"\"\nassert a in s; s=s.replace(a,b); open(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ncd .. && REDACTED && cat > $S/msg-rules.txt <<'EOF'\nfix(site): apply the _headers and _redirects rules in the worker\n\nCloudflare's documentation says _headers and _redirects are not applied\nto responses a Pages worker returns. Every page now goes through the\nworker, so on production the pages.dev noindex header, the API's CORS\nand JSON types, the API catalog's linkset type and the /spec/ redirect\ncould all be lost. The worker now applies the same rules to every file\nit passes through, and serves the redirects from the table that writes\n_redirects. A test checks the worker's rules equal public/_headers, and\nthree tests against an asset server that applies no rules failed before\nthis change.\n\nRefs #127\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Jea2Va3FATnCydAsWsbLXR\nEOF\ngit add -A site && git status --short && git commit -q -F $S/msg-rules.txt && git push -q origin feature/issue-127-agent-ready && git rev-parse HEAD && git ls-remote origin feature/issue-127-agent-ready","description":"Commit and push the worker static-rules fix"}},"wireIngestContext":{"toolu_0117RTFzsCDypTrjpEE5eLC2":{"cwd":"/Users/danielbentes/agent-capability-standard/.claude/worktrees/i127/site"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"0136f407-4ab0-4a24-840c-3615372676ca","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Ch1BMwVxzqS5aBaEtt2RT","requestRef":"3ea2c074-06db-42f4-b8ff-4b736aab91b0","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"61dc5885-bd42-40d9-aac3-d2d72f0050de","timestamp":"2026-11-13T15:40:21.603Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-2","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ef9f3fc8-12b6-4fe4-9f49-aaeedec05648","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/danielbentes/agent-capability-standard/.claude/worktrees/i127/site","sessionId":"ef9f3fc8-12b6-4fe4-9f49-aaeedec05648","version":"2.1.322","gitBranch":"feature/issue-127-agent-ready","slug":"i-just-came-across-imperative-newell"}
