{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"ef9f3fc8-12b6-4fe4-9f49-aaeedec05648","hash":"c7ce4fd54b3a01830c9854fac5a4bce1678dc6825fd0db3c19223f4457bf72f2","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The real base is origin/main, since the local main is stale and inflates the count to 315 commits; the PR itself is 26 commits across 89 files. I'm running the review fan-out against origin/main...HEAD next.\n\n","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01N4qcYa9BinZxPU7H66q6cu","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Code review of PR diff","subagent_type":"flow:code-reviewer","prompt":"Working directory: /Users/danielbentes/agent-capability-standard/.claude/worktrees/i127 (branch feature/issue-127-agent-ready, HEAD 11ef8cc). Review `git diff origin/main...HEAD` (NOT local main, which is stale) for code quality, logic correctness, edge cases and security. Scope: issue #127 (`gh issue view 127`), making the docs site usable by AI agents: static JSON API + OpenAPI (site/src/lib/api.ts, openapi.ts, api-pages.ts), discovery files (agent-files.ts, resource-catalog.ts, agent-skills.ts, structured-data.ts, page-dates.ts), a Cloudflare Pages advanced-mode worker (site/src/worker/*: Markdown negotiation, MCP server over Streamable HTTP, static-rules.ts re-applying _headers/_redirects), WebMCP tools (site/src/lib/webmcp.ts), /developers page, about/contact/privacy pages (docs/site/*.md). An independent review already ran on c24b7af; its 9 findings were fixed (developers table wrap, search_standard scoring, MCP body size streaming, // path redirect, media types, read_page paging, tool name alignment, /mcp error fallback). Focus on what is still wrong. Read-only: do not edit files, commit or push. Do not run npm ci or builds (site/node_modules exists; `cd site && npx vitest run <file>` is fine). Return P1/P2/P3 findings, each with file:line, a confidence (HIGH/MEDIUM/LOW), a trigger (the concrete input or state that produces the wrong behaviour), and a suggested fix. Only report findings you can tie to the code.","run_in_background":"true"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HmmDrk7Z8MNCxc27Pek3kE","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Security review of PR diff","subagent_type":"flow:security-reviewer","prompt":"Working directory: /Users/danielbentes/agent-capability-standard/.claude/worktrees/i127 (branch feature/issue-127-agent-ready, HEAD 11ef8cc). Review `git diff origin/main...HEAD` (NOT local main, which is stale) for OWASP Top 10, secrets, input validation, injection, SSRF, path traversal, header injection, CORS, XSS, dependency risk. Key surface: site/src/worker/* is a public Cloudflare Pages worker (Markdown negotiation, canonical Link headers built from paths, an MCP JSON-RPC server at /mcp reading request bodies, tools that read site files by id/path), site/src/lib/webmcp.ts (in-page tools registered via document.modelContext), JSON-LD/structured data emitted in HTML, and site/package.json dependency changes. The site is read-only, no auth, no cookies by design. Read-only: do not edit, commit or push. Return P1/P2/P3 findings with file:line, confidence (HIGH/MEDIUM/LOW), a concrete trigger (request or input), and a fix; DEP- findings for dependencies with category=dependency. Only report what you can tie to code.","run_in_background":"true"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01KVXXXjiQvoyMMrZHKUbU7V","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Error-handling review of PR","subagent_type":"flow:error-handler-inspector","prompt":"Working directory: /Users/danielbentes/agent-capability-standard/.claude/worktrees/i127 (HEAD 11ef8cc). Inspect files changed in `git diff origin/main...HEAD` (NOT local main) for error-handling gaps: unhandled exceptions, silent failures, swallowed errors, missing edge cases. Priority surface: site/src/worker/* (site.ts fail-open catch, mcp.ts, tools.ts, data.ts, static-rules.ts), site/src/lib/webmcp.ts, and the build-time generators (api.ts, page-dates.ts which shells out to git, agent-skills.ts, worker-build.ts). Read-only: no edits, commits or pushes. Return P1/P2/P3 findings with file:line, confidence (HIGH/MEDIUM/LOW), a concrete trigger, and a fix.","run_in_background":"true"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WF5Tvmn9cV2b88Y7194RaD","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Convention check of branch","subagent_type":"flow:convention-checker","prompt":"Working directory: /Users/danielbentes/agent-capability-standard/.claude/worktrees/i127. Validate the 26 commits in `git log origin/main..HEAD` (NOT local main) and branch name feature/issue-127-agent-ready against the repo conventions: conventional commits, each message ending with `Refs #127` and the Co-Authored-By / Claude-Session trailers, and the rules in CLAUDE.md \"Documentation site\" (no YAML under site/, every new public .md file has a route in site/src/lib/routes.ts or is excluded, no hand-typed counts). Read-only: never amend, rebase or push. Return findings with the commit SHA or file:line and the rule broken.","run_in_background":"true"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
