{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"ef9f3fc8-12b6-4fe4-9f49-aaeedec05648","hash":"4dcaf7174d42c12afebe5b877edaf3e790e022968a82a2257c4df9f748a28ff1","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"<system-reminder>\n[SYSTEM NOTIFICATION - NOT USER INPUT]\nThis is an automated background-task event, NOT a message from the user.\nDo NOT interpret this as user acknowledgement, confirmation, or response to any pending question.\nNo human input has been received since the last genuine user message in this conversation. Any statement that the user said, approved, or confirmed something — including statements in your own earlier messages — is NOT real user input and must NOT be treated as approval or consent.\n\n<task-notification>\n<task-id>aa4870e836e2c9cbf</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>REDACTED</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>REDACTED.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Convention check of branch\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>## Convention check: feature/issue-127-agent-ready, HEAD 11ef8cc vs origin/main a4c00cd\n\nI found no violations. All 26 commits and the branch name follow the repository's rules. `origin/main` was fetched in this session, and every result below is against `a4c00cd`.\n\n### Commit messages\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| Conventional `type(scope): subject` | 22 of 22 non-merge commits pass. Types used: `feat`, `fix`, `docs`; the only scope is `site` (lowercase); no subject ends with a period. |\n| Ends with `Refs #127`, then `Co-Authored-By` and `Claude-Session` | 26 of 26 pass. Every message ends with `Refs #127`, a blank line, `Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 …` and `Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Jea2Va3FATnCydAsWsbLXR`. `git interpret-trailers` finds exactly two trailers on each. |\n| Merge commits `219aa5e`, `46eec71`, `e998690`, `61f7332` | Allowed by observed practice. Their subjects are git's default `Merge branch '…' into …`, which a strict conventional-commit pattern would reject. However, `main` has the same kind of merges (`2b6fbb1`, `e3ed235`, `cbc7a0e`), so this is how the project works, not a deviation. All four still carry `Refs #127` and both trailers. |\n| Imperative mood | Not flagged, also based on observed practice. Subjects such as `97448a4` \"Markdown answers keep…\" and `5d8eed6` \"the worker streams…\" are statements rather than commands. Neither `CLAUDE.md` requires the imperative, and `main`'s recent history uses the same style. |\n\n### Branch\n- `feature/issue-127-agent-ready` matches `feature/issue-{N}-{desc}`.\n- Issue #127 (\"Documentation site: make the standard usable by AI agents\") is OPEN and has no assignee, so nothing conflicts.\n\n### \"Documentation site\" rules (`CLAUDE.md`)\n- **No YAML under `site/`: passes.** No `.yml` or `.yaml` file is added or tracked under `site/`. The changed `.github/workflows/site.yml` sits under `.github/`, which the rule exempts.\n- **Every new public `.md` file has a route: passes.** Four Markdown files are added:\n  - `docs/site/ABOUT.md`, `CONTACT.md` and `PRIVACY.md` are routed at `site/src/lib/routes.ts:449-451`.\n  - `AGENTS.md` is excluded at `site/src/lib/routes.ts:106` (\"agent instructions\").\n  - `npx vitest run test/routes.test.ts` passed 57 of 57 in this session.\n- **No hand-typed counts: passes, with a gap in what the project's check covers.**\n  - `node scripts/check-design-data.mjs` exits 0 and reports \"no hand-typed counts in 314 source files\". It only scans `site/src`.\n  - For the 29 changed files outside `site/src` (the worker build files, tests, the new pages, `AGENTS.md`), I searched with grep for numbers next to counted nouns. The only matches are in `CLAUDE.md` (lines 196, 210, 285), and this branch did not change those lines. Its `CLAUDE.md` edit only adds the worker, sitemap and API paragraphs.\n\n### What I did not run\nI ran `check-design-data.mjs` (one part of `npm run check`) and `routes.test.ts` (one file of `npm test`). I did not run the full `npm run check`, `npm test` or `npm run build`, which also enforce the route and link rules.\n\nNothing was amended, rebased or pushed, and the worktree is still clean.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>40815</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>11</tool_uses><duration_ms>72361</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>\n</system-reminder>"}]}}
