{"parentUuid":"0b6dc90e-78a5-41fc-ace7-aa122c5ac98f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch1BtVNDUxoFfu2zAa7rU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MdFNZKkeXA3DbYnBkD9UdK","name":"mcp__plugin_cloudflare_cloudflare-docs__search_cloudflare_documentation","input":{"query":"Pages Functions daily request limit exceeded free plan what happens static assets fail open"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3004,"cache_read_input_tokens":242396,"output_tokens":227,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":122},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3004,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":227,"cache_read_input_tokens":242396,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3004,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3004},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":399,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01MdFNZKkeXA3DbYnBkD9UdK":{"query":"Pages Functions daily request limit exceeded free plan what happens static assets fail open"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"bcf9672c-3e6f-4e51-9e4d-f58b68cc01e5","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Ch1BtV4NH28WiRfN6zvmx","requestRef":"7c9d4c69-a0df-463d-8f4b-48317c7e328f","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"4ba0b504-c6e5-4628-b272-7d0295a1c07b","timestamp":"2026-11-13T15:47:10.637Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-2","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ef9f3fc8-12b6-4fe4-9f49-aaeedec05648","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/danielbentes/agent-capability-standard/.claude/worktrees/i127","sessionId":"ef9f3fc8-12b6-4fe4-9f49-aaeedec05648","version":"2.1.322","gitBranch":"feature/issue-127-agent-ready","slug":"i-just-came-across-imperative-newell"}
{"parentUuid":"4ba0b504-c6e5-4628-b272-7d0295a1c07b","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"e74cfc96-6716-44df-8893-a9a64e019abc","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MdFNZKkeXA3DbYnBkD9UdK","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"results\":[{\"similarity\":0.9993407130241394,\"url\":\"https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/functions/routing/\",\"title\":\"Routing\",\"text\":\"## Fail open / closed\\n\\nIf on the Workers Free plan, you can configure how Pages behaves when your daily free tier allowance of Pages Functions requests is exhausted. If, for example, you are performing authentication checks or other critical functionality in your Pages Functions, you may wish to disable your Pages project when the allowance is exhausted.\\n\\n1. In the Cloudflare dashboard, go to the **Workers & Pages** page.  \\n[Go to **Workers & Pages** ↗](https://dash.cloudflare.com/?to=/:account/workers-and-pages)\\n2. Select your Pages project.\\n3. Go to **Settings** \\\\> **Runtime** \\\\> **Fail open / closed**.\\n\\n\\\"Fail open\\\" means that static assets will continue to be served, even if Pages Functions would ordinarily have run first. \\\"Fail closed\\\" means an error page will be returned, rather than static assets.\\n\\nThe daily request limit for Pages Functions can be removed entirely by upgrading to [Workers Standard](/workers/platform/pricing/#workers).\\n\\n### Limits\\n\\nFunctions invocation routes have the following limits:\\n\\n* You must have at least one include rule.\\n* You may have no more than 100 include/exclude rules combined.\\n* Each rule may have no more than 100 characters.\\n\\nWas this helpful?\\n\\nYesNo\\n\\n## On this page\\n\\n[![](/_astro/logo.te5VL_aD.svg)Docs](/)\\n\\n\"},{\"similarity\":0.9929810762405396,\"url\":\"https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/functions/pricing/\",\"title\":\"Pricing\",\"text\":\"# Pricing\\n\\nLast updated Sep 8, 2026|Copy as Markdown|[View as Markdown](index.md)|[Agent setup](/agent-setup/)\\n\\nRequests to your Functions are billed as Cloudflare Workers requests. Workers plans and pricing can be found [in the Workers documentation](/workers/platform/pricing/).\\n\\n## Paid Plans\\n\\nRequests to your Pages functions count towards your quota for Workers Paid plans, including requests from your Function to KV or Durable Object bindings.\\n\\nPages supports the [Standard usage model](/workers/platform/pricing/#example-pricing-standard-usage-model).\\n\\nNote\\n\\nWorkers Enterprise accounts are billed based on the usage model specified in their contract. To switch to the Standard usage model, reach out to your account team. Some Workers Enterprise customers maintain the ability to [change usage models](/workers/platform/pricing/#how-to-switch-usage-models).\\n\\n### Static asset requests\\n\\nOn both free and paid plans, requests to static assets are free and unlimited. A request is considered static when it does not invoke Functions. Refer to [Functions invocation routes](/pages/functions/routing/#functions-invocation-routes) to learn more about when Functions are invoked.\\n\\n## Free Plan\\n\\nRequests to your Pages Functions count towards your quota for the Workers Free plan. For example, you could use 50,000 Functions requests and 50,000 Workers requests to use your full 100,000 daily request usage. The free plan daily request limit resets at midnight UTC.\\n\\nWas this helpful?\\n\\nYesNo\\n\\n## On this page\\n\\n[![](/_astro/logo.te5VL_aD.svg)Docs](/)\\n\\n\"},{\"similarity\":0.8659330606460571,\"url\":\"https://developers.cloudflare.com/d1/platform/pricing/\",\"title\":\"Pricing\",\"text\":\"## Frequently Asked Questions\\n\\nFrequently asked questions related to D1 pricing:\\n\\n### Will D1 always have a Free plan?\\n\\nYes, the [Workers Free plan](/workers/platform/pricing/#workers) will always include the ability to prototype and experiment with D1 for free.\\n\\n### What happens if I exceed the daily limits on reads and writes, or the total storage limit, on the Free plan?\\n\\nWhen your account hits the daily read and/or write limits, you will not be able to run queries against D1\\\\. D1 API will return errors to your client indicating that your daily limits have been exceeded. Once you have reached your included storage limit, you will need to delete unused databases or clean up stale data before you can insert new data, create or alter tables or create indexes and triggers.\\n\\nUpgrading to the Workers Paid plan will remove these limits, typically within minutes.\\n\\n### What happens if I exceed the monthly included reads, writes and/or storage on the paid tier?\\n\\nYou will be billed for the additional reads, writes and storage according to [D1's pricing metrics](/d1/platform/pricing/#billing-metrics).\\n\\n### How can I estimate my (eventual) bill?\\n\\n\"},{\"similarity\":0.8410503268241882,\"url\":\"https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/static-assets/billing-and-limitations/\",\"title\":\"Billing And Limitations\",\"text\":\"---\\ndescription: Billing, troubleshooting, and limitations for Static assets on Workers\\ntitle: Billing and Limitations\\nimage: https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/static-assets/billing-and-limitations/og.png?v=8760418ba33a23ed\\n---\\n\\n[Skip to content](#main-content)\\n\\n> Documentation Index  \\n> Fetch the complete documentation index at: https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/llms.txt  \\n> Use this file to discover all available pages before exploring further.\\n\\n# Billing and Limitations\\n\\nLast updated Nov 12, 2026|Copy as Markdown|[View as Markdown](index.md)|[Agent setup](/agent-setup/)\\n\\n## Billing\\n\\nRequests to a project with static assets can either return static assets or invoke the Worker script, depending on if the request [matches a static asset or not](/workers/static-assets/routing/).\\n\\n* Requests to static assets are free and unlimited. Requests to the Worker script (for example, in the case of SSR content) are billed according to Workers pricing. Refer to [pricing](/workers/platform/pricing/#example-2) for an example.\\n* There is no additional cost for storing Assets.\\n* **Important note for free tier users**: When using [run\\\\_worker\\\\_first](/workers/static-assets/binding/#run%5Fworker%5Ffirst), requests matching the specified patterns will always invoke your Worker script. If you exceed your free tier request limits, these requests will receive a 429 (Too Many Requests) response instead of falling back to static asset serving. Negative patterns (patterns beginning with `!/`) will continue to serve assets correctly, as requests are directed to assets, without invoking your Worker script.\\n\\n## Limitations\\n\\nSee the [Platform Limits](/workers/platform/limits/#static-assets)\\n\\n### Range requests\\n\\n\"},{\"similarity\":0.8097986578941345,\"url\":\"https://developers.cloudflare.com/d1/reference/faq/\",\"title\":\"Faq\",\"text\":\"## Pricing\\n\\n### Will D1 always have a Free plan?\\n\\nYes, the [Workers Free plan](/workers/platform/pricing/#workers) will always include the ability to prototype and experiment with D1 for free.\\n\\n### What happens if I exceed the daily limits on reads and writes, or the total storage limit, on the Free plan?\\n\\nWhen your account hits the daily read and/or write limits, you will not be able to run queries against D1\\\\. D1 API will return errors to your client indicating that your daily limits have been exceeded. Once you have reached your included storage limit, you will need to delete unused databases or clean up stale data before you can insert new data, create or alter tables or create indexes and triggers.\\n\\nUpgrading to the Workers Paid plan will remove these limits, typically within minutes.\\n\\n### What happens if I exceed the monthly included reads, writes and/or storage on the paid tier?\\n\\nYou will be billed for the additional reads, writes and storage according to [D1's pricing metrics](/d1/platform/pricing/#billing-metrics).\\n\\n### How can I estimate my (eventual) bill?\\n\\n\"},{\"similarity\":0.802091121673584,\"url\":\"https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/platform/limits/\",\"title\":\"Limits\",\"text\":\"## Daily requests\\n\\nWorkers scale automatically across the Cloudflare global network. There is no general limit on requests per second.\\n\\nAccounts on the Workers Free plan have a daily request limit of 100,000 requests, resetting at midnight UTC. When a Worker exceeds this limit, Cloudflare returns **Error 1027**.\\n\\n| Route mode  | Behavior                                                                      |\\n| ----------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\\n| Fail open   | Bypasses the Worker. Requests behave as if no Worker is configured.           |\\n| Fail closed | Returns a Cloudflare 1027 error page. Use this for security-critical Workers. |\\n\\nYou can configure the fail mode by toggling the corresponding [route](/workers/configuration/routing/routes/).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Subrequests\\n\\nA subrequest is any request a Worker makes using the [Fetch API](/workers/runtime-apis/fetch/) or to Cloudflare services like [R2](/r2/), [KV](/kv/), or [D1](/d1/).\\n\\n\"},{\"similarity\":0.6981702446937561,\"url\":\"https://developers.cloudflare.com/changelog/post/2026-09-01-d1-free-tier-limit-enforcement/\",\"title\":\"2026 09 01 D1 Free Tier Limit Enforcement\",\"text\":\"## D1 enforces free tier daily query limits\\n\\n[D1](/d1/)\\n\\nCopy as Markdown|[View as Markdown](index.md)|[Agent setup](/agent-setup/)\\n\\nBeginning September 1, 2026, D1 queries on the [Workers Free plan](/workers/platform/pricing/#workers) will fail when an account exceeds the daily [row read or row write limits](/d1/platform/pricing/). Queries via the [Workers Binding API](/d1/worker-api/) and the [REST API](/api/resources/d1/subresources/database/methods/create/) will return errors until the limit resets at midnight UTC. Stored data is not affected.\\n\\nYou will receive email alerts when the daily limit is reached. The following errors indicate that a limit has been exceeded:\\n\\n| Error                                                                                                                                     | Description                                        |\\n| ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------- |\\n| Your account has exceeded D1's free tier daily row read limit. Upgrade to a paid plan or wait until tomorrow (midnight UTC) to continue.  | The account has reached its daily row read limit.  |\\n| Your account has exceeded D1's free tier daily row write limit. Upgrade to a paid plan or wait until tomorrow (midnight UTC) to continue. | The account has reached its daily row write limit. |\\n\\n\"},{\"similarity\":0.6637728214263916,\"url\":\"https://developers.cloudflare.com/changelog/product/d1/\",\"title\":\"D1\",\"text\":\"For more information, refer to [D1 data location](/d1/configuration/data-location/).\\n\\nSep 1, 2026\\n\\n[D1 enforces free tier daily query limits](/changelog/post/2026-09-01-d1-free-tier-limit-enforcement/)\\n\\n[D1](/d1/)\\n\\nBeginning September 1, 2026, D1 queries on the [Workers Free plan](/workers/platform/pricing/#workers) will fail when an account exceeds the daily [row read or row write limits](/d1/platform/pricing/). Queries via the [Workers Binding API](/d1/worker-api/) and the [REST API](/api/resources/d1/subresources/database/methods/create/) will return errors until the limit resets at midnight UTC. Stored data is not affected.\\n\\nYou will receive email alerts when the daily limit is reached. The following errors indicate that a limit has been exceeded:\\n\\n| Error                                                                                                                                     | Description                                        |\\n| ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------- |\\n| Your account has exceeded D1's free tier daily row read limit. Upgrade to a paid plan or wait until tomorrow (midnight UTC) to continue.  | The account has reached its daily row read limit.  |\\n| Your account has exceeded D1's free tier daily row write limit. Upgrade to a paid plan or wait until tomorrow (midnight UTC) to continue. | The account has reached its daily row write limit. |\\n\\n\"},{\"similarity\":0.6066305041313171,\"url\":\"https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/platform/spend-management/\",\"title\":\"Spend Management\",\"text\":\"# Spending limits\\n\\nLast updated Nov 13, 2026|Copy as Markdown|[View as Markdown](index.md)|[Agent setup](/agent-setup/)\\n\\n[Set a spending limit](/billing/manage/spend-management/) on Workers usage charges. The limit covers requests and CPU time across all Workers in your account, after included usage. It excludes the monthly subscription fee.\\n\\nTo configure a limit, follow [Set a spending limit in the dashboard](/billing/manage/spend-management/#set-a-spending-limit-in-the-dashboard) or [Manage spending limits and alerts with the cf CLI](/billing/manage/spend-management/cli/).\\n\\n## What stops at the limit\\n\\nOnce the limit takes effect, Cloudflare rejects new invocations of your Workers, including:\\n\\n* Incoming HTTP requests.\\n* Cron Triggers.\\n* Queue consumer invocations.\\n* Email Worker invocations.\\n* Calls from other Workers or Durable Objects.\\n\\nHTTP visitors receive error `1103`. This error has other causes, so check **Billing** \\\\> **Spend Management** before contacting support. Requests rejected by the spending limit are not billed as Worker invocations.\\n\\nStatic assets served without running your Worker continue to be available. Requests that need Worker code, such as requests routed through `run_worker_first`, can fail. A limit does not delete your Workers or assets.\\n\\n## Plan for application dependencies\\n\\nA Workers limit applies to the whole account, rather than one application or environment. For example, a test Worker can reach the shared limit and interrupt a production Worker in the same account.\\n\\n\"},{\"similarity\":0.5900054574012756,\"url\":\"https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/static-assets/billing-and-limitations/\",\"title\":\"Billing And Limitations\",\"text\":\"## Limitations\\n\\nSee the [Platform Limits](/workers/platform/limits/#static-assets)\\n\\n### Range requests\\n\\nWhen a request for a static asset includes a `Range` header, Workers returns `200 OK` with the full file instead of `206 Partial Content`, and the response has no `Content-Range` or `Accept-Ranges` header. Some clients need range support, for example Safari when it plays video.\\n\\nTo serve byte ranges, route the affected paths to your Worker with [run\\\\_worker\\\\_first](/workers/static-assets/binding/#run%5Fworker%5Ffirst). In your Worker, fetch the file with `env.ASSETS.fetch()`, then return a `206 Partial Content` response that contains the requested bytes and a `Content-Range` header.\\n\\n## Troubleshooting\\n\\n* `assets.bucket is a required field` — if you see this error, you need to update Wrangler to at least `3.78.10` or later. `bucket` is not a required field.\\n* Asset requests fail after a deployment — HTML and asset requests may use different versions. An older page may also request a file missing from the version handling that request. Refer to [Version skew and static assets](/workers/versions-and-deployments/version-skew/).\\n\\nWas this helpful?\\n\\nYesNo\\n\\n## On this page\\n\\n[![](/_astro/logo.te5VL_aD.svg)Docs](/)\\n\\n\"},{\"similarity\":0.5428529381752014,\"url\":\"https://developers.cloudflare.com/kv/platform/pricing/\",\"title\":\"Pricing\",\"text\":\"# Pricing\\n\\nLast updated Oct 30, 2026|Copy as Markdown|[View as Markdown](index.md)|[Agent setup](/agent-setup/)\\n\\nWorkers KV is included in both the Free and Paid [Workers plans](/workers/platform/pricing/).\\n\\n|               | Free plan1    | Paid plan                                                                                                   |\\n| ------------- | ------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\\n| Keys read     | 100,000 / day | 10 million/month, + $0.50/million                                                                           |\\n| Keys written  | 1,000 / day   | 1 million/month, + $5.00/million                                                                            |\\n| Keys deleted  | 1,000 / day   | 1 million/month, + $5.00/million                                                                            |\\n| List requests | 1,000 / day   | 1 million/month, + $5.00/million                                                                            |\\n| Stored data   | 1 GB          | 1 GB, + $0.50/ GB-month                                                                                     |\\n| Namespaces    | 1,000         | Unlimited, with a default limit of 1,000\\\\. First 1,000 included + $0.10 per additional namespace per month. |\\n\\nRefer to [KV limits](/kv/platform/limits/#workers-kv) for namespace creation limits and limit increases.\\n\\n1 The Workers Free plan includes limited Workers KV usage. Daily usage limits reset daily at 00:00 UTC. If you exceed any one of these limits, further operations of that type will fail with an error.\\n\\nNote\\n\\nWorkers KV pricing for read, write and delete operations is on a per-key basis. Bulk read operations are billed by the amount of keys read in a bulk read operation.\\n\\n## Pricing FAQ\\n\\n### How much do additional namespaces cost?\\n\\n\"},{\"similarity\":0.3864353895187378,\"url\":\"https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/platform/pricing/\",\"title\":\"Pricing\",\"text\":\"KV documentation\\n\\nTo learn more about KV, refer to the [KV documentation](/kv/).\\n\\n## Hyperdrive\\n\\nHyperdrive is included in both the Free and Paid [Workers plans](/workers/platform/pricing/).\\n\\n|                                         | Free plan[1](#user-content-fn-1) | Paid plan |\\n| --------------------------------------- | -------------------------------- | --------- |\\n| Database queries[2](#user-content-fn-2) | 100,000 / day                    | Unlimited |\\n\\nFootnotes\\n\\n1: The Workers Free plan includes limited Hyperdrive usage. All limits reset daily at 00:00 UTC. If you exceed any one of these limits, further operations of that type will fail with an error.\\n\\n2: Database queries refers to any database statement made via Hyperdrive, whether a query (`SELECT`), a modification (`INSERT`,`UPDATE`, or `DELETE`) or a schema change (`CREATE`, `ALTER`, `DROP`).\\n\\n## Footnotes\\n\\n1. The Workers Free plan includes limited Hyperdrive usage. All limits reset daily at 00:00 UTC. If you exceed any one of these limits, further operations of that type will fail with an error. [↩](#user-content-fnref-1)\\n2. Database queries refers to any database statement made via Hyperdrive, whether a query (`SELECT`), a modification (`INSERT`,`UPDATE`, or `DELETE`) or a schema change (`CREATE`, `ALTER`, `DROP`). [↩](#user-content-fnref-2)\\n\\nHyperdrive documentation\\n\\nTo learn more about Hyperdrive, refer to the [Hyperdrive documentation](/hyperdrive/).\\n\\n## Queues\\n\\nCloudflare Queues charges for operations and for queues above the included amount on the Workers Paid plan.\\n\\n\"},{\"similarity\":0.38552767038345337,\"url\":\"https://developers.cloudflare.com/browser-run/faq/\",\"title\":\"Faq\",\"text\":\"## Errors & Troubleshooting\\n\\n### Error: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'fetch')\\n\\nThis error typically occurs because your Puppeteer launch is not receiving the browser binding. To resolve this error, pass your browser binding into `puppeteer.launch`.\\n\\n### Error: 429 browser time limit exceeded\\n\\nThis error (`Unable to create new browser: code: 429: message: Browser time limit exceeded for today`) indicates you have hit the daily browser-instance limit on the Workers Free plan. [Workers Free plan accounts are capped at 10 minutes of browser use a day](/browser-run/limits/#workers-free). Once you exceed that limit, further creation attempts return a 429 error until the next UTC day.\\n\\nTo resolve this error, [upgrade to a Workers Paid plan](/workers/platform/pricing/) which allows for more than 10 minutes of usage a day and has higher [limits](/browser-run/limits/#workers-paid). If you recently upgraded but still see this error, try redeploying your Worker to ensure your usage is correctly associated with your new plan.\\n\\n### Error: 422 unprocessable entity\\n\\nA `422 Unprocessable Entity` error usually means that Browser Run was not able to complete an action because of an issue with the site.\\n\\nThis can happen if:\\n\\n* The website consumes too much memory during rendering.\\n* The page itself crashed or returned an error before the action completed.\\n* The request exceeded one of the [timeout limits](/browser-run/reference/timeouts/) for page load, element load, or an action.\\n\\nMost often, this error is caused by a timeout. You can review the different timers and their limits in the [Quick Actions timeouts reference](/browser-run/reference/timeouts/).\\n\\n### Why is my page content missing or incomplete?\\n\\nIf your screenshots, PDFs, or scraped content are missing elements that appear when viewing the page in a browser, the page likely has not finished loading before Browser Run captures the output.\\n\\n\"},{\"similarity\":0.3796478509902954,\"url\":\"https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/platform/limits/\",\"title\":\"Limits\",\"text\":\"## Cache API limits\\n\\n| Feature             | Workers Free | Workers Paid |\\n| ------------------- | ------------ | ------------ |\\n| Maximum object size | 512 MB       | 512 MB       |\\n| Calls per request   | 50           | 1,000        |\\n\\nCalls per request is the number of `put()`, `match()`, or `delete()` Cache API calls per request. This shares the same quota as subrequests (`fetch()`).\\n\\nNote\\n\\nThe size of chunked response bodies (`Transfer-Encoding: chunked`) is not known in advance. Calling `.put()` with such a response blocks subsequent `.put()` calls until the current one completes.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Log size\\n\\n| Limit                | Value  |\\n| -------------------- | ------ |\\n| Log data per request | 256 KB |\\n\\nThis limit covers all data emitted via `console.log()` statements, exceptions, request metadata, and headers for a single request. After exceeding this limit, the system does not record additional context for that request in logs, tail logs, or [Tail Workers](/workers/observability/logs/tail-workers/).\\n\\nRefer to the [Workers Trace Event Logpush documentation](/workers/observability/logs/logpush/#limits) for limits on fields sent to Logpush destinations.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Image Resizing with Workers\\n\\nRefer to the [Image Resizing documentation](/images/optimization/transformations/overview/) for limits that apply when using Image Resizing with Workers.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Static Assets\\n\\n\"},{\"similarity\":0.37404119968414307,\"url\":\"https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/platform/pricing/\",\"title\":\"Pricing\",\"text\":\"## Workers KV\\n\\nWorkers KV is included in both the Free and Paid [Workers plans](/workers/platform/pricing/).\\n\\n|               | Free plan1    | Paid plan                                                                                                   |\\n| ------------- | ------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\\n| Keys read     | 100,000 / day | 10 million/month, + $0.50/million                                                                           |\\n| Keys written  | 1,000 / day   | 1 million/month, + $5.00/million                                                                            |\\n| Keys deleted  | 1,000 / day   | 1 million/month, + $5.00/million                                                                            |\\n| List requests | 1,000 / day   | 1 million/month, + $5.00/million                                                                            |\\n| Stored data   | 1 GB          | 1 GB, + $0.50/ GB-month                                                                                     |\\n| Namespaces    | 1,000         | Unlimited, with a default limit of 1,000\\\\. First 1,000 included + $0.10 per additional namespace per month. |\\n\\nRefer to [KV limits](/kv/platform/limits/#workers-kv) for namespace creation limits and limit increases.\\n\\n1 The Workers Free plan includes limited Workers KV usage. Daily usage limits reset daily at 00:00 UTC. If you exceed any one of these limits, further operations of that type will fail with an error.\\n\\nNote\\n\\nWorkers KV pricing for read, write and delete operations is on a per-key basis. Bulk read operations are billed by the amount of keys read in a bulk read operation.\\n\\nKV documentation\\n\\nTo learn more about KV, refer to the [KV documentation](/kv/).\\n\\n## Hyperdrive\\n\\nHyperdrive is included in both the Free and Paid [Workers plans](/workers/platform/pricing/).\\n\\n\"},{\"similarity\":0.3557373583316803,\"url\":\"https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/platform/limits/\",\"title\":\"Limits\",\"text\":\"## Files\\n\\nPages uploads each file on your site to Cloudflare's globally distributed network to deliver a low latency experience to every user that visits your site. Cloudflare Pages sites can contain up to 20,000 files on the Free plan.\\n\\nPaid plans (such as Pro, Business, and Enterprise plans) can have up to 100,000 files per site. To enable this increased limit, set the environment variable `PAGES_WRANGLER_MAJOR_VERSION=4` in your Pages project settings.\\n\\n## File size\\n\\nThe maximum file size for a single Cloudflare Pages site asset is 25 MiB.\\n\\nLarger Files\\n\\nTo serve larger files, consider uploading them to [R2](/r2/) and utilizing the [public bucket](/r2/buckets/public-buckets/) feature. You can also use [custom domains](/r2/buckets/public-buckets/#connect-a-bucket-to-a-custom-domain), such as `static.example.com`, for serving these files.\\n\\n## Functions\\n\\nRequests to [Pages functions](/pages/functions/) count towards your quota for Workers plans, including requests from your Function to KV or Durable Object bindings.\\n\\nPages supports the [Standard usage model](/workers/platform/pricing/#example-pricing-standard-usage-model).\\n\\n## Headers\\n\\nA `_headers` file can have a maximum of 100 header rules.\\n\\nAn individual header in a `_headers` file can have a maximum of 2,000 characters. For managing larger headers, it is recommended to implement [Pages Functions](/pages/functions/).\\n\\n## Preview deployments\\n\\nYou can have an unlimited number of [preview deployments](/pages/configuration/preview-deployments/) active on your project at a time.\\n\\n## Redirects\\n\\n\"},{\"similarity\":0.3338557183742523,\"url\":\"https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/platform/limits/\",\"title\":\"Limits\",\"text\":\"| Feature                                                                     | Workers Free | Workers Paid               |\\n| --------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------ | -------------------------- |\\n| [Requests](#daily-requests)                                                 | 100,000/day  | No limit                   |\\n| [CPU time](#cpu-time)                                                       | 10 ms        | 5 min                      |\\n| [Memory](#memory)                                                           | 128 MB       | 128 MB                     |\\n| [Subrequests](#subrequests)                                                 | 50/request   | 10,000/request             |\\n| [Simultaneous outgoing connections/request](#simultaneous-open-connections) | 6            | 6                          |\\n| [Environment variables](#environment-variables)                             | 64/Worker    | 128/Worker                 |\\n| [Environment variable size](#environment-variables)                         | 5 KB         | 5 KB                       |\\n| [Worker size](#worker-size)                                                 | 64 MiB       | 64 MiB                     |\\n| [Worker startup time](#worker-startup-time)                                 | 1 second     | 1 second                   |\\n| [Number of Workers](#number-of-workers)                                     | 100          | 500[1](#user-content-fn-1) |\\n| Number of [Cron Triggers](/workers/configuration/cron-triggers/)per account | 5            | 250                        |\\n| Number of [Static Asset](#static-assets) files per Worker version           | 20,000       | 100,000                    |\\n| Individual [Static Asset](#static-assets) file size                         | 25 MiB       | 25 MiB                     |\\n\\nNeed a higher limit?\\n\\n\"},{\"similarity\":0.31842294335365295,\"url\":\"https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/static-assets/migration-guides/vercel-to-workers/react-router/\",\"title\":\"React Router\",\"text\":\"## Troubleshooting\\n\\n* **The build fails with `Could not load virtual:react-router/server-manifest`.** Either the `v8_viteEnvironmentApi` future flag is missing, or `vercelPreset()` is still configured.\\n* **React Router 7.10 or later rejects `unstable_viteEnvironmentApi`.** The flag was renamed to `v8_viteEnvironmentApi`. Some starter templates still use the old name.\\n* **The install fails with `ERESOLVE`.** `@vercel/remix` pins Remix 2, and `@cloudflare/vite-plugin` requires Vite 6.1 or later. Remove `@vercel/remix`, upgrade Vite, and reinstall from a clean lockfile.\\n* **The codemod fails with `Registry error: HTTP request failed`.** This happens behind TLS-inspecting proxies. Use `npx codemod@0.18.13 remix/2/react-router/upgrade --no-interactive`.\\n* **Every SSR route returns `500` with `renderToPipeableStream is not a function`.** The application has no `app/entry.server.tsx`, so React Router uses its Node.js default entry. Create an entry that uses `renderToReadableStream`, based on the [React Router starter template ↗︎](https://github.com/cloudflare/templates/blob/main/react-router-starter-template/app/entry.server.tsx). Static assets and `.data` requests still succeed, so check an SSR route.\\n* **Remix `?_data` requests stop working.** React Router v7 uses `/<route>.data` endpoints. Browser tabs that loaded the old bundle can fail one navigation after the cutover.\\n\\n## Related resources\\n\\n* [React Router framework guide](/workers/framework-guides/web-apps/react-router/)\\n* [Migrate from Vercel to Workers](/workers/static-assets/migration-guides/vercel-to-workers/)\\n* [Cloudflare Vite plugin](/workers/vite-plugin/)\\n\\nWas this helpful?\\n\\nYesNo\\n\\n## On this page\\n\\n[![](/_astro/logo.te5VL_aD.svg)Docs](/)\\n\\n\"}]}"}]},"uuid":"abd68b85-604f-4871-86fd-af6cb34ab025","timestamp":"2026-11-13T15:47:15.341Z","toolUseResult":"{\"results\":[{\"similarity\":0.9993407130241394,\"url\":\"https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/functions/routing/\",\"title\":\"Routing\",\"text\":\"## Fail open / closed\\n\\nIf on the Workers Free plan, you can configure how Pages behaves when your daily free tier allowance of Pages Functions requests is exhausted. If, for example, you are performing authentication checks or other critical functionality in your Pages Functions, you may wish to disable your Pages project when the allowance is exhausted.\\n\\n1. In the Cloudflare dashboard, go to the **Workers & Pages** page.  \\n[Go to **Workers & Pages** ↗](https://dash.cloudflare.com/?to=/:account/workers-and-pages)\\n2. Select your Pages project.\\n3. Go to **Settings** \\\\> **Runtime** \\\\> **Fail open / closed**.\\n\\n\\\"Fail open\\\" means that static assets will continue to be served, even if Pages Functions would ordinarily have run first. \\\"Fail closed\\\" means an error page will be returned, rather than static assets.\\n\\nThe daily request limit for Pages Functions can be removed entirely by upgrading to [Workers Standard](/workers/platform/pricing/#workers).\\n\\n### Limits\\n\\nFunctions invocation routes have the following limits:\\n\\n* You must have at least one include rule.\\n* You may have no more than 100 include/exclude rules combined.\\n* Each rule may have no more than 100 characters.\\n\\nWas this helpful?\\n\\nYesNo\\n\\n## On this page\\n\\n[![](/_astro/logo.te5VL_aD.svg)Docs](/)\\n\\n\"},{\"similarity\":0.9929810762405396,\"url\":\"https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/functions/pricing/\",\"title\":\"Pricing\",\"text\":\"# Pricing\\n\\nLast updated Sep 8, 2026|Copy as Markdown|[View as Markdown](index.md)|[Agent setup](/agent-setup/)\\n\\nRequests to your Functions are billed as Cloudflare Workers requests. Workers plans and pricing can be found [in the Workers documentation](/workers/platform/pricing/).\\n\\n## Paid Plans\\n\\nRequests to your Pages functions count towards your quota for Workers Paid plans, including requests from your Function to KV or Durable Object bindings.\\n\\nPages supports the [Standard usage model](/workers/platform/pricing/#example-pricing-standard-usage-model).\\n\\nNote\\n\\nWorkers Enterprise accounts are billed based on the usage model specified in their contract. To switch to the Standard usage model, reach out to your account team. Some Workers Enterprise customers maintain the ability to [change usage models](/workers/platform/pricing/#how-to-switch-usage-models).\\n\\n### Static asset requests\\n\\nOn both free and paid plans, requests to static assets are free and unlimited. A request is considered static when it does not invoke Functions. Refer to [Functions invocation routes](/pages/functions/routing/#functions-invocation-routes) to learn more about when Functions are invoked.\\n\\n## Free Plan\\n\\nRequests to your Pages Functions count towards your quota for the Workers Free plan. For example, you could use 50,000 Functions requests and 50,000 Workers requests to use your full 100,000 daily request usage. The free plan daily request limit resets at midnight UTC.\\n\\nWas this helpful?\\n\\nYesNo\\n\\n## On this page\\n\\n[![](/_astro/logo.te5VL_aD.svg)Docs](/)\\n\\n\"},{\"similarity\":0.8659330606460571,\"url\":\"https://developers.cloudflare.com/d1/platform/pricing/\",\"title\":\"Pricing\",\"text\":\"## Frequently Asked Questions\\n\\nFrequently asked questions related to D1 pricing:\\n\\n### Will D1 always have a Free plan?\\n\\nYes, the [Workers Free plan](/workers/platform/pricing/#workers) will always include the ability to prototype and experiment with D1 for free.\\n\\n### What happens if I exceed the daily limits on reads and writes, or the total storage limit, on the Free plan?\\n\\nWhen your account hits the daily read and/or write limits, you will not be able to run queries against D1\\\\. D1 API will return errors to your client indicating that your daily limits have been exceeded. Once you have reached your included storage limit, you will need to delete unused databases or clean up stale data before you can insert new data, create or alter tables or create indexes and triggers.\\n\\nUpgrading to the Workers Paid plan will remove these limits, typically within minutes.\\n\\n### What happens if I exceed the monthly included reads, writes and/or storage on the paid tier?\\n\\nYou will be billed for the additional reads, writes and storage according to [D1's pricing metrics](/d1/platform/pricing/#billing-metrics).\\n\\n### How can I estimate my (eventual) bill?\\n\\n\"},{\"similarity\":0.8410503268241882,\"url\":\"https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/static-assets/billing-and-limitations/\",\"title\":\"Billing And Limitations\",\"text\":\"---\\ndescription: Billing, troubleshooting, and limitations for Static assets on Workers\\ntitle: Billing and Limitations\\nimage: https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/static-assets/billing-and-limitations/og.png?v=8760418ba33a23ed\\n---\\n\\n[Skip to content](#main-content)\\n\\n> Documentation Index  \\n> Fetch the complete documentation index at: https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/llms.txt  \\n> Use this file to discover all available pages before exploring further.\\n\\n# Billing and Limitations\\n\\nLast updated Nov 12, 2026|Copy as Markdown|[View as Markdown](index.md)|[Agent setup](/agent-setup/)\\n\\n## Billing\\n\\nRequests to a project with static assets can either return static assets or invoke the Worker script, depending on if the request [matches a static asset or not](/workers/static-assets/routing/).\\n\\n* Requests to static assets are free and unlimited. Requests to the Worker script (for example, in the case of SSR content) are billed according to Workers pricing. Refer to [pricing](/workers/platform/pricing/#example-2) for an example.\\n* There is no additional cost for storing Assets.\\n* **Important note for free tier users**: When using [run\\\\_worker\\\\_first](/workers/static-assets/binding/#run%5Fworker%5Ffirst), requests matching the specified patterns will always invoke your Worker script. If you exceed your free tier request limits, these requests will receive a 429 (Too Many Requests) response instead of falling back to static asset serving. Negative patterns (patterns beginning with `!/`) will continue to serve assets correctly, as requests are directed to assets, without invoking your Worker script.\\n\\n## Limitations\\n\\nSee the [Platform Limits](/workers/platform/limits/#static-assets)\\n\\n### Range requests\\n\\n\"},{\"similarity\":0.8097986578941345,\"url\":\"https://developers.cloudflare.com/d1/reference/faq/\",\"title\":\"Faq\",\"text\":\"## Pricing\\n\\n### Will D1 always have a Free plan?\\n\\nYes, the [Workers Free plan](/workers/platform/pricing/#workers) will always include the ability to prototype and experiment with D1 for free.\\n\\n### What happens if I exceed the daily limits on reads and writes, or the total storage limit, on the Free plan?\\n\\nWhen your account hits the daily read and/or write limits, you will not be able to run queries against D1\\\\. D1 API will return errors to your client indicating that your daily limits have been exceeded. Once you have reached your included storage limit, you will need to delete unused databases or clean up stale data before you can insert new data, create or alter tables or create indexes and triggers.\\n\\nUpgrading to the Workers Paid plan will remove these limits, typically within minutes.\\n\\n### What happens if I exceed the monthly included reads, writes and/or storage on the paid tier?\\n\\nYou will be billed for the additional reads, writes and storage according to [D1's pricing metrics](/d1/platform/pricing/#billing-metrics).\\n\\n### How can I estimate my (eventual) bill?\\n\\n\"},{\"similarity\":0.802091121673584,\"url\":\"https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/platform/limits/\",\"title\":\"Limits\",\"text\":\"## Daily requests\\n\\nWorkers scale automatically across the Cloudflare global network. There is no general limit on requests per second.\\n\\nAccounts on the Workers Free plan have a daily request limit of 100,000 requests, resetting at midnight UTC. When a Worker exceeds this limit, Cloudflare returns **Error 1027**.\\n\\n| Route mode  | Behavior                                                                      |\\n| ----------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\\n| Fail open   | Bypasses the Worker. Requests behave as if no Worker is configured.           |\\n| Fail closed | Returns a Cloudflare 1027 error page. Use this for security-critical Workers. |\\n\\nYou can configure the fail mode by toggling the corresponding [route](/workers/configuration/routing/routes/).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Subrequests\\n\\nA subrequest is any request a Worker makes using the [Fetch API](/workers/runtime-apis/fetch/) or to Cloudflare services like [R2](/r2/), [KV](/kv/), or [D1](/d1/).\\n\\n\"},{\"similarity\":0.6981702446937561,\"url\":\"https://developers.cloudflare.com/changelog/post/2026-09-01-d1-free-tier-limit-enforcement/\",\"title\":\"2026 09 01 D1 Free Tier Limit Enforcement\",\"text\":\"## D1 enforces free tier daily query limits\\n\\n[D1](/d1/)\\n\\nCopy as Markdown|[View as Markdown](index.md)|[Agent setup](/agent-setup/)\\n\\nBeginning September 1, 2026, D1 queries on the [Workers Free plan](/workers/platform/pricing/#workers) will fail when an account exceeds the daily [row read or row write limits](/d1/platform/pricing/). Queries via the [Workers Binding API](/d1/worker-api/) and the [REST API](/api/resources/d1/subresources/database/methods/create/) will return errors until the limit resets at midnight UTC. Stored data is not affected.\\n\\nYou will receive email alerts when the daily limit is reached. The following errors indicate that a limit has been exceeded:\\n\\n| Error                                                                                                                                     | Description                                        |\\n| ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------- |\\n| Your account has exceeded D1's free tier daily row read limit. Upgrade to a paid plan or wait until tomorrow (midnight UTC) to continue.  | The account has reached its daily row read limit.  |\\n| Your account has exceeded D1's free tier daily row write limit. Upgrade to a paid plan or wait until tomorrow (midnight UTC) to continue. | The account has reached its daily row write limit. |\\n\\n\"},{\"similarity\":0.6637728214263916,\"url\":\"https://developers.cloudflare.com/changelog/product/d1/\",\"title\":\"D1\",\"text\":\"For more information, refer to [D1 data location](/d1/configuration/data-location/).\\n\\nSep 1, 2026\\n\\n[D1 enforces free tier daily query limits](/changelog/post/2026-09-01-d1-free-tier-limit-enforcement/)\\n\\n[D1](/d1/)\\n\\nBeginning September 1, 2026, D1 queries on the [Workers Free plan](/workers/platform/pricing/#workers) will fail when an account exceeds the daily [row read or row write limits](/d1/platform/pricing/). Queries via the [Workers Binding API](/d1/worker-api/) and the [REST API](/api/resources/d1/subresources/database/methods/create/) will return errors until the limit resets at midnight UTC. Stored data is not affected.\\n\\nYou will receive email alerts when the daily limit is reached. The following errors indicate that a limit has been exceeded:\\n\\n| Error                                                                                                                                     | Description                                        |\\n| ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------- |\\n| Your account has exceeded D1's free tier daily row read limit. Upgrade to a paid plan or wait until tomorrow (midnight UTC) to continue.  | The account has reached its daily row read limit.  |\\n| Your account has exceeded D1's free tier daily row write limit. Upgrade to a paid plan or wait until tomorrow (midnight UTC) to continue. | The account has reached its daily row write limit. |\\n\\n\"},{\"similarity\":0.6066305041313171,\"url\":\"https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/platform/spend-management/\",\"title\":\"Spend Management\",\"text\":\"# Spending limits\\n\\nLast updated Nov 13, 2026|Copy as Markdown|[View as Markdown](index.md)|[Agent setup](/agent-setup/)\\n\\n[Set a spending limit](/billing/manage/spend-management/) on Workers usage charges. The limit covers requests and CPU time across all Workers in your account, after included usage. It excludes the monthly subscription fee.\\n\\nTo configure a limit, follow [Set a spending limit in the dashboard](/billing/manage/spend-management/#set-a-spending-limit-in-the-dashboard) or [Manage spending limits and alerts with the cf CLI](/billing/manage/spend-management/cli/).\\n\\n## What stops at the limit\\n\\nOnce the limit takes effect, Cloudflare rejects new invocations of your Workers, including:\\n\\n* Incoming HTTP requests.\\n* Cron Triggers.\\n* Queue consumer invocations.\\n* Email Worker invocations.\\n* Calls from other Workers or Durable Objects.\\n\\nHTTP visitors receive error `1103`. This error has other causes, so check **Billing** \\\\> **Spend Management** before contacting support. Requests rejected by the spending limit are not billed as Worker invocations.\\n\\nStatic assets served without running your Worker continue to be available. Requests that need Worker code, such as requests routed through `run_worker_first`, can fail. A limit does not delete your Workers or assets.\\n\\n## Plan for application dependencies\\n\\nA Workers limit applies to the whole account, rather than one application or environment. For example, a test Worker can reach the shared limit and interrupt a production Worker in the same account.\\n\\n\"},{\"similarity\":0.5900054574012756,\"url\":\"https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/static-assets/billing-and-limitations/\",\"title\":\"Billing And Limitations\",\"text\":\"## Limitations\\n\\nSee the [Platform Limits](/workers/platform/limits/#static-assets)\\n\\n### Range requests\\n\\nWhen a request for a static asset includes a `Range` header, Workers returns `200 OK` with the full file instead of `206 Partial Content`, and the response has no `Content-Range` or `Accept-Ranges` header. Some clients need range support, for example Safari when it plays video.\\n\\nTo serve byte ranges, route the affected paths to your Worker with [run\\\\_worker\\\\_first](/workers/static-assets/binding/#run%5Fworker%5Ffirst). In your Worker, fetch the file with `env.ASSETS.fetch()`, then return a `206 Partial Content` response that contains the requested bytes and a `Content-Range` header.\\n\\n## Troubleshooting\\n\\n* `assets.bucket is a required field` — if you see this error, you need to update Wrangler to at least `3.78.10` or later. `bucket` is not a required field.\\n* Asset requests fail after a deployment — HTML and asset requests may use different versions. An older page may also request a file missing from the version handling that request. Refer to [Version skew and static assets](/workers/versions-and-deployments/version-skew/).\\n\\nWas this helpful?\\n\\nYesNo\\n\\n## On this page\\n\\n[![](/_astro/logo.te5VL_aD.svg)Docs](/)\\n\\n\"},{\"similarity\":0.5428529381752014,\"url\":\"https://developers.cloudflare.com/kv/platform/pricing/\",\"title\":\"Pricing\",\"text\":\"# Pricing\\n\\nLast updated Oct 30, 2026|Copy as Markdown|[View as Markdown](index.md)|[Agent setup](/agent-setup/)\\n\\nWorkers KV is included in both the Free and Paid [Workers plans](/workers/platform/pricing/).\\n\\n|               | Free plan1    | Paid plan                                                                                                   |\\n| ------------- | ------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\\n| Keys read     | 100,000 / day | 10 million/month, + $0.50/million                                                                           |\\n| Keys written  | 1,000 / day   | 1 million/month, + $5.00/million                                                                            |\\n| Keys deleted  | 1,000 / day   | 1 million/month, + $5.00/million                                                                            |\\n| List requests | 1,000 / day   | 1 million/month, + $5.00/million                                                                            |\\n| Stored data   | 1 GB          | 1 GB, + $0.50/ GB-month                                                                                     |\\n| Namespaces    | 1,000         | Unlimited, with a default limit of 1,000\\\\. First 1,000 included + $0.10 per additional namespace per month. |\\n\\nRefer to [KV limits](/kv/platform/limits/#workers-kv) for namespace creation limits and limit increases.\\n\\n1 The Workers Free plan includes limited Workers KV usage. Daily usage limits reset daily at 00:00 UTC. If you exceed any one of these limits, further operations of that type will fail with an error.\\n\\nNote\\n\\nWorkers KV pricing for read, write and delete operations is on a per-key basis. Bulk read operations are billed by the amount of keys read in a bulk read operation.\\n\\n## Pricing FAQ\\n\\n### How much do additional namespaces cost?\\n\\n\"},{\"similarity\":0.3864353895187378,\"url\":\"https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/platform/pricing/\",\"title\":\"Pricing\",\"text\":\"KV documentation\\n\\nTo learn more about KV, refer to the [KV documentation](/kv/).\\n\\n## Hyperdrive\\n\\nHyperdrive is included in both the Free and Paid [Workers plans](/workers/platform/pricing/).\\n\\n|                                         | Free plan[1](#user-content-fn-1) | Paid plan |\\n| --------------------------------------- | -------------------------------- | --------- |\\n| Database queries[2](#user-content-fn-2) | 100,000 / day                    | Unlimited |\\n\\nFootnotes\\n\\n1: The Workers Free plan includes limited Hyperdrive usage. All limits reset daily at 00:00 UTC. If you exceed any one of these limits, further operations of that type will fail with an error.\\n\\n2: Database queries refers to any database statement made via Hyperdrive, whether a query (`SELECT`), a modification (`INSERT`,`UPDATE`, or `DELETE`) or a schema change (`CREATE`, `ALTER`, `DROP`).\\n\\n## Footnotes\\n\\n1. The Workers Free plan includes limited Hyperdrive usage. All limits reset daily at 00:00 UTC. If you exceed any one of these limits, further operations of that type will fail with an error. [↩](#user-content-fnref-1)\\n2. Database queries refers to any database statement made via Hyperdrive, whether a query (`SELECT`), a modification (`INSERT`,`UPDATE`, or `DELETE`) or a schema change (`CREATE`, `ALTER`, `DROP`). [↩](#user-content-fnref-2)\\n\\nHyperdrive documentation\\n\\nTo learn more about Hyperdrive, refer to the [Hyperdrive documentation](/hyperdrive/).\\n\\n## Queues\\n\\nCloudflare Queues charges for operations and for queues above the included amount on the Workers Paid plan.\\n\\n\"},{\"similarity\":0.38552767038345337,\"url\":\"https://developers.cloudflare.com/browser-run/faq/\",\"title\":\"Faq\",\"text\":\"## Errors & Troubleshooting\\n\\n### Error: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'fetch')\\n\\nThis error typically occurs because your Puppeteer launch is not receiving the browser binding. To resolve this error, pass your browser binding into `puppeteer.launch`.\\n\\n### Error: 429 browser time limit exceeded\\n\\nThis error (`Unable to create new browser: code: 429: message: Browser time limit exceeded for today`) indicates you have hit the daily browser-instance limit on the Workers Free plan. [Workers Free plan accounts are capped at 10 minutes of browser use a day](/browser-run/limits/#workers-free). Once you exceed that limit, further creation attempts return a 429 error until the next UTC day.\\n\\nTo resolve this error, [upgrade to a Workers Paid plan](/workers/platform/pricing/) which allows for more than 10 minutes of usage a day and has higher [limits](/browser-run/limits/#workers-paid). If you recently upgraded but still see this error, try redeploying your Worker to ensure your usage is correctly associated with your new plan.\\n\\n### Error: 422 unprocessable entity\\n\\nA `422 Unprocessable Entity` error usually means that Browser Run was not able to complete an action because of an issue with the site.\\n\\nThis can happen if:\\n\\n* The website consumes too much memory during rendering.\\n* The page itself crashed or returned an error before the action completed.\\n* The request exceeded one of the [timeout limits](/browser-run/reference/timeouts/) for page load, element load, or an action.\\n\\nMost often, this error is caused by a timeout. You can review the different timers and their limits in the [Quick Actions timeouts reference](/browser-run/reference/timeouts/).\\n\\n### Why is my page content missing or incomplete?\\n\\nIf your screenshots, PDFs, or scraped content are missing elements that appear when viewing the page in a browser, the page likely has not finished loading before Browser Run captures the output.\\n\\n\"},{\"similarity\":0.3796478509902954,\"url\":\"https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/platform/limits/\",\"title\":\"Limits\",\"text\":\"## Cache API limits\\n\\n| Feature             | Workers Free | Workers Paid |\\n| ------------------- | ------------ | ------------ |\\n| Maximum object size | 512 MB       | 512 MB       |\\n| Calls per request   | 50           | 1,000        |\\n\\nCalls per request is the number of `put()`, `match()`, or `delete()` Cache API calls per request. This shares the same quota as subrequests (`fetch()`).\\n\\nNote\\n\\nThe size of chunked response bodies (`Transfer-Encoding: chunked`) is not known in advance. Calling `.put()` with such a response blocks subsequent `.put()` calls until the current one completes.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Log size\\n\\n| Limit                | Value  |\\n| -------------------- | ------ |\\n| Log data per request | 256 KB |\\n\\nThis limit covers all data emitted via `console.log()` statements, exceptions, request metadata, and headers for a single request. After exceeding this limit, the system does not record additional context for that request in logs, tail logs, or [Tail Workers](/workers/observability/logs/tail-workers/).\\n\\nRefer to the [Workers Trace Event Logpush documentation](/workers/observability/logs/logpush/#limits) for limits on fields sent to Logpush destinations.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Image Resizing with Workers\\n\\nRefer to the [Image Resizing documentation](/images/optimization/transformations/overview/) for limits that apply when using Image Resizing with Workers.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Static Assets\\n\\n\"},{\"similarity\":0.37404119968414307,\"url\":\"https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/platform/pricing/\",\"title\":\"Pricing\",\"text\":\"## Workers KV\\n\\nWorkers KV is included in both the Free and Paid [Workers plans](/workers/platform/pricing/).\\n\\n|               | Free plan1    | Paid plan                                                                                                   |\\n| ------------- | ------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\\n| Keys read     | 100,000 / day | 10 million/month, + $0.50/million                                                                           |\\n| Keys written  | 1,000 / day   | 1 million/month, + $5.00/million                                                                            |\\n| Keys deleted  | 1,000 / day   | 1 million/month, + $5.00/million                                                                            |\\n| List requests | 1,000 / day   | 1 million/month, + $5.00/million                                                                            |\\n| Stored data   | 1 GB          | 1 GB, + $0.50/ GB-month                                                                                     |\\n| Namespaces    | 1,000         | Unlimited, with a default limit of 1,000\\\\. First 1,000 included + $0.10 per additional namespace per month. |\\n\\nRefer to [KV limits](/kv/platform/limits/#workers-kv) for namespace creation limits and limit increases.\\n\\n1 The Workers Free plan includes limited Workers KV usage. Daily usage limits reset daily at 00:00 UTC. If you exceed any one of these limits, further operations of that type will fail with an error.\\n\\nNote\\n\\nWorkers KV pricing for read, write and delete operations is on a per-key basis. Bulk read operations are billed by the amount of keys read in a bulk read operation.\\n\\nKV documentation\\n\\nTo learn more about KV, refer to the [KV documentation](/kv/).\\n\\n## Hyperdrive\\n\\nHyperdrive is included in both the Free and Paid [Workers plans](/workers/platform/pricing/).\\n\\n\"},{\"similarity\":0.3557373583316803,\"url\":\"https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/platform/limits/\",\"title\":\"Limits\",\"text\":\"## Files\\n\\nPages uploads each file on your site to Cloudflare's globally distributed network to deliver a low latency experience to every user that visits your site. Cloudflare Pages sites can contain up to 20,000 files on the Free plan.\\n\\nPaid plans (such as Pro, Business, and Enterprise plans) can have up to 100,000 files per site. To enable this increased limit, set the environment variable `PAGES_WRANGLER_MAJOR_VERSION=4` in your Pages project settings.\\n\\n## File size\\n\\nThe maximum file size for a single Cloudflare Pages site asset is 25 MiB.\\n\\nLarger Files\\n\\nTo serve larger files, consider uploading them to [R2](/r2/) and utilizing the [public bucket](/r2/buckets/public-buckets/) feature. You can also use [custom domains](/r2/buckets/public-buckets/#connect-a-bucket-to-a-custom-domain), such as `static.example.com`, for serving these files.\\n\\n## Functions\\n\\nRequests to [Pages functions](/pages/functions/) count towards your quota for Workers plans, including requests from your Function to KV or Durable Object bindings.\\n\\nPages supports the [Standard usage model](/workers/platform/pricing/#example-pricing-standard-usage-model).\\n\\n## Headers\\n\\nA `_headers` file can have a maximum of 100 header rules.\\n\\nAn individual header in a `_headers` file can have a maximum of 2,000 characters. For managing larger headers, it is recommended to implement [Pages Functions](/pages/functions/).\\n\\n## Preview deployments\\n\\nYou can have an unlimited number of [preview deployments](/pages/configuration/preview-deployments/) active on your project at a time.\\n\\n## Redirects\\n\\n\"},{\"similarity\":0.3338557183742523,\"url\":\"https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/platform/limits/\",\"title\":\"Limits\",\"text\":\"| Feature                                                                     | Workers Free | Workers Paid               |\\n| --------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------ | -------------------------- |\\n| [Requests](#daily-requests)                                                 | 100,000/day  | No limit                   |\\n| [CPU time](#cpu-time)                                                       | 10 ms        | 5 min                      |\\n| [Memory](#memory)                                                           | 128 MB       | 128 MB                     |\\n| [Subrequests](#subrequests)                                                 | 50/request   | 10,000/request             |\\n| [Simultaneous outgoing connections/request](#simultaneous-open-connections) | 6            | 6                          |\\n| [Environment variables](#environment-variables)                             | 64/Worker    | 128/Worker                 |\\n| [Environment variable size](#environment-variables)                         | 5 KB         | 5 KB                       |\\n| [Worker size](#worker-size)                                                 | 64 MiB       | 64 MiB                     |\\n| [Worker startup time](#worker-startup-time)                                 | 1 second     | 1 second                   |\\n| [Number of Workers](#number-of-workers)                                     | 100          | 500[1](#user-content-fn-1) |\\n| Number of [Cron Triggers](/workers/configuration/cron-triggers/)per account | 5            | 250                        |\\n| Number of [Static Asset](#static-assets) files per Worker version           | 20,000       | 100,000                    |\\n| Individual [Static Asset](#static-assets) file size                         | 25 MiB       | 25 MiB                     |\\n\\nNeed a higher limit?\\n\\n\"},{\"similarity\":0.31842294335365295,\"url\":\"https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/static-assets/migration-guides/vercel-to-workers/react-router/\",\"title\":\"React Router\",\"text\":\"## Troubleshooting\\n\\n* **The build fails with `Could not load virtual:react-router/server-manifest`.** Either the `v8_viteEnvironmentApi` future flag is missing, or `vercelPreset()` is still configured.\\n* **React Router 7.10 or later rejects `unstable_viteEnvironmentApi`.** The flag was renamed to `v8_viteEnvironmentApi`. Some starter templates still use the old name.\\n* **The install fails with `ERESOLVE`.** `@vercel/remix` pins Remix 2, and `@cloudflare/vite-plugin` requires Vite 6.1 or later. Remove `@vercel/remix`, upgrade Vite, and reinstall from a clean lockfile.\\n* **The codemod fails with `Registry error: HTTP request failed`.** This happens behind TLS-inspecting proxies. Use `npx codemod@0.18.13 remix/2/react-router/upgrade --no-interactive`.\\n* **Every SSR route returns `500` with `renderToPipeableStream is not a function`.** The application has no `app/entry.server.tsx`, so React Router uses its Node.js default entry. Create an entry that uses `renderToReadableStream`, based on the [React Router starter template ↗︎](https://github.com/cloudflare/templates/blob/main/react-router-starter-template/app/entry.server.tsx). Static assets and `.data` requests still succeed, so check an SSR route.\\n* **Remix `?_data` requests stop working.** React Router v7 uses `/<route>.data` endpoints. Browser tabs that loaded the old bundle can fail one navigation after the cutover.\\n\\n## Related resources\\n\\n* [React Router framework guide](/workers/framework-guides/web-apps/react-router/)\\n* [Migrate from Vercel to Workers](/workers/static-assets/migration-guides/vercel-to-workers/)\\n* [Cloudflare Vite plugin](/workers/vite-plugin/)\\n\\nWas this helpful?\\n\\nYesNo\\n\\n## On this page\\n\\n[![](/_astro/logo.te5VL_aD.svg)Docs](/)\\n\\n\"}]}","mcpMeta":{"_meta":{"io.modelcontextprotocol/serverInfo":{"name":"docs-ai-search","version":"0.5.0"}},"structuredContent":{"results":[{"similarity":0.9993407130241394,"url":"https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/functions/routing/","title":"Routing","text":"## Fail open / closed\n\nIf on the Workers Free plan, you can configure how Pages behaves when your daily free tier allowance of Pages Functions requests is exhausted. If, for example, you are performing authentication checks or other critical functionality in your Pages Functions, you may wish to disable your Pages project when the allowance is exhausted.\n\n1. In the Cloudflare dashboard, go to the **Workers & Pages** page.  \n[Go to **Workers & Pages** ↗](https://dash.cloudflare.com/?to=/:account/workers-and-pages)\n2. Select your Pages project.\n3. Go to **Settings** \\> **Runtime** \\> **Fail open / closed**.\n\n\"Fail open\" means that static assets will continue to be served, even if Pages Functions would ordinarily have run first. \"Fail closed\" means an error page will be returned, rather than static assets.\n\nThe daily request limit for Pages Functions can be removed entirely by upgrading to [Workers Standard](/workers/platform/pricing/#workers).\n\n### Limits\n\nFunctions invocation routes have the following limits:\n\n* You must have at least one include rule.\n* You may have no more than 100 include/exclude rules combined.\n* Each rule may have no more than 100 characters.\n\nWas this helpful?\n\nYesNo\n\n## On this page\n\n[![](/_astro/logo.te5VL_aD.svg)Docs](/)\n\n"},{"similarity":0.9929810762405396,"url":"https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/functions/pricing/","title":"Pricing","text":"# Pricing\n\nLast updated Sep 8, 2026|Copy as Markdown|[View as Markdown](index.md)|[Agent setup](/agent-setup/)\n\nRequests to your Functions are billed as Cloudflare Workers requests. Workers plans and pricing can be found [in the Workers documentation](/workers/platform/pricing/).\n\n## Paid Plans\n\nRequests to your Pages functions count towards your quota for Workers Paid plans, including requests from your Function to KV or Durable Object bindings.\n\nPages supports the [Standard usage model](/workers/platform/pricing/#example-pricing-standard-usage-model).\n\nNote\n\nWorkers Enterprise accounts are billed based on the usage model specified in their contract. To switch to the Standard usage model, reach out to your account team. Some Workers Enterprise customers maintain the ability to [change usage models](/workers/platform/pricing/#how-to-switch-usage-models).\n\n### Static asset requests\n\nOn both free and paid plans, requests to static assets are free and unlimited. A request is considered static when it does not invoke Functions. Refer to [Functions invocation routes](/pages/functions/routing/#functions-invocation-routes) to learn more about when Functions are invoked.\n\n## Free Plan\n\nRequests to your Pages Functions count towards your quota for the Workers Free plan. For example, you could use 50,000 Functions requests and 50,000 Workers requests to use your full 100,000 daily request usage. The free plan daily request limit resets at midnight UTC.\n\nWas this helpful?\n\nYesNo\n\n## On this page\n\n[![](/_astro/logo.te5VL_aD.svg)Docs](/)\n\n"},{"similarity":0.8659330606460571,"url":"https://developers.cloudflare.com/d1/platform/pricing/","title":"Pricing","text":"## Frequently Asked Questions\n\nFrequently asked questions related to D1 pricing:\n\n### Will D1 always have a Free plan?\n\nYes, the [Workers Free plan](/workers/platform/pricing/#workers) will always include the ability to prototype and experiment with D1 for free.\n\n### What happens if I exceed the daily limits on reads and writes, or the total storage limit, on the Free plan?\n\nWhen your account hits the daily read and/or write limits, you will not be able to run queries against D1\\. D1 API will return errors to your client indicating that your daily limits have been exceeded. Once you have reached your included storage limit, you will need to delete unused databases or clean up stale data before you can insert new data, create or alter tables or create indexes and triggers.\n\nUpgrading to the Workers Paid plan will remove these limits, typically within minutes.\n\n### What happens if I exceed the monthly included reads, writes and/or storage on the paid tier?\n\nYou will be billed for the additional reads, writes and storage according to [D1's pricing metrics](/d1/platform/pricing/#billing-metrics).\n\n### How can I estimate my (eventual) bill?\n\n"},{"similarity":0.8410503268241882,"url":"https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/static-assets/billing-and-limitations/","title":"Billing And Limitations","text":"---\ndescription: Billing, troubleshooting, and limitations for Static assets on Workers\ntitle: Billing and Limitations\nimage: https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/static-assets/billing-and-limitations/og.png?v=8760418ba33a23ed\n---\n\n[Skip to content](#main-content)\n\n> Documentation Index  \n> Fetch the complete documentation index at: https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/llms.txt  \n> Use this file to discover all available pages before exploring further.\n\n# Billing and Limitations\n\nLast updated Nov 12, 2026|Copy as Markdown|[View as Markdown](index.md)|[Agent setup](/agent-setup/)\n\n## Billing\n\nRequests to a project with static assets can either return static assets or invoke the Worker script, depending on if the request [matches a static asset or not](/workers/static-assets/routing/).\n\n* Requests to static assets are free and unlimited. Requests to the Worker script (for example, in the case of SSR content) are billed according to Workers pricing. Refer to [pricing](/workers/platform/pricing/#example-2) for an example.\n* There is no additional cost for storing Assets.\n* **Important note for free tier users**: When using [run\\_worker\\_first](/workers/static-assets/binding/#run%5Fworker%5Ffirst), requests matching the specified patterns will always invoke your Worker script. If you exceed your free tier request limits, these requests will receive a 429 (Too Many Requests) response instead of falling back to static asset serving. Negative patterns (patterns beginning with `!/`) will continue to serve assets correctly, as requests are directed to assets, without invoking your Worker script.\n\n## Limitations\n\nSee the [Platform Limits](/workers/platform/limits/#static-assets)\n\n### Range requests\n\n"},{"similarity":0.8097986578941345,"url":"https://developers.cloudflare.com/d1/reference/faq/","title":"Faq","text":"## Pricing\n\n### Will D1 always have a Free plan?\n\nYes, the [Workers Free plan](/workers/platform/pricing/#workers) will always include the ability to prototype and experiment with D1 for free.\n\n### What happens if I exceed the daily limits on reads and writes, or the total storage limit, on the Free plan?\n\nWhen your account hits the daily read and/or write limits, you will not be able to run queries against D1\\. D1 API will return errors to your client indicating that your daily limits have been exceeded. Once you have reached your included storage limit, you will need to delete unused databases or clean up stale data before you can insert new data, create or alter tables or create indexes and triggers.\n\nUpgrading to the Workers Paid plan will remove these limits, typically within minutes.\n\n### What happens if I exceed the monthly included reads, writes and/or storage on the paid tier?\n\nYou will be billed for the additional reads, writes and storage according to [D1's pricing metrics](/d1/platform/pricing/#billing-metrics).\n\n### How can I estimate my (eventual) bill?\n\n"},{"similarity":0.802091121673584,"url":"https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/platform/limits/","title":"Limits","text":"## Daily requests\n\nWorkers scale automatically across the Cloudflare global network. There is no general limit on requests per second.\n\nAccounts on the Workers Free plan have a daily request limit of 100,000 requests, resetting at midnight UTC. When a Worker exceeds this limit, Cloudflare returns **Error 1027**.\n\n| Route mode  | Behavior                                                                      |\n| ----------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Fail open   | Bypasses the Worker. Requests behave as if no Worker is configured.           |\n| Fail closed | Returns a Cloudflare 1027 error page. Use this for security-critical Workers. |\n\nYou can configure the fail mode by toggling the corresponding [route](/workers/configuration/routing/routes/).\n\n---\n\n## Subrequests\n\nA subrequest is any request a Worker makes using the [Fetch API](/workers/runtime-apis/fetch/) or to Cloudflare services like [R2](/r2/), [KV](/kv/), or [D1](/d1/).\n\n"},{"similarity":0.6981702446937561,"url":"https://developers.cloudflare.com/changelog/post/2026-09-01-d1-free-tier-limit-enforcement/","title":"2026 09 01 D1 Free Tier Limit Enforcement","text":"## D1 enforces free tier daily query limits\n\n[D1](/d1/)\n\nCopy as Markdown|[View as Markdown](index.md)|[Agent setup](/agent-setup/)\n\nBeginning September 1, 2026, D1 queries on the [Workers Free plan](/workers/platform/pricing/#workers) will fail when an account exceeds the daily [row read or row write limits](/d1/platform/pricing/). Queries via the [Workers Binding API](/d1/worker-api/) and the [REST API](/api/resources/d1/subresources/database/methods/create/) will return errors until the limit resets at midnight UTC. Stored data is not affected.\n\nYou will receive email alerts when the daily limit is reached. The following errors indicate that a limit has been exceeded:\n\n| Error                                                                                                                                     | Description                                        |\n| ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------- |\n| Your account has exceeded D1's free tier daily row read limit. Upgrade to a paid plan or wait until tomorrow (midnight UTC) to continue.  | The account has reached its daily row read limit.  |\n| Your account has exceeded D1's free tier daily row write limit. Upgrade to a paid plan or wait until tomorrow (midnight UTC) to continue. | The account has reached its daily row write limit. |\n\n"},{"similarity":0.6637728214263916,"url":"https://developers.cloudflare.com/changelog/product/d1/","title":"D1","text":"For more information, refer to [D1 data location](/d1/configuration/data-location/).\n\nSep 1, 2026\n\n[D1 enforces free tier daily query limits](/changelog/post/2026-09-01-d1-free-tier-limit-enforcement/)\n\n[D1](/d1/)\n\nBeginning September 1, 2026, D1 queries on the [Workers Free plan](/workers/platform/pricing/#workers) will fail when an account exceeds the daily [row read or row write limits](/d1/platform/pricing/). Queries via the [Workers Binding API](/d1/worker-api/) and the [REST API](/api/resources/d1/subresources/database/methods/create/) will return errors until the limit resets at midnight UTC. Stored data is not affected.\n\nYou will receive email alerts when the daily limit is reached. The following errors indicate that a limit has been exceeded:\n\n| Error                                                                                                                                     | Description                                        |\n| ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------- |\n| Your account has exceeded D1's free tier daily row read limit. Upgrade to a paid plan or wait until tomorrow (midnight UTC) to continue.  | The account has reached its daily row read limit.  |\n| Your account has exceeded D1's free tier daily row write limit. Upgrade to a paid plan or wait until tomorrow (midnight UTC) to continue. | The account has reached its daily row write limit. |\n\n"},{"similarity":0.6066305041313171,"url":"https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/platform/spend-management/","title":"Spend Management","text":"# Spending limits\n\nLast updated Nov 13, 2026|Copy as Markdown|[View as Markdown](index.md)|[Agent setup](/agent-setup/)\n\n[Set a spending limit](/billing/manage/spend-management/) on Workers usage charges. The limit covers requests and CPU time across all Workers in your account, after included usage. It excludes the monthly subscription fee.\n\nTo configure a limit, follow [Set a spending limit in the dashboard](/billing/manage/spend-management/#set-a-spending-limit-in-the-dashboard) or [Manage spending limits and alerts with the cf CLI](/billing/manage/spend-management/cli/).\n\n## What stops at the limit\n\nOnce the limit takes effect, Cloudflare rejects new invocations of your Workers, including:\n\n* Incoming HTTP requests.\n* Cron Triggers.\n* Queue consumer invocations.\n* Email Worker invocations.\n* Calls from other Workers or Durable Objects.\n\nHTTP visitors receive error `1103`. This error has other causes, so check **Billing** \\> **Spend Management** before contacting support. Requests rejected by the spending limit are not billed as Worker invocations.\n\nStatic assets served without running your Worker continue to be available. Requests that need Worker code, such as requests routed through `run_worker_first`, can fail. A limit does not delete your Workers or assets.\n\n## Plan for application dependencies\n\nA Workers limit applies to the whole account, rather than one application or environment. For example, a test Worker can reach the shared limit and interrupt a production Worker in the same account.\n\n"},{"similarity":0.5900054574012756,"url":"https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/static-assets/billing-and-limitations/","title":"Billing And Limitations","text":"## Limitations\n\nSee the [Platform Limits](/workers/platform/limits/#static-assets)\n\n### Range requests\n\nWhen a request for a static asset includes a `Range` header, Workers returns `200 OK` with the full file instead of `206 Partial Content`, and the response has no `Content-Range` or `Accept-Ranges` header. Some clients need range support, for example Safari when it plays video.\n\nTo serve byte ranges, route the affected paths to your Worker with [run\\_worker\\_first](/workers/static-assets/binding/#run%5Fworker%5Ffirst). In your Worker, fetch the file with `env.ASSETS.fetch()`, then return a `206 Partial Content` response that contains the requested bytes and a `Content-Range` header.\n\n## Troubleshooting\n\n* `assets.bucket is a required field` — if you see this error, you need to update Wrangler to at least `3.78.10` or later. `bucket` is not a required field.\n* Asset requests fail after a deployment — HTML and asset requests may use different versions. An older page may also request a file missing from the version handling that request. Refer to [Version skew and static assets](/workers/versions-and-deployments/version-skew/).\n\nWas this helpful?\n\nYesNo\n\n## On this page\n\n[![](/_astro/logo.te5VL_aD.svg)Docs](/)\n\n"},{"similarity":0.5428529381752014,"url":"https://developers.cloudflare.com/kv/platform/pricing/","title":"Pricing","text":"# Pricing\n\nLast updated Oct 30, 2026|Copy as Markdown|[View as Markdown](index.md)|[Agent setup](/agent-setup/)\n\nWorkers KV is included in both the Free and Paid [Workers plans](/workers/platform/pricing/).\n\n|               | Free plan1    | Paid plan                                                                                                   |\n| ------------- | ------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Keys read     | 100,000 / day | 10 million/month, + $0.50/million                                                                           |\n| Keys written  | 1,000 / day   | 1 million/month, + $5.00/million                                                                            |\n| Keys deleted  | 1,000 / day   | 1 million/month, + $5.00/million                                                                            |\n| List requests | 1,000 / day   | 1 million/month, + $5.00/million                                                                            |\n| Stored data   | 1 GB          | 1 GB, + $0.50/ GB-month                                                                                     |\n| Namespaces    | 1,000         | Unlimited, with a default limit of 1,000\\. First 1,000 included + $0.10 per additional namespace per month. |\n\nRefer to [KV limits](/kv/platform/limits/#workers-kv) for namespace creation limits and limit increases.\n\n1 The Workers Free plan includes limited Workers KV usage. Daily usage limits reset daily at 00:00 UTC. If you exceed any one of these limits, further operations of that type will fail with an error.\n\nNote\n\nWorkers KV pricing for read, write and delete operations is on a per-key basis. Bulk read operations are billed by the amount of keys read in a bulk read operation.\n\n## Pricing FAQ\n\n### How much do additional namespaces cost?\n\n"},{"similarity":0.3864353895187378,"url":"https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/platform/pricing/","title":"Pricing","text":"KV documentation\n\nTo learn more about KV, refer to the [KV documentation](/kv/).\n\n## Hyperdrive\n\nHyperdrive is included in both the Free and Paid [Workers plans](/workers/platform/pricing/).\n\n|                                         | Free plan[1](#user-content-fn-1) | Paid plan |\n| --------------------------------------- | -------------------------------- | --------- |\n| Database queries[2](#user-content-fn-2) | 100,000 / day                    | Unlimited |\n\nFootnotes\n\n1: The Workers Free plan includes limited Hyperdrive usage. All limits reset daily at 00:00 UTC. If you exceed any one of these limits, further operations of that type will fail with an error.\n\n2: Database queries refers to any database statement made via Hyperdrive, whether a query (`SELECT`), a modification (`INSERT`,`UPDATE`, or `DELETE`) or a schema change (`CREATE`, `ALTER`, `DROP`).\n\n## Footnotes\n\n1. The Workers Free plan includes limited Hyperdrive usage. All limits reset daily at 00:00 UTC. If you exceed any one of these limits, further operations of that type will fail with an error. [↩](#user-content-fnref-1)\n2. Database queries refers to any database statement made via Hyperdrive, whether a query (`SELECT`), a modification (`INSERT`,`UPDATE`, or `DELETE`) or a schema change (`CREATE`, `ALTER`, `DROP`). [↩](#user-content-fnref-2)\n\nHyperdrive documentation\n\nTo learn more about Hyperdrive, refer to the [Hyperdrive documentation](/hyperdrive/).\n\n## Queues\n\nCloudflare Queues charges for operations and for queues above the included amount on the Workers Paid plan.\n\n"},{"similarity":0.38552767038345337,"url":"https://developers.cloudflare.com/browser-run/faq/","title":"Faq","text":"## Errors & Troubleshooting\n\n### Error: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'fetch')\n\nThis error typically occurs because your Puppeteer launch is not receiving the browser binding. To resolve this error, pass your browser binding into `puppeteer.launch`.\n\n### Error: 429 browser time limit exceeded\n\nThis error (`Unable to create new browser: code: 429: message: Browser time limit exceeded for today`) indicates you have hit the daily browser-instance limit on the Workers Free plan. [Workers Free plan accounts are capped at 10 minutes of browser use a day](/browser-run/limits/#workers-free). Once you exceed that limit, further creation attempts return a 429 error until the next UTC day.\n\nTo resolve this error, [upgrade to a Workers Paid plan](/workers/platform/pricing/) which allows for more than 10 minutes of usage a day and has higher [limits](/browser-run/limits/#workers-paid). If you recently upgraded but still see this error, try redeploying your Worker to ensure your usage is correctly associated with your new plan.\n\n### Error: 422 unprocessable entity\n\nA `422 Unprocessable Entity` error usually means that Browser Run was not able to complete an action because of an issue with the site.\n\nThis can happen if:\n\n* The website consumes too much memory during rendering.\n* The page itself crashed or returned an error before the action completed.\n* The request exceeded one of the [timeout limits](/browser-run/reference/timeouts/) for page load, element load, or an action.\n\nMost often, this error is caused by a timeout. You can review the different timers and their limits in the [Quick Actions timeouts reference](/browser-run/reference/timeouts/).\n\n### Why is my page content missing or incomplete?\n\nIf your screenshots, PDFs, or scraped content are missing elements that appear when viewing the page in a browser, the page likely has not finished loading before Browser Run captures the output.\n\n"},{"similarity":0.3796478509902954,"url":"https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/platform/limits/","title":"Limits","text":"## Cache API limits\n\n| Feature             | Workers Free | Workers Paid |\n| ------------------- | ------------ | ------------ |\n| Maximum object size | 512 MB       | 512 MB       |\n| Calls per request   | 50           | 1,000        |\n\nCalls per request is the number of `put()`, `match()`, or `delete()` Cache API calls per request. This shares the same quota as subrequests (`fetch()`).\n\nNote\n\nThe size of chunked response bodies (`Transfer-Encoding: chunked`) is not known in advance. Calling `.put()` with such a response blocks subsequent `.put()` calls until the current one completes.\n\n---\n\n## Log size\n\n| Limit                | Value  |\n| -------------------- | ------ |\n| Log data per request | 256 KB |\n\nThis limit covers all data emitted via `console.log()` statements, exceptions, request metadata, and headers for a single request. After exceeding this limit, the system does not record additional context for that request in logs, tail logs, or [Tail Workers](/workers/observability/logs/tail-workers/).\n\nRefer to the [Workers Trace Event Logpush documentation](/workers/observability/logs/logpush/#limits) for limits on fields sent to Logpush destinations.\n\n---\n\n## Image Resizing with Workers\n\nRefer to the [Image Resizing documentation](/images/optimization/transformations/overview/) for limits that apply when using Image Resizing with Workers.\n\n---\n\n## Static Assets\n\n"},{"similarity":0.37404119968414307,"url":"https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/platform/pricing/","title":"Pricing","text":"## Workers KV\n\nWorkers KV is included in both the Free and Paid [Workers plans](/workers/platform/pricing/).\n\n|               | Free plan1    | Paid plan                                                                                                   |\n| ------------- | ------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Keys read     | 100,000 / day | 10 million/month, + $0.50/million                                                                           |\n| Keys written  | 1,000 / day   | 1 million/month, + $5.00/million                                                                            |\n| Keys deleted  | 1,000 / day   | 1 million/month, + $5.00/million                                                                            |\n| List requests | 1,000 / day   | 1 million/month, + $5.00/million                                                                            |\n| Stored data   | 1 GB          | 1 GB, + $0.50/ GB-month                                                                                     |\n| Namespaces    | 1,000         | Unlimited, with a default limit of 1,000\\. First 1,000 included + $0.10 per additional namespace per month. |\n\nRefer to [KV limits](/kv/platform/limits/#workers-kv) for namespace creation limits and limit increases.\n\n1 The Workers Free plan includes limited Workers KV usage. Daily usage limits reset daily at 00:00 UTC. If you exceed any one of these limits, further operations of that type will fail with an error.\n\nNote\n\nWorkers KV pricing for read, write and delete operations is on a per-key basis. Bulk read operations are billed by the amount of keys read in a bulk read operation.\n\nKV documentation\n\nTo learn more about KV, refer to the [KV documentation](/kv/).\n\n## Hyperdrive\n\nHyperdrive is included in both the Free and Paid [Workers plans](/workers/platform/pricing/).\n\n"},{"similarity":0.3557373583316803,"url":"https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/platform/limits/","title":"Limits","text":"## Files\n\nPages uploads each file on your site to Cloudflare's globally distributed network to deliver a low latency experience to every user that visits your site. Cloudflare Pages sites can contain up to 20,000 files on the Free plan.\n\nPaid plans (such as Pro, Business, and Enterprise plans) can have up to 100,000 files per site. To enable this increased limit, set the environment variable `PAGES_WRANGLER_MAJOR_VERSION=4` in your Pages project settings.\n\n## File size\n\nThe maximum file size for a single Cloudflare Pages site asset is 25 MiB.\n\nLarger Files\n\nTo serve larger files, consider uploading them to [R2](/r2/) and utilizing the [public bucket](/r2/buckets/public-buckets/) feature. You can also use [custom domains](/r2/buckets/public-buckets/#connect-a-bucket-to-a-custom-domain), such as `static.example.com`, for serving these files.\n\n## Functions\n\nRequests to [Pages functions](/pages/functions/) count towards your quota for Workers plans, including requests from your Function to KV or Durable Object bindings.\n\nPages supports the [Standard usage model](/workers/platform/pricing/#example-pricing-standard-usage-model).\n\n## Headers\n\nA `_headers` file can have a maximum of 100 header rules.\n\nAn individual header in a `_headers` file can have a maximum of 2,000 characters. For managing larger headers, it is recommended to implement [Pages Functions](/pages/functions/).\n\n## Preview deployments\n\nYou can have an unlimited number of [preview deployments](/pages/configuration/preview-deployments/) active on your project at a time.\n\n## Redirects\n\n"},{"similarity":0.3338557183742523,"url":"https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/platform/limits/","title":"Limits","text":"| Feature                                                                     | Workers Free | Workers Paid               |\n| --------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------ | -------------------------- |\n| [Requests](#daily-requests)                                                 | 100,000/day  | No limit                   |\n| [CPU time](#cpu-time)                                                       | 10 ms        | 5 min                      |\n| [Memory](#memory)                                                           | 128 MB       | 128 MB                     |\n| [Subrequests](#subrequests)                                                 | 50/request   | 10,000/request             |\n| [Simultaneous outgoing connections/request](#simultaneous-open-connections) | 6            | 6                          |\n| [Environment variables](#environment-variables)                             | 64/Worker    | 128/Worker                 |\n| [Environment variable size](#environment-variables)                         | 5 KB         | 5 KB                       |\n| [Worker size](#worker-size)                                                 | 64 MiB       | 64 MiB                     |\n| [Worker startup time](#worker-startup-time)                                 | 1 second     | 1 second                   |\n| [Number of Workers](#number-of-workers)                                     | 100          | 500[1](#user-content-fn-1) |\n| Number of [Cron Triggers](/workers/configuration/cron-triggers/)per account | 5            | 250                        |\n| Number of [Static Asset](#static-assets) files per Worker version           | 20,000       | 100,000                    |\n| Individual [Static Asset](#static-assets) file size                         | 25 MiB       | 25 MiB                     |\n\nNeed a higher limit?\n\n"},{"similarity":0.31842294335365295,"url":"https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/static-assets/migration-guides/vercel-to-workers/react-router/","title":"React Router","text":"## Troubleshooting\n\n* **The build fails with `Could not load virtual:react-router/server-manifest`.** Either the `v8_viteEnvironmentApi` future flag is missing, or `vercelPreset()` is still configured.\n* **React Router 7.10 or later rejects `unstable_viteEnvironmentApi`.** The flag was renamed to `v8_viteEnvironmentApi`. Some starter templates still use the old name.\n* **The install fails with `ERESOLVE`.** `@vercel/remix` pins Remix 2, and `@cloudflare/vite-plugin` requires Vite 6.1 or later. Remove `@vercel/remix`, upgrade Vite, and reinstall from a clean lockfile.\n* **The codemod fails with `Registry error: HTTP request failed`.** This happens behind TLS-inspecting proxies. Use `npx codemod@0.18.13 remix/2/react-router/upgrade --no-interactive`.\n* **Every SSR route returns `500` with `renderToPipeableStream is not a function`.** The application has no `app/entry.server.tsx`, so React Router uses its Node.js default entry. Create an entry that uses `renderToReadableStream`, based on the [React Router starter template ↗︎](https://github.com/cloudflare/templates/blob/main/react-router-starter-template/app/entry.server.tsx). Static assets and `.data` requests still succeed, so check an SSR route.\n* **Remix `?_data` requests stop working.** React Router v7 uses `/<route>.data` endpoints. Browser tabs that loaded the old bundle can fail one navigation after the cutover.\n\n## Related resources\n\n* [React Router framework guide](/workers/framework-guides/web-apps/react-router/)\n* [Migrate from Vercel to Workers](/workers/static-assets/migration-guides/vercel-to-workers/)\n* [Cloudflare Vite plugin](/workers/vite-plugin/)\n\nWas this helpful?\n\nYesNo\n\n## On this page\n\n[![](/_astro/logo.te5VL_aD.svg)Docs](/)\n\n"}]}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"4ba0b504-c6e5-4628-b272-7d0295a1c07b","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"session_id":"ef9f3fc8-12b6-4fe4-9f49-aaeedec05648","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/danielbentes/agent-capability-standard/.claude/worktrees/i127","sessionId":"ef9f3fc8-12b6-4fe4-9f49-aaeedec05648","version":"2.1.322","gitBranch":"feature/issue-127-agent-ready","slug":"i-just-came-across-imperative-newell"}
