{"parentUuid":"910cfb99-5470-4e96-8639-ea019a2c9659","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch1EJ6HJnSQXCWr6VtuEG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XzmKFW8AFigwuaw1m9Fuua","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/danielbentes/agent-capability-standard/.claude/worktrees/i127 && REDACTED && cat > $S/msg-review3.txt <<'EOF'\nfix(site): plural searches, headings with \">\", ids with stopwords\n\nThe re-review of the previous fix found two regressions and a gap:\n- Whole-word matching exposed a stemmer that gave \"verifies\" and\n  \"verify\" different stems, so plural searches lost the pages named in\n  the singular. \"-ies\" now becomes \"-y\" and a final \"-y\" becomes \"-i\",\n  in the one stem function the build and the worker share.\n- Splitting read_page's section on every \">\" made a heading such as\n  \"A map<K,V> annotation\" unreadable. The whole text is tried as one\n  heading first, and the path form splits only on \" > \".\n- A workflow id with a stopword (monitor_and_replan) never earned its\n  id bonus, because the query drops stopwords; the id's do too now.\n\nRefs #127\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Jea2Va3FATnCydAsWsbLXR\nEOF\ngit add -A site && git commit -q -F $S/msg-review3.txt && git push -q origin feature/issue-127-agent-ready && git rev-parse --short HEAD && git ls-remote origin feature/issue-127-agent-ready | cut -c1-7","description":"Commit and push the re-review fixes"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1185,"cache_read_input_tokens":337934,"output_tokens":771,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":91},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1185,"epheme