{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"ef9f3fc8-12b6-4fe4-9f49-aaeedec05648","hash":"36f8e81025512bfdbe7d340f4ecfb8195daa0f44d9ed77c4eaa4a77b3bc50f5e","message":{"role":"system","content":[{"type":"text","text":"While bypass permissions mode is active:\n\nYou can do much of your work through the Bash tool when it is the simpler route: read files with cat, head, or sed -n, search with grep and find, and make small, mechanical file changes with sed, heredocs, or short scripts instead of the dedicated Read, Edit, or Write tools. The choice is yours: prefer Edit or Write when a shell edit would be fragile, such as exact or multi-line replacements, or sed/awk flags that differ between GNU and BSD/macOS."}]}}
