{"parentUuid":"e45612bf-dc07-425b-9411-fb3cc93275b2","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch2jaY6eEa2UoU5ucpskA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01QV98dqsyQqTYMkxsv7sjjc","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"curl -s https://ora.ai/llms.txt | grep -iE 'scan|api|rescan|POST' | head -20","description":"Look for ora.ai scan API usage"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":723,"cache_read_input_tokens":145578,"output_tokens":120,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":723,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":120,"cache_read_input_tokens":145578,"cache_creation_input_tokens":723,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":723},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":890,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01QV98dqsyQqTYMkxsv7sjjc":{"command":"curl -s https://ora.ai/llms.txt | grep -iE 'scan|api|rescan|POST' | head -20","description":"Look for ora.ai scan API usage"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"be2e03b2-1d01-4974-ae9c-cbd3c4e2c4f7","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Ch2jaXqmZp4LTfSaUbkAe","requestRef":"26f48cd8-3353-4b7d-bdc9-fce0048c89fc","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","attributionMcpServer":"claude-in-chrome","attributionMcpTool":"tabs_close_mcp","type":"assistant","uuid":"a3654a85-42a8-4c3a-adee-601bed2dbaeb","timestamp":"2026-11-14T11:23:19.251Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-2","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ef9f3fc8-12b6-4fe4-9f49-aaeedec05648","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/danielbentes/agent-capability-standard/.claude/worktrees/i127","sessionId":"ef9f3fc8-12b6-4fe4-9f49-aaeedec05648","version":"2.1.322","gitBranch":"feature/issue-127-agent-ready","slug":"i-just-came-across-imperative-newell"}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"ef9f3fc8-12b6-4fe4-9f49-aaeedec05648","hash":"ff484cd98cd780f0bb241f56534f9a387aaf5a86ffcb45b2fd15646cf66f0487","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QV98dqsyQqTYMkxsv7sjjc","type":"tool_result","content":"> ora is the standard for optimizing your site so agents can actually use and recommend you. Scan a URL, watch real agents try to use it, and fix what turns them away.\n- Scan a domain, an MCP server URL, or an MCP App, and get a 0-100 score, an A-F grade, and a four-layer breakdown.\n- Search the paid-capability index: pay-per-call API endpoints (x402/MPP) with per-call USD prices and no API key, liveness-checked by rolling unpaid 402 probes - via the `search_capabilities` MCP tool or the directory.\n- Public URLs only. ora cannot scan private or internal sites, or login-gated content.\n- A fresh scan takes about 30 seconds. Some checks (\"deep\") use live agent and LLM evaluation and resolve asynchronously after that.\n- [Request examples](https://ora.ai/agents.md#ask-this-website): POST JSON and GET queries, streaming, limits, and retries.\n- [API documentation](https://ora.ai/openapi.json): complete request and evidence-response schemas for `/ask`.\n- Primary agent interface (all tools, including feedback): MCP server at https://ora.ai/api/mcp\n- Searching or reading these docs (search_docs, get_docs_page, get_endpoint; read-only): docs MCP server at https://ora.ai/api/docs/mcp\n- In the browser (WebMCP): every ora page registers site tools via document.modelContext - scan_domain, get_score, get_leaderboard - wrapping the same REST endpoints below\n- Look up a cached score: GET https://ora.ai/api/score/{domain} (always try this before scanning)\n- Run a fresh scan: POST https://ora.ai/api/scan (only on a cache miss or an explicit rescan; a 202 with a Location header means deeper analysis is still finishing - poll that URL)\n- Poll after scanning: GET https://ora.ai/api/score/{domain} until analysisStatus === \"complete\"\n- Run a subset of checks or re-verify a fix: POST https://ora.ai/api/scan/checks (body: url + checkIds from /api/checks; no aggregate score)\n- Discover products by intent: GET https://ora.ai/api/discover?intent=...\n- Read agent feedback: GET https://ora.ai/api/feedback/{domain}\n- Run an agent journey (a real agent attempts a curated task against a domain; trajectory streams as SSE): POST https://ora.ai/api/journey/runs, then open the returned stream_url - intents at GET /api/journey/intents, runnable agents at GET /api/journey/agents; partners holding an ora-issued API key can send a custom free-text task instead of a curated intent, shape at https://ora.ai/api/openapi.json (CLI: npx ax@0.10 deep-journey <url> --intent <id>; MCP: run_journey, then get_journey_run)\n- Read a finished journey (verdict, step count, trajectory, insight): GET https://ora.ai/api/journey/runs/{id}\n- Get or create a domain's journey in one call (ora picks the task and the agent; returns the existing journey, or runs one if there is none): POST https://ora.ai/api/journey/domains/{host} - requires an ora-issued partner API key, shape at https://ora.ai/api/openapi.json\n- Check your partner API key's usage and daily or monthly limits (scans, journeys): GET https://ora.ai/api/usage - requires an ora-issued partner API key, shape at https://ora.ai/api/openapi.json","is_error":false}]}}
