{"parentUuid":"81cbde08-6f50-48b0-aa3e-0854ab5a8e96","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"e01b7892-db0a-48da-bb76-c03aafabadb6","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01H8xZon1v1uWdDwfHHLhcav","type":"tool_result","content":"<persisted-output>\nOutput too large (114.9KB). Full output saved to: /Users/danielbentes/.REDACTED.txt\n\nPreview (first 2KB):\nHTTP/2 200 \n{\"domain\":\"acs.synapti.ai\",\"url\":\"https://acs.synapti.ai\",\"finalUrl\":\"https://acs.synapti.ai/\",\"score\":78,\"maxScore\":100,\"grade\":\"B\",\"analysisStatus\":\"complete\",\"pendingChecks\":[],\"ctaMessage\":\"Strong foundation. Real gaps in the experience layer.\",\"ctaTier\":\"high\",\"layers\":[{\"id\":\"discovery\",\"name\":\"Discovery\",\"description\":\"Can agents find and recommend you?\",\"checks\":[{\"id\":\"ard-catalog\",\"name\":\"ARD discovery\",\"description\":\"One catalog that tells agents everything you offer them: MCP servers, APIs, agents, and skills. Without it, every agent has to hunt for your capabilities page by page. We look where ARD v0.91 tells agents to look: an Agentic Resource Discovery catalog at /.well-known/ard.json, or one your homepage points to with a <link rel=\\\"ard\\\"> tag (an HTTP Link header with rel=\\\"ard\\\" also counts). The predecessor /.well-known/ai-catalog.json and rel=\\\"ai-catalog\\\" still count, with a nudge to move. Entries published only through a robots.txt Agentmap directive or as JSON-LD on your homepage are noted without the point, since agents resolving your domain are not required to read them. Weighted at 1 point while ecosystem adoption is early (2026-08 audit; was 3).\",\"status\":\"pass\",\"score\":1,\"maxScore\":1,\"details\":\"ARD catalog valid at /.well-known/ard.json - 5/5 entries\",\"recommendation\":\"Add a trustManifest with an identity (a did:web, https or spiffe URI on your own domain) to catalog entries, plus any attestations, provenance or signature, so clients can verify your resources with progressive trust\",\"bonus\":false,\"specUrl\":\"https://agenticresourcediscovery.org/\",\"data\":{\"entryCount\":5,\"validEntryCount\":5,\"hasTrustManifest\":false,\"hasRegistry\":false,\"hasUrnIdentifiers\":true,\"source\":\"ard\"},\"maturity\":\"verified\",\"tier\":\"required\"},{\"id\":\"ai-catalog-published\",\"name\":\"AI Catalog discovery\",\"description\":\"The AI Catalog Standard (ai-catalog.io, Agent-Card WG) specifies its own discovery path, /.well-known/ai-catalog.json, separately from ARD's a\n...\n</persisted-output>","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"dae92f0c-3fbc-4a69-af5b-e066341c7183","timestamp":"2026-11-14T11:23:31.684Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"HTTP/2 200 \n{\"domain\":\"acs.synapti.ai\",\"url\":\"https://acs.synapti.ai\",\"finalUrl\":\"https://acs.synapti.ai/\",\"score\":78,\"maxScore\":100,\"grade\":\"B\",\"analysisStatus\":\"complete\",\"pendingChecks\":[],\"ctaMessage\":\"Strong foundation. Real gaps in the experience layer.\",\"ctaTier\":\"high\",\"layers\":[{\"id\":\"discovery\",\"name\":\"Discovery\",\"description\":\"Can agents find and recommend you?\",\"checks\":[{\"id\":\"ard-catalog\",\"name\":\"ARD discovery\",\"description\":\"One catalog that tells agents everything you offer them: MCP servers, APIs, agents, and skills. Without it, every agent has to hunt for your capabilities page by page. We look where ARD v0.91 tells agents to look: an Agentic Resource Discovery catalog at /.well-known/ard.json, or one your homepage points to with a <link rel=\\\"ard\\\"> tag (an HTTP Link header with rel=\\\"ard\\\" also counts). The predecessor /.well-known/ai-catalog.json and rel=\\\"ai-catalog\\\" still count, with a nudge to move. Entries published only through a robots.txt Agentmap directive or as JSON-LD on your homepage are noted without the point, since agents resolving your domain are not required to read them. Weighted at 1 point while ecosystem adoption is early (2026-08 audit; was 3).\",\"status\":\"pass\",\"score\":1,\"maxScore\":1,\"details\":\"ARD catalog valid at /.well-known/ard.json - 5/5 entries\",\"recommendation\":\"Add a trustManifest with an identity (a did:web, https or spiffe URI on your own domain) to catalog entries, plus any attestations, provenance or signature, so clients can verify your resources with progressive trust\",\"bonus\":false,\"specUrl\":\"https://agenticresourcediscovery.org/\",\"data\":{\"entryCount\":5,\"validEntryCount\":5,\"hasTrustManifest\":false,\"hasRegistry\":false,\"hasUrnIdentifiers\":true,\"source\":\"ard\"},\"maturity\":\"verified\",\"tier\":\"required\"},{\"id\":\"ai-catalog-published\",\"name\":\"AI Catalog discovery\",\"description\":\"The AI Catalog Standard (ai-catalog.io, Agent-Card WG) specifies its own discovery path, /.well-known/ai-catalog.json, separately from ARD's ard.json. Serving a valid catalog there keeps you discoverable by consumers that follow that spec. Bonus: earns credit when present, never costs points.\",\"status\":\"pass\",\"score\":1,\"maxScore\":1,\"details\":\"Valid AI Catalog at /.well-known/ai-catalog.json (spec 1.0) - 5/5 entries\",\"recommendation\":\"Serve a valid catalog at /.well-known/ai-catalog.json - the AI Catalog Standard's own discovery path - so consumers following that spec (see https://ai-catalog.io/) also find you. The entries can match those in /.well-known/ard.json, with two differences: this standard's document also needs \\\"specVersion\\\": \\\"1.0\\\" at the top level, and it has no single trustManifest field. Trust metadata goes in a trustManifests array: each manifest names its contributor (an absolute URI) and carries real evidence such as a signature, attestations or provenance, and an entry can carry several; leave the array out when you have none.\",\"bonus\":true,\"specUrl\":\"https://ai-catalog.io/\",\"data\":{\"entryCount\":5,\"validEntryCount\":5},\"maturity\":\"emerging\",\"tier\":\"emerging\"},{\"id\":\"ard-entries-valid\",\"name\":\"ARD entry validity\",\"description\":\"Each entry in your catalog is complete enough for an agent to actually use it: a urn:air identifier on your own domain, a display name, a media type, and exactly one of a url or inline data. Validated against ARD v0.91's entry model on the catalog the ARD discovery check found (ard.json, a rel=\\\"ard\\\" source, else the legacy ai-catalog.json); the AI Catalog Standard's lighter entry rules are graded by the AI Catalog discovery check. Only applies when the catalog exists; partial adoption earns credit and never costs points.\",\"status\":\"pass\",\"score\":2,\"maxScore\":2,\"details\":\"All 5 entries valid with domain-anchored urn:air identifiers (catalog at /.well-known/ard.json)\",\"recommendation\":\"Make every catalog entry fully valid: a domain-anchored urn:air identifier, a displayName, a media type, and exactly one of url or data. Applies to the catalog at /.well-known/ard.json, behind a rel=\\\"ard\\\" link, or at the legacy /.well-known/ai-catalog.json.\",\"bonus\":false,\"specUrl\":\"https://ai-catalog.io/\",\"maturity\":\"verified\",\"tier\":\"recommended\"},{\"id\":\"ard-trust-manifest\",\"name\":\"ARD trust manifest\",\"description\":\"Trust signals inside your catalog (verified identity, compliance attestations, signatures) that let cautious agents pick you over an unverified alternative. The trust model comes from the AI Catalog Standard and is validated on whichever path serves your catalog. Only applies when the catalog exists; never costs points.\",\"status\":\"fail\",\"score\":0,\"maxScore\":2,\"details\":\"No entry carries a trustManifest or trustManifests\",\"recommendation\":\"Add a trustManifest with an identity (a did:web, https or spiffe URI on your own domain) to catalog entries, plus any attestations, provenance or signature, so clients can verify your resources with progressive trust\",\"bonus\":true,\"specUrl\":\"https://ai-catalog.io/\",\"maturity\":\"emerging\",\"tier\":\"emerging\"},{\"id\":\"agentic-search-specific\",\"name\":\"Developer resource discoverability\",\"description\":\"Can an agent find your developer resources with the searches it would really run? We search for your API docs and expect your own docs page among the results, then for your MCP server, SDK or CLI and, when you have one, expect your own page for it. Pages on other sites, including other companies with a similar name, don't count, unless your homepage or llms.txt links that site's docs, or your homepage redirects to a parent company's site and the page's address names your product. GitHub repos count only in an org your site links to.\",\"status\":\"fail\",\"score\":0,\"maxScore\":4,\"details\":\"In a search for your API docs, none of the 10 results is your official docs. In a search for your MCP server, SDK or CLI, none of the 10 results is your own, although the scan found one on your site\",\"recommendation\":\"Make sure a web search for your product's API docs returns your own docs page, and a search for your MCP server, SDK or CLI returns your own pages for those tools. Keep docs on your own domain or a subdomain, or link your docs site from your homepage or llms.txt, give each tool its own page (for example /mcp) with the tool name in the title, put your product name and \\\"API\\\" in the docs title and main heading, and link your GitHub org from your homepage.\",\"bonus\":false,\"maturity\":\"verified\",\"tier\":\"recommended\",\"estScoreGain\":5.6},{\"id\":\"brand-search-accuracy\",\"name\":\"Brand name discoverability\",\"description\":\"When people search for your brand together with your main product, your domain should be in the top results. If it is not, agents cannot reliably tell you apart from lookalikes and resellers.\",\"status\":\"fail\",\"score\":0,\"maxScore\":3,\"details\":\"acs.synapti.ai was not in the top 10 for \\\"Synapti agent capability standard\\\" or \\\"Synapti grounded agency\\\"\",\"recommendation\":\"Make sure your own domain ranks in the top results when people search your brand together with your main product (for example \\\"Acme payments API\\\"). Ora first reads product terms from your homepage's JSON-LD keywords or knowsAbout, or its meta keywords tag. If none qualifies, it checks the main service's serviceType in JSON-LD, then a short product phrase in the page title. If those do not qualify, it checks product names in the homepage business's JSON-LD offers. Use clear product terms that also appear on the page. If no term qualifies, Ora searches your brand name alone. If your domain does not rank, your brand may be too generic, conflict with a more established term, or not yet indexed. Strengthen it by describing your main product clearly in your homepage title and headings, earning press mentions that link to your domain, and avoiding redirect chains that mask your main domain in search results.\",\"bonus\":false,\"data\":{\"query\":\"Synapti agent capability standard\",\"term\":\"agent capability standard\",\"termSource\":\"picked\",\"bareBrandReason\":null,\"rank\":null,\"matchCount\":0,\"mode\":\"site_term\",\"searches\":[{\"query\":\"Synapti agent capability standard\",\"rank\":null,\"matchCount\":0,\"score\":0},{\"query\":\"Synapti grounded agency\",\"rank\":null,\"matchCount\":0,\"score\":0}]},\"maturity\":\"verified\",\"tier\":\"required\",\"estScoreGain\":4.2},{\"id\":\"robots-ai-policy-quality\",\"name\":\"robots.txt AI crawler policy\",\"description\":\"Whether your robots.txt lets the AI search crawlers (OAI-SearchBot, Claude-SearchBot, PerplexityBot) read your public pages, so AI search can find you. Blocking AI training crawlers such as GPTBot and ClaudeBot is your choice and never lowers this score.\",\"status\":\"pass\",\"score\":1,\"maxScore\":1,\"details\":\"AI search crawlers: allowed in 18 of 18 checks (3 crawlers on 6 pages). AI training crawlers: allowed in 12 of 12 checks (2 crawlers on 6 pages), not scored. No applicable crawl or usage restriction found for 3 search crawlers (oai-searchbot, claude-searchbot, perplexitybot) on 6 public pages: https://acs.synapti.ai/, https://acs.synapti.ai/about/, https://acs.synapti.ai/capabilities/measure/, https://acs.synapti.ai/compliance/iso-42001/ai-policy-template/, https://acs.synapti.ai/guides/skills/digital-twin-bootstrap/, https://acs.synapti.ai/start/glossary/. Declared policy only; absence of a Content Signal expresses no usage preference. Paths outside this sample, live bot access, indexing, and model training are not verified\",\"recommendation\":\"In robots.txt, allow the AI search crawlers (OAI-SearchBot, Claude-SearchBot, PerplexityBot) to read your public pages, so AI search can find and cite them. The result shows which pages and which robots.txt lines block them. Keep private and account pages blocked. Blocking AI training crawlers such as GPTBot and ClaudeBot is your choice and never lowers this score. Visits that people ask an AI to make are covered by a separate check. Serve robots.txt as plain text: a server error makes crawlers treat the whole site as blocked, and an HTML page gives them no rules.\",\"bonus\":false,\"data\":{\"robotsUrl\":\"https://acs.synapti.ai/robots.txt\",\"robotsFinalUrl\":\"https://acs.synapti.ai/robots.txt\",\"robotsHttpStatus\":200,\"evaluatedUrls\":[\"https://acs.synapti.ai/\",\"https://acs.synapti.ai/about/\",\"https://acs.synapti.ai/capabilities/measure/\",\"https://acs.synapti.ai/compliance/iso-42001/ai-policy-template/\",\"https://acs.synapti.ai/guides/skills/digital-twin-bootstrap/\",\"https://acs.synapti.ai/start/glossary/\"],\"evaluatedCrawlers\":[\"oai-searchbot\",\"claude-searchbot\",\"perplexitybot\",\"gptbot\",\"claudebot\"],\"coverage\":{\"search\":{\"permitted\":18,\"evaluated\":18},\"training\":{\"permitted\":12,\"evaluated\":12}},\"access\":[{\"url\":\"https://acs.synapti.ai/\",\"agent\":\"oai-searchbot\",\"purpose\":\"search\",\"scored\":true,\"access\":\"allowed\",\"source\":\"explicit\",\"rule\":\"Allow: /\",\"line\":10,\"usageSignal\":\"search\",\"permission\":\"permitted\",\"ruleTruncated\":false},{\"url\":\"https://acs.synapti.ai/\",\"agent\":\"claude-searchbot\",\"purpose\":\"search\",\"scored\":true,\"access\":\"allowed\",\"source\":\"explicit\",\"rule\":\"Allow: /\",\"line\":10,\"usageSignal\":\"search\",\"permission\":\"permitted\",\"ruleTruncated\":false},{\"url\":\"https://acs.synapti.ai/\",\"agent\":\"perplexitybot\",\"purpose\":\"search\",\"scored\":true,\"access\":\"allowed\",\"source\":\"explicit\",\"rule\":\"Allow: /\",\"line\":10,\"usageSignal\":\"search\",\"permission\":\"permitted\",\"ruleTruncated\":false},{\"url\":\"https://acs.synapti.ai/\",\"agent\":\"gptbot\",\"purpose\":\"training\",\"scored\":false,\"access\":\"allowed\",\"source\":\"wildcard\",\"rule\":\"Allow: /\",\"line\":2,\"usageSignal\":\"ai-train\",\"permission\":\"permitted\",\"ruleTruncated\":false},{\"url\":\"https://acs.synapti.ai/\",\"agent\":\"claudebot\",\"purpose\":\"training\",\"scored\":false,\"access\":\"allowed\",\"source\":\"wildcard\",\"rule\":\"Allow: /\",\"line\":2,\"usageSignal\":\"ai-train\",\"permission\":\"permitted\",\"ruleTruncated\":false},{\"url\":\"https://acs.synapti.ai/about/\",\"agent\":\"oai-searchbot\",\"purpose\":\"search\",\"scored\":true,\"access\":\"allowed\",\"source\":\"explicit\",\"rule\":\"Allow: /\",\"line\":10,\"usageSignal\":\"search\",\"permission\":\"permitted\",\"ruleTruncated\":false},{\"url\":\"https://acs.synapti.ai/about/\",\"agent\":\"claude-searchbot\",\"purpose\":\"search\",\"scored\":true,\"access\":\"allowed\",\"source\":\"explicit\",\"rule\":\"Allow: /\",\"line\":10,\"usageSignal\":\"search\",\"permission\":\"permitted\",\"ruleTruncated\":false},{\"url\":\"https://acs.synapti.ai/about/\",\"agent\":\"perplexitybot\",\"purpose\":\"search\",\"scored\":true,\"access\":\"allowed\",\"source\":\"explicit\",\"rule\":\"Allow: /\",\"line\":10,\"usageSignal\":\"search\",\"permission\":\"permitted\",\"ruleTruncated\":false},{\"url\":\"https://acs.synapti.ai/about/\",\"agent\":\"gptbot\",\"purpose\":\"training\",\"scored\":false,\"access\":\"allowed\",\"source\":\"wildcard\",\"rule\":\"Allow: /\",\"line\":2,\"usageSignal\":\"ai-train\",\"permission\":\"permitted\",\"ruleTruncated\":false},{\"url\":\"https://acs.synapti.ai/about/\",\"agent\":\"claudebot\",\"purpose\":\"training\",\"scored\":false,\"access\":\"allowed\",\"source\":\"wildcard\",\"rule\":\"Allow: /\",\"line\":2,\"usageSignal\":\"ai-train\",\"permission\":\"permitted\",\"ruleTruncated\":false},{\"url\":\"https://acs.synapti.ai/capabilities/measure/\",\"agent\":\"oai-searchbot\",\"purpose\":\"search\",\"scored\":true,\"access\":\"allowed\",\"source\":\"explicit\",\"rule\":\"Allow: /\",\"line\":10,\"usageSignal\":\"search\",\"permission\":\"permitted\",\"ruleTruncated\":false},{\"url\":\"https://acs.synapti.ai/capabilities/measure/\",\"agent\":\"claude-searchbot\",\"purpose\":\"search\",\"scored\":true,\"access\":\"allowed\",\"source\":\"explicit\",\"rule\":\"Allow: /\",\"line\":10,\"usageSignal\":\"search\",\"permission\":\"permitted\",\"ruleTruncated\":false},{\"url\":\"https://acs.synapti.ai/capabilities/measure/\",\"agent\":\"perplexitybot\",\"purpose\":\"search\",\"scored\":true,\"access\":\"allowed\",\"source\":\"explicit\",\"rule\":\"Allow: /\",\"line\":10,\"usageSignal\":\"search\",\"permission\":\"permitted\",\"ruleTruncated\":false},{\"url\":\"https://acs.synapti.ai/capabilities/measure/\",\"agent\":\"gptbot\",\"purpose\":\"training\",\"scored\":false,\"access\":\"allowed\",\"source\":\"wildcard\",\"rule\":\"Allow: /\",\"line\":2,\"usageSignal\":\"ai-train\",\"permission\":\"permitted\",\"ruleTruncated\":false},{\"url\":\"https://acs.synapti.ai/capabilities/measure/\",\"agent\":\"claudebot\",\"purpose\":\"training\",\"scored\":false,\"access\":\"allowed\",\"source\":\"wildcard\",\"rule\":\"Allow: /\",\"line\":2,\"usageSignal\":\"ai-train\",\"permission\":\"permitted\",\"ruleTruncated\":false},{\"url\":\"https://acs.synapti.ai/compliance/iso-42001/ai-policy-template/\",\"agent\":\"oai-searchbot\",\"purpose\":\"search\",\"scored\":true,\"access\":\"allowed\",\"source\":\"explicit\",\"rule\":\"Allow: /\",\"line\":10,\"usageSignal\":\"search\",\"permission\":\"permitted\",\"ruleTruncated\":false},{\"url\":\"https://acs.synapti.ai/compliance/iso-42001/ai-policy-template/\",\"agent\":\"claude-searchbot\",\"purpose\":\"search\",\"scored\":true,\"access\":\"allowed\",\"source\":\"explicit\",\"rule\":\"Allow: /\",\"line\":10,\"usageSignal\":\"search\",\"permission\":\"permitted\",\"ruleTruncated\":false},{\"url\":\"https://acs.synapti.ai/compliance/iso-42001/ai-policy-template/\",\"agent\":\"perplexitybot\",\"purpose\":\"search\",\"scored\":true,\"access\":\"allowed\",\"source\":\"explicit\",\"rule\":\"Allow: /\",\"line\":10,\"usageSignal\":\"search\",\"permission\":\"permitted\",\"ruleTruncated\":false},{\"url\":\"https://acs.synapti.ai/compliance/iso-42001/ai-policy-template/\",\"agent\":\"gptbot\",\"purpose\":\"training\",\"scored\":false,\"access\":\"allowed\",\"source\":\"wildcard\",\"rule\":\"Allow: /\",\"line\":2,\"usageSignal\":\"ai-train\",\"permission\":\"permitted\",\"ruleTruncated\":false},{\"url\":\"https://acs.synapti.ai/compliance/iso-42001/ai-policy-template/\",\"agent\":\"claudebot\",\"purpose\":\"training\",\"scored\":false,\"access\":\"allowed\",\"source\":\"wildcard\",\"rule\":\"Allow: /\",\"line\":2,\"usageSignal\":\"ai-train\",\"permission\":\"permitted\",\"ruleTruncated\":false},{\"url\":\"https://acs.synapti.ai/guides/skills/digital-twin-bootstrap/\",\"agent\":\"oai-searchbot\",\"purpose\":\"search\",\"scored\":true,\"access\":\"allowed\",\"source\":\"explicit\",\"rule\":\"Allow: /\",\"line\":10,\"usageSignal\":\"search\",\"permission\":\"permitted\",\"ruleTruncated\":false},{\"url\":\"https://acs.synapti.ai/guides/skills/digital-twin-bootstrap/\",\"agent\":\"claude-searchbot\",\"purpose\":\"search\",\"scored\":true,\"access\":\"allowed\",\"source\":\"explicit\",\"rule\":\"Allow: /\",\"line\":10,\"usageSignal\":\"search\",\"permission\":\"permitted\",\"ruleTruncated\":false},{\"url\":\"https://acs.synapti.ai/guides/skills/digital-twin-bootstrap/\",\"agent\":\"perplexitybot\",\"purpose\":\"search\",\"scored\":true,\"access\":\"allowed\",\"source\":\"explicit\",\"rule\":\"Allow: /\",\"line\":10,\"usageSignal\":\"search\",\"permission\":\"permitted\",\"ruleTruncated\":false},{\"url\":\"https://acs.synapti.ai/guides/skills/digital-twin-bootstrap/\",\"agent\":\"gptbot\",\"purpose\":\"training\",\"scored\":false,\"access\":\"allowed\",\"source\":\"wildcard\",\"rule\":\"Allow: /\",\"line\":2,\"usageSignal\":\"ai-train\",\"permission\":\"permitted\",\"ruleTruncated\":false},{\"url\":\"https://acs.synapti.ai/guides/skills/digital-twin-bootstrap/\",\"agent\":\"claudebot\",\"purpose\":\"training\",\"scored\":false,\"access\":\"allowed\",\"source\":\"wildcard\",\"rule\":\"Allow: /\",\"line\":2,\"usageSignal\":\"ai-train\",\"permission\":\"permitted\",\"ruleTruncated\":false},{\"url\":\"https://acs.synapti.ai/start/glossary/\",\"agent\":\"oai-searchbot\",\"purpose\":\"search\",\"scored\":true,\"access\":\"allowed\",\"source\":\"explicit\",\"rule\":\"Allow: /\",\"line\":10,\"usageSignal\":\"search\",\"permission\":\"permitted\",\"ruleTruncated\":false},{\"url\":\"https://acs.synapti.ai/start/glossary/\",\"agent\":\"claude-searchbot\",\"purpose\":\"search\",\"scored\":true,\"access\":\"allowed\",\"source\":\"explicit\",\"rule\":\"Allow: /\",\"line\":10,\"usageSignal\":\"search\",\"permission\":\"permitted\",\"ruleTruncated\":false},{\"url\":\"https://acs.synapti.ai/start/glossary/\",\"agent\":\"perplexitybot\",\"purpose\":\"search\",\"scored\":true,\"access\":\"allowed\",\"source\":\"explicit\",\"rule\":\"Allow: /\",\"line\":10,\"usageSignal\":\"search\",\"permission\":\"permitted\",\"ruleTruncated\":false},{\"url\":\"https://acs.synapti.ai/start/glossary/\",\"agent\":\"gptbot\",\"purpose\":\"training\",\"scored\":false,\"access\":\"allowed\",\"source\":\"wildcard\",\"rule\":\"Allow: /\",\"line\":2,\"usageSignal\":\"ai-train\",\"permission\":\"permitted\",\"ruleTruncated\":false},{\"url\":\"https://acs.synapti.ai/start/glossary/\",\"agent\":\"claudebot\",\"purpose\":\"training\",\"scored\":false,\"access\":\"allowed\",\"source\":\"wildcard\",\"rule\":\"Allow: /\",\"line\":2,\"usageSignal\":\"ai-train\",\"permission\":\"permitted\",\"ruleTruncated\":false}],\"contentSignalCount\":0,\"contentSignals\":[],\"usageGroupCount\":0,\"usageRules\":[]},\"maturity\":\"verified\",\"tier\":\"required\"},{\"id\":\"mcp-registry-listed\",\"name\":\"Listed in MCP registries\",\"description\":\"Agents find MCP servers through registries the way people find apps through app stores. We check the official MCP Registry and Smithery for an entry verified against your domain, and look for an npm or PyPI package of yours that runs as an MCP server.\",\"status\":\"fail\",\"score\":0,\"maxScore\":3,\"details\":\"No verified entry in the official MCP Registry or on Smithery, and no npm or PyPI package of yours that runs as an MCP server. To pass, publish the server to the official MCP Registry under your domain's namespace (com.example/server for example.com), get a verified Smithery listing with non-zero usage, or publish it to npm or PyPI with \\\"mcp\\\" in the package name and your site as its homepage. On npm it needs a `bin` entry so `npx` can start it; on PyPI its summary has to say it is an MCP server. You can also link the registry entry or npm package from your homepage or docs. Smithery did not answer our lookups.\",\"recommendation\":\"Publish your MCP server where agent platforms look for one: the official MCP Registry (registry.modelcontextprotocol.io) under your domain's namespace, Smithery (smithery.ai), or an npm or PyPI package that runs as an MCP server, with \\\"mcp\\\" in the package name. On npm give it a `bin` entry so `npx` can start it; on PyPI say it is an MCP server in its summary. Link the registry entry or package from your homepage or docs, or set the package's homepage to your site, so we can confirm it is yours.\",\"bonus\":false,\"maturity\":\"verified\",\"tier\":\"recommended\",\"estScoreGain\":4.2},{\"id\":\"npm-sdk-package\",\"name\":\"NPM/PyPI SDK package\",\"description\":\"An official SDK or CLI on NPM or PyPI gives agents and the developers steering them a ready-made way in, instead of hand-rolling every API call.\",\"status\":\"pass\",\"score\":1,\"maxScore\":1,\"details\":\"NPM package found: @synapti/trail-plugin - \\\"Trail v0.2 live-hook capture — Claude Code plugin. Subscribes to PostToolUse, UserPromptSubmit, SessionStart, SessionEnd hooks and builds the packet incrementally. Augments (does not replace) the post-hoc @synapti/trail-capture CLI.\\\"\",\"recommendation\":\"Publish a JavaScript/TypeScript SDK package on npm so developers can integrate your API programmatically. In package.json set `repository` to your source repo and `homepage` to your product domain - these links are how agents confirm the package is your official SDK rather than a third-party tool with a similar name.\",\"bonus\":false,\"maturity\":\"verified\",\"tier\":\"recommended\"},{\"id\":\"agent-rules-repo\",\"name\":\"Agent platform configs\",\"description\":\"Published rules or config files for AI coding tools (Claude, Cursor, Windsurf). They teach coding agents to use your product correctly from the first prompt.\",\"status\":\"pass\",\"score\":1,\"maxScore\":1,\"details\":\"Agent config found: github.com/synaptiai/agent-capability-standard/blob/main/AGENTS.md\",\"recommendation\":\"Add an AGENTS.md or .cursorrules file to your public GitHub repo with instructions for how AI coding agents should interact with your codebase. Then make sure the repo is documented in the entry-point pages agents read - homepage, docs, and llms.txt - so it can be discovered without guessing.\",\"bonus\":false,\"maturity\":\"emerging\",\"tier\":\"emerging\"},{\"id\":\"agent-plugins-repo\",\"name\":\"Agent Plugins manifest\",\"description\":\"An Agent Plugins manifest (plugin.json) in your public GitHub repos, bundling skills and MCP servers into one installable package. An emerging format, so it never costs points.\",\"status\":\"warning\",\"score\":0,\"maxScore\":1,\"details\":\"Plugin manifest found without the Agent Plugins $schema identifier: github.com/synaptiai/agent-capability-standard/blob/main/.claude-plugin/plugin.json\",\"recommendation\":\"Declare conformance by adding \\\"$schema\\\": \\\"https://agent-plugins.org/schemas/1.0.0/plugin.schema.json\\\" to plugin.json\",\"bonus\":true,\"specUrl\":\"https://agent-plugins.org/specification\",\"draft\":true,\"maturity\":\"emerging\",\"tier\":\"emerging\"},{\"id\":\"registry-branding\",\"name\":\"Registry branding\",\"description\":\"Your MCP registry entry has a display name, icon, and description. Agents choosing between servers see this first; a bare entry looks abandoned.\",\"status\":\"pass\",\"score\":2,\"maxScore\":2,\"details\":\"MCP manifest has full branding (name, icon, description) at https://acs.synapti.ai/.well-known/mcp/server-card.json\",\"recommendation\":\"Give the server card of each MCP server a display name (title), an icon (icons[].src), and a description - all three together are what reads as a complete, branded listing agents can present. Serve each card at <server URL>/server-card or list it in /.well-known/ai-catalog.json; the older /.well-known/mcp/server-card.json at your origin is still read.\",\"bonus\":false,\"maturity\":\"emerging\",\"tier\":\"emerging\"},{\"id\":\"chatgpt-app-listed\",\"name\":\"ChatGPT app listed\",\"description\":\"Listed in the ChatGPT app directory, where hundreds of millions of users can pull your product into a conversation by name. Upside-only: the directory is curated and gated, so absence never costs points.\",\"status\":\"fail\",\"score\":0,\"maxScore\":2,\"details\":\"Not found in ChatGPT app directory\",\"recommendation\":\"Submit your app to the ChatGPT apps / connectors directory (the apps-in-ChatGPT surface) so ChatGPT users can discover and use your product.\",\"bonus\":true,\"maturity\":\"verified\",\"tier\":\"recommended\",\"estScoreGain\":1.5},{\"id\":\"noindex-directives\",\"name\":\"Homepage not hidden from search\",\"description\":\"Agents often find a site by searching the web. A noindex tag or X-Robots-Tag header removes the page from search results, so we check the homepage for one.\",\"status\":\"pass\",\"score\":1,\"maxScore\":1,\"details\":\"No noindex on the homepage: no robots, googlebot or bingbot meta tag and no X-Robots-Tag header hides it from search.\",\"recommendation\":\"Remove the noindex directive from your homepage: the robots, googlebot or bingbot meta tag in the page head, or an X-Robots-Tag response header. Common causes are a staging setting left on after launch (in WordPress, Settings > Reading > Discourage search engines), an SEO plugin setting, or a host adding the header, as preview builds often do. Verify with `curl -sI https://yourdomain.com | grep -i x-robots-tag` and by searching the page source for name=\\\"robots\\\".\",\"bonus\":false,\"specUrl\":\"https://developers.google.com/search/docs/crawling-indexing/block-indexing\",\"maturity\":\"verified\",\"tier\":\"recommended\"}],\"score\":6,\"maxScore\":16},{\"id\":\"accessibility\",\"name\":\"Access\",\"description\":\"Can agents access your data and understand you?\",\"checks\":[{\"id\":\"sitemap\",\"name\":\"Sitemap exists\",\"description\":\"A map of every page you want found. Agents use your XML sitemap to discover content without crawling blind, so gaps here mean pages that never get read.\",\"status\":\"pass\",\"score\":1,\"maxScore\":1,\"details\":\"Valid sitemap found at https://acs.synapti.ai/sitemap.xml with 172 entries\",\"recommendation\":\"Add a valid XML sitemap at /sitemap.xml listing all indexable URLs. Include lastmod dates and keep it under 50MB.\",\"bonus\":false,\"maturity\":\"verified\",\"tier\":\"required\"},{\"id\":\"content-no-js\",\"name\":\"Content without JavaScript\",\"description\":\"Most AI crawlers never run JavaScript. If your pages need it to show content, agents see a blank site. We fetch your pages with JavaScript off and check the content is still there.\",\"status\":\"pass\",\"score\":5,\"maxScore\":5,\"details\":\"Homepage: 12223 chars, semantic headings (1 H1 + 8 H2s + 15 H3s), 5.3% content ratio. 5 of 5 sampled inner pages have text without JavaScript.\",\"recommendation\":\"Serve at least 500 characters of meaningful homepage content in raw HTML. Add a clear H1, keep deeper heading levels sequential, and remove excessive non-content markup. Inner pages need their main text in the raw HTML too, not only after JavaScript runs.\",\"bonus\":false,\"maturity\":\"verified\",\"tier\":\"required\"},{\"id\":\"bot-detection\",\"name\":\"Not blocked by bot detection\",\"description\":\"Your bot protection may be turning away the visitors you want. We check whether AI agents can reach your site without being blocked.\",\"status\":\"pass\",\"score\":2,\"maxScore\":2,\"details\":\"Site accessible to 4 agent user-agents (ChatGPT-User, OAI-SearchBot, Claude-User, PerplexityBot).\",\"recommendation\":\"Let the agents that act for users and search (ChatGPT-User, OAI-SearchBot, Claude-User, PerplexityBot) through your WAF and bot rules. On Cloudflare, allow verified bots rather than matching User-Agent strings, which anyone can fake.\",\"bonus\":false,\"maturity\":\"verified\",\"tier\":\"required\"},{\"id\":\"agent-discovery-file\",\"name\":\"Agent discovery file\",\"description\":\"A dedicated endpoint that tells arriving agents what you are and where to start, like a front desk for automated visitors.\",\"status\":\"pass\",\"score\":2,\"maxScore\":2,\"details\":\"Agent Skills index (agentskills.io) found at /.well-known/agent-skills/index.json with 42 skill(s)\",\"recommendation\":\"Publish an Agent Skills index at /.well-known/agent-skills/index.json that lists your capabilities, with each skill carrying a name and a description so agents can find and parse what you offer.\",\"bonus\":false,\"maturity\":\"emerging\",\"tier\":\"emerging\"},{\"id\":\"agent-skills-index-v2\",\"name\":\"Agent Skills index conformance (v0.2.0)\",\"description\":\"Your published agent skills follow the current discovery spec, so tools can verify and install them safely. We check /.well-known/agent-skills/index.json for the v0.2.0 schema and typed entries, then verify one artifact digest (SKILL.md or archive).\",\"status\":\"pass\",\"score\":2,\"maxScore\":2,\"details\":\"Index v0.2.0 conformant; verified SHA-256 of \\\"attribute\\\" (skill-md); 41 other skills present; not fetched\",\"recommendation\":\"Upgrade /.well-known/agent-skills/index.json to the v0.2.0 schema: add \\\"$schema\\\": \\\"https://schemas.agentskills.io/discovery/0.2.0/schema.json\\\", and give every entry a type (skill-md or archive), url, and digest. Use \\\"digest\\\": \\\"sha256:<64 lowercase hex chars>\\\" (e.g. \\\"digest\\\": \\\"sha256:a3f1...\\\") - a bare \\\"sha256\\\": \\\"<hex>\\\" field is also accepted. Compute the value from the artifact's raw bytes. For archives, hash the ZIP or tar.gz download itself; a separate skill-md entry is not required.\",\"bonus\":true,\"maturity\":\"emerging\",\"tier\":\"emerging\"},{\"id\":\"a2a-agent-card\",\"name\":\"A2A / agent-card\",\"description\":\"A business card for agent-to-agent contact: who you are, what you can do, and how to reach you, published at /.well-known/agent-card.json (the A2A protocol).\",\"status\":\"fail\",\"score\":0,\"maxScore\":2,\"details\":\"No A2A agent card found at /.well-known/agent-card.json\",\"recommendation\":\"Publish an Agent-to-Agent (A2A) agent card at /.well-known/agent-card.json describing your agent's capabilities, skills, and contact endpoint.\",\"bonus\":true,\"maturity\":\"emerging\",\"tier\":\"emerging\"},{\"id\":\"skills-sh-listed\",\"name\":\"Listed on skills.sh\",\"description\":\"Official skills published on skills.sh, the public directory where agents and developers browse for ready-made capabilities.\",\"status\":\"pass\",\"score\":1,\"maxScore\":1,\"details\":\"48 official skills published on skills.sh - 52 total installs (skills.sh/synaptiai)\",\"recommendation\":\"Publish agent skills on skills.sh so AI agents can discover your product's capabilities. Create a SKILL.md in your GitHub repo and register it with 'npx skills add'. See skills.sh/docs.\",\"bonus\":false,\"maturity\":\"emerging\",\"tier\":\"emerging\"},{\"id\":\"pricing-md\",\"name\":\"pricing.md exists\",\"description\":\"An agent comparing options needs your prices in a form it can read. We check for a machine-readable pricing file at /pricing.md.\",\"status\":\"na\",\"score\":0,\"maxScore\":2,\"details\":\"No pricing.md found - agents need machine-readable pricing to compare products and make purchase recommendations\",\"recommendation\":\"Create a /pricing.md file with your pricing tiers, features, and limits in plain markdown. This lets AI","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"persistedOutputPath":"/Users/danielbentes/.REDACTED.txt","persistedOutputSize":117681},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"81cbde08-6f50-48b0-aa3e-0854ab5a8e96","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"session_id":"ef9f3fc8-12b6-4fe4-9f49-aaeedec05648","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/danielbentes/agent-capability-standard/.claude/worktrees/i127","sessionId":"ef9f3fc8-12b6-4fe4-9f49-aaeedec05648","version":"2.1.322","gitBranch":"feature/issue-127-agent-ready","slug":"i-just-came-across-imperative-newell"}
