{"parentUuid":"b3327a61-14e3-42cf-b9db-0dedcd9fb4fd","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch2jc3CeN8gt7gg4BbQ9v","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2579,"cache_read_input_tokens":148809,"output_tokens":2183,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":883},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2579,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2183,"cache_read_input_tokens":148809,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2579,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2579},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":16022,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"c4de00ae-90e8-4ea6-94ac-e8c3bbd44cb3","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Ch2jc2wWTJPznZJt78WVV","requestRef":"a6a5566e-8652-4231-888c-ad38a2d6e1ae","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"e96fec98-e836-4e77-8fc5-ac8bd308a8a7","timestamp":"2026-11-14T11:23:54.839Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-2","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ef9f3fc8-12b6-4fe4-9f49-aaeedec05648","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/danielbentes/agent-capability-standard","sessionId":"ef9f3fc8-12b6-4fe4-9f49-aaeedec05648","version":"2.1.322","gitBranch":"feature/issue-127-agent-ready","slug":"i-just-came-across-imperative-newell"}
{"parentUuid":"e96fec98-e836-4e77-8fc5-ac8bd308a8a7","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch2jc3CeN8gt7gg4BbQ9v","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"PR #128 is merged and deployed, and I checked it on the live site. The ora.ai score went from **24 (F) to 78 (B)**. I also added one caching fix before merging.\n\n**Fail open.** It's already on. I read the `acs-docs` project settings through the Cloudflare API: fail open is on for both production and preview. If the free plan's 100,000 daily worker requests run out, the pages keep loading.\n\n**Does every page view need the worker?** No, but I recommend keeping it. On ordinary pages it does three things:\n- it answers in Markdown when an agent asks for Markdown or identifies itself as an AI crawler;\n- it returns a Markdown \"page not found\" for unknown pages;\n- it adds the headers agents use to find things.\n\nIt costs no speed. I measured the time to first response before and after the deploy, as the median of 8 requests per page from here:\n\n| Page | Before the worker | With the worker |\n|---|---|---|\n| Home | 120 ms | 105 ms |\n| A capability page | 131 ms | 89 ms |\n| The Standard (largest page) | 132 ms | 130 ms |\n\nThe only real cost is the daily request allowance, and fail open covers that. The alternative is to run the worker only on the home page, `/mcp`, the API and the `.md` addresses. Then other pages would no longer answer Markdown to agents that ask for it.\n\n**Is the site slow?** I couldn't make it slow in Chrome. The home page paints at 0.12 s, a capability page at 0.2 s, and the Standard page at 0.3 s. One first load showed 5.8 s, but that was because the automated browser tab wasn't in front; it wasn't the site. Compressed, the home page is 22 KB and the Standard page 86 KB.\n\n**Caching.** One real problem, now fixed:\n- **Before:** fonts, styles and scripts were cached for only 4 hours, then re-checked with the server. That probably explains slow-feeling visits after a break.\n- **Now:** these files have a content hash in their names, so the site tells browsers to keep them for a year. This is live.\n- **Pages:** these stay \"always re-check\". That's correct for pages: the check is cheap, and you see new content right after a deploy.\n\nIf one particular thing felt slow, such as opening search or one page, tell me which and I'll measure it.\n\n**Live checks after the deploy.** All passed:\n- Markdown for agents on the home page, for AI crawlers, and at `.md` addresses;\n- the Markdown \"page not found\";\n- the `/spec/` redirect;\n- the API with its JSON error;\n- every discovery file, plus the about, contact, privacy and developers pages;\n- the MCP server answers and its search works;\n- pages.dev copies are hidden from search engines, and the real site isn't.\n\n**Score by section:**\n\n| Section | Score |\n|---|---|\n| Discovery | 6/16 |\n| Access | 45/46 |\n| Usability | 83/101 |\n\n**What's still missing:**\n- **Fixable on the site, honestly:**\n  - one in-page tool description is over Chrome's 150-character guidance;\n  - the in-page tools can't browse the list of pages;\n  - the API description doesn't use its error format on every response, and only 3 of 11 responses have typed schemas;\n  - the home page's structured data could link more real profiles, such as LinkedIn or Wikidata, if they exist.\n- **Needs you:**\n  - listing the MCP server in the official MCP Registry or on Smithery (publishing outside the repo);\n  - search ranking for the docs and the brand, which builds over time.\n- **Left out on purpose, because they would be fake:** login, OAuth, rate limits, idempotency keys, async jobs, a sandbox, an A2A agent card, and a postal address.\n\nDo you want a follow-up PR for the first group? It's small: fix the tool description, add a page-browsing tool, and tighten the API description. It should be worth a few more points."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2579,"cache_read_input_tokens":148809,"output_tokens":2183,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":883},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2579,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2183,"cache_read_input_tokens":148809,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2579,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2579},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"c4de00ae-90e8-4ea6-94ac-e8c3bbd44cb3","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Ch2jc2wWTJPznZJt78WVV","requestRef":"a6a5566e-8652-4231-888c-ad38a2d6e1ae","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"f6dfbeae-48fe-4a57-9850-fe8a876af944","timestamp":"2026-11-14T11:24:00.788Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-2","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ef9f3fc8-12b6-4fe4-9f49-aaeedec05648","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/danielbentes/agent-capability-standard","sessionId":"ef9f3fc8-12b6-4fe4-9f49-aaeedec05648","version":"2.1.322","gitBranch":"feature/issue-127-agent-ready","slug":"i-just-came-across-imperative-newell"}
