 details of fixable checks"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"0d611753-2f1d-494b-9ca6-9ef763d96209","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Ch2k3vazks7h8UGVGgM7n","requestRef":"8c0fb236-b139-484f-b2d1-0064ddcbab35","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"ccbb607d-a02e-46ff-8e41-7af30b4a12f2","timestamp":"2026-11-14T11:29:34.023Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-2","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ef9f3fc8-12b6-4fe4-9f49-aaeedec05648","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/danielbentes/agent-capability-standard","sessionId":"ef9f3fc8-12b6-4fe4-9f49-aaeedec05648","version":"2.1.322","gitBranch":"main","slug":"i-just-came-across-imperative-newell"}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"ef9f3fc8-12b6-4fe4-9f49-aaeedec05648","hash":"adcf92ef8bbb9b9192447fe48b21f383ef3e321913b47efe0f2b09ba37a52b02","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014nYu7i9otexn2Y9mA72ceQ","type":"tool_result","content":"### webmcp-schema-quality\nEach tool and each of its parameters has a description, within Chrome's suggested size limits, so an agent knows what to send.\nDETAILS: 1 of 4 tool schemas are harder for an agent to use than they need to be: read_page 1 parameter description is over Chrome's 150-character guidance.\nREC: Describe each tool in a sentence that says what it does and returns, and give every parameter in inputSchema a description. Keep both short: Chrome's WebMCP guidance suggests size limits for each.\nDATA: null\n\n### webmcp-coverage\nThe tools cover the core flow for this kind of site, such as search, cart and checkout for a store.\nDETAILS: The tool set covers 2 of the 3 things an agent needs on a docs site; it cannot navigate the documentation tree.\nREC: Register tools for the core flow of your kind of site, such as search, product detail, cart and checkout for a store, so an agent can finish the job on the page.\nDATA: null\n\n### webmcp-entry-point\nTools register through document.modelContext, the entry point the current draft defines.\nDETAILS: Every tool registers through the deprecated navigator.modelContext alias; move them to document.modelContext before the alias is removed.\nREC: Register tools on document.modelContext. Fall back to navigator.modelContext only when document.modelContext is missing, since current browsers deprecate the alias.\nDATA: null\n\n### api-error-model\nA typed error schema in your OpenAPI spec, so agents know every failure shape in advance and can handle each one deliberately.\nDETAILS: Partial typed error model: error schema defined but not consistently referenced (or vice versa)\nREC: Document your error responses in your OpenAPI spec: give 4xx and 5xx responses a typed error schema (or use RFC 9457 application/problem+json). A consistent error object with a machine-readable code and a human-readable message lets agents handle failures without guessing.\nDATA: null\n\n### function-calling-compat\nWhether your API spec translates cleanly into the function-calling format ChatGPT, Claude, and Gemini actually consume. Incompatible specs mean agents cannot call you even when they want to.\nDETAILS: Partial compatibility: 11/11 operationIds, 3/11 typed schemas\nREC: Ensure API endpoints have unique operation IDs, typed schemas, and descriptions compatible with LLM function-calling formats.\nDATA: null\n\n### json-ld-entity-linking\nsameAs links from your structured data to your official profiles (GitHub, LinkedIn, app stores). They let AIs confirm that every mention of you is actually you.\nDETAILS: Entity linking to github.com  - add more authority profiles (Wikipedia, Wikidata, LinkedIn, GitHub)\nREC: Add sameAs links in your JSON-LD structured data pointing to your Wikipedia page, Wikidata entry, GitHub org, and social profiles. This helps AI disambiguate your brand from similarly named entities.\nDATA: null\n\n### pagination-shape\nA predictable way to page through lists, cursor-based preferred. Without one, agents read page one and quietly miss the rest of your data.\nDETAILS: No pagination pattern found in OpenAPI spec\nREC: Use a consistent, documented pagination shape on your list endpoints (cursor-based preferred) and define the pagination fields in your OpenAPI response schemas, so agents can page through results without guessing the shape.\nDATA: null\nShell cwd was reset to /Users/danielbentes/agent-capability-standard","is_error":false}]}}
