{"parentUuid":"633d535b-ebcc-45e6-8cd9-5a6625323a70","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"environment","snapshot":{"workingDirectory":"/Users/danielbentes/agent-capability-standard/.claude/worktrees/i-followup","isWorktree":true,"isGitRepo":true,"additionalWorkingDirectories":[],"platform":"darwin","shell":"zsh","osVersion":"Darwin 27.2.0","scratchpadDirectory":"REDACTED"},"changes":[{"field":"workingDirectory","from":"/Users/danielbentes/agent-capability-standard/.claude/worktrees/i-followup/site"}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"7dabc55e-a41e-4136-a5cb-ecb9b59e2771","timestamp":"2026-11-14T11:34:11.202Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n# Environment update\n - Primary working directory: /Users/danielbentes/agent-capability-standard/.claude/worktrees/i-followup (was /Users/danielbentes/agent-capability-standard/.claude/worktrees/i-followup/site)\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"ef9f3fc8-12b6-4fe4-9f49-aaeedec05648","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/danielbentes/agent-capability-standard/.claude/worktrees/i-followup","sessionId":"ef9f3fc8-12b6-4fe4-9f49-aaeedec05648","version":"2.1.322","gitBranch":"feature/agent-ready-followup","slug":"i-just-came-across-imperative-newell"}
{"parentUuid":"7dabc55e-a41e-4136-a5cb-ecb9b59e2771","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch2kQiiTuBMxfJNVXDQPB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RFtqoxVPuWW4tnckQjHLmD","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"REDACTED; cat > $S/pr-followup.md <<'EOF'\n## Summary\n\nFixes the agent-readiness gaps on acs.synapti.ai that can be fixed honestly, from the ora.ai scan of 14 November 2026 (score 78, grade B).\n\n- **Browsing the docs in the page.** Each page registers a fifth read-only WebMCP tool, `list_pages`. With no arguments it lists every section and its pages. With a section id it lists that section's pages by sidebar group, each with its URL, Markdown URL and summary. It reads `/api/v1/pages.json`. The MCP server keeps its four tools: ora's focus check passes at four, and an MCP client can read the same list from `/api/v1/pages.json` or `/llms.txt`.\n- **Shorter parameter description.** `read_page`'s `section` description is now under Chrome's 150-character guidance for WebMCP parameters. The test now holds every parameter to 150 characters.\n- **API errors.** Every operation in `/openapi.json` now documents the 503 `application/problem+json` response, with `Retry-After`, that the worker gives on any `/api/` path whose file cannot be read. Before, only the three operations that take an id referenced the error schema. Each 200 schema also states `type: object` beside its `$ref`, for tools that don't follow references.\n- **Structured data.** The plugin's JSON-LD now links its skills.sh listing, which was checked to exist.\n\n## Verification\n\nOn 453c289:\n\n- `npm run check`: no errors.\n- `npm test`: 46 files, 1124 tests pass. New tests cover `list_pages` (all sections, one section, an unknown section, an empty argument), the 150-character limit, and the 503 response on every operation.\n- `npm run build`: every check-dist check passes.\n- `list_pages` was run against the built `pages.json`: 172 pages in 11 sections (13,451 characters); the Specification section is 3,183 characters.\n\n## Not included\n\n- ora reports that the tools register through `navigator.modelContext`. The code uses `document.modelContext` whenever it exists, and ora's own WebMCP check found `document.modelContext.registerTool` in the bundle. The scanner's browser probably provides only the older entry point. Nothing to change.\n- **Fake features:** pagination, rate limits, idempotency keys, async jobs, a sandbox and authentication. The API has none of these, and adding them only to pass a check would make it fake.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01Jea2Va3FATnCydAsWsbLXR\nEOF\ngh pr create --repo synaptiai/agent-capability-standard --base main --head feature/agent-ready-followup --title \"feat(site): list_pages tool, documented API errors, skills.sh link\" --body-file $S/pr-followup.md","description":"Open the follow-up pull request"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":945,"cache_read_input_tokens":208966,"output_tokens":1106,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":945,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1106,"cache_read_input_tokens":208966,"cache_creation_input_tokens":945,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":945},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":10184,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01RFtqoxVPuWW4tnckQjHLmD":{"command":"REDACTED; cat > $S/pr-followup.md <<'EOF'\n## Summary\n\nFixes the agent-readiness gaps on acs.synapti.ai that can be fixed honestly, from the ora.ai scan of 14 November 2026 (score 78, grade B).\n\n- **Browsing the docs in the page.** Each page registers a fifth read-only WebMCP tool, `list_pages`. With no arguments it lists every section and its pages. With a section id it lists that section's pages by sidebar group, each with its URL, Markdown URL and summary. It reads `/api/v1/pages.json`. The MCP server keeps its four tools: ora's focus check passes at four, and an MCP client can read the same list from `/api/v1/pages.json` or `/llms.txt`.\n- **Shorter parameter description.** `read_page`'s `section` description is now under Chrome's 150-character guidance for WebMCP parameters. The test now holds every parameter to 150 characters.\n- **API errors.** Every operation in `/openapi.json` now documents the 503 `application/problem+json` response, with `Retry-After`, that the worker gives on any `/api/` path whose file cannot be read. Before, only the three operations that take an id referenced the error schema. Each 200 schema also states `type: object` beside its `$ref`, for tools that don't follow references.\n- **Structured data.** The plugin's JSON-LD now links its skills.sh listing, which was checked to exist.\n\n## Verification\n\nOn 453c289:\n\n- `npm run check`: no errors.\n- `npm test`: 46 files, 1124 tests pass. New tests cover `list_pages` (all sections, one section, an unknown section, an empty argument), the 150-character limit, and the 503 response on every operation.\n- `npm run build`: every check-dist check passes.\n- `list_pages` was run against the built `pages.json`: 172 pages in 11 sections (13,451 characters); the Specification section is 3,183 characters.\n\n## Not included\n\n- ora reports that the tools register through `navigator.modelContext`. The code uses `document.modelContext` whenever it exists, and ora's own WebMCP check found `document.modelContext.registerTool` in the bundle. The scanner's browser probably provides only the older entry point. Nothing to change.\n- **Fake features:** pagination, rate limits, idempotency keys, async jobs, a sandbox and authentication. The API has none of these, and adding them only to pass a check would make it fake.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01Jea2Va3FATnCydAsWsbLXR\nEOF\ngh pr create --repo synaptiai/agent-capability-standard --base main --head feature/agent-ready-followup --title \"feat(site): list_pages tool, documented API errors, skills.sh link\" --body-file $S/pr-followup.md","description":"Open the follow-up pull request"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"c05ed822-781c-4840-b760-57032c899f8e","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Ch2kQiV58m27HCUv9r6Ap","requestRef":"bf918b36-f5a6-496a-a9a3-092a1c52939f","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"efc18615-420b-4293-b552-df14e45c5b08","timestamp":"2026-11-14T11:34:22.328Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-2","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ef9f3fc8-12b6-4fe4-9f49-aaeedec05648","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/danielbentes/agent-capability-standard/.claude/worktrees/i-followup","sessionId":"ef9f3fc8-12b6-4fe4-9f49-aaeedec05648","version":"2.1.322","gitBranch":"feature/agent-ready-followup","slug":"i-just-came-across-imperative-newell"}
