h building or improving a website to be agent-ready; `ora` covers discovering products, checking scores, and submitting feedback via ora. |\n| `list_checks` | List the full catalog of checks behind the agent-readiness score: every check id with its layer, max score, applicability, tier, maturity, and beta flag. Optional `scoringVersion`. Same document as `GET /api/checks`. |\n| `run_checks` | Run a selected subset of checks against a URL and get per-check results back - the re-verify step after shipping a fix. Pass `url`, `checkIds` (ids from `list_checks`), and optional `mcpUrl`. Always executes live, spends one daily scan-budget unit, and returns no aggregate score. Same shape as `POST /api/scan/checks`. |\n| `run_journey` | Send a real AI agent at a site on a task and get ora's verdict, step count, and insight. Pass `domain`, and either a curated `intent` (`pricing` by default; also `signup`, `api-docs`, `integrate`, `support`, and more) or, with an ora partner API key as the connection's `Authorization: Bearer` header, a free-text `task` (4-300 characters). Optional `agent` picks from the public roster. Same limits as `POST /api/journey/runs`; a target at its cap answers with its most recent stored run. Waits up to 50 seconds; a longer run returns `nextAction` pointing at `get_journey_run`. |\n| `get_journey_run` | Keep following a run that `run_journey` started: pass `run_id`. Waits up to 50 seconds, then returns the verdict and insight, or `nextAction` to call again while the agent is still working. Starts no run and spends no allowance. |\n| `generate_agent_files` | Draft the files agents look for on a site (`/.well-known/ard.json`, `/.well-known/ai-catalog.json`, `/.well-known/poppy.json`; `include` adds `llms.txt`, `robots.txt`, `api-catalog`, `mcp-server-card`, or `all`) from ora's last scan of the `domain`. Returns each file's path, exact body, and review notes. Same files as `GET /api/agent-files/{domain}`. |\n\n### Skills\n\nThe same server hands coding