{"parentUuid":"61048c55-e144-4dd0-b749-a07264edc520","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch2pyKWpyfsPEC23Pvikz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"PR #129 is merged and live; the deploy succeeded. I re-ran the affected checks on the live site with ora's re-verify endpoint. A full re-scan isn't possible yet: ora served its scan from 11:23 from cache, before this deploy.\n\n**Fixed:**\n- **In-page tools:** 6.4/8 → **8/8**. ora read the new 5-tool set, accepted every parameter description against Chrome's limit, and now reports that agents can \"search or browse the catalog, read a page\". That should take the total from 78 to about 80 the next time ora runs a full scan.\n- **Live content:**\n  - every API operation now documents the 503 error;\n  - the home page links the skills.sh listing;\n  - the developers page lists `list_pages`.\n\n**Unchanged:**\n- **API error model (1/3) and function-calling compatibility (1/2).** ora still counts 3 of 11 operations as having typed schemas. Three is exactly the number of operations that take an id. So it most likely counts typed inputs, and the other 8 operations take no input at all. ora doesn't publish how either check is scored. Getting the points would mean adding parameters or error cases that don't exist, so I've stopped there.\n- **Entry-point warning, worth 0 points.** The code uses the current entry point. ora's own WebMCP check found that call in the page's script, so the warning seems to come from ora's test browser.\n- **Organization profiles (0.5/1).** This needs real LinkedIn or Wikidata addresses for Synapti, if they exist.\n\nTwo questions from before are still open:\n- Do you want the Markdown token-count header? It's a small PR.\n- Which content signals should the site send: yes to all three, or leave AI training out?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":578,"cache_read_input_tokens":236430,"output_tokens":916,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":349},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":578,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":916,"cache_read_input_tokens":236430,"cache_creation_input_tokens":578,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":578},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"79d26134-abbb-4074-9150-6e90cabcb566","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Ch2pyKFxJHhEMSqFN5EjF","requestRef":"61e5039f-159e-410b-bebe-f4230deb934b","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","type":"assistant","uuid":"a76b0ff7-eb64-4eb5-96ae-30bcc8dd822f","timestamp":"2026-11-14T12:34:10.781Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-2","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"ef9f3fc8-12b6-4fe4-9f49-aaeedec05648","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/danielbentes/agent-capability-standard/.claude/worktrees/i-followup","sessionId":"ef9f3fc8-12b6-4fe4-9f49-aaeedec05648","version":"2.1.322","gitBranch":"feature/agent-ready-followup","slug":"i-just-came-across-imperative-newell"}
