AP_PATH}\\n`;"," }"," "]}]},{"filePath":"/Users/danielbentes/agent-capability-standard/.claude/worktrees/i-signals/site/src/lib/developers.ts","hunks":[{"oldStart":191,"oldLines":6,"newStart":191,"newLines":7,"lines":["   'Every page has a Markdown copy at its URL followed by index.md; the home page\\'s is /index.md. Each HTML page links to it with <link rel=\"alternate\" type=\"text/markdown\">.',","   'The same copy is served at the page\\'s URL with .md in place of the final slash (/capabilities/mutate.md), and at the page\\'s own URL to a request whose Accept header prefers text/markdown. A page that does not exist answers 404 in Markdown to a client that is not a browser.',","   'Each copy opens with front matter (title, description, canonical and last_updated), then the page with a top-level heading. Links in a copy point at the other pages\\' copies, so an agent can follow them without reading HTML. Figures are given as tables or lists with the same data.',","+  'Each Markdown answer carries X-Markdown-Tokens, an estimate of its length in tokens (one per four characters), and every answer carries Content-Signal: search=yes, ai-input=yes, ai-train=yes: the content may be used in search, as input to AI answers and for AI training.',","   `llms.txt lists the main pages of each section and links one llms.txt per section, which lists every copy. llms-full.txt holds the current Standard, every capability page and every workflow page in one file. The sitemap is at /sitemap.xml.`,"," ];"," "]}]},{"filePath":"/Users/danielbentes/agent-capability-standard/.claude/worktrees/i-signals/site/src/lib/structured-data.ts","hunks":[{"oldStart":15,"oldLines":6,"newStart":15,"newLines":7,"lines":["   name: 'Synapti',","   url: 'https://synapti.ai',","   github: 'https://github.com/synaptiai',","+  linkedin: 'https://www.linkedin.com/company/synapti-ai/',"," } as const;"," "," interface PluginJson {"]},{"oldStart":63,"oldLines":7,"newStart":64,"newLines":7,"lines":["         '@id